{"parentUuid":"416aeb8d-b171-4ee4-85b2-fa2aebd9a103","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdHgYxPALUbcKTenJLhE5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015CoEV2qTdtTJwKzRoYwfeC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit add crates/core/src/extractor/component.rs crates/core/src/extractor/interface.rs crates/core/src/extractor/mod.rs\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(extractor): fix component-mapping rename ordering and alias collapse\n\nAdversarial review found two related correctness bugs in how static\nproperty assignments (displayName, defaultProps) and identifier\naliases rename/find ComponentMapping entries:\n\n1. try_scan_display_name renamed mapping.component_name to the\n   *string value* of `X.displayName = \"...\"` immediately. When that\n   string differs from the variable identifier (a real pattern — an\n   internal implementation name exposed under a nicer public\n   displayName), a later `X.defaultProps = {...}` referencing the\n   *original* identifier could no longer find the mapping. Fixed by\n   deferring the rename: try_scan_display_name now records the pending\n   rename on the collector and finish() applies it as the very last\n   step, after every other scan has already had its chance to look\n   mappings up by their original identifier for the whole file.\n\n2. try_rename_identifier_wrapped_component renamed the matched mapping\n   in place. A second, different alias to the same base\n   (`const A = Base; const Bcopy = Base;`) could never find the base\n   again — the first alias had already renamed it away — silently\n   dropping the second alias with no trace. Fixed by cloning the\n   matched mapping under the new name instead of mutating it, with the\n   base's own (implementation-only) name filtered out of the final\n   output in finish() via a new aliased_away set.\n\nAlso extracted two shared helpers this touched anyway: static_member_\nassignment (X.Y = <expr> parsing, shared by try_scan_display_name and\ntry_scan_default_props — they were previously identical end to end)\nand as_const_literal (the `const X = <expr> as const` name+cast-peel\nprologue shared by try_collect_const_enum and try_collect_const_array).\n\nAll existing tests (including the antd Button rename and day-picker\nfixtures) still pass unchanged — these were real but previously\nuntested edge cases, not regressions in already-covered behavior.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10\ngit log --oneline -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":429,"cache_read_input_tokens":682330,"output_tokens":853,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":429,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":853,"cache_read_input_tokens":682330,"cache_creation_input_tokens":429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":429},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHgYseuKgcrGkNjD3rov","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fbfd800-2613-4758-a504-8893681803aa","timestamp":"2026-07-22T19:54:50.750Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
