{"parentUuid":"45baabfe-395e-4055-a3f1-8748e2e9b498","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Explanatory"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9374c953-193d-4e33-8f85-7618a48f652e","timestamp":"2026-07-22T20:11:30.885Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"9374c953-193d-4e33-8f85-7618a48f652e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdHhqcLkWak1HPYNqNqhF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W4djvJoGSVi3bEBSPwigKJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit add crates/core/src/pipeline/mod.rs crates/core/src/pipeline/watch.rs crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(pipeline): fix watch-mode's real correctness and perf gaps\n\nAdversarial review found watch mode wasn't actually correct or\nincremental in four compounding ways:\n\n1. WatchSession::initialize() rebuilt GlobalSourceData by hand\n   (discover -> parse -> merge only), skipping Phase 3.5 (@types/react\n   Full-mode merge) and Phase 3.6 (ambient lib.d.ts merge, this\n   session's own earlier feature) entirely. The cold `output` it\n   returned was correct (built via a real extract() call done\n   separately just for that output), but self.global — what every\n   subsequent update_file() resolves against — was not. Fixed by\n   factoring extract() into extract_with_global(), a single real\n   pipeline run shared by both the one-shot and watch-mode paths, so\n   there's exactly one implementation to keep in sync going forward.\n\n2. ReverseDeps::build was never called — reverse_deps stayed\n   permanently empty, so update_file's BFS dependent-propagation only\n   ever found the changed file itself, never files that import it.\n   Fixed by computing it in initialize() from the now-correctly-merged\n   global (required changing the field from Arc<ReverseDeps> to\n   ArcSwap<ReverseDeps> so initialize() can populate it with &self).\n\n3. Found while writing a real-tempdir test for #2: update_file's\n   `changed` path isn't canonicalized, but discover_files' walker (via\n   the `ignore` crate) resolves symlinks in the paths it reports (e.g.\n   macOS's /var -> /private/var) — so a file-watcher-reported path\n   would never match reverse_deps'/global's keys unless canonicalized\n   the same way, silently finding no dependents regardless of #2's\n   fix. Added canonicalize_best_effort (falls back to canonicalizing\n   the parent dir when the full path doesn't resolve yet, so a file's\n   key stays stable across its own create/delete transitions).\n\n4. resolve_ts_lib_paths re-ran a fresh oxc_resolver filesystem walk on\n   every ResolutionContext::new — i.e. every single update_file call —\n   even though its result (options.src_dirs never changes within a\n   session) can't change between saves. Added\n   ResolutionContext::new_with_cached_ambient_global_files and cached\n   the computed value once on WatchSession at initialize().\n\nAlso fixed the same-shaped bug in Phase 3.5/3.6 themselves: both merged\nfreshly-parsed .d.ts data into `global` without draining its\ndiagnostics first, silently losing anything the extractor flagged\nwhile parsing @types/react or a lib.d.ts file specifically (an\nexcessive-nesting trip, a parse error). Extracted the shared\nmerge_cached_dts_file helper, used by both phases, which drains first.\n\nTwo pre-existing tests encoded the old (incorrect) assumption that\nupdate_file's affected_files/diagnostics keys would exactly echo a\nraw, non-canonicalized input path — updated to canonicalize the\ncomparison value instead of the behavior under test.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10\ngit log --oneline -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_tokens":787400,"output_tokens":1250,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":562,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":787400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":562},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHhqUqoA2tSFzjVY1i7m","type":"assistant","uuid":"baf4b196-ad59-4bf3-b7c5-b64ac7beed2e","timestamp":"2026-07-22T20:11:47.363Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
