{"parentUuid":"40a9f006-7471-416c-86a1-2cd466f4e433","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdHjFqUKBAzGwnX63S6k6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UrSfZCH6KWWKEcxGqDGQBk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit add crates/binding/src/lib.rs crates/cli/src/commands/check.rs crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs \\\n  crates/cli/src/config.rs crates/cli/src/main.rs crates/core/src/react_types.rs\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(cli): fix --json exit codes, scope the flag honestly, stop silently defaulting react-version\n\nAdversarial review found --json was broken in three ways:\n\n1. extract --json returned before the error-diagnostic exit-code\n   check, so it always exited 0 even on hard errors — the one signal\n   CI actually depends on. Fixed by refactoring cmd_extract/cmd_check\n   to return the intended exit code as a value instead of calling\n   std::process::exit() deep inside business logic — makes the\n   decision testable (added a real regression test) and lets main() be\n   the only place that actually terminates the process.\n\n2. --json was a global clap flag, so `check`/`watch`/`inspect --help`\n   all advertised it while silently ignoring it (only cmd_extract ever\n   read it). Scoped it to a per-command field on ExtractArgs/CheckArgs\n   instead: extract already had a natural machine-readable output to\n   gate, and check's diagnostics were an easy, coherent fit to wire up\n   for real. watch/inspect no longer claim to accept a flag that did\n   nothing.\n\n3. node/tsx subprocess stderr was sent to Stdio::null(), so a\n   docgen.config.ts that failed to evaluate produced a generic \"failed\n   to evaluate (exit status: 1)\" with the real syntax error/stack\n   trace thrown away. Now piped and included in the error message.\n   Also wrapped the spawn() failure itself with a clear \"is node\n   installed and on PATH?\" message instead of a bare OS error.\n\nAlso fixed --react-version silently defaulting to react19 on any\nunrecognized value (a typo, or a NAPI caller bypassing the\n'react18' | 'react19' TS type) across all three places that mapped it:\ndocgen.config.ts's reactVersion, the --react-version CLI flag, and\nJsExtractOptions.reactVersion. Added a single\nreact_types::parse_react_version, used by all three, that errors\ninstead of defaulting — matches this crate's own non-negotiable #6.\nLeft --react-version as Option<String> rather than also converting it\nto a clap::ValueEnum (would additionally get --help enumeration and\nparse-time rejection) — a smaller, separate polish on top of the\nnow-fixed correctness issue, not the core problem the review flagged.\n\nThe NAPI conversion change (impl From -> impl TryFrom) required\ncreate_session's return type to change from a bare u32 to\nnapi::Result<u32> so it can reject an invalid reactVersion instead of\nsilently proceeding with react19.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10\ngit log --oneline -6"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":895679,"output_tokens":1090,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":701,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":895679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":701},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHjFiPR3pZkeEZ52cquv","type":"assistant","uuid":"393afeea-5315-47b6-94e8-de3d793615eb","timestamp":"2026-07-22T20:30:21.906Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entry