{"parentUuid":"b2c2bf26-e49f-452e-8545-14188596ebfa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdHkHBqZSEh4YMaEVUdiy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017nB7TaKynXp1dBLstS7a7b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(resolver): correct mistagged OpaqueReason variants and consolidate diagnostics\n\nTwo OpaqueReason tags were factually wrong: a multi-param function was\ntagged ConditionalType, and an unparsable raw type expression was tagged\nDepthExceeded. Added MultiParamFunction and UnsupportedExpression variants\nso consumers filtering/reporting on OpaqueReason see the real cause.\n\nnamed.rs's step-7 fallback returns PropType::Named, not Opaque, but its\ndiagnostic said \"it will appear as opaque\" — corrected to \"unexpanded\nnamed reference\" to match the actual returned type.\n\nThe three independent MaxDepthExceeded diagnostic constructions (named.rs,\nchain.rs, collected.rs) had drifted out of sync — only one included the\n\"may indicate a circular type reference\" help text. Consolidated into a\nsingle resolver::max_depth_diagnostic() helper all three call sites share.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\"\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":498,"cache_read_input_tokens":98642,"output_tokens":435,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":498,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":98642,"cache_creation_input_tokens":498,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":498},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHkHAUD3YMuG1MgbYG6x","type"