{"parentUuid":"7fe592f1-ffae-4400-bd88-f0f4f40c4a2b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdHkc9CqmxStytLBzc9Fw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UYtBqrVnCXVUfT2A26K9RF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nrefactor(diagnostics): shared io_read_error constructor, drop internal jargon, cheaper grouping\n\nThe \"Failed to read '{path}': {error}\" IoError diagnostic was built inline\nidentically at two call sites (pipeline/mod.rs, pipeline/watch.rs). Added\nDiagnostic::io_read_error() as the single source of truth.\n\nchain.rs's unresolvable-type diagnostic exposed \"(scoped key: 'file:name')\"\n— an internal cache-key format, not something a consumer can act on.\nReplaced with \"(resolved to 'name' in 'file')\", shown only when import\nresolution actually redirected the type somewhere other than where it\nwas referenced, which is the actually-useful piece of that internal state.\n\ncli/output.rs's group_diagnostics allocated a format!(\"{:?}\", code) string\nper diagnostic purely to compare DiagnosticCode values that already\nimplement PartialEq — compare by reference instead.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":130659,"output_tokens":429,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":429,"cache_read_input_tokens":130659,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHkc73N1xUwEgXNMWN1b","type":"assistant","u