{"parentUuid":"533ba6b8-5aad-4ecd-9438-7cb28c31dddb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdHmGjsUi45cVnJ41RYFM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NaJz71VembqgfZVvvUUEBg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(resolver): wire up barrel/re-export chain resolution, drop dead diagnostic codes\n\nimport_map.rs's resolve_reexport_chain (and ReExportStep) were fully\nimplemented and unit-tested in isolation but never called from anywhere\nin production code — a type imported through a barrel file (`export {\nX } from './x'` or `export * from './x'`, the standard index.ts pattern\nin every real component library) resolved to the barrel itself, which\ndoesn't declare the type, and silently degraded to \"Cannot resolve type\".\n\nresolve_to_canonical now follows the chain via a new follow_reexports()\nhelper: after landing on a file via direct import, it checks whether the\ntype is actually declared there, and if not, follows named re-exports or\ntries each wildcard source in turn (recursing through multi-level\nbarrels, depth-capped at 8) until it finds where the type really lives.\nFalls back to the original (file, name) — and the existing \"cannot\nresolve\" diagnostic — if the chain doesn't lead anywhere.\n\nwildcard_sources/wildcard_sources_for were a separate, now-provably-dead\nprecomputed index: resolve_reexport_chain already recomputes the same\ninformation from re_export_map directly, so the field, its population\nloop, and the accessor added nothing and are removed.\n\nAlso removed 4 DiagnosticCode variants (PandaCodegenMissing,\nComponentDetectionFailed, BarrelResolutionFailed, CallableComponent)\nconfirmed never constructed anywhere in the codebase or referenced by\nany JS/TS consumer — BarrelResolutionFailed in particular stays unused\neven after this fix, since every failure path it could describe already\nfalls through to the existing UnresolvableImpo