{"parentUuid":"bf1b4e31-482d-4c6f-99d0-5d6ee688876d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ1ds43BM63VwcUNBxMF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RZA4eAQ36EB65katV1dceZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"head -60 README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":373820,"output_tokens":2236,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":334,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2236,"cache_read_input_tokens":373820,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":334},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ1dpch9qcKRpotvQheG","type":"assistant","uuid":"a270e266-7e34-4abc-804e-97a062d2ac87","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:05:23.278Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"a270e266-7e34-4abc-804e-97a062d2ac87","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01RZA4eAQ36EB65katV1dceZ","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk read README.md --max-lines 60\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":21},"type":"attachment","uuid":"073e3cd7-6815-469c-bfc8-9cd6fc0a08e1","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:05:23.300Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"a270e266-7e34-4abc-804e-97a062d2ac87","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4a9674fb-a972-4853-9f41-80d247c8ddd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RZA4eAQ36EB65katV1dceZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# oxc-react-docgen\n\nReact component prop extraction powered by [OXC](https://oxc.rs). Parses TypeScript natively in Rust — no TypeScript compiler program, no type-checking pass, no startup tax.\n\n> **Status:** Core extraction, NAPI bindings, Vite plugin, CLI, and `docgen.config.ts` loading are complete.\n\n## Why\n\n`react-docgen-typescript` spins up a full TypeScript `Program` to extract props. On a mid-size design system this takes seconds — enough to noticeably delay Storybook startup and make HMR feel sluggish. OXC parses each file in parallel with no type-checking pass, so cold extraction on a 15-component fixture set (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, Radix) takes **32ms**.\n\nThe CLI can emit an RDT-compatible shape via `--format rdt` (see [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md)). The Vite plugin and NAPI binding currently expose this tool's own canonical format only — not a drop-in RDT replacement at that layer yet.\n\n## Install\n\n`@oxc-react-docgen/napi`, `@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin`, and `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` are not yet published to npm — there are no per-platform prebuilt binaries to install today. Until a release ships:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/castrog/oxc-react-codegen\ncd oxc-react-codegen\npnpm install\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/napi run build:napi   # builds the native addon for your platform\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin build\n```\n\n`pnpm run build:napi` (not a bare `cargo build`) matters: it invokes `napi build`, which places the compiled addon exactly where `packages/napi/index.js`'s generated loader expects it. This works as a monorepo-local dependency today; there are no published per-platform packages for it to fall back to yet. See [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md) if you're moving off `react-docgen-typescript` and want to know exactly what's compatible today.\n\n## Vite plugin\n\n```ts\n// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { oxcReactDocgen } from '@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin'\nexport default defineConfig({\nimport docgen from 'virtual:oxc-react-docgen'\n{\n        }\n    }\n}\n[120 more lines]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5fb63ef6-9162-4a90-946f-385e9c6cf973","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:05:25.143Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# oxc-react-docgen\n\nReact component prop extraction powered by [OXC](https://oxc.rs). Parses TypeScript natively in Rust — no TypeScript compiler program, no type-checking pass, no startup tax.\n\n> **Status:** Core extraction, NAPI bindings, Vite plugin, CLI, and `docgen.config.ts` loading are complete.\n\n## Why\n\n`react-docgen-typescript` spins up a full TypeScript `Program` to extract props. On a mid-size design system this takes seconds — enough to noticeably delay Storybook startup and make HMR feel sluggish. OXC parses each file in parallel with no type-checking pass, so cold extraction on a 15-component fixture set (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, Radix) takes **32ms**.\n\nThe CLI can emit an RDT-compatible shape via `--format rdt` (see [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md)). The Vite plugin and NAPI binding currently expose this tool's own canonical format only — not a drop-in RDT replacement at that layer yet.\n\n## Install\n\n`@oxc-react-docgen/napi`, `@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin`, and `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` are not yet published to npm — there are no per-platform prebuilt binaries to install today. Until a release ships:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/castrog/oxc-react-codegen\ncd oxc-react-codegen\npnpm install\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/napi run build:napi   # builds the native addon for your platform\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin build\n```\n\n`pnpm run build:napi` (not a bare `cargo build`) matters: it invokes `napi build`, which places the compiled addon exactly where `packages/napi/index.js`'s generated loader expects it. This works as a monorepo-local dependency today; there are no published per-platform packages for it to fall back to yet. See [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md) if you're moving off `react-docgen-typescript` and want to know exactly what's compatible today.\n\n## Vite plugin\n\n```ts\n// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { oxcReactDocgen } from '@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin'\nexport default defineConfig({\nimport docgen from 'virtual:oxc-react-docgen'\n{\n        }\n    }\n}\n[120 more lines]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a270e266-7e34-4abc-804e-97a062d2ac87","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
