{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"86d84afa-8b4d-4e61-a203-351d1e29d989","snapshotMessageId":"2d93fb8d-67fc-4c7a-bd90-c69f34d027cf","trackingPath":"docs/adr/0001-oxc-over-typescript-compiler.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-07-23T00:09:40.339Z","realParentDir":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr"},"timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:40.357Z"}
{"parentUuid":"937a49d5-610a-4b7e-ac0c-e22e1fcfbd7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ1zGms7UVv6ozeZdmsf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the four seed ADRs, grounded in verified facts from this session's investigation."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_read_input_tokens":396845,"output_tokens":740,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":396845,"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ1zBoDjpCDkjmSRKkD1","type":"assistant","uuid":"8fa9ff03-e1b0-480d-bada-e965d6b940da","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:35.172Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"8fa9ff03-e1b0-480d-bada-e965d6b940da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ1zGms7UVv6ozeZdmsf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019JhEaMWse4HPq6H8m45xYz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0001-oxc-over-typescript-compiler.md","content":"# 0001. Parse with OXC instead of the TypeScript compiler\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive — true since the project started)\n\n## Context\n\n`react-docgen-typescript` extracts props by spinning up a full TypeScript\n`Program` — real type-checking, not just parsing. On a mid-size design system\nthat takes seconds, which shows up as slow Storybook startup and sluggish\nHMR. We wanted prop extraction fast enough to run on every file save without\nanyone noticing.\n\n## Decision\n\nParse TypeScript/TSX with OXC — a Rust parser with no type-checking pass —\nand resolve prop types structurally from the AST instead of asking a type\nchecker. Cold extraction on a 15-component fixture set (shadcn, MUI, Chakra,\nMantine, React Aria, Radix) takes 32ms.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Parsing runs in parallel per file with no shared `Program` state to build\n  or invalidate — this is most of the speed win, not just OXC being a fast\n  parser.\n- We give up real type inference. Conditional types, mapped types over an\n  unbound generic, and a few `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes can't be\n  resolved without one — see `docs/type-checker-integration.md` for the full\n  list.\n- Every one of those gaps degrades to a `Diagnostic` plus an `Opaque` prop\n  type, never a silent wrong answer (`crates/core/CLAUDE.md` non-negotiable\n  #6) — the speed trade-off costs completeness, never correctness.\n- `typescript-go`'s Corsa API may eventually let us add real type inference\n  back in without giving up the parallel-parse architecture — tracked in\n  `docs/type-checker-integration.md`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_read_input_tokens":396845,"output_tokens":740,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":396845,"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":379},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ1zBoDjpCDkjmSRKkD1","type":"assistant","uuid":"86d84afa-8b4d-4e61-a203-351d1e29d989","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:40.336Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"86d84afa-8b4d-4e61-a203-351d1e29d989","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4a9674fb-a972-4853-9f41-80d247c8ddd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019JhEaMWse4HPq6H8m45xYz","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0001-oxc-over-typescript-compiler.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"57f7c0be-c961-4ad9-9ecd-bb27e9a14268","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:40.425Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0001-oxc-over-typescript-compiler.md","content":"# 0001. Parse with OXC instead of the TypeScript compiler\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive — true since the project started)\n\n## Context\n\n`react-docgen-typescript` extracts props by spinning up a full TypeScript\n`Program` — real type-checking, not just parsing. On a mid-size design system\nthat takes seconds, which shows up as slow Storybook startup and sluggish\nHMR. We wanted prop extraction fast enough to run on every file save without\nanyone noticing.\n\n## Decision\n\nParse TypeScript/TSX with OXC — a Rust parser with no type-checking pass —\nand resolve prop types structurally from the AST instead of asking a type\nchecker. Cold extraction on a 15-component fixture set (shadcn, MUI, Chakra,\nMantine, React Aria, Radix) takes 32ms.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Parsing runs in parallel per file with no shared `Program` state to build\n  or invalidate — this is most of the speed win, not just OXC being a fast\n  parser.\n- We give up real type inference. Conditional types, mapped types over an\n  unbound generic, and a few `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes can't be\n  resolved without one — see `docs/type-checker-integration.md` for the full\n  list.\n- Every one of those gaps degrades to a `Diagnostic` plus an `Opaque` prop\n  type, never a silent wrong answer (`crates/core/CLAUDE.md` non-negotiable\n  #6) — the speed trade-off costs completeness, never correctness.\n- `typescript-go`'s Corsa API may eventually let us add real type inference\n  back in without giving up the parallel-parse architecture — tracked in\n  `docs/type-checker-integration.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"86d84afa-8b4d-4e61-a203-351d1e29d989","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"57f7c0be-c961-4ad9-9ecd-bb27e9a14268","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Write","toolUseID":"toolu_019JhEaMWse4HPq6H8m45xYz","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":65},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c0e0e95e-27b9-4146-973d-e7f35e6b5c35","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:40.425Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"c0e0e95e-27b9-4146-973d-e7f35e6b5c35","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Explanatory"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"06592dbc-0401-4d80-8764-e286f4a8286b","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:40.429Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"7e661228-cf26-43b8-9609-f387d7cb07ab","snapshotMessageId":"2d93fb8d-67fc-4c7a-bd90-c69f34d027cf","trackingPath":"docs/adr/0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-07-23T00:09:48.944Z","realParentDir":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr"},"timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:48.975Z"}
{"parentUuid":"06592dbc-0401-4d80-8764-e286f4a8286b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ1zrxBAJh5kJq1UyFtZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ErFVnrQ5CqUuEStviS2mQv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md","content":"# 0002. Hand-write Serialize/Deserialize for PropType instead of deriving it\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\n`PropType` and `CollectedType` are recursive enums — variants nest through\n`Vec`/`Box`/`Option` back into the same type (`Union`, `Object`, `Array`,\n...). At some point this project derived `Serialize`/`Deserialize` directly\non a tagged `PropType` (`#[serde(tag = \"kind\")]`) and had to raise\n`#![recursion_limit]` to 2048 to get it to compile — each nesting level wraps\nthe generated serializer in another layer during codegen, and the default\nlimit (128) isn't enough for a real component tree.\n\n## Decision\n\n`PropType`, `CollectedType`, and `OpaqueReason` don't derive\n`Serialize`/`Deserialize`. Each has a hand-written impl (`to_json_value`/\n`from_json_value` for the first two) that builds a `serde_json::Value`\ndirectly instead of going through serde's derive machinery.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Adding a new variant means updating the manual match in both directions by\n  hand — the compiler won't remind you the way a derive would.\n  `resolver/mod.rs`'s \"no wildcard matches\" convention is what catches a\n  missed arm here instead.\n- `CollectedObjectField` (a struct nested inside `CollectedType::Object`, not\n  an enum) still derives normally — the recursion problem is specific to the\n  recursive *enums*, not every type that touches them.\n- The `#![recursion_limit = \"2048\"]` attribute in `crates/core/src/lib.rs` is\n  left over from the old derive-based design. Verified 2026-07-22: the full\n  workspace builds and every test passes with it removed — nothing in the\n  current manual-impl code path needs it. Worth deleting as a follow-up;\n  left as-is here since confirming that wasn't the point of this decision.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n`serde(remote)`, or just keeping the recursion-limit bump — both keep the\nderive, so you inherit the compile-time cost and a cryptic \"recursion limit\nexceeded\" the moment someone adds one more level of nesting. Manual impls\ntrade a bit of hand-maintenance for a predictable compile time.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_read_input_tokens":397224,"output_tokens":895,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":895,"cache_read_input_tokens":397224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ1zpaJJ2AJeJn4CbWAP","type":"assistant","uuid":"7e661228-cf26-43b8-9609-f387d7cb07ab","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:48.934Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
