{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"cadf1dcc-e127-4fd6-9caa-7b50f28aaa0f","snapshotMessageId":"2d93fb8d-67fc-4c7a-bd90-c69f34d027cf","trackingPath":"docs/adr/0003-positional-msgpack-cache-encoding.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-07-23T00:09:56.040Z","realParentDir":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr"},"timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:56.061Z"}
{"parentUuid":"97791fbd-5f36-41b2-a5be-19813a7deaa3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ21WLxjWCoQsgBGhDxz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RkdrtawLDprSjufNaF7vK1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0003-positional-msgpack-cache-encoding.md","content":"# 0003. Cache the DTS parse cache with positional (not named) MessagePack\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\nThe DTS parse cache persists `SourceData` across runs so unchanged `.d.ts`\nfiles don't get re-parsed. `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — the default,\nand what this project uses — encode structs *positionally*: as an array of\nfield values in declaration order, not a map of field names. A `_named`\nvariant encodes as a map instead, at a size and speed cost we haven't needed\nto pay.\n\n## Decision\n\nUse plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice`, and treat `SourceData`'s field\norder as part of the wire format. A `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` constant\n(`crates/core/src/cache.rs`) gets bumped whenever a field is added anywhere\nbut the end of the struct, removed, or reordered — any change that would\nshift decode position for cache entries written before the change. A version\nmismatch discards the whole cache rather than risk decoding an old entry into\nthe wrong field.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Smaller, faster cache files than named encoding — the whole point.\n- Adding a field to `SourceData` (or anything it contains) requires\n  remembering to bump `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` if it isn't appended at the very\n  end. Easy to forget — `const_arrays` (added mid-struct) is exactly the case\n  this version bump was added to cover.\n- A forgotten bump doesn't fail loudly. It decodes as plausible-looking but\n  wrong data — the worst kind of bug. There's no compiler check for this;\n  it's a discipline problem, not a type-safety one.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1015,"cache_read_input_tokens":398084,"output_tokens":705,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1015,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":398084,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1015,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1015},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ21TfEM85njCUygYE2b","type":"assistant","uuid":"cadf1dcc-e127-4fd6-9caa-7b50f28aaa0f","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:56.037Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"cadf1dcc-e127-4fd6-9caa-7b50f28aaa0f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4a9674fb-a972-4853-9f41-80d247c8ddd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RkdrtawLDprSjufNaF7vK1","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0003-positional-msgpack-cache-encoding.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"afd9735d-7ef3-4e0a-9405-b6a8dcacb96a","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:09:56.130Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0003-positional-msgpack-cache-encoding.md","content":"# 0003. Cache the DTS parse cache with positional (not named) MessagePack\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\nThe DTS parse cache persists `SourceData` across runs so unchanged `.d.ts`\nfiles don't get re-parsed. `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — the default,\nand what this project uses — encode structs *positionally*: as an array of\nfield values in declaration order, not a map of field names. A `_named`\nvariant encodes as a map instead, at a size and speed cost we haven't needed\nto pay.\n\n## Decision\n\nUse plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice`, and treat `SourceData`'s field\norder as part of the wire format. A `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` constant\n(`crates/core/src/cache.rs`) gets bumped whenever a field is added anywhere\nbut the end of the struct, removed, or reordered — any change that would\nshift decode position for cache entries written before the change. A version\nmismatch discards the whole cache rather than risk decoding an old entry into\nthe wrong field.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Smaller, faster cache files than named encoding — the whole point.\n- Adding a field to `SourceData` (or anything it contains) requires\n  remembering to bump `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` if it isn't appended at the very\n  end. Easy to forget — `const_arrays` (added mid-struct) is exactly the case\n  this version bump was added to cover.\n- A forgotten bump doesn't fail loudly. It decodes as plausible-looking but\n  wrong data — the worst kind of bug. There's no compiler check for this;\n  it's a discipline problem, not a type-safety one.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cadf1dcc-e127-4fd6-9caa-7b50f28aaa0f","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
