{"parentUuid":"4ac9d532-07f5-4be2-b27c-a48dc5bf0ed1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ269ppjPwV3j7AnPzhX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N16a2HJc6r7TAFVmVFEY8t","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\ndocs: add ADR convention, seed four retroactive records, add a writing skill\n\nFilled the gap between STATUS.md (what's true now) and rdt-coverage.md\n(what broke and why) — neither captures why a hard-to-reverse decision\nwas made in the first place. docs/adr/README.md sets the bar: numbered,\nimmutable, four sections max, and a concrete banned-word list plus\nbefore/after table so \"avoid AI slop\" means something checkable instead\nof a vibe.\n\nSeeded four real decisions rather than an empty directory:\n- 0001: OXC over the TypeScript compiler (grounded in README's 32ms figure)\n- 0002: manual Serialize/Deserialize for PropType (grounded in a verified\n  finding — the crate's #![recursion_limit = \"2048\"] is leftover from an\n  old derive-based design; confirmed the full workspace builds and all\n  tests pass with it removed, so it's dead weight now, not load-bearing)\n- 0003: positional (non-named) msgpack cache encoding, tied to the\n  CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION discipline already in cache.rs\n- 0004: deferring type-checker integration, pointing at the existing\n  deep-dive in type-checker-integration.md rather than duplicating it\n\n.claude/skills/adr/SKILL.md gives agents the workflow (when it's\nwarranted, how to number, ground claims in something checkable, self-\nreview before saving) without duplicating the README's rules verbatim —\none source of truth for the writing bar, not two copies to drift apart.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -15\ngit log --oneline -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_toke