{"parentUuid":"3000d0a6-9bb6-4e08-905a-23a3f1f602bd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ27JbCZHkxuNrwhpAqU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Set up: `docs/adr/` with a README defining the convention (when to write one, numbering/immutability rules, a concrete banned-word list with before/after examples), a template, and four seeded ADRs covering real decisions — OXC over the TS compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack caching, and deferring type-checker integration. Added `.claude/skills/adr/SKILL.md` so agents can write new ones following the same bar without duplicating the rules (it points at the README as the single source of truth).\n\nOne thing that fell out of writing ADR 0002: I verified `crates/core/src/lib.rs`'s `#![recursion_limit = \"2048\"]` is leftover from an old derive-based design — the full workspace builds and all 191 tests pass with it removed. Noted it in the ADR as a follow-up rather than fixing it now, since that wasn't what you asked for this round. Let me know if you want it deleted.\n\nThe GitHub Issues/Projects question from before is still open — want me to act on that too, or leave it for now?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1401,"cache_read_input_tokens":405297,"output_tokens":590,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1401,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":405297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1401},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ27CAzRrF4LRyJQVAQT","type":"assistant","uuid":"57023916-24e3-48a0-9c48-3fcf5d8fb5d2","timestam