{"parentUuid":"a537991a-41cd-4408-ab5c-0342466ed722","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ2DdxCEnMCgJLg3fBLP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407522,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1976,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407522,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1976,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407522},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"unavailable"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdJ2DafFUcBsH1MYMaZXV","type":"assistant","uuid":"f87ccce0-f9d4-4e1b-be28-1f23bbe4d7e5","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:13:00.187Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"f87ccce0-f9d4-4e1b-be28-1f23bbe4d7e5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ2DdxCEnMCgJLg3fBLP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good catch — my current criteria (\"hard to reverse, not obvious from code\") is broader than \"architectural.\" That's the wrong bar; a lot of hard-to-reverse things are just implementation details, not architecture. Let me tighten it."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407522,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1976,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407522,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1976,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407522},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"unavailable"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdJ2DafFUcBsH1MYMaZXV","type":"assistant","uuid":"6c00f44d-dd74-4675-8d78-17a05deb9bff","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:13:01.228Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"6c00f44d-dd74-4675-8d78-17a05deb9bff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ2DdxCEnMCgJLg3fBLP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vs9gPc2HTXHtsFg6xTmr1r","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407522,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1976,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407522,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1976,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407522},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"unavailable"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdJ2DafFUcBsH1MYMaZXV","type":"assistant","uuid":"2472fd1b-ff6f-4a0a-a8c8-6dced710f022","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:13:01.866Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"2472fd1b-ff6f-4a0a-a8c8-6dced710f022","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bd085ae8-2f39-49b8-ab63-4ab8f3a29f4d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vs9gPc2HTXHtsFg6xTmr1r","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Architecture Decision Records\n2\t\n3\tShort, dated records of decisions that are expensive to reverse and not obvious\n4\tfrom reading the code. Not a changelog, not a design doc, not a place to\n5\texplain what the code does — comments and `ARCHITECTURE.md` already do that.\n6\t\n7\t## When to write one\n8\t\n9\tAsk: if this gets reverted in a year, what breaks, and would anyone know why?\n10\tIf the answer is \"nothing\" or \"it's obvious,\" skip it.\n11\t\n12\tGood candidates:\n13\t\n14\t- Choosing OXC over the TypeScript compiler\n15\t- A serialization format with a hidden constraint (msgpack's positional encoding)\n16\t- Dropping a dependency, or an approach that was tried and abandoned\n17\t\n18\tNot ADR material:\n19\t\n20\t- A bug fix — commit message, and if it's the kind of thing that could recur,\n21\t  a line in `rdt-coverage.md`\n22\t- A behavior-preserving refactor — commit message is enough\n23\t- Anything already obvious from the code or from `CLAUDE.md`'s non-negotiables\n24\t\n25\t## Format\n26\t\n27\tOne file per decision: `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.md`, numbered sequentially,\n28\tnever reused. Copy `0000-template.md` to start.\n29\t\n30\t- **Never edit history.** If a decision changes, write a new ADR and mark the\n31\t  old one's status `Superseded by 000X`. Don't rewrite the old file to look\n32\t  like you knew all along.\n33\t- **Status** is one of: `Accepted`, `Superseded by NNNN`, `Deprecated`.\n34\t- Keep it short. If the technical depth doesn't fit on a screen, split it into\n35\t  its own doc and link it — see `0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md`\n36\t  pointing at `type-checker-integration.md` instead of inlining it.\n37\t\n38\t## Writing it\n39\t\n40\tWrite like you're explaining it to the next engineer over their shoulder, not\n41\tpresenting it to a committee.\n42\t\n43\t**Cut the filler.** If a sentence still means the same thing without a word,\n44\tdelete the word.\n45\t\n46\t| Instead of | Write |\n47\t|---|---|\n48\t| \"It's worth noting that this decision was made in order to leverage OXC's robust parsing capabilities\" | \"OXC parses in parallel with no type-checking pass\" |\n49\t| \"This represents a significant improvement in performance\" | \"32ms instead of several seconds\" |\n50\t| \"We decided to essentially utilize a positional encoding approach\" | \"We use positional encoding\" |\n51\t| \"In conclusion, this architecture provides a solid foundation going forward\" | (delete — you already said the thing) |\n52\t\n53\t**Banned by default:** *leverage, utilize, robust, seamless, cutting-edge,\n54\tessentially, basically, in order to, it's worth noting, it is important to\n55\tnote, at the end of the day.* If one is genuinely the precise technical word\n56\tfor something, fine — but check first.\n57\t\n58\t**Concrete beats vague.** Name the file, the number, the benchmark. \"Slow\" is\n59\tnot a fact; \"several seconds on a mid-size design system\" is.\n60\t\n61\t**Active voice, plain structure.** \"We chose X because Y\" beats \"X was chosen\n62\tdue to Y considerations.\" Sentence-case headers, not Title Case.\n63\t\n64\t**Show the trade-off, not just the win.** A decision with no downside isn't a\n65\tdecision, it's a fact. Say what it costs.\n66\t\n67\t## What good looks like\n68\t\n69\tRead `0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md` — a real bug behind it, a real\n70\tnumber (`recursion_limit = 2048`), a real consequence, four sections, no\n71\tthroat-clearing.\n72\t"}]},"uuid":"7d463165-85f3-4fc3-8921-08046d147efc","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:13:01.955Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/README.md","content":"# Architecture Decision Records\n\nShort, dated records of decisions that are expensive to reverse and not obvious\nfrom reading the code. Not a changelog, not a design doc, not a place to\nexplain what the code does — comments and `ARCHITECTURE.md` already do that.\n\n## When to write one\n\nAsk: if this gets reverted in a year, what breaks, and would anyone know why?\nIf the answer is \"nothing\" or \"it's obvious,\" skip it.\n\nGood candidates:\n\n- Choosing OXC over the TypeScript compiler\n- A serialization format with a hidden constraint (msgpack's positional encoding)\n- Dropping a dependency, or an approach that was tried and abandoned\n\nNot ADR material:\n\n- A bug fix — commit message, and if it's the kind of thing that could recur,\n  a line in `rdt-coverage.md`\n- A behavior-preserving refactor — commit message is enough\n- Anything already obvious from the code or from `CLAUDE.md`'s non-negotiables\n\n## Format\n\nOne file per decision: `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.md`, numbered sequentially,\nnever reused. Copy `0000-template.md` to start.\n\n- **Never edit history.** If a decision changes, write a new ADR and mark the\n  old one's status `Superseded by 000X`. Don't rewrite the old file to look\n  like you knew all along.\n- **Status** is one of: `Accepted`, `Superseded by NNNN`, `Deprecated`.\n- Keep it short. If the technical depth doesn't fit on a screen, split it into\n  its own doc and link it — see `0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md`\n  pointing at `type-checker-integration.md` instead of inlining it.\n\n## Writing it\n\nWrite like you're explaining it to the next engineer over their shoulder, not\npresenting it to a committee.\n\n**Cut the filler.** If a sentence still means the same thing without a word,\ndelete the word.\n\n| Instead of | Write |\n|---|---|\n| \"It's worth noting that this decision was made in order to leverage OXC's robust parsing capabilities\" | \"OXC parses in parallel with no type-checking pass\" |\n| \"This represents a significant improvement in performance\" | \"32ms instead of several seconds\" |\n| \"We decided to essentially utilize a positional encoding approach\" | \"We use positional encoding\" |\n| \"In conclusion, this architecture provides a solid foundation going forward\" | (delete — you already said the thing) |\n\n**Banned by default:** *leverage, utilize, robust, seamless, cutting-edge,\nessentially, basically, in order to, it's worth noting, it is important to\nnote, at the end of the day.* If one is genuinely the precise technical word\nfor something, fine — but check first.\n\n**Concrete beats vague.** Name the file, the number, the benchmark. \"Slow\" is\nnot a fact; \"several seconds on a mid-size design system\" is.\n\n**Active voice, plain structure.** \"We chose X because Y\" beats \"X was chosen\ndue to Y considerations.\" Sentence-case headers, not Title Case.\n\n**Show the trade-off, not just the win.** A decision with no downside isn't a\ndecision, it's a fact. Say what it costs.\n\n## What good looks like\n\nRead `0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md` — a real bug behind it, a real\nnumber (`recursion_limit = 2048`), a real consequence, four sections, no\nthroat-clearing.\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2472fd1b-ff6f-4a0a-a8c8-6dced710f022","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
