ly the case this version bump was added to cover.\n- A forgotten bump doesn't fail loudly. It decodes as plausible-looking but wrong data — the worst kind of bug. There's no compiler check for this; it's a discipline problem, not a type-safety one.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":30,"newStart":5,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," ## Context"," ","-The DTS parse cache persists `SourceData` across runs so unchanged `.d.ts`","-files don't get re-parsed. `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — the default,","-and what this project uses — encode structs *positionally*: as an array of","-field values in declaration order, not a map of field names. A `_named`","-variant encodes as a map instead, at a size and speed cost we haven't needed","-to pay.","+The DTS parse cache persists `SourceData` across runs so unchanged `.d.ts` files don't get re-parsed. `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — the default, and what this project uses — encode structs *positionally*: as an array of field values in declaration order, not a map of field names. A `_named` variant encodes as a map instead, at a size and speed cost we haven't needed to pay."," "," ## Decision"," ","-Use plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice`, and treat `SourceData`'s field","-order as part of the wire format. A `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` constant","-(`crates/core/src/cache.rs`) gets bumped whenever a field is added anywhere","-but the end of the struct, removed, or reordered — any change that would","-shift decode position for cache entries written before the change. A version","-mismatch discards the whole cache rather than risk decoding an old entry into","-the wrong field.","+Use plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice`, and treat `SourceData`'s field order as part of the wire format. A `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` constant (`crates/core/src/cache.rs`) gets bumped whenever a field is added anywhere but the end of the struct, removed, or reordered — any change that would shift decode position for cache entries written before the change. A version mismatch discards the whole cache rather than risk decoding an old entry into the wrong field."," "," ## Consequences"," "," - Smaller, faster cache files than named encoding — the whole point.","-- Adding a field to `SourceData` (or anything it contains) requires","-  remembering to bump `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` if it isn't appended at the very","-  end. Easy to forget — `const_arrays` (added mid-struct) is exactly the case","-  this version bump was added to cover.","-- A forgotten bump doesn't fail loudly. It decodes as plausible-looking but","-  wrong data — the worst kind of bug. There's no compiler check for this;","-  it's a discipline problem, not a type-safety one.","+- Adding a field to `SourceData` (or anything it contains) requires remembering to bump `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` if it isn't appended at the very end. Easy to forget — `const_arrays` (added mid-struct) is exactly the case this version bump was added to cover.","+- A forgotten bump doesn't fail loudly. It decodes as plausible-looking but wrong data — the worst kind of bug. There's no compiler check for this; it's a discipline problem, not a type-safety one."]}],"originalFile":"# 0003. Cache the DTS parse cache with positional (not named) MessagePack\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\nThe DTS parse cache persists `SourceData` across runs so unchanged `.d.ts`\nfiles don't get re-parsed. `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — the default,\nand what this project uses — encode structs *positionally*: as an array of\nfield values in declaration order, not a map of field names. A `_named`\nvariant encodes as a map instead, at a size and speed cost we haven't needed\nto pay.\n\n## Decision\n\nUse plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice`, and treat `SourceData`'s field\norder as part of the wire format. A `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` constant\n(`crates/core/src/cache.rs`) gets bumped whenever a field is added anywhere\nbut the end of the struct, removed, or reordered — any change that would\nshift decode position for cache entries written before the change. A version\nmismatch discards the whole cache rather than risk decoding an old entry into\nthe wrong field.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Smaller, faster cache files than named encoding — the whole point.\n- Adding a field to `SourceData` (or anything it contains) requires\n  remembering to bump `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` if it isn't appended at the very\n  end. Easy to forget — `const_arrays` (added mid-struct) is exactly the case\n  this version bump was added to cover.\n- A forgotten bump doesn't fail loudly. It decodes as plausible-looking but\n  wrong data — the worst kind of bug. There's no compiler check for this;\n  it's a discipline problem, not a type-safety one.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d39d8219-3330-4998-bad7-04ef3e52c380","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"2b89a8f9-bab4-47ed-80c2-59db6b377e6f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Write","toolUseID":"toolu_01XYTshZKaiZ8om5G5nc6uKc","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":56},"type":"attachment","uuid":"da8a4b66-f7fa-4320-a9ef-e3bc36e756e6","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:23:45.823Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"da8a4b66-f7fa-4320-a9ef-e3bc36e756e6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Explanatory"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cf074ea1-f018-4bd2-99af-879af95d0c9c","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:23:45.909Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"cf074ea1-f018-4bd2-99af-879af95d0c9c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ35EyE3g7sTepzLe6gP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MkV6FegbgeHFaWt9fm62w1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md","content":"# 0004. Defer full type-checker integration\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\nOXC's structural, no-type-checking approach (`0001`) can't resolve conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, or a few `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes — these need real type inference. `typescript-go` (TypeScript 7.0's Rust/Go port, \"Corsa\") is the plausible future path, but its public API for this isn't stable yet.\n\n## Decision\n\nDon't integrate a type checker now. Every gap that would need one degrades to a `Diagnostic` plus an `Opaque` prop type instead of a wrong answer, and gets tracked in `docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s \"Known gaps summary\" table. Revisit when Corsa's API stabilizes.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A real, bounded set of real-world types (see `docs/type-checker-integration.md` for the current list) shows up as `Opaque` in extraction output until this changes.\n- No dependency on an unstable, fast-moving API in the meantime.\n- The gap list needs to stay current in `docs/type-checker-integration.md` and `docs/rdt-coverage.md` as new patterns get found — otherwise this ADR quietly goes stale.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":808,"cache_read_input_tokens":424464,"output_tokens":548,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":808,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":548,"cache_read_input_tokens":424464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":808},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ359JQgW8f22mjWAZZ9","type":"assistant","uuid":"61e5ed8a-4787-4935-bba4-3a099de81885","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:23:52.663Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"61e5ed8a-4787-4935-bba4-3a099de81885","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2767ee7d-d768-4fc5-b864-ecc99fbdd4cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MkV6FegbgeHFaWt9fm62w1","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"b9edc529-c87e-401b-8e87-652a6167c0d7","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:23:52.748Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md","content":"# 0004. Defer full type-checker integration\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\nOXC's structural, no-type-checking approach (`0001`) can't resolve conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, or a few `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes — these need real type inference. `typescript-go` (TypeScript 7.0's Rust/Go port, \"Corsa\") is the plausible future path, but its public API for this isn't stable yet.\n\n## Decision\n\nDon't integrate a type checker now. Every gap that would need one degrades to a `Diagnostic` plus an `Opaque` prop type instead of a wrong answer, and gets tracked in `docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s \"Known gaps summary\" table. Revisit when Corsa's API stabilizes.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A real, bounded set of real-world types (see `docs/type-checker-integration.md` for the current list) shows up as `Opaque` in extraction output until this changes.\n- No dependency on an unstable, fast-moving API in the meantime.\n- The gap list needs to stay current in `docs/type-checker-integration.md` and `docs/rdt-coverage.md` as new patterns get found — otherwise this ADR quietly goes stale.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":25,"newStart":5,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," ## Context"," ","-OXC's structural, no-type-checking approach (`0001`) can't resolve","-conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, or a few","-`@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes — these need real type inference.","-`typescript-go` (TypeScript 7.0's Rust/Go port, \"Corsa\") is the plausible","-future path, but its public API for this isn't stable yet.","+OXC's structural, no-type-checking approach (`0001`) can't resolve conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, or a few `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes — these need real type inference. `typescript-go` (TypeScript 7.0's Rust/Go port, \"Corsa\") is the plausible future path, but its public API for this isn't stable yet."," "," ## Decision"," ","-Don't integrate a type checker now. Every gap that would need one degrades to","-a `Diagnostic` plus an `Opaque` prop type instead of a wrong answer, and gets","-tracked in `docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s \"Known gaps summary\" table. Revisit when","-Corsa's API stabilizes.","+Don't integrate a type checker now. Every gap that would need one degrades to a `Diagnostic` plus an `Opaque` prop type instead of a wrong answer, and gets tracked in `docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s \"Known gaps summary\" table. Revisit when Corsa's API stabilizes."," "," ## Consequences"," ","-- A real, bounded set of real-world types (see `docs/type-checker-integration.md`","-  for the current list) shows up as `Opaque` in extraction output until this","-  changes.","+- A real, bounded set of real-world types (see `docs/type-checker-integration.md` for the current list) shows up as `Opaque` in extraction output until this changes."," - No dependency on an unstable, fast-moving API in the meantime.","-- The gap list needs to stay current in `docs/type-checker-integration.md`","-  and `docs/rdt-coverage.md` as new patterns get found — otherwise this ADR","-  quietly goes stale.","+- The gap list needs to stay current in `docs/type-checker-integration.md` and `docs/rdt-coverage.md` as new patterns get found — otherwise this ADR quietly goes stale."]}],"originalFile":"# 0004. Defer full type-checker integration\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n**Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\nOXC's structural, no-type-checking approach (`0001`) can't resolve\nconditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, or a few\n`@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes — these need real type inference.\n`typescript-go` (TypeScript 7.0's Rust/Go port, \"Corsa\") is the plausible\nfuture path, but its public API for this isn't stable yet.\n\n## Decision\n\nDon't integrate a type checker now. Every gap that would need one degrades to\na `Diagnostic` plus an `Opaque` prop type instead of a wrong answer, and gets\ntracked in `docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s \"Known gaps summary\" table. Revisit when\nCorsa's API stabilizes.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A real, bounded set of real-world types (see `docs/type-checker-integration.md`\n  for the current list) shows up as `Opaque` in extraction output until this\n  changes.\n- No dependency on an unstable, fast-moving API in the meantime.\n- The gap list needs to stay current in `docs/type-checker-integration.md`\n  and `docs/rdt-coverage.md` as new patterns get found — otherwise this ADR\n  quietly goes stale.\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61e5ed8a-4787-4935-bba4-3a099de81885","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
