{"parentUuid":"70b1d599-bad0-48de-bbec-749a310fd04f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ381qHJp5z2SpGouqt1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":428686,"output_tokens":1558,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1597,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1558,"cache_read_input_tokens":428686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1597},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ37yNStdVrGNfMgxvSU","type":"assistant","uuid":"0d8bc458-a77b-419f-ae43-e907e51342d4","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:24:29.718Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"0d8bc458-a77b-419f-ae43-e907e51342d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ381qHJp5z2SpGouqt1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A5AViWxQhTisNyKnc4Kanx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-07-22\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are tested. Config file loading, cross-package `.d.ts` resolution, and watch mode are fully implemented — not stubs, despite what older docs in this repo used to say. If you find another doc contradicting this file, this file wins.\n\n## Numbers\n\n- 191 Rust tests (21 cli + 158 core unit + 8 snapshot + 4 napi binding), 18 vitest — all green\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n\n## What's not built yet\n\n- **Preset system** (`@oxc-react-docgen/presets`) — named `PipelineOptions` bundles. Config-side only, no Rust changes needed.\n- **LSP server** — `lsp-types` is a dependency; nothing built on it.\n- **Barrel/re-export scoped-key allocation caching** — `resolver/chain.rs` / `named.rs` / `template.rs` build a `\"{file}:{name}\"` scoped-key string on every lookup. A `Borrow`-based type-map key would let lookups happen without allocating. Real but unbenchmarked — do as a focused perf pass if profiling shows it matters.\n- **DTS cache has no dirty-flag or size cap** (`cache.rs`) — rewrites the whole cache file on every run regardless of whether anything changed, and has no upper bound on how large the on-disk cache can grow. Low severity (requires local write access, and an attacker with that already has better options) — worth fixing for large monorepos before it becomes a real cost.\n\n## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs, not on the roadmap unless typescript-go's Corsa API stabilizes (see `type-checker-integration.md`).\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, deferring type-checker integration. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":428686,"output_tokens":1558,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1597,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1558,"cache_read_input_tokens":428686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1597},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ37yNStdVrGNfMgxvSU","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2067f91-5a1c-4ced-9aed-1f2e394a0dba","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:24:38.270Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"c2067f91-5a1c-4ced-9aed-1f2e394a0dba","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2767ee7d-d768-4fc5-b864-ecc99fbdd4cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A5AViWxQhTisNyKnc4Kanx","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/STATUS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"701e9068-133e-43aa-a881-33a2be2de0fd","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:24:38.356Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-07-22\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are tested. Config file loading, cross-package `.d.ts` resolution, and watch mode are fully implemented — not stubs, despite what older docs in this repo used to say. If you find another doc contradicting this file, this file wins.\n\n## Numbers\n\n- 191 Rust tests (21 cli + 158 core unit + 8 snapshot + 4 napi binding), 18 vitest — all green\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n\n## What's not built yet\n\n- **Preset system** (`@oxc-react-docgen/presets`) — named `PipelineOptions` bundles. Config-side only, no Rust changes needed.\n- **LSP server** — `lsp-types` is a dependency; nothing built on it.\n- **Barrel/re-export scoped-key allocation caching** — `resolver/chain.rs` / `named.rs` / `template.rs` build a `\"{file}:{name}\"` scoped-key string on every lookup. A `Borrow`-based type-map key would let lookups happen without allocating. Real but unbenchmarked — do as a focused perf pass if profiling shows it matters.\n- **DTS cache has no dirty-flag or size cap** (`cache.rs`) — rewrites the whole cache file on every run regardless of whether anything changed, and has no upper bound on how large the on-disk cache can grow. Low severity (requires local write access, and an attacker with that already has better options) — worth fixing for large monorepos before it becomes a real cost.\n\n## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs, not on the roadmap unless typescript-go's Corsa API stabilizes (see `type-checker-integration.md`).\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, deferring type-checker integration. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":58,"newStart":2,"newLines":30,"lines":[" "," **Updated:** 2026-07-22"," ","-Core extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are","-tested. Config file loading, cross-package `.d.ts` resolution, and watch mode","-are fully implemented — not stubs, despite what older docs in this repo used","-to say. If you find another doc contradicting this file, this file wins.","+Core extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are tested. Config file loading, cross-package `.d.ts` resolution, and watch mode are fully implemented — not stubs, despite what older docs in this repo used to say. If you find another doc contradicting this file, this file wins."," "," ## Numbers"," ","-- 191 Rust tests (21 cli + 158 core unit + 8 snapshot + 4 napi binding), 18","-  vitest — all green","+- 191 Rust tests (21 cli + 158 core unit + 8 snapshot + 4 napi binding), 18 vitest — all green"," - `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean","-- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript`","-  (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui,","-  base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda,","-  react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion,","-  tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)","+- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)"," "," ## What's not built yet"," ","-- **Preset system** (`@oxc-react-docgen/presets`) — named `PipelineOptions`","-  bundles. Config-side only, no Rust changes needed.","+- **Preset system** (`@oxc-react-docgen/presets`) — named `PipelineOptions` bundles. Config-side only, no Rust changes needed."," - **LSP server** — `lsp-types` is a dependency; nothing built on it.","-- **Barrel/re-export scoped-key allocation caching** — `resolver/chain.rs` /","-  `named.rs` / `template.rs` build a `\"{file}:{name}\"` scoped-key string on","-  every lookup. A `Borrow`-based type-map key would let lookups happen","-  without allocating. Real but unbenchmarked — do as a focused perf pass if","-  profiling shows it matters.","-- **DTS cache has no dirty-flag or size cap** (`cache.rs`) — rewrites the","-  whole cache file on every run regardless of whether anything changed, and","-  has no upper bound on how large the on-disk cache can grow. Low severity","-  (requires local write access, and an attacker with that already has better","-  options) — worth fixing for large monorepos before it becomes a real cost.","+- **Barrel/re-export scoped-key allocation caching** — `resolver/chain.rs` / `named.rs` / `template.rs` build a `\"{file}:{name}\"` scoped-key string on every lookup. A `Borrow`-based type-map key would let lookups happen without allocating. Real but unbenchmarked — do as a focused perf pass if profiling shows it matters.","+- **DTS cache has no dirty-flag or size cap** (`cache.rs`) — rewrites the whole cache file on every run regardless of whether anything changed, and has no upper bound on how large the on-disk cache can grow. Low severity (requires local write access, and an attacker with that already has better options) — worth fixing for large monorepos before it becomes a real cost."," "," ## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker"," ","-See the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full,","-maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an","-unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all","-need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs, not on the","-roadmap unless typescript-go's Corsa API stabilizes (see","-`type-checker-integration.md`).","+See the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs, not on the roadmap unless typescript-go's Corsa API stabilizes (see `type-checker-integration.md`)."," "," ## Where to look next"," ","-- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found","-  during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated;","-  it's the project's memory.","-- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the","-  TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack","-  encoding, deferring type-checker integration. Write a new one when you make","-  a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).","+- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.","+- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, deferring type-checker integration. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`)."," - **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`"," - **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`"," - **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`","-- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** →","-  `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference","+- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference"]}],"originalFile":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-07-22\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are\ntested. Config file loading, cross-package `.d.ts` resolution, and watch mode\nare fully implemented — not stubs, despite what older docs in this repo used\nto say. If you find another doc contradicting this file, this file wins.\n\n## Numbers\n\n- 191 Rust tests (21 cli + 158 core unit + 8 snapshot + 4 napi binding), 18\n  vitest — all green\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript`\n  (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui,\n  base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda,\n  react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion,\n  tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n\n## What's not built yet\n\n- **Preset system** (`@oxc-react-docgen/presets`) — named `PipelineOptions`\n  bundles. Config-side only, no Rust changes needed.\n- **LSP server** — `lsp-types` is a dependency; nothing built on it.\n- **Barrel/re-export scoped-key allocation caching** — `resolver/chain.rs` /\n  `named.rs` / `template.rs` build a `\"{file}:{name}\"` scoped-key string on\n  every lookup. A `Borrow`-based type-map key would let lookups happen\n  without allocating. Real but unbenchmarked — do as a focused perf pass if\n  profiling shows it matters.\n- **DTS cache has no dirty-flag or size cap** (`cache.rs`) — rewrites the\n  whole cache file on every run regardless of whether anything changed, and\n  has no upper bound on how large the on-disk cache can grow. Low severity\n  (requires local write access, and an attacker with that already has better\n  options) — worth fixing for large monorepos before it becomes a real cost.\n\n## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full,\nmaintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an\nunbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all\nneed real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs, not on the\nroadmap unless typescript-go's Corsa API stabilizes (see\n`type-checker-integration.md`).\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found\n  during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated;\n  it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the\n  TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack\n  encoding, deferring type-checker integration. Write a new one when you make\n  a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** →\n  `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c2067f91-5a1c-4ced-9aed-1f2e394a0dba","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
