{"parentUuid":"ad3db2d5-5899-4273-bc04-f30296c459b1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ3ChEEBcRw8d1XHNTLT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0195fr4bfyyo4hS1SJfYEHgN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"echo \"=== crates/core/CLAUDE.md ===\"; cat crates/core/CLAUDE.md\necho \"=== crates/cli/CLAUDE.md ===\"; cat crates/cli/CLAUDE.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2900,"cache_read_input_tokens":435797,"output_tokens":272,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2900,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":272,"cache_read_input_tokens":435797,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2900,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2900},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ3CeK7FtNLGTu7aNnNh","type":"assistant","uuid":"616ad5fa-8566-43b9-a5af-eefe5797e279","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:31.618Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"616ad5fa-8566-43b9-a5af-eefe5797e279","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_0195fr4bfyyo4hS1SJfYEHgN","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== crates/core/CLAUDE.md ===\\\"; rtk read crates/core/CLAUDE.md\\necho \\\"=== crates/cli/CLAUDE.md ===\\\"; rtk read crates/cli/CLAUDE.md\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":17},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eeb4755a-bb3e-4884-982f-b00afa7d89b7","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:31.637Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"616ad5fa-8566-43b9-a5af-eefe5797e279","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2767ee7d-d768-4fc5-b864-ecc99fbdd4cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0195fr4bfyyo4hS1SJfYEHgN","type":"tool_result","content":"=== crates/core/CLAUDE.md ===\n\n# crates/core\n\nPure extraction logic — no terminal, no NAPI, no async. Everything here must be `Send + Sync` for rayon.\n\n## Module layout\n\n```\ntypes/          — shared data types (the contract between phases)\nextractor/      — OXC AST visitor → SourceData\nresolver/       — SourceData + GlobalSourceData → ComponentEntry\npipeline/       — orchestration: discover → parse → merge → resolve\ncache.rs        — DTS parse cache (mtime+size invalidation, msgpack)\nimport_map.rs   — import resolution map\nknown.rs        — library-specific type shortcuts (SxProps, VariantProps…)\nreact_types.rs  — React builtin recognition + notable HTML attrs\n```\n\n## Types discipline\n\nWhen adding a public type, run through the checklist in the `rust-types` skill. Canonical reference: `src/types/diagnostic.rs`.\n\n## Resolver\n\n`resolve_component()` is called in parallel via rayon. All inputs must be owned or `Arc`-wrapped — no borrowed data crosses thread boundaries. `ResolveState` accumulates diagnostics and visited-type tracking for a single resolution call; it is not shared.\n\n## Snapshot tests\n\nSeven fixtures in `crates/core/tests/snapshots/`. If a change affects output, regenerate with `/snapshot` before committing.\n=== crates/cli/CLAUDE.md ===\n\n# crates/cli\n\nThin command layer — no extraction logic. Each command parses args and delegates to `oxc-react-docgen-core::pipeline`.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nmain.rs              — Cli struct, Command enum, *Args structs, main(), init_tracing()\ncommands/            — one file per subcommand (extract, watch, inspect, check, completions)\nconfig.rs            — docgen.config.ts loading, maps to PipelineOptions\noutput.rs            — comfy-table formatting helpers\n```\n\n## Rules\n\nAll user-facing output goes through `output.rs` or the tracing subscriber — never `println!` in command handlers. Error display uses `miette`. Progress uses `indicatif`.\n\nConfig loading (`config.rs`) runs the user's `docgen.config.ts` via node+tsx. The config file path is passed via env var, not embedded in a shell string — command injection risk otherwise.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f940a59f-f1a2-40a6-80c6-6001376f2e34","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:33.363Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== crates/core/CLAUDE.md ===\n\n# crates/core\n\nPure extraction logic — no terminal, no NAPI, no async. Everything here must be `Send + Sync` for rayon.\n\n## Module layout\n\n```\ntypes/          — shared data types (the contract between phases)\nextractor/      — OXC AST visitor → SourceData\nresolver/       — SourceData + GlobalSourceData → ComponentEntry\npipeline/       — orchestration: discover → parse → merge → resolve\ncache.rs        — DTS parse cache (mtime+size invalidation, msgpack)\nimport_map.rs   — import resolution map\nknown.rs        — library-specific type shortcuts (SxProps, VariantProps…)\nreact_types.rs  — React builtin recognition + notable HTML attrs\n```\n\n## Types discipline\n\nWhen adding a public type, run through the checklist in the `rust-types` skill. Canonical reference: `src/types/diagnostic.rs`.\n\n## Resolver\n\n`resolve_component()` is called in parallel via rayon. All inputs must be owned or `Arc`-wrapped — no borrowed data crosses thread boundaries. `ResolveState` accumulates diagnostics and visited-type tracking for a single resolution call; it is not shared.\n\n## Snapshot tests\n\nSeven fixtures in `crates/core/tests/snapshots/`. If a change affects output, regenerate with `/snapshot` before committing.\n=== crates/cli/CLAUDE.md ===\n\n# crates/cli\n\nThin command layer — no extraction logic. Each command parses args and delegates to `oxc-react-docgen-core::pipeline`.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nmain.rs              — Cli struct, Command enum, *Args structs, main(), init_tracing()\ncommands/            — one file per subcommand (extract, watch, inspect, check, completions)\nconfig.rs            — docgen.config.ts loading, maps to PipelineOptions\noutput.rs            — comfy-table formatting helpers\n```\n\n## Rules\n\nAll user-facing output goes through `output.rs` or the tracing subscriber — never `println!` in command handlers. Error display uses `miette`. Progress uses `indicatif`.\n\nConfig loading (`config.rs`) runs the user's `docgen.config.ts` via node+tsx. The config file path is passed via env var, not embedded in a shell string — command injection risk otherwise.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"616ad5fa-8566-43b9-a5af-eefe5797e279","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
