{"parentUuid":"732507d2-0110-4b22-896b-fa337f86c81a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ3DHaxVMe8Rh9rVF1nJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0177QjVsPAvdAJFuTsz4Zxf6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"echo \"=== CONTRIBUTING.md sample ===\"; sed -n '1,25p' CONTRIBUTING.md\necho \"=== type-checker-integration.md sample (later section) ===\"; sed -n '40,75p' docs/type-checker-integration.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":438697,"output_tokens":185,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1117,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":185,"cache_read_input_tokens":438697,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1117},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ3DEAL2wNsRFas4MRTt","type":"assistant","uuid":"9a93e691-9430-4a3a-b2de-c34b1d58f462","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:38.958Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"9a93e691-9430-4a3a-b2de-c34b1d58f462","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2767ee7d-d768-4fc5-b864-ecc99fbdd4cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0177QjVsPAvdAJFuTsz4Zxf6","type":"tool_result","content":"=== CONTRIBUTING.md sample ===\n# Contributing\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n| Tool | Min version | Notes |\n|------|------------|-------|\n| Rust | 1.94 | `rustup update stable` |\n| proto | latest | manages Node/pnpm versions from `.prototools` |\n| pnpm | 9 | via proto, or `npm i -g pnpm` |\n\nAfter installing proto, run `moon setup` once to pull the pinned Node version and any other tool versions declared in `.prototools`.\n\n## Build & test\n\n```bash\n# Rust\ncargo build                                            # dev build\ncargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core                   # unit + snapshot tests\ncargo clippy -p oxc-react-docgen-core -- -D warnings\ncargo fmt --all\n\n# TypeScript\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin test      # 14 vitest tests\n\n# Accuracy comparison (informational — exits 0 regardless of gaps)\n=== type-checker-integration.md sample (later section) ===\n\nTypeScript 7.0 RC shipped 2026-06-18. This is the Go rewrite of the compiler (\"tsgo\"),\nnot a JavaScript refactor. The key changes:\n\n- **TypeScript 6.0** = last JavaScript-based tsc (maintenance only)\n- **TypeScript 7.0** = Go rewrite; 10× build speed, same semantics\n- **Strada API** (ts.createProgram, checker.getTypeAtLocation, LanguageService) = **completely dropped** in TS 7.0 — no shim, no compatibility layer\n- **react-docgen-typescript** depends on Strada; it is **broken under TS 7.0**\n\n### Corsa API\n\nThe tsgo team is building \"Corsa\" as the replacement public API. Status:\n\n- Corsa API: **not yet stable** — targeting TypeScript 7.1 (estimated late 2026 / early 2027)\n- Current tsgo exports minimal surface: `check()`, `build()`, basic diagnostics\n- No `getTypeAtLocation` equivalent yet\n- Plugin system and language service extensions TBD\n\n### tsgolint precedent (OXC team)\n\nThe OXC team already tackled cross-language integration with `tsgolint`:\n- Spawns `tsgo` as a subprocess\n- Communicates via JSON IPC using tsgo's internal (unstable) shims\n- This pattern works but depends on internal APIs that will break when Corsa lands\n\nWe should NOT follow the tsgolint approach — it creates maintenance debt on an unstable\ninternal API. Wait for Corsa.\n\n### Why oxc-react-docgen is unaffected by TS 7.0\n\nWe parse TypeScript with OXC (Rust), not tsc. We have no dependency on the Strada API.\nConsumers running TS 7.0 can use oxc-react-docgen without any changes. This is a\ncompetitive advantage during the TS 6→7 migration window.\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"06f62939-b30e-4977-8cd5-ec3ae8460155","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:39.088Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== CONTRIBUTING.md sample ===\n# Contributing\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n| Tool | Min version | Notes |\n|------|------------|-------|\n| Rust | 1.94 | `rustup update stable` |\n| proto | latest | manages Node/pnpm versions from `.prototools` |\n| pnpm | 9 | via proto, or `npm i -g pnpm` |\n\nAfter installing proto, run `moon setup` once to pull the pinned Node version and any other tool versions declared in `.prototools`.\n\n## Build & test\n\n```bash\n# Rust\ncargo build                                            # dev build\ncargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core                   # unit + snapshot tests\ncargo clippy -p oxc-react-docgen-core -- -D warnings\ncargo fmt --all\n\n# TypeScript\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin test      # 14 vitest tests\n\n# Accuracy comparison (informational — exits 0 regardless of gaps)\n=== type-checker-integration.md sample (later section) ===\n\nTypeScript 7.0 RC shipped 2026-06-18. This is the Go rewrite of the compiler (\"tsgo\"),\nnot a JavaScript refactor. The key changes:\n\n- **TypeScript 6.0** = last JavaScript-based tsc (maintenance only)\n- **TypeScript 7.0** = Go rewrite; 10× build speed, same semantics\n- **Strada API** (ts.createProgram, checker.getTypeAtLocation, LanguageService) = **completely dropped** in TS 7.0 — no shim, no compatibility layer\n- **react-docgen-typescript** depends on Strada; it is **broken under TS 7.0**\n\n### Corsa API\n\nThe tsgo team is building \"Corsa\" as the replacement public API. Status:\n\n- Corsa API: **not yet stable** — targeting TypeScript 7.1 (estimated late 2026 / early 2027)\n- Current tsgo exports minimal surface: `check()`, `build()`, basic diagnostics\n- No `getTypeAtLocation` equivalent yet\n- Plugin system and language service extensions TBD\n\n### tsgolint precedent (OXC team)\n\nThe OXC team already tackled cross-language integration with `tsgolint`:\n- Spawns `tsgo` as a subprocess\n- Communicates via JSON IPC using tsgo's internal (unstable) shims\n- This pattern works but depends on internal APIs that will break when Corsa lands\n\nWe should NOT follow the tsgolint approach — it creates maintenance debt on an unstable\ninternal API. Wait for Corsa.\n\n### Why oxc-react-docgen is unaffected by TS 7.0\n\nWe parse TypeScript with OXC (Rust), not tsc. We have no dependency on the Strada API.\nConsumers running TS 7.0 can use oxc-react-docgen without any changes. This is a\ncompetitive advantage during the TS 6→7 migration window.\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9a93e691-9430-4a3a-b2de-c34b1d58f462","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
