{"parentUuid":"af093d1e-bd18-4164-95ae-94896d8777a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ3DgSsoFsMsr82E86Q7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1234,"cache_read_input_tokens":439814,"output_tokens":490,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1234,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":439814,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1234},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ3DW7XVFNezrjoUEx1U","type":"assistant","uuid":"da875075-7cbf-42ce-ac05-0ddc2601bda4","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:47.306Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"da875075-7cbf-42ce-ac05-0ddc2601bda4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ3DgSsoFsMsr82E86Q7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FsSaWXHUqTTb3wxb1u6a1C","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/type-checker-integration.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1234,"cache_read_input_tokens":439814,"output_tokens":490,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1234,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":439814,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1234},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ3DW7XVFNezrjoUEx1U","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef381412-55b0-4d69-91e4-847ae6055697","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:47.834Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"ef381412-55b0-4d69-91e4-847ae6055697","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2767ee7d-d768-4fc5-b864-ecc99fbdd4cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FsSaWXHUqTTb3wxb1u6a1C","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Type Checker Integration: Future Work\n2\t\n3\tThis document describes which resolver gaps genuinely require a TypeScript type checker,\n4\tthe state of the tsgo (TypeScript 7.0) ecosystem, and the integration plan for when the\n5\tCorsa API is stable.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## What we can fix structurally (no type checker needed)\n10\t\n11\tThe six fundamental gap patterns discovered during the RDT compatibility audit break into\n12\ttwo groups:\n13\t\n14\t**Fixable now — pure AST/structural:**\n15\t\n16\t| Gap | Root cause | Fix location |\n17\t|-----|-----------|-------------|\n18\t| TSMethodSignature param loss | Hardcoded `vec![Raw(\"...\")]` instead of reading `ms.params.items` | `extractor/mod.rs:359-374`, `476-492` |\n19\t| React namespace recognition (SVGAttributes, etc.) | Missing entries in `is_react_builtin` and `html_element_for` | `react_types.rs`, `resolver/named.rs` |\n20\t| `Readonly<T>` transparent wrapper | Missing arm in `extractor/alias.rs` | `extractor/alias.rs` |\n21\t| `typeof` expression depth | `typeof Primitive.button` not followed through | `extractor/mod.rs` TSTypeQuery arm |\n22\t| Inline `Pick<T,K>` in `extends` | Step 1 silences Pick regardless of type_args | `resolver/chain.rs` step 0.5 |\n23\t\n24\t**Implementation plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-28-structural-gap-fixes.md`\n25\t\n26\t**Deferred — require type inference:**\n27\t\n28\t| Gap | Why it needs a type checker |\n29\t|-----|----------------------------|\n30\t| Generic parameter substitution (`List<T>` where T flows from call-site) | OXC gives us the AST node `T`, but to know T's concrete value we need the checker's `getTypeAtLocation` or its tsgo equivalent |\n31\t| Conditional types (`T extends U ? A : B`) | Already emitted as `opaque` — correct behavior. Full evaluation requires the checker |\n32\t| Mapped types (`{ [K in keyof T]: ... }`) | Already emitted as `opaque` — correct behavior |\n33\t| Multi-level generic propagation | A chain like `type ButtonProps = ComponentProps<typeof Button>` where Button is defined elsewhere can be 3-4 hops; our import resolver follows same-file chains but cross-file generic substitution requires the type checker |\n34\t\n35\t---\n36\t\n37\t## TypeScript 7.0 / tsgo ecosystem status (as of 2026-06-28)\n38\t\n39\t### What happened\n40\t\n41\tTypeScript 7.0 RC shipped 2026-06-18. This is the Go rewrite of the compiler (\"tsgo\"),\n42\tnot a JavaScript refactor. The key changes:\n43\t\n44\t- **TypeScript 6.0** = last JavaScript-based tsc (maintenance only)\n45\t- **TypeScript 7.0** = Go rewrite; 10× build speed, same semantics\n46\t- **Strada API** (ts.createProgram, checker.getTypeAtLocation, LanguageService) = **completely dropped** in TS 7.0 — no shim, no compatibility layer\n47\t- **react-docgen-typescript** depends on Strada; it is **broken under TS 7.0**\n48\t\n49\t### Corsa API\n50\t\n51\tThe tsgo team is building \"Corsa\" as the replacement public API. Status:\n52\t\n53\t- Corsa API: **not yet stable** — targeting TypeScript 7.1 (estimated late 2026 / early 2027)\n54\t- Current tsgo exports minimal surface: `check()`, `build()`, basic diagnostics\n55\t- No `getTypeAtLocation` equivalent yet\n56\t- Plugin system and language service extensions TBD\n57\t\n58\t### tsgolint precedent (OXC team)\n59\t\n60\tThe OXC team already tackled cross-language integration with `tsgolint`:\n61\t- Spawns `tsgo` as a subprocess\n62\t- Communicates via JSON IPC using tsgo's internal (unstable) shims\n63\t- This pattern works but depends on internal APIs that will break when Corsa lands\n64\t\n65\tWe should NOT follow the tsgolint approach — it creates maintenance debt on an unstable\n66\tinternal API. Wait for Corsa.\n67\t\n68\t### Why oxc-react-docgen is unaffected by TS 7.0\n69\t\n70\tWe parse TypeScript with OXC (Rust), not tsc. We have no dependency on the Strada API.\n71\tConsumers running TS 7.0 can use oxc-react-docgen without any changes. This is a\n72\tcompetitive advantage during the TS 6→7 migration window.\n73\t\n74\t---\n75\t\n76\t## Integration architecture (when Corsa is stable)\n77\t\n78\tThe integration should be **opt-in**, not always-on. Most projects need only the structural\n79\tanalysis for prop documentation. The type checker adds latency (~100-500ms cold start) and\n80\ta Node.js process dependency that many CI environments won't want.\n81\t\n82\t### Proposed design\n83\t\n84\t```\n85\t┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n86\t│  oxc-react-docgen  (current — always runs)              │\n87\t│  OXC AST parse → extractor → resolver → ExtractionOutput│\n88\t│  Props: structurally knowable types only                 │\n89\t│  Generics: emitted as PropType::Named or opaque         │\n90\t└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘\n91\t                           │ optional\n92\t                  ─────────▼─────────\n93\t                 │  Corsa enrichment  │\n94\t                 │  (future opt-in)   │\n95\t                 │                   │\n96\t                 │  For each prop     │\n97\t                 │  with opaque/Named │\n98\t                 │  type: call Corsa  │\n99\t                 │  getTypeAtLocation │\n100\t                 │  → replace with    │\n101\t                 │  resolved PropType │\n102\t                  ───────────────────\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\t**CLI flag:** `--with-type-checker` (default: off)\n106\t**Config key:** `docgen.config.ts → typeChecker: true | { path: string }`\n107\t**Node requirement:** Node 22+ (tsgo ships as npm package)\n108\t\n109\t### Specific Corsa operations needed\n110\t\n111\tWhen the Corsa API is available, the following operations unblock the deferred gaps:\n112\t\n113\t| Operation | Corsa API (expected) | Gap resolved |\n114\t|-----------|---------------------|--------------|\n115\t| Resolve generic type argument at call site | `checker.getTypeArguments(typeRef)` | Generic param substitution |\n116\t| Evaluate conditional type | `checker.resolveConditionalType(node)` | Conditional opaque |\n117\t| Expand mapped type | `checker.getIndexedAccessType(type, key)` | Mapped opaque |\n118\t| Follow `typeof expr` | `checker.getTypeOfExpression(expr)` | typeof depth |\n119\t\n120\tThe integration point is `resolver/chain.rs:resolve_props_chain` — after step 5 fails to\n121\tfind the interface in our global map, step 6 currently emits an `UnresolvableImport`\n122\tdiagnostic. With Corsa, a step 5.5 would ask the type checker for the props instead.\n123\t\n124\t### File plan (future)\n125\t\n126\t```\n127\tcrates/core/src/typechecker/          (new module, feature-gated)\n128\t  mod.rs              — feature gate, public API surface\n129\t  corsa_bridge.rs     — subprocess IPC with tsgo/Corsa\n130\t  prop_enricher.rs    — walk ExtractionOutput, replace opaque props\n131\t```\n132\t\n133\tFeature gate: `cargo build --features=type-checker` — keeps the no-Node-dependency\n134\tbuild path as the default.\n135\t\n136\t---\n137\t\n138\t## Timeline\n139\t\n140\t| Milestone | When | What it unlocks |\n141\t|-----------|------|----------------|\n142\t| TS 7.0 RC | 2026-06-18 (done) | Confirms Strada is dropped; competitive window opens |\n143\t| TS 7.1 release candidate | ~Q4 2026 | Corsa API draft; begin bridge prototype |\n144\t| TS 7.1 stable + Corsa stable | ~Q1 2027 | Implement generic substitution, `typeof` depth |\n145\t| Public release of `--with-type-checker` | ~Q1 2027 | Feature-complete RDT replacement |\n146\t\n147\tUntil then: fix the 5 structural gaps (see implementation plan), ship, and let users\n148\tmigrate to oxc-react-docgen during the TS 7 disruption window.\n149\t"}]},"uuid":"9cbd1857-e890-4b25-92ca-c5dd75d4af3b","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:25:47.917Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/type-checker-integration.md","content":"# Type Checker Integration: Future Work\n\nThis document describes which resolver gaps genuinely require a TypeScript type checker,\nthe state of the tsgo (TypeScript 7.0) ecosystem, and the integration plan for when the\nCorsa API is stable.\n\n---\n\n## What we can fix structurally (no type checker needed)\n\nThe six fundamental gap patterns discovered during the RDT compatibility audit break into\ntwo groups:\n\n**Fixable now — pure AST/structural:**\n\n| Gap | Root cause | Fix location |\n|-----|-----------|-------------|\n| TSMethodSignature param loss | Hardcoded `vec![Raw(\"...\")]` instead of reading `ms.params.items` | `extractor/mod.rs:359-374`, `476-492` |\n| React namespace recognition (SVGAttributes, etc.) | Missing entries in `is_react_builtin` and `html_element_for` | `react_types.rs`, `resolver/named.rs` |\n| `Readonly<T>` transparent wrapper | Missing arm in `extractor/alias.rs` | `extractor/alias.rs` |\n| `typeof` expression depth | `typeof Primitive.button` not followed through | `extractor/mod.rs` TSTypeQuery arm |\n| Inline `Pick<T,K>` in `extends` | Step 1 silences Pick regardless of type_args | `resolver/chain.rs` step 0.5 |\n\n**Implementation plan:** `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-28-structural-gap-fixes.md`\n\n**Deferred — require type inference:**\n\n| Gap | Why it needs a type checker |\n|-----|----------------------------|\n| Generic parameter substitution (`List<T>` where T flows from call-site) | OXC gives us the AST node `T`, but to know T's concrete value we need the checker's `getTypeAtLocation` or its tsgo equivalent |\n| Conditional types (`T extends U ? A : B`) | Already emitted as `opaque` — correct behavior. Full evaluation requires the checker |\n| Mapped types (`{ [K in keyof T]: ... }`) | Already emitted as `opaque` — correct behavior |\n| Multi-level generic propagation | A chain like `type ButtonProps = ComponentProps<typeof Button>` where Button is defined elsewhere can be 3-4 hops; our import resolver follows same-file chains but cross-file generic substitution requires the type checker |\n\n---\n\n## TypeScript 7.0 / tsgo ecosystem status (as of 2026-06-28)\n\n### What happened\n\nTypeScript 7.0 RC shipped 2026-06-18. This is the Go rewrite of the compiler (\"tsgo\"),\nnot a JavaScript refactor. The key changes:\n\n- **TypeScript 6.0** = last JavaScript-based tsc (maintenance only)\n- **TypeScript 7.0** = Go rewrite; 10× build speed, same semantics\n- **Strada API** (ts.createProgram, checker.getTypeAtLocation, LanguageService) = **completely dropped** in TS 7.0 — no shim, no compatibility layer\n- **react-docgen-typescript** depends on Strada; it is **broken under TS 7.0**\n\n### Corsa API\n\nThe tsgo team is building \"Corsa\" as the replacement public API. Status:\n\n- Corsa API: **not yet stable** — targeting TypeScript 7.1 (estimated late 2026 / early 2027)\n- Current tsgo exports minimal surface: `check()`, `build()`, basic diagnostics\n- No `getTypeAtLocation` equivalent yet\n- Plugin system and language service extensions TBD\n\n### tsgolint precedent (OXC team)\n\nThe OXC team already tackled cross-language integration with `tsgolint`:\n- Spawns `tsgo` as a subprocess\n- Communicates via JSON IPC using tsgo's internal (unstable) shims\n- This pattern works but depends on internal APIs that will break when Corsa lands\n\nWe should NOT follow the tsgolint approach — it creates maintenance debt on an unstable\ninternal API. Wait for Corsa.\n\n### Why oxc-react-docgen is unaffected by TS 7.0\n\nWe parse TypeScript with OXC (Rust), not tsc. We have no dependency on the Strada API.\nConsumers running TS 7.0 can use oxc-react-docgen without any changes. This is a\ncompetitive advantage during the TS 6→7 migration window.\n\n---\n\n## Integration architecture (when Corsa is stable)\n\nThe integration should be **opt-in**, not always-on. Most projects need only the structural\nanalysis for prop documentation. The type checker adds latency (~100-500ms cold start) and\na Node.js process dependency that many CI environments won't want.\n\n### Proposed design\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  oxc-react-docgen  (current — always runs)              │\n│  OXC AST parse → extractor → resolver → ExtractionOutput│\n│  Props: structurally knowable types only                 │\n│  Generics: emitted as PropType::Named or opaque         │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘\n                           │ optional\n                  ─────────▼─────────\n                 │  Corsa enrichment  │\n                 │  (future opt-in)   │\n                 │                   │\n                 │  For each prop     │\n                 │  with opaque/Named │\n                 │  type: call Corsa  │\n                 │  getTypeAtLocation │\n                 │  → replace with    │\n                 │  resolved PropType │\n                  ───────────────────\n```\n\n**CLI flag:** `--with-type-checker` (default: off)\n**Config key:** `docgen.config.ts → typeChecker: true | { path: string }`\n**Node requirement:** Node 22+ (tsgo ships as npm package)\n\n### Specific Corsa operations needed\n\nWhen the Corsa API is available, the following operations unblock the deferred gaps:\n\n| Operation | Corsa API (expected) | Gap resolved |\n|-----------|---------------------|--------------|\n| Resolve generic type argument at call site | `checker.getTypeArguments(typeRef)` | Generic param substitution |\n| Evaluate conditional type | `checker.resolveConditionalType(node)` | Conditional opaque |\n| Expand mapped type | `checker.getIndexedAccessType(type, key)` | Mapped opaque |\n| Follow `typeof expr` | `checker.getTypeOfExpression(expr)` | typeof depth |\n\nThe integration point is `resolver/chain.rs:resolve_props_chain` — after step 5 fails to\nfind the interface in our global map, step 6 currently emits an `UnresolvableImport`\ndiagnostic. With Corsa, a step 5.5 would ask the type checker for the props instead.\n\n### File plan (future)\n\n```\ncrates/core/src/typechecker/          (new module, feature-gated)\n  mod.rs              — feature gate, public API surface\n  corsa_bridge.rs     — subprocess IPC with tsgo/Corsa\n  prop_enricher.rs    — walk ExtractionOutput, replace opaque props\n```\n\nFeature gate: `cargo build --features=type-checker` — keeps the no-Node-dependency\nbuild path as the default.\n\n---\n\n## Timeline\n\n| Milestone | When | What it unlocks |\n|-----------|------|----------------|\n| TS 7.0 RC | 2026-06-18 (done) | Confirms Strada is dropped; competitive window opens |\n| TS 7.1 release candidate | ~Q4 2026 | Corsa API draft; begin bridge prototype |\n| TS 7.1 stable + Corsa stable | ~Q1 2027 | Implement generic substitution, `typeof` depth |\n| Public release of `--with-type-checker` | ~Q1 2027 | Feature-complete RDT replacement |\n\nUntil then: fix the 5 structural gaps (see implementation plan), ship, and let users\nmigrate to oxc-react-docgen during the TS 7 disruption window.\n","numLines":149,"startLine":1,"totalLines":149}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef381412-55b0-4d69-91e4-847ae6055697","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
