{"parentUuid":"3c0ec5ed-a7f1-44a3-b65a-764ff3ec9372","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01DQZtn8xrUYRQVaYevfb9V4","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== rust-style/SKILL.md ===\\\"; rtk read .claude/skills/rust-style/SKILL.md\\necho \\\"=== check.md ===\\\"; rtk read .claude/commands/check.md\\necho \\\"=== snapshot.md ===\\\"; rtk read .claude/commands/snapshot.md\\necho \\\"=== npm stub README sample ===\\\"; rtk read packages/napi/npm/darwin-arm64/README.md\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":28},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1ebe6051-0546-4d07-95c0-80c6ea28008d","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:26:58.352Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"3c0ec5ed-a7f1-44a3-b65a-764ff3ec9372","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2767ee7d-d768-4fc5-b864-ecc99fbdd4cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DQZtn8xrUYRQVaYevfb9V4","type":"tool_result","content":"=== rust-style/SKILL.md ===\n---\nname: rust-style\ndescription: Apply when writing or modifying Rust code in this project.\n---\n\n**Goal:** Code correct by construction, readable under churn, performant in hot paths.\n\n## Project-specific decisions\n\nThese are non-negotiables, not preferences:\n\n- Internal maps: `FxHashMap`. JSON-output maps: `BTreeMap` (deterministic key ordering).\n- Type/prop names: `CompactString` — avoids heap allocation for strings ≤24 bytes.\n- No `unwrap()` outside `#[cfg(test)]` — use `?` and let callers decide what to do with failure.\n\n## Control flow\n\n`let...else` keeps the happy path flat:\n\n```rust\nlet Some(entry) = map.get(key) else { return None };\nlet Ok(parsed) = input.parse::<u32>() else { continue };\n```\n\n## Matching\n\nNo wildcards — a compile error on unhandled variants is a feature:\n\n```rust\nmatch status { Status::Ok => .., Status::Err => .. }  // compiler tells you when Status grows\nmatch status { Status::Ok => .., _ => .. }             // silently misses new variants\n```\n\nFull `match` over `matches!` for the same reason.\n\n## Types\n\nNewtypes when a bare type allows confusion. Enums when a bool parameter hides intent:\n\n```rust\nstruct ScopedKey(CompactString);         // not: String\nenum Visibility { Public, Private }      // not: is_public: bool\n```\n\nExplicit destructuring gets compiler errors when structs change:\n\n```rust\nlet ComponentEntry { display_name, file_path, .. } = entry;\n```\n\n## Naming\n\nShadow variables through transformations — no `raw_`/`parsed_`/`trimmed_` prefixes:\n\n```rust\nlet path = args.path;\nlet path = path.canonicalize()?;\nlet path = path.join(\"config.toml\");\n```\n\n## Comments\n\nOnly when the WHY is non-obvious: a hidden constraint, a workaround, a non-obvious invariant. Not what the code does.\n=== check.md ===\nRun the verification suite and report status. Do not fix anything.\n\n```bash\ncargo clippy -p oxc-react-docgen-core -- -D warnings 2>&1\ncargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core 2>&1\ncargo insta pending-snapshots 2>/dev/null && echo \"⚠ pending snapshots\" || echo \"✓ no pending snapshots\"\n```\n\nReport: warnings, failing tests, pending snapshots. Stop there.\n=== snapshot.md ===\nUpdate and review snapshot tests.\n\n```bash\nINSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core 2>&1\ncargo insta review\n```\n\nAfter `cargo insta review` completes, run `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core` once more to confirm all snapshots pass.\n=== npm stub README sample ===\n# `@oxc-react-docgen/napi-darwin-arm64`\n\nThis is the **aarch64-apple-darwin** binary for `@oxc-react-docgen/napi`","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0cbf18f3-4e0a-490d-887a-f0770f48eaee","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:27:00.585Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== rust-style/SKILL.md ===\n---\nname: rust-style\ndescription: Apply when writing or modifying Rust code in this project.\n---\n\n**Goal:** Code correct by construction, readable under churn, performant in hot paths.\n\n## Project-specific decisions\n\nThese are non-negotiables, not preferences:\n\n- Internal maps: `FxHashMap`. JSON-output maps: `BTreeMap` (deterministic key ordering).\n- Type/prop names: `CompactString` — avoids heap allocation for strings ≤24 bytes.\n- No `unwrap()` outside `#[cfg(test)]` — use `?` and let callers decide what to do with failure.\n\n## Control flow\n\n`let...else` keeps the happy path flat:\n\n```rust\nlet Some(entry) = map.get(key) else { return None };\nlet Ok(parsed) = input.parse::<u32>() else { continue };\n```\n\n## Matching\n\nNo wildcards — a compile error on unhandled variants is a feature:\n\n```rust\nmatch status { Status::Ok => .., Status::Err => .. }  // compiler tells you when Status grows\nmatch status { Status::Ok => .., _ => .. }             // silently misses new variants\n```\n\nFull `match` over `matches!` for the same reason.\n\n## Types\n\nNewtypes when a bare type allows confusion. Enums when a bool parameter hides intent:\n\n```rust\nstruct ScopedKey(CompactString);         // not: String\nenum Visibility { Public, Private }      // not: is_public: bool\n```\n\nExplicit destructuring gets compiler errors when structs change:\n\n```rust\nlet ComponentEntry { display_name, file_path, .. } = entry;\n```\n\n## Naming\n\nShadow variables through transformations — no `raw_`/`parsed_`/`trimmed_` prefixes:\n\n```rust\nlet path = args.path;\nlet path = path.canonicalize()?;\nlet path = path.join(\"config.toml\");\n```\n\n## Comments\n\nOnly when the WHY is non-obvious: a hidden constraint, a workaround, a non-obvious invariant. Not what the code does.\n=== check.md ===\nRun the verification suite and report status. Do not fix anything.\n\n```bash\ncargo clippy -p oxc-react-docgen-core -- -D warnings 2>&1\ncargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core 2>&1\ncargo insta pending-snapshots 2>/dev/null && echo \"⚠ pending snapshots\" || echo \"✓ no pending snapshots\"\n```\n\nReport: warnings, failing tests, pending snapshots. Stop there.\n=== snapshot.md ===\nUpdate and review snapshot tests.\n\n```bash\nINSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core 2>&1\ncargo insta review\n```\n\nAfter `cargo insta review` completes, run `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core` once more to confirm all snapshots pass.\n=== npm stub README sample ===\n# `@oxc-react-docgen/napi-darwin-arm64`\n\nThis is the **aarch64-apple-darwin** binary for `@oxc-react-docgen/napi`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c0ec5ed-a7f1-44a3-b65a-764ff3ec9372","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","