{"parentUuid":"a5e4a23e-e6fd-4a38-9e0e-2e6e8633bf69","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ3igCZGSctgQB9LZWJA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J3mvLVwxGKiSXyPxbccq5L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\ndocs: stop hard-wrapping markdown, fix a stale plan reference\n\nEvery doc I wrote this session (docs/adr/*, the adr skill, STATUS.md,\narchive/README.md) was hard-wrapped at ~80 columns, while the rest of\nthe repo (README, ARCHITECTURE, CONTRIBUTING, MIGRATING) already uses\none-line-per-paragraph and lets the editor soft-wrap. Fixed all of them,\nplus two pre-existing offenders that predate this session\n(docs/rdt-coverage.md, docs/type-checker-integration.md, and small\nsections of ARCHITECTURE.md/README.md) — hard-wrapping causes noisy\ndiffs the moment a sentence gets edited, which matters most for exactly\nthese actively-maintained docs.\n\nVerified no content was lost: normalized (whitespace-collapsed) diffs\nagainst the prior commit show only the intended changes — blockquote\ncontinuation markers removed, a couple of mid-word hyphen line-breaks\nthe old wrap had introduced now join correctly, and one stale reference\nto a path that no longer exists.\n\nThat stale reference: type-checker-integration.md pointed at\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-28-structural-gap-fixes.md, which this\nsession already archived to docs/archive/2026-06-28-structural-gap-fixes.md.\nFixed the link and noted the plan is done.\n\nLeft docs/archive/*'s other frozen historical files alone — they're\nexplicitly not-edited-again historical record, so the \"avoid noisy\ndiffs on future edits\" rationale for reflowing doesn't apply to them.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -15\ngit log --oneline -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_inpu