{"parentUuid":"14ab3367-5e9c-494d-8c7c-733e3f51995d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdJ6qqrH1HvPSGWzuu2C2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI does exist though — I showed you the full `.github/workflows/ci.yml` a few turns back (lint, test, deny, coverage, bench, a Node matrix, an install matrix). I was wrong to point at \"CI doesn't call moon today\" as an argument against moon — that's a fact about the current file, not a verdict on whether moon would help. Those are different claims and I conflated them.\n\nLooking again with that corrected: CI currently runs the *entire* matrix on every single push, regardless of what changed — a docs-only commit still triggers the full Rust suite, bench, both Node versions, and both package-manager install checks. That's exactly the problem moon's affected-detection exists to solve in a polyglot monorepo, and moon's already configured here (`workspace.yml` + six `moon.yml` files, correctly modeling the one real cross-project dependency). Wiring `moon ci` into the GitHub workflow to only run what's actually affected by a given diff is a much smaller lift than what I was proposing (hand-rebuilding ordering in the `justfile`), and it's the kind of case moon is genuinely built for.\n\nRevised recommendation: keep both moon and proto. Proto's the toolchain manager moon natively integrates with (`moon setup` already reads `.prototools` directly) — swapping to mise would mean maintaining a seam between two tools instead of using the one moon already talks to. I'd rather spend the effort making CI actually use moon's affected-graph than rip out a working, correctly-modeled setup because of a premise that didn't hold up.\n\nWant me to wire `moon ci` (or per-project affected checks) into the GitHub workflow so untouched projects actually get skipped?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":80,"cache_read_input_tokens":542679,"output_tokens":2863,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":80,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2863,"cache_read_input_tokens":542679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":80,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":80},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJ6qmFTTyfsmUWJ9vNHc","type":"assistant","uuid":"a24b329e-487a-4932-a209-8f9ff2574bcc","timestamp":"2026-07-23T01:13:47.703Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
