{"parentUuid":"3016164a-4f3d-4ae0-8cb1-a72dc55b4327","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdKGvg2yxXDECstKav9LA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NWCovHrURp8g5YakBcqLJZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nchore(license): adopt AGPL-3.0-or-later, replace stale MIT everywhere\n\nThe new orin-dx/oxc-react-docgen repo's initial commit shipped a real\nAGPLv3 LICENSE file, but every package.json/Cargo.toml here still\nclaimed MIT (the placeholder from project scaffolding) — a real\nconflict between what the license file says and what the packages\ndeclare. AGPL-3.0-or-later is the confirmed intended license.\n\nAdded the LICENSE file (copied from the target repo, standard FSF\nAGPLv3 text — its own body includes the \"or later version\" option\nclause, hence the -or-later SPDX suffix), updated all 13\npackage.json license fields (the 3 real npm packages plus their 10\nper-platform binary stubs) and Cargo.toml's workspace license, and\nfixed README's License section.\n\ncargo-deny's license allow-list didn't include AGPL-3.0-or-later —\nconfirmed this would have hard-failed `cargo deny check licenses`\n(our own crates rejected by our own policy) before adding it.\n\nAlso merged in the few genuine Rust-specific .gitignore entries the\ntarget repo's generic `cargo new` template .gitignore had that this\nrepo's (already more complete) one didn't: a debug/ build dir,\nrustfmt .rs.bk backups, MSVC .pdb files, cargo-mutants output.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -15\ngit log --oneline -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_read_input_tokens":588839,"output_tokens":596,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens"