{"parentUuid":"81e04eb8-acbe-4faa-bbae-5fd37ce46bad","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_019R61Gs2HEMHfhevGBV8MVK","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":64},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a64eef01-0398-42ef-a941-f92243b55bac","timestamp":"2026-07-24T22:14:47.830Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"a64eef01-0398-42ef-a941-f92243b55bac","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/type-checker-integration.md","snippet":"1\t# Type Checker Integration: Future Work\n2\t\n3\tThis document describes which resolver gaps genuinely require a TypeScript type checker, the state of the tsgo (TypeScript 7.0) ecosystem, and the integration plan for when the Corsa API is stable.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## What we can fix structurally (no type checker needed)\n8\t\n9\tThe six fundamental gap patterns discovered during the RDT compatibility audit break into two groups:\n10\t\n11\t**Fixable now — pure AST/structural:**\n12\t\n13\t| Gap                                               | Root cause                                                        | Fix location                          |\n14\t| ------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n15\t| TSMethodSignature param loss                      | Hardcoded `vec![Raw(\"...\")]` instead of reading `ms.params.items` | `extractor/mod.rs:359-374`, `476-492` |\n16\t| React namespace recognition (SVGAttributes, etc.) | Missing entries in `is_react_builtin` and `html_element_for`      | `react_types.rs`, `resolver/named.rs` |\n17\t| `Readonly<T>` transparent wrapper                 | Missing arm in `extractor/alias.rs`                               | `extractor/alias.rs`                  |\n18\t| `typeof` expression depth                         | `typeof Primitive.button` not followed through                    | `extractor/mod.rs` TSTypeQuery arm    |\n19\t| Inline `Pick<T,K>` in `extends`                   | Step 1 silences Pick regardless of type_args                      | `resolver/chain.rs` step 0.5          |\n20\t\n21\t**Implementation plan:** `docs/archive/2026-06-28-structural-gap-fixes.md` (done — see `docs/STATUS.md`)\n22\t\n23\t**Deferred — require type inference:**\n24\t\n25\t| Gap                                                                     | Why it needs a type checker                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n26\t| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n27\t| Generic parameter substitution (`List<T>` where T flows from call-site) | OXC gives us the AST node `T`, but to know T's concrete value we need the checker's `getTypeAtLocation` or its tsgo equivalent                                                                                                |\n28\t| Conditional types (`T extends U ? A : B`)                               | Already emitted as `opaque` — correct behavior. Full evaluation requires the checker                                                                                                                                          |\n29\t| Mapped types (`{ [K in keyof T]: ... }`)                                | Already emitted as `opaque` — correct behavior                                                                                                                                                                                |\n30\t| Multi-level generic propagation                                         | A chain like `type ButtonProps = ComponentProps<typeof Button>` where Button is defined elsewhere can be 3-4 hops; our import resolver follows same-file chains but cross-file generic substitution requires the type checker |\n31\t\n32\t---\n33\t\n34\t## TypeScript 7.0 / tsgo ecosystem status (as of 2026-06-28)\n35\t\n36\t### What happened\n37\t\n38\tTypeScript 7.0 RC shipped 2026-06-18. This is the Go rewrite of the compiler (\"tsgo\"), not a JavaScript refactor. The key changes:\n39\t\n40\t- **TypeScript 6.0** = last JavaScript-based tsc (maintenance only)\n41\t- **TypeScript 7.0** = Go rewrite; 10× build speed, same semantics\n42\t- **Strada API** (ts.createProgram, checker.getTypeAtLocation, LanguageService) = **completely dropped** in TS 7.0 — no shim, no compatibility layer\n43\t- **react-docgen-typescript** depends on Strada; it is **broken under TS 7.0**\n44\t\n45\t### Corsa API\n46\t\n47\tThe tsgo team is building \"Corsa\" as the replacement public API. Status:\n48\t\n49\t- Corsa API: **not yet stable** — targeting TypeScript 7.1 (estimated late 2026 / early 2027)\n50\t- Current tsgo exports minimal surface: `check()`, `build()`, basic diagnostics\n51\t- No `getTypeAtLocation` equivalent yet\n52\t- Plugin system and language service extensions TBD\n53\t\n54\t### tsgolint precedent (OXC team)\n55\t\n56\tThe OXC team already tackled cross-language integration with `tsgolint`:\n57\t\n58\t- Spawns `tsgo` as a subprocess\n59\t- Communicates via JSON IPC using tsgo's internal (unstable) shims\n60\t- This pattern works but depends on internal APIs that will break when Corsa lands\n61\t\n62\tWe should NOT follow the tsgolint approach — it creates maintenance debt on an unstable internal API. Wait for Corsa.\n63\t\n64\t### Why oxc-react-docgen is unaffected by TS 7.0\n65\t\n66\tWe parse TypeScript with OXC (Rust), not tsc. We have no dependency on the Strada API. Consumers running TS 7.0 can use oxc-react-docgen without any changes. This is a competitive advantage during the TS 6→7 migration window.\n67\t\n68\t---\n69\t\n70\t## Integration architecture (when Corsa is stable)\n71\t\n72\tThe integration should be **opt-in**, not always-on. Most projects need only the structural analysis for prop documentation. The type checker adds latency (~100-500ms cold start) and a Node.js process dependency that many CI environments won't want.\n73\t\n74\t### Proposed design\n75\t\n76\t```\n77\t┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n78\t│  oxc-react-docgen  (current — always runs)              │\n79\t│  OXC AST parse → extractor → resolver → ExtractionOutput│\n80\t│  Props: structurally knowable types only                 │\n81\t│  Generics: emitted as PropType::Named or opaque         │\n82\t└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘\n83\t                           │ optional\n84\t                  ─────────▼─────────\n85\t                 │  Corsa enrichment  │\n86\t                 │  (future opt-in)   │\n87\t                 │                   │\n88\t                 │  For each prop     │\n89\t                 │  with opaque/Named │\n90\t                 │  type: call Corsa  │\n91\t                 │  getTypeAtLocation │\n92\t                 │  → replace with    │\n93\t                 │  resolved PropType │\n94\t                  ───────────────────\n95\t```\n96\t\n97\t**CLI flag:** `--with-type-checker` (default: off)\n98\t**Config key:** `docgen.config.ts → typeChecker: true | { path: string }`\n99\t**Node requirement:** Node 22+ (tsgo ships as npm package)\n100\t\n101\t### Specific Corsa operations needed\n102\t\n103\tWhen the Corsa API is available, the following operations unblock the deferred gaps:\n104\t\n105\t| Operation                                  | Corsa API (expected)                      | Gap resolved               |\n106\t| ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n107\t| Resolve generic type argument at call site | `checker.getTypeArguments(typeRef)`       | Generic param substitution |\n108\t| Evaluate conditional type                  | `checker.resolveConditionalType(node)`    | Conditional opaque         |\n109\t| Expand mapped type                         | `checker.getIndexedAccessType(type, key)` | Mapped opaque              |\n110\t| Follow `typeof expr`                       | `checker.getTypeOfExpression(expr)`       | typeof depth               |\n111\t\n112\tThe integration point is `resolver/chain.rs:resolve_props_chain` — after step 5 fails to find the interface in our global map, step 6 currently emits an `UnresolvableImport` diagnostic. With Corsa, a step 5.5 would ask the type checker for the props instead.\n113\t\n114\t### File plan (future)\n115\t\n116\t```\n117\tcrates/core/src/typechecker/          (new module, feature-gated)\n118\t  mod.rs              — feature gate, public API surface\n119\t  corsa_bridge.rs     — subprocess IPC with tsgo/Corsa\n\n... [17 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"399dec95-6fc0-4195-a873-b02fa1a98b4a","timestamp":"2026-07-24T22:14:47.882Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
