{"parentUuid":"6df3d668-6b32-48ab-aae9-a40f6dd8e8b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdMgKXEyj1gELA5kw5rVt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ws6M2EKpyW3Bi5DwgEAsqg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat: add oxlint — pedantic for source, relaxed for tests, real findings fixed\n\nNo TS/JS linting existed anywhere in the repo before this (no eslint,\nno oxlint). Enabled correctness/suspicious/pedantic/perf/style categories\nfor real source (packages/vite-plugin/src, napi's hand-maintained\nindex.d.ts, the cli npm wrapper, apps/validate/src) — genuinely strict,\nnot just the default correctness-only baseline.\n\noxlint's config format can't scope *categories* per file glob (overrides\nonly support individual `rules`, confirmed against its own schema) — so\nthe \"relaxed for tests\" split happens via two separate invocations with\nCLI category flags (-A pedantic -A perf -A style for tests), not a\nconfig-file override. The override block still adds the vitest plugin\nfor test files and turns off node/no-sync for the two genuinely\none-shot script contexts (apps/validate's CLI scripts, the cli npm\nwrapper) where blocking sync I/O is correct, not a mistake — a rule\nwritten for long-running servers doesn't fit a script that runs once\nand exits.\n\nTurned off ~19 rules that were pure noise against this codebase's actual\nconventions rather than real quality signal: no-magic-numbers flagged\nevery numeric literal, id-length fought the codebase's deliberate short\nnames, sort-keys/sort-imports/sort-vars have no real value, curly/\nno-ternary/func-style are house-style opinions that fought existing\ncode, capitalized-comments/no-inline-comments/require-unicode-regexp\nare niche nitpicks. Checked what remained across ~130 findings, then\nfixed each real one: two instances of genuine dead code (an unused\n`normalize` function, an unused `mkdirSync` import), 3 unused imports,\na nested ternary refactored into an if-else chain, inconsistent catch\nvariable names, array callback references needing explicit wrapping,\na negated condition, direct member access converted to destructuring,\nand a useless `?? []` fallback on a Set constructor.\n\nTwo findings were false positives for a specific, deliberate reason,\nnot real issues: vite-plugin's configureServer hook must return its\nteardown function synchronously, so its fire-and-forget .then()/.catch()\nchain can't become async/await without breaking that contract — used a\nblock-scoped oxlint-disable/enable with a comment explaining why, rather\nthan silencing the rule everywhere it might apply.\n\nVerified no behavior changed: vite-plugin's 18 tests and tsc build pass,\nand — since several fixes touched apps/validate's actual data-collection\nlogic — ran the real end-to-end compare:all pipeline against all 20\nfixtures before and after (via git stash) and confirmed byte-identical\noutput (551/5840 props, 2 identical matches, 5418 misses — this low\nnumber predates every change here and isn't a regression; RDT counts\nseveral non-component exports like hooks and helper functions as\n\"components\" that this tool correctly doesn't).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10\ngit log --oneline -2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":794243,"output_tokens":1136,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1136,"cache_read_input_tokens":794243,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdMgKQE3cCGh7xd8ANLHW","type":"assistant","uuid":"37712c54-7c95-4f56-8e77-0102a1cb62d4","timestamp":"2026-07-24T22:34:15.812Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
