{"parentUuid":"9fcafeb4-6969-44d3-8072-48725e8225b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdMgQ1vVzMjxBj4zbW8EP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both created. Let me link them from `docs/STATUS.md` so the roadmap doc points at the real tracking issues."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":797648,"output_tokens":201,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":201,"cache_read_input_tokens":797648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdMgPwbYrjXvbMBSaUZu3","type":"assistant","uuid":"7ca75c3a-ef0e-493f-84e4-23d58ddc4931","timestamp":"2026-07-24T22:35:04.336Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"7ca75c3a-ef0e-493f-84e4-23d58ddc4931","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdMgQ1vVzMjxBj4zbW8EP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019U23tsJNrTpxmqGTqaZqPq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/STATUS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":797648,"output_tokens":201,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":201,"cache_read_input_tokens":797648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdMgPwbYrjXvbMBSaUZu3","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea713573-29c8-4b68-b74a-a6182991999b","timestamp":"2026-07-24T22:35:04.894Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"ea713573-29c8-4b68-b74a-a6182991999b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c5a617ab-e925-4f00-b112-70026e39294a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019U23tsJNrTpxmqGTqaZqPq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Status\n2\t\n3\t**Updated:** 2026-07-22\n4\t\n5\tCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are tested. Config file loading, cross-package `.d.ts` resolution, and watch mode are fully implemented — not stubs, despite what older docs in this repo used to say. If you find another doc contradicting this file, this file wins.\n6\t\n7\t## Numbers\n8\t\n9\t- 191 Rust tests (21 cli + 158 core unit + 8 snapshot + 4 napi binding), 18 vitest — all green\n10\t- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean\n11\t- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n12\t\n13\t## What's not built yet\n14\t\n15\t- **Preset system** (`@oxc-react-docgen/presets`) — named `PipelineOptions` bundles. Config-side only, no Rust changes needed.\n16\t- **LSP server** — `lsp-types` is a dependency; nothing built on it.\n17\t- **Barrel/re-export scoped-key allocation caching** — `resolver/chain.rs` / `named.rs` / `template.rs` build a `\"{file}:{name}\"` scoped-key string on every lookup. A `Borrow`-based type-map key would let lookups happen without allocating. Real but unbenchmarked — do as a focused perf pass if profiling shows it matters.\n18\t- **DTS cache has no dirty-flag or size cap** (`cache.rs`) — rewrites the whole cache file on every run regardless of whether anything changed, and has no upper bound on how large the on-disk cache can grow. Low severity (requires local write access, and an attacker with that already has better options) — worth fixing for large monorepos before it becomes a real cost.\n19\t\n20\t## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n21\t\n22\tSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs, not on the roadmap unless typescript-go's Corsa API stabilizes (see `type-checker-integration.md`).\n23\t\n24\t## Where to look next\n25\t\n26\t- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n27\t- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, deferring type-checker integration. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n28\t- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`\n29\t- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n30\t- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n31\t- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n32\t"}]},"uuid":"1642703e-1c0e-41a6-b8b7-bb829270f892","timestamp":"2026-07-24T22:35:04.991Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-07-22\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are tested. Config file loading, cross-package `.d.ts` resolution, and watch mode are fully implemented — not stubs, despite what older docs in this repo used to say. If you find another doc contradicting this file, this file wins.\n\n## Numbers\n\n- 191 Rust tests (21 cli + 158 core unit + 8 snapshot + 4 napi binding), 18 vitest — all green\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n\n## What's not built yet\n\n- **Preset system** (`@oxc-react-docgen/presets`) — named `PipelineOptions` bundles. Config-side only, no Rust changes needed.\n- **LSP server** — `lsp-types` is a dependency; nothing built on it.\n- **Barrel/re-export scoped-key allocation caching** — `resolver/chain.rs` / `named.rs` / `template.rs` build a `\"{file}:{name}\"` scoped-key string on every lookup. A `Borrow`-based type-map key would let lookups happen without allocating. Real but unbenchmarked — do as a focused perf pass if profiling shows it matters.\n- **DTS cache has no dirty-flag or size cap** (`cache.rs`) — rewrites the whole cache file on every run regardless of whether anything changed, and has no upper bound on how large the on-disk cache can grow. Low severity (requires local write access, and an attacker with that already has better options) — worth fixing for large monorepos before it becomes a real cost.\n\n## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs, not on the roadmap unless typescript-go's Corsa API stabilizes (see `type-checker-integration.md`).\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, deferring type-checker integration. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea713573-29c8-4b68-b74a-a6182991999b","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.217","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
