{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-07-24T23:28:50.513Z","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>w3830vi6c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/6e77fa42-b39d-4d85-9370-fe0b0fa9b104/tasks/w3830vi6c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Multi-model adversarial review of everything since cc2ff97 — bugs, perf, competitive-fit vs react-docgen-typescript\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"totalFindings\":23,\"confirmedCount\":13,\"confirmed\":[{\"file\":\"crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs\",\"line\":150,\"dimension\":\"correctness\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"summary\":\"named.rs's 'cannot resolve' diagnostic wasn't given the same barrel-resolved-location note that chain.rs just gained, so the two diagnostic-quality fixes are now inconsistent\",\"detail\":\"chain.rs's unresolvable-type diagnostic (step 6) was upgraded in this range to say '(resolved to X in Y)' when import/re-export resolution redirected the lookup elsewhere, specifically because barrel resolution can now legitimately move `canonical_file`/`canonical_name` away from `consuming_file`/`type_name`. named.rs's step-7 unresolvable diagnostic goes through the exact same `resolve_to_canonical` (and therefore the same barrel-following) but was left with the old flat message ('Cannot resolve type ... — it will appear as an unexpanded named reference') with no equivalent location note, even though it can now hit the identical barrel-redirect case chain.rs was fixed for.\",\"suggested_fix\":\"Factor the resolved_elsewhere/location_note logic out of chain.rs into a shared helper (similar to `max_depth_diagnostic`) and use it in both chain.rs and named.rs so the two 'cannot resolve' diagnostics stay consistent.\",\"area\":\"resolver-diagnostics\",\"votes\":[{\"refuted\":false,\"reasoning\":\"Verified against current code; every factual claim in the finding holds.\\n\\n1. chain.rs did gain the note in this range. `git diff cc2ff97..HEAD -- crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs` shows the step-6 diagnostic changed from \\\"Cannot resolve type '{}' in '{}' (scoped key: '{}')\\\" to \\\"Cannot resolve type '{}' in '{}'{}\\\" plus a new `resolved_elsewhere`/`location_note` block at /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs:161-181, with a comment explicitly citing re-exports/barrel files as the motivation.\\n\\n2. named.rs's step-7 diagnostic was touched in the same range (wording changed from \\\"it will appear as opaque\\\" to \\\"it will appear as an unexpanded named reference\\\") but got no location note: /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs:148-161.\\n\\n3. Both call the same `resolve_to_canonical` (named.rs:46-48, chain.rs:143-144), and that function does the recursive barrel following via `follow_reexports` (/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/src/resolver/import.rs:16-83). When the chain terminates without finding a declaration it returns `(barrel_file, name)` unchanged — exactly the case where `canonical_file != consuming_file` — and the lookup then falls through steps 3/4 (alias/interface), 5 (known), 6, 6.5, 6.7 to step 7. So named.rs is genuinely reachable in the same barrel-redirect state chain.rs was fixed for, and `canonical_file`/`canonical_name` are still in scope at named.rs:149, so the fix is a copy of the four lines from chain.rs.\\n\\nCaveat on impact, consistent with the stated low severity: this is diagnostic-message text only. No prop is dropped, no type is mistyped, no diagnostic is suppressed (the warning still fires with code `UnresolvableImport`), and there is no hot-path cost. It is a debuggability/consistency gap: a user chasing a barrel-file miss at the prop-type level sees \\\"Cannot resolve type 'X' in 'consumer.tsx'\\\" with no hint that resolution actually landed in some index.ts. Real, small, cheap to fix.\"},{\"reasoning\":\"Verified against the current code and the actual diff range.\\n\\n`/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs:159-176` (step 6, unresolvable): in this range the message was changed from `\\\"Cannot resolve type 'X' in 'F' (scoped key: 'file:name')\\\"` to computing `resolved_elsewhere = canonical_file != consuming_file || canonical_name != type_name` and appending `\\\" (resolved to 'N' in 'F')\\\"`, with a comment explicitly citing re-exports/barrel files as the reason.\\n\\n`/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs:149-160` (step 7, unresolvable): still the flat `\\\"Cannot resolve type '{}' in '{}' — it will appear as an unexpanded named reference\\\"` with no location note.\\n\\nBoth functions derive their lookup key from the same call: chain.rs:143 and named.rs:46-48 both call `resolve_to_canonical(name, consuming_file, ctx, &amp;mut state.diagnostics)` with the same `unwrap_or_else` fallback to `(consuming_file, name)`. So named.rs can reach step 7 with `canonical_file`/`canonical_name` redirected by barrel/re-export following exactly as chain.rs can, and in that case its warning names only `consuming_file` — the precise confusion the chain.rs edit was made to remove. The inconsistency is real and reachable, not hypothetical.\\n\\nScope/severity check (adversarial): this is message text only. No diagnostic is dropped (non-negotiable #6 is satisfied — a Warning with `DiagnosticCode::UnresolvableImport` is still emitted), no prop type changes, no allocation added to a hot path (the note is only built on the unresolvable path). Also worth noting named.rs never carried the old `(scoped key: ...)` text either, so this is a pre-existing gap that the chain.rs improvement newly exposed rather than a regression introduced by the range. That caps it at a genuine low-severity diagnostic-quality nit, which matches the stated severity — so I could not refute it.\",\"refuted\":false}]},{\"file\":\"crates/core/src/resolver/import.rs\",\"line\":68,\"dimension\":\"performance\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"summary\":\"Wildcard (`export * from`) re-export resolution has no memoization, so a barrel with several star re-exports re-walks and re-allocates the full chain for every prop that references a name it exports\",\"detail\":\"`ReExportStep::Wildcards` iterates every `export * from` specifier and recursively calls `follow_reexports` for each, discarding all work if the eventual match isn't found (or redoing it per distinct `name` queried against the same barrel). For a component library with a deep barrel (`index.ts` re-exporting from 10+ modules), every distinct prop-type name that round-trips through that barrel re-walks the same specifier list and re-resolves the same import specifiers via `resolve_import_specifier`, with no cache keyed on `(file, name)` — this is exactly the kind of per-file repeated computation the project's performance non-negotiables call out (accidental repeated computation on a path that runs per-type).\",\"suggested_fix\":\"Consider caching resolved `(barrel_file, name) -&gt; (canonical_file, canonical_name)` pairs in `ResolutionContext` (read-only after construction, so safe across the rayon-parallel resolve calls) to avoid re-walking the same wildcard chain for every reference to names re-exported through the same barrel.\",\"area\":\"resolver-diagnostics\",\"votes\":[{\"refuted\":false,\"reasoning\":\"Confirmed by reading and by measurement. crates/core/src/resolver/import.rs:51-82 `follow_reexports` has no cache; the `Wildcards` arm re-resolves every `export * from` specifier via `resolve_import_specifier` and recurses with `name.clone()`, discarding all work on a miss, and `ImportResolutionMap::resolve_reexport_chain` (import_map.rs:94-115) rebuilds a Vec of cloned specifier Strings on every call while `is_declared_at` does up to 4 `format!` allocations per node. No `(file, name)` memo exists anywhere; ResolutionContext (resolver/mod.rs:96-121) holds only immutable indexes.\\n\\nI instrumented follow_reexports/resolve_import_specifier with atomic counters plus a timer and built two synthetic projects inside crates/core (release build), then reverted all edits (git status clean).\\n\\nProbe A (1 component, 72 distinct prop types through a 12-way star barrel): total_extract=25.5ms, follow_time=686us, follow_calls=540, wildcard_specs=864, resolve_spec=540 — linear per lookup (~12 specifier resolutions per name), not an exponential blowup.\\n\\nProbe B (40 components each importing the same 8 barrel types = 320 queries over 8 distinct (file,name) keys), A/B'd against a throwaway global Mutex&lt;FxHashMap&gt; memo\n... (truncated 81323 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/6e77fa42-b39d-4d85-9370-fe0b0fa9b104/tasks/w3830vi6c.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/subagents/workflows/wf_fd05719e-c01/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/workflows/scripts/post-session-adversarial-review-wf_fd05719e-c01.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_fd05719e-c01'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>54</agent_count><agents_done>54</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>1</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1686335</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>563</tool_uses><duration_ms>920012</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
