{"parentUuid":"62ee2ba6-8da6-46b9-9fce-52aaac12773f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a93efbbf-d554-43f4-8215-0c7aba37141b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZyAGfdEzwAz8zBBH8NH4g","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Import and canonical resolution.\n2\t\n3\tuse camino::{Utf8Path, Utf8PathBuf};\n4\tuse compact_str::CompactString;\n5\tuse rustc_hash::FxHashSet;\n6\t\n7\tuse crate::import_map::ReExportStep;\n8\tuse crate::types::*;\n9\t\n10\tuse super::ResolutionContext;\n11\t\n12\t/// Re-export chains in real code are shallow (one or two barrel hops); this\n13\t/// only guards against a pathological or cyclic `export * from` graph.\n14\tconst MAX_REEXPORT_DEPTH: u8 = 8;\n15\t\n16\t/// Resolve `name` to its canonical `(file_path, name)` pair.\n17\t/// Returns `None` if `name` is a local declaration (not imported).\n18\tpub(super) fn resolve_to_canonical(\n19\t    name: &str,\n20\t    consuming_file: &Utf8Path,\n21\t    ctx: &ResolutionContext,\n22\t    diagnostics: &mut Vec<Diagnostic>,\n23\t) -> Option<(Utf8PathBuf, String)> {\n24\t    if let Some(import_ref) = ctx.import_map.find_import(consuming_file, name) {\n25\t        let resolved_file = resolve_import_specifier(&import_ref.specifier, consuming_file, ctx, diagnostics)?;\n26\t        let canonical_name = import_ref.exported_name.to_string();\n27\t        let mut visited = FxHashSet::default();\n28\t        return Some(follow_reexports(resolved_file, canonical_name, ctx, diagnostics, &mut visited, 0));\n29\t    }\n30\t\n31\t    // Namespace-import member access: `import * as React from \"react\"` then a\n32\t    // reference to `React.DependencyList`. `find_import` only tracks the\n33\t    // namespace binding itself (\"React\", with `exported_name == \"*\"`) — a\n34\t    // literal dotted name like \"React.DependencyList\" is never itself a\n35\t    // binding, so the lookup above always misses it. Split off the namespace\n36\t    // prefix and route the member name through the namespace's own import\n37\t    // specifier instead.\n38\t    let (namespace, member) = name.split_once('.')?;\n39\t    let namespace_ref = ctx.import_map.find_import(consuming_file, namespace)?;\n40\t    if namespace_ref.exported_name != \"*\" {\n41\t        return None;\n42\t    }\n43\t    let resolved_file = resolve_import_specifier(&namespace_ref.specifier, consuming_file, ctx, diagnostics)?;\n44\t    let mut visited = FxHashSet::default();\n45\t    Some(follow_reexports(resolved_file, member.to_string(), ctx, diagnostics, &mut visited, 0))\n46\t}\n47\t\n48\t/// A directly-imported name may land on a barrel file (`export { X } from\n49\t/// './x'` or `export * from './x'`) that doesn't declare `name` itself —\n50\t/// ubiquitous in real component libraries' `index.ts` files. Follow the\n51\t/// re-export chain until we reach a file that actually declares `name`, or\n52\t/// run out of chain to follow — in which case the original (barrel_file,\n53\t/// name) is returned unchanged, so the caller's existing \"cannot resolve\"\n54\t/// diagnostic still fires exactly as it did before this existed.\n55\tfn follow_reexports(\n56\t    file: Utf8PathBuf,\n57\t    name: String,\n58\t    ctx: &ResolutionContext,\n59\t    diagnostics: &mut Vec<Diagnostic>,\n60\t    visited: &mut FxHashSet<(Utf8PathBuf, CompactString)>,\n61\t    depth: u8,\n62\t) -> (Utf8PathBuf, String) {\n63\t    if depth >= MAX_REEXPORT_DEPTH || is_declared_at(&ctx.global, &file, &name) {\n64\t        return (file, name);\n65\t    }\n66\t    // Real barrels commonly share descendants (several sub-barrels wildcarding\n67\t    // the same underlying `types.ts`, say) — without this, re-exploring an\n68\t    // already-visited (file, name) pair from a different parent multiplies out\n69\t    // to branching_factor^depth calls instead of one call per graph node. This\n70\t    // also subsumes cycle detection: a cycle revisits a pair by definition.\n71\t    if !visited.insert((file.clone(), CompactString::from(name.as_str()))) {\n72\t        return (file, name);\n73\t    }\n74\t    match ctx.import_map.resolve_reexport_chain(&file, &name, &ctx.global) {\n75\t        Some(ReExportStep::Named { source_specifier, source_name }) => {"}]},"uuid":"deb69e52-8c0d-4cf4-ac1a-106fd6ce9c96","timestamp":"2026-07-24T23:36:03.552Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/src/resolver/import.rs","content":"//! Import and canonical resolution.\n\nuse camino::{Utf8Path, Utf8PathBuf};\nuse compact_str::CompactString;\nuse rustc_hash::FxHashSet;\n\nuse crate::import_map::ReExportStep;\nuse crate::types::*;\n\nuse super::ResolutionContext;\n\n/// Re-export chains in real code are shallow (one or two barrel hops); this\n/// only guards against a pathological or cyclic `export * from` graph.\nconst MAX_REEXPORT_DEPTH: u8 = 8;\n\n/// Resolve `name` to its canonical `(file_path, name)` pair.\n/// Returns `None` if `name` is a local declaration (not imported).\npub(super) fn resolve_to_canonical(\n    name: &str,\n    consuming_file: &Utf8Path,\n    ctx: &ResolutionContext,\n    diagnostics: &mut Vec<Diagnostic>,\n) -> Option<(Utf8PathBuf, String)> {\n    if let Some(import_ref) = ctx.import_map.find_import(consuming_file, name) {\n        let resolved_file = resolve_import_specifier(&import_ref.specifier, consuming_file, ctx, diagnostics)?;\n        let canonical_name = import_ref.exported_name.to_string();\n        let mut visited = FxHashSet::default();\n        return Some(follow_reexports(resolved_file, canonical_name, ctx, diagnostics, &mut visited, 0));\n    }\n\n    // Namespace-import member access: `import * as React from \"react\"` then a\n    // reference to `React.DependencyList`. `find_import` only tracks the\n    // namespace binding itself (\"React\", with `exported_name == \"*\"`) — a\n    // literal dotted name like \"React.DependencyList\" is never itself a\n    // binding, so the lookup above always misses it. Split off the namespace\n    // prefix and route the member name through the namespace's own import\n    // specifier instead.\n    let (namespace, member) = name.split_once('.')?;\n    let namespace_ref = ctx.import_map.find_import(consuming_file, namespace)?;\n    if namespace_ref.exported_name != \"*\" {\n        return None;\n    }\n    let resolved_file = resolve_import_specifier(&namespace_ref.specifier, consuming_file, ctx, diagnostics)?;\n    let mut visited = FxHashSet::default();\n    Some(follow_reexports(resolved_file, member.to_string(), ctx, diagnostics, &mut visited, 0))\n}\n\n/// A directly-imported name may land on a barrel file (`export { X } from\n/// './x'` or `export * from './x'`) that doesn't declare `name` itself —\n/// ubiquitous in real component libraries' `index.ts` files. Follow the\n/// re-export chain until we reach a file that actually declares `name`, or\n/// run out of chain to follow — in which case the original (barrel_file,\n/// name) is returned unchanged, so the caller's existing \"cannot resolve\"\n/// diagnostic still fires exactly as it did before this existed.\nfn follow_reexports(\n    file: Utf8PathBuf,\n    name: String,\n    ctx: &ResolutionContext,\n    diagnostics: &mut Vec<Diagnostic>,\n    visited: &mut FxHashSet<(Utf8PathBuf, CompactString)>,\n    depth: u8,\n) -> (Utf8PathBuf, String) {\n    if depth >= MAX_REEXPORT_DEPTH || is_declared_at(&ctx.global, &file, &name) {\n        return (file, name);\n    }\n    // Real barrels commonly share descendants (several sub-barrels wildcarding\n    // the same underlying `types.ts`, say) — without this, re-exploring an\n    // already-visited (file, name) pair from a different parent multiplies out\n    // to branching_factor^depth calls instead of one call per graph node. This\n    // also subsumes cycle detection: a cycle revisits a pair by definition.\n    if !visited.insert((file.clone(), CompactString::from(name.as_str()))) {\n        return (file, name);\n    }\n 