{"parentUuid":"de73d8f5-da56-45da-949c-e8008b6e1611","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdMmytckAyaSbkjebb9B7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M2ButDcintfwbMaWZJH4uX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(ci): fix moon affected-detection — it never actually ran, plus a gating hole it was masking\n\nAdversarial review (Opus 5 + Fable 5) caught that moon 2.3.3's `query\nprojects` has no --base/--head flags at all (confirmed against its own\n--help). The literal command in b06e303 failed immediately with a clap\nparse error, which both fail-open branches then caught — so every CI\nrun since that commit landed has silently taken the \"moon query failed\n— running everything\" path. The affected-detection feature never once\nengaged; it fails open by design, so nothing was WRONGLY skipped, but\nthe commit's stated benefit (skip untouched language groups) was dead\non arrival.\n\nFixed by reading the base from MOON_BASE (moon's actual mechanism,\nverified empirically: same-commit base+head returns zero affected\nprojects on a clean tree, a dirty single-file edit attributes correctly\nto exactly the right project, and a real 34-commit range with genuine\nRust changes correctly flags both language groups). Also verified\nMOON_HEAD is silently ignored — moon always diffs against whatever's\ncurrently on disk, which is exactly github.sha here since\nactions/checkout already put us there, so there's nothing to fix about\nthat, just a misleading comment to correct.\n\nFixing #1 without a second change would have opened a real gating hole\nthat the dead detection was accidentally masking: the category-mapping\nloop had arms for core/cli/crates-binding (rust) and vite-plugin/napi\n(typescript) but nothing for `validate` (apps/validate) or\n`packages/cli` — the latter wasn't even registered as a moon project at\nall, despite being explicitly linted/formatted by the `format` job. A\nPR touching only apps/validate/src or packages/cli/bin/cli.js — the\nexact tree 31fd9f5 hand-edited for lint fixes — would have gotten zero\nCI coverage of the files it changed the moment detection started\nworking. Registered packages/cli as `cli-npm` in\n.moon/workspace.yml, mapped both to typescript, and added a catch-all\ndefault arm (fail open, not silently ungated) for any future project\nsomeone adds to workspace.yml and forgets to map here.\n\nAlso fixed .moon/workspace.yml's vcs.defaultBranch: master — no such\nref exists, this repo's default branch is main. Verified causal: `moon\nci core:build` (moon's own CI entry point) hard-fails resolving\n'master' as an unknown revision; the bare --affected form (used\nelsewhere) doesn't consult defaultBranch at all since it compares\nworking-tree status, so this was narrower than the review first\nsuggested, but real for anything that does use it.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10\ngit log --oneline -2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":178,"cache_read_input_tokens":932581,"output_tokens":1059,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":178},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1059,"cache_read_input_tokens":932581,"cache_creation_input_tokens":178,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":178,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdMmymoipiteBvscHRKGJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"66482113-9fcb-448c-9bc8-04d179d4043a","timestamp":"2026-07-24T23:48:30.305Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli