{"parentUuid":"d2d166d2-a82b-4153-ab76-b83270e342ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPGUJUExm2cvXhb2ULjP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NwwMqVZX2rHcXRxbqHDBx6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, glob, os\n\nmd_files = []\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    dirs[:] = [d for d in dirs if d not in ('node_modules', 'target', '.git', 'dist')]\n    for f in files:\n        if f.endswith('.md'):\n            md_files.append(os.path.join(root, f))\n\ndef check_file(path):\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8', errors='replace') as fh:\n        lines = fh.read().split('\\n')\n    in_code = False\n    para = []\n    flagged = []\n    def flush():\n        if len(para) > 1:\n            # ignore blocks that are lists/tables/headings (each line starts with -,*,|,#,>,digit.)\n            markers = ('-', '*', '|', '>', '#')\n            is_list_like = all(l.lstrip().startswith(markers) or re.match(r'^\\d+\\.', l.lstrip()) for l in para if l.strip())\n            if not is_list_like:\n                flagged.append(list(para))\n        para.clear()\n    for line in lines:\n        stripped = line.strip()\n        if stripped.startswith('```') or stripped.startswith('~~~'):\n            in_code = not in_code\n            flush()\n            continue\n        if in_code:\n            continue\n        if stripped == '':\n            flush()\n            continue\n        para.append(line)\n    flush()\n    return flagged\n\nfor path in sorted(md_files):\n    flagged = check_file(path)\n    if flagged:\n        print(f\"=== {path} ({len(flagged)} wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\")\n        for block in flagged[:2]:\n            for l in block:\n                print(\"   \", l[:100])\n            print(\"   ...\")\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":580,"cache_read_input_tokens":168783,"output_tokens":1174,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":580,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1174,"cache_read_input_tokens":168783,"cache_creation_input_tokens":580,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":580},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPGUH3AVEHr6YFRw8tBg","type":"assistant","uuid":"8b53835d-438f-43d7-a58c-522fe5844900","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:42:38.461Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"8b53835d-438f-43d7-a58c-522fe5844900","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3129edff-280e-4bc2-ac9a-02718d779751","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NwwMqVZX2rHcXRxbqHDBx6","type":"tool_result","content":"=== ./.claude/skills/adr/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: adr\n    description: Apply when an architectural decision was just made — one shaping system structure, boun\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./.claude/skills/rust-style/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: rust-style\n    description: Apply when writing or modifying Rust code in this project.\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./.claude/skills/rust-types/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: rust-types\n    description: Apply when defining new public structs or enums.\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./.claude/skills/rustdoc/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: rustdoc\n    description: Apply when writing doc comments on public Rust items.\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./ARCHITECTURE.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Created fresh for each `resolve_component()` call. Holds:\n    - Visited-type set for cycle detection (`FxHashSet<CompactString>`)\n    - Current recursion depth\n    - Accumulated diagnostics\n   ...\n=== ./README.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    The CLI is a single Rust binary (`crates/cli`) — argument parsing, output formatting, and\n    `--format rdt`/`--format storybook` serialization all live there and nowhere else.\n    `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` (once published) is a thin npm wrapper that just execs the platform-appropri\n   ...\n    [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — setup, code style, commit conventions.  \n    [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) — pipeline, modules, key design decisions.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/00-MASTER-PLAN.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    A Rust-powered React prop extraction tool that replaces `react-docgen-typescript`.\n    - **10-100x faster** via OXC (no TypeScript compiler program)\n    - **Cross-package monorepo support** via import graph + .d.ts parsing\n    - **Drop-in RDT output** for existing Storybook setups\n    - **World-class CLI** with miette diagnostics\n    - **Vite plugin** — primary delivery mechanism\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/01-PHASE0-REPO-SETUP.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Bootstrap the complete repository skeleton. No logic, no algorithms — just structure,\n    tooling, and the workspace Cargo.toml so every subsequent agent has a stable foundation.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/02-PHASE1A-TYPES.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Define every data type shared across the system. This is the contract every\n    other agent depends on. Correctness and completeness here is more important\n    than anything else. No logic — only type definitions.\n   ...\n    All path operations use `camino::{Utf8Path, Utf8PathBuf}` — never `std::path::Path`.\n    This eliminates `.to_str().unwrap()` patterns throughout the codebase.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/03-PHASE2A-EXTRACTOR.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Walk OXC AST for a single file, collect everything into a `SourceData`.\n    This is the most complex Rust code in the project.\n    Zero cross-file dependencies — each call is completely independent.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/04-PHASE2B2C-3A3B.md (4 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Given a `GlobalSourceData`, build lookup structures that allow the resolver to\n    trace any type name → its canonical declaration file.\n    This is pure data transformation — no I/O.\n   ...\n    A single function that recognizes named generic type patterns and returns either\n    resolved props or a simplified PropType. No trait objects, no dynamic dispatch —\n    just a match arm.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/05-PHASE4-5-NAPI-CLI-PLUGINS.md (4 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Expose three functions to Node.js: extract(), extractFile(), closeSession().\n    Keep the boundary thin — JSON string across the NAPI boundary, not complex NAPI types.\n   ...\n    Simple, focused CLI. Four subcommands. Rich miette diagnostics.\n    Clean summary output. No TUI.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/06-SERIALIZERS-TESTS-GOTCHAS.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    All three formats are produced from the same `ExtractionOutput`.\n    No separate extraction — just different views.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/07-AGENT-DISPATCH.md (18 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    9 Claude Code sessions in total, across 6 phases.\n    Each session gets: its briefing document + the master plan + types.rs (after Phase 1a).\n   ...\n    Prompt to Claude Code:\n    > \"Set up the oxc-react-docgen repository according to the attached plan.\n    > Create all workspace files, stub source files, CI workflow, and fixture directory structure.\n    > Run `cargo build` and `cargo test` to verify everything compiles before finishing.\n    > Do not implement any logic — only structure, Cargo.toml files, and empty stubs.\"\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/08-OPEN-QUESTIONS.md (17 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Tracks gaps in the phase specs, decisions needed before implementation, and\n    accuracy/DX concerns to carry forward into each phase.\n   ...\n    Follows `vite.config.ts` / `eslint.config.js` convention. Short, obvious in\n    context, no collision risk. Config shape mirrors `PipelineOptions` + a\n    `propFilter` function.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/10-PLUGIN-SPEC.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    `packages/vite-plugin/tests/unit/`  \n    `vi.mock('@oxc-react-docgen/napi', factory)` — mock all NAPI calls.  \n    Test each hook's logic in isolation by calling `plugin.hotUpdate.call(thisCtx, opts)` directly.  \n    `pool: 'threads'` (safe — no native binary loaded).\n   ...\n    `packages/vite-plugin/tests/integration/`  \n    `createServer({ configFile: false, middlewareMode: true, plugins: [oxcReactDocgen(...)] })`  \n    Gate with `NAPI_BINARY_AVAILABLE` env var.  \n    `pool: 'forks'` (required — native `.node` binary cannot load in worker threads).\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/10-QUALITY-AND-ARCHITECTURE.md (11 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ### R1 — Add snapshot tests (before touching anything)\n    Add `insta` snapshot tests for every fixture's extraction output. These are the safety net for the e\n   ...\n    ### R2 — `types/` split\n    Split `types.rs` into `types/collected.rs`, `types/output.rs`, `types/diagnostic.rs`, `types/global.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/2026-06-25-phase6-integration-tests.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Add two scripts:\n    - `run:ours` — for manual one-off runs (outputs JSON to stdout)\n    - `compare:all` — for the moon task: runs baseline + compare in sequence\n   ...\n    Expected flow:\n    1. Moon runs `cli:build` (cargo build, ~1s if cached)\n    2. Moon runs `validate:compare` (generates baselines, prints diff)\n    3. Final lines show the SUMMARY block\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/2026-06-28-structural-gap-fixes.md (34 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Five gaps found in `docs/rdt-coverage.md` and `docs/type-checker-integration.md`.\n    These are NOT the deferred gaps (generics, conditionals, mapped types) — those require\n    the Corsa API (TypeScript 7.1, est. Q1 2027). These five are fixable today.\n   ...\n    Run tests with: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core`\n    Snapshot test specifically: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core --test snapshots`\n    Regenerate snapshots: `INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core --test snapshots`\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/2026-07-07-adversarial-analysis-fixes.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n      In `config.rs`, at the point where `try_load_config` currently returns `None` after successfully p\n      - No `docgen.config.ts` found at all → current default behavior, fine, no error.\n      - A `docgen.config.ts` IS found (and successfully executes/parses) → since schema mapping to `Pipe\n   ...\n      For Step 1: run the full snapshot suite, update snapshots if the `[ROOT]` redaction needs adjustin\n      For Steps 2-3: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` should show no new warnings\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/adversarial-analysis-2026-06-28.md (45 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Testing methodology: fresh `react-docgen-typescript` baseline vs our tool across all fixture librari\n    prop-by-prop diff, plus adversarial code review of the resolver and extractor layers.\n   ...\n    Coverage on shared TSX fixtures (rdt-compat + shadcn): **Avatar: ✅ perfect match**. All others have\n    documented gaps. DTS fixtures (chakra, mantine, mui, radix, react-aria) cannot be compared to RDT\n    because RDT requires real TypeScript source, not declaration files.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/type-checker-integration.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    The OXC team already tackled cross-language integration with `tsgolint`:\n    - Spawns `tsgo` as a subprocess\n    - Communicates via JSON IPC using tsgo's internal (unstable) shims\n    - This pattern works but depends on internal APIs that will break when Corsa lands\n   ...","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"062e33d8-6ea0-4082-b649-efc2e79ca7a0","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:42:40.597Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== ./.claude/skills/adr/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: adr\n    description: Apply when an architectural decision was just made — one shaping system structure, boun\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./.claude/skills/rust-style/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: rust-style\n    description: Apply when writing or modifying Rust code in this project.\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./.claude/skills/rust-types/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: rust-types\n    description: Apply when defining new public structs or enums.\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./.claude/skills/rustdoc/SKILL.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ---\n    name: rustdoc\n    description: Apply when writing doc comments on public Rust items.\n    ---\n   ...\n=== ./ARCHITECTURE.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Created fresh for each `resolve_component()` call. Holds:\n    - Visited-type set for cycle detection (`FxHashSet<CompactString>`)\n    - Current recursion depth\n    - Accumulated diagnostics\n   ...\n=== ./README.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    The CLI is a single Rust binary (`crates/cli`) — argument parsing, output formatting, and\n    `--format rdt`/`--format storybook` serialization all live there and nowhere else.\n    `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` (once published) is a thin npm wrapper that just execs the platform-appropri\n   ...\n    [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — setup, code style, commit conventions.  \n    [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) — pipeline, modules, key design decisions.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/00-MASTER-PLAN.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    A Rust-powered React prop extraction tool that replaces `react-docgen-typescript`.\n    - **10-100x faster** via OXC (no TypeScript compiler program)\n    - **Cross-package monorepo support** via import graph + .d.ts parsing\n    - **Drop-in RDT output** for existing Storybook setups\n    - **World-class CLI** with miette diagnostics\n    - **Vite plugin** — primary delivery mechanism\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/01-PHASE0-REPO-SETUP.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Bootstrap the complete repository skeleton. No logic, no algorithms — just structure,\n    tooling, and the workspace Cargo.toml so every subsequent agent has a stable foundation.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/02-PHASE1A-TYPES.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Define every data type shared across the system. This is the contract every\n    other agent depends on. Correctness and completeness here is more important\n    than anything else. No logic — only type definitions.\n   ...\n    All path operations use `camino::{Utf8Path, Utf8PathBuf}` — never `std::path::Path`.\n    This eliminates `.to_str().unwrap()` patterns throughout the codebase.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/03-PHASE2A-EXTRACTOR.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Walk OXC AST for a single file, collect everything into a `SourceData`.\n    This is the most complex Rust code in the project.\n    Zero cross-file dependencies — each call is completely independent.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/04-PHASE2B2C-3A3B.md (4 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Given a `GlobalSourceData`, build lookup structures that allow the resolver to\n    trace any type name → its canonical declaration file.\n    This is pure data transformation — no I/O.\n   ...\n    A single function that recognizes named generic type patterns and returns either\n    resolved props or a simplified PropType. No trait objects, no dynamic dispatch —\n    just a match arm.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/05-PHASE4-5-NAPI-CLI-PLUGINS.md (4 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Expose three functions to Node.js: extract(), extractFile(), closeSession().\n    Keep the boundary thin — JSON string across the NAPI boundary, not complex NAPI types.\n   ...\n    Simple, focused CLI. Four subcommands. Rich miette diagnostics.\n    Clean summary output. No TUI.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/06-SERIALIZERS-TESTS-GOTCHAS.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    All three formats are produced from the same `ExtractionOutput`.\n    No separate extraction — just different views.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/07-AGENT-DISPATCH.md (18 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    9 Claude Code sessions in total, across 6 phases.\n    Each session gets: its briefing document + the master plan + types.rs (after Phase 1a).\n   ...\n    Prompt to Claude Code:\n    > \"Set up the oxc-react-docgen repository according to the attached plan.\n    > Create all workspace files, stub source files, CI workflow, and fixture directory structure.\n    > Run `cargo build` and `cargo test` to verify everything compiles before finishing.\n    > Do not implement any logic — only structure, Cargo.toml files, and empty stubs.\"\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/08-OPEN-QUESTIONS.md (17 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Tracks gaps in the phase specs, decisions needed before implementation, and\n    accuracy/DX concerns to carry forward into each phase.\n   ...\n    Follows `vite.config.ts` / `eslint.config.js` convention. Short, obvious in\n    context, no collision risk. Config shape mirrors `PipelineOptions` + a\n    `propFilter` function.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/10-PLUGIN-SPEC.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    `packages/vite-plugin/tests/unit/`  \n    `vi.mock('@oxc-react-docgen/napi', factory)` — mock all NAPI calls.  \n    Test each hook's logic in isolation by calling `plugin.hotUpdate.call(thisCtx, opts)` directly.  \n    `pool: 'threads'` (safe — no native binary loaded).\n   ...\n    `packages/vite-plugin/tests/integration/`  \n    `createServer({ configFile: false, middlewareMode: true, plugins: [oxcReactDocgen(...)] })`  \n    Gate with `NAPI_BINARY_AVAILABLE` env var.  \n    `pool: 'forks'` (required — native `.node` binary cannot load in worker threads).\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/10-QUALITY-AND-ARCHITECTURE.md (11 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    ### R1 — Add snapshot tests (before touching anything)\n    Add `insta` snapshot tests for every fixture's extraction output. These are the safety net for the e\n   ...\n    ### R2 — `types/` split\n    Split `types.rs` into `types/collected.rs`, `types/output.rs`, `types/diagnostic.rs`, `types/global.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/2026-06-25-phase6-integration-tests.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Add two scripts:\n    - `run:ours` — for manual one-off runs (outputs JSON to stdout)\n    - `compare:all` — for the moon task: runs baseline + compare in sequence\n   ...\n    Expected flow:\n    1. Moon runs `cli:build` (cargo build, ~1s if cached)\n    2. Moon runs `validate:compare` (generates baselines, prints diff)\n    3. Final lines show the SUMMARY block\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/2026-06-28-structural-gap-fixes.md (34 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Five gaps found in `docs/rdt-coverage.md` and `docs/type-checker-integration.md`.\n    These are NOT the deferred gaps (generics, conditionals, mapped types) — those require\n    the Corsa API (TypeScript 7.1, est. Q1 2027). These five are fixable today.\n   ...\n    Run tests with: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core`\n    Snapshot test specifically: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core --test snapshots`\n    Regenerate snapshots: `INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core --test snapshots`\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/2026-07-07-adversarial-analysis-fixes.md (2 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n      In `config.rs`, at the point where `try_load_config` currently returns `None` after successfully p\n      - No `docgen.config.ts` found at all → current default behavior, fine, no error.\n      - A `docgen.config.ts` IS found (and successfully executes/parses) → since schema mapping to `Pipe\n   ...\n      For Step 1: run the full snapshot suite, update snapshots if the `[ROOT]` redaction needs adjustin\n      For Steps 2-3: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` should show no new warnings\n   ...\n=== ./docs/archive/adversarial-analysis-2026-06-28.md (45 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    Testing methodology: fresh `react-docgen-typescript` baseline vs our tool across all fixture librari\n    prop-by-prop diff, plus adversarial code review of the resolver and extractor layers.\n   ...\n    Coverage on shared TSX fixtures (rdt-compat + shadcn): **Avatar: ✅ perfect match**. All others have\n    documented gaps. DTS fixtures (chakra, mantine, mui, radix, react-aria) cannot be compared to RDT\n    because RDT requires real TypeScript source, not declaration files.\n   ...\n=== ./docs/type-checker-integration.md (1 wrapped paragraph(s)) ===\n    The OXC team already tackled cross-language integration with `tsgolint`:\n    - Spawns `tsgo` as a subprocess\n    - Communicates via JSON IPC using tsgo's internal (unstable) shims\n    - This pattern works but depends on internal APIs that will break when Corsa lands\n   ..."