{"parentUuid":"61ff90fa-0caf-49f7-9172-da0ea5600d69","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPGVMT6tbv8PmT9CjN4e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let's separate real hard-wrapping from false positives (frontmatter blocks, intro+list combos, intentional trailing-space line breaks). Checking the live docs first — README.md and ARCHITECTURE.md."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5073,"cache_read_input_tokens":169363,"output_tokens":1064,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5073,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":169363,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5073},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPGVKjfb2WGUyx1rMncz","type":"assistant","uuid":"496993ec-beec-4379-b657-4615415da834","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:42:53.549Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"496993ec-beec-4379-b657-4615415da834","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPGVMT6tbv8PmT9CjN4e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G37Ru9BAtDELTqH9PcB76q","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5073,"cache_read_input_tokens":169363,"output_tokens":1064,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5073,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":169363,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5073},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPGVKjfb2WGUyx1rMncz","type":"assistant","uuid":"94d6d217-2afa-4b86-ad4d-6d1003f4f594","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:42:53.971Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"94d6d217-2afa-4b86-ad4d-6d1003f4f594","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3129edff-280e-4bc2-ac9a-02718d779751","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G37Ru9BAtDELTqH9PcB76q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# oxc-react-docgen\n2\t\n3\tReact component prop extraction powered by [OXC](https://oxc.rs). Parses TypeScript natively in Rust — no TypeScript compiler program, no type-checking pass, no startup tax.\n4\t\n5\t> **Status:** Core extraction, NAPI bindings, Vite plugin, CLI, and `docgen.config.ts` loading are complete.\n6\t\n7\t## Why\n8\t\n9\t`react-docgen-typescript` spins up a full TypeScript `Program` to extract props. On a mid-size design system this takes seconds — enough to noticeably delay Storybook startup and make HMR feel sluggish. OXC parses each file in parallel with no type-checking pass, so cold extraction on a 15-component fixture set (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, Radix) takes **32ms**.\n10\t\n11\tThe CLI can emit an RDT-compatible shape via `--format rdt` (see [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md)). The Vite plugin and NAPI binding currently expose this tool's own canonical format only — not a drop-in RDT replacement at that layer yet.\n12\t\n13\t## Install\n14\t\n15\t`@oxc-react-docgen/napi`, `@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin`, and `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` are not yet published to npm — there are no per-platform prebuilt binaries to install today. Until a release ships:\n16\t\n17\t```bash\n18\tgit clone https://github.com/orin-dx/oxc-react-docgen\n19\tcd oxc-react-docgen\n20\tpnpm install\n21\tpnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/napi run build:napi   # builds the native addon for your platform\n22\tpnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin build\n23\t```\n24\t\n25\t`pnpm run build:napi` (not a bare `cargo build`) matters: it invokes `napi build`, which places the compiled addon exactly where `packages/napi/index.js`'s generated loader expects it. This works as a monorepo-local dependency today; there are no published per-platform packages for it to fall back to yet. See [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md) if you're moving off `react-docgen-typescript` and want to know exactly what's compatible today.\n26\t\n27\t## Vite plugin\n28\t\n29\t```ts\n30\t// vite.config.ts\n31\timport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n32\timport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\n33\timport { oxcReactDocgen } from '@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin'\n34\t\n35\texport default defineConfig({\n36\t  plugins: [\n37\t    react(),\n38\t    oxcReactDocgen({ srcDirs: ['src'] }),\n39\t  ],\n40\t})\n41\t```\n42\t\n43\tMetadata is available on the `virtual:oxc-react-docgen` module and pushed via HMR as components change:\n44\t\n45\t```ts\n46\timport docgen from 'virtual:oxc-react-docgen'\n47\t\n48\tdocgen.components['Button'].props\n49\t// {\n50\t//   variant: {\n51\t//     type: { kind: 'literalUnion', members: ['default', 'destructive', 'outline'], hasDefault: true },\n52\t//     required: false,\n53\t//     defaultValue: { value: '\"default\"', computed: false },\n54\t//     description: '',\n55\t//   },\n56\t//   ...\n57\t// }\n58\t```\n59\t\n60\t## CLI\n61\t\n62\tThe CLI is a single Rust binary (`crates/cli`) — argument parsing, output formatting, and\n63\t`--format rdt`/`--format storybook` serialization all live there and nowhere else.\n64\t`@oxc-react-docgen/cli` (once published) is a thin npm wrapper that just execs the platform-appropriate compiled binary; it deliberately contains no reimplementation of CLI behavior, so there's exactly one place that behavior can drift.\n65\t\n66\t```bash\n67\t# Once published: npx @oxc-react-docgen/cli extract --src src/ --out docgen.json\n68\t# From source today: ./target/release/oxc-react-docgen (after cargo build --release)\n69\t\n70\t# One-shot extraction\n71\toxc-react-docgen extract --src src/ --out docgen.json\n72\t\n73\t# Inspect a single file\n74\toxc-react-docgen inspect src/components/Button.tsx\n75\t\n76\t# Watch mode\n77\toxc-react-docgen watch --src src/\n78\t\n79\t# Shell completions\n80\toxc-react-docgen completions zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_oxc-react-docgen\n81\t\n82\t# Full HTML attribute expansion instead of the default curated subset\n83\toxc-react-docgen extract --src src/ --html-attributes full\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\tSettings can also live in `docgen.config.ts` (`srcDirs`, `htmlAttributes`, `reactVersion`, `crossPackage`, and more — see `crates/cli/src/config.rs` for the full schema) instead of CLI flags.\n87\t\n88\t## Output shape\n89\t\n90\t```json\n91\t{\n92\t  \"components\": {\n93\t    \"Button\": {\n94\t      \"displayName\": \"Button\",\n95\t      \"filePath\": \"src/components/Button.tsx\",\n96\t      \"props\": {\n97\t        \"variant\": {\n98\t          \"type\": { \"kind\": \"literalUnion\", \"members\": [\"default\", \"destructive\", \"outline\"], \"hasDefault\": true },\n99\t          \"required\": false,\n100\t          \"defaultValue\": { \"value\": \"\\\"default\\\"\", \"computed\": false },\n101\t          \"description\": \"Visual style variant.\",\n102\t          \"tags\": {}\n103\t        }\n104\t      },\n105\t      \"inheritance\": [\n106\t        { \"typeName\": \"ButtonHTMLAttributes\", \"htmlElement\": \"button\", \"omitted\": [], \"totalProps\": 147 }\n107\t      ],\n108\t      \"notableInherited\": {\n109\t        \"onClick\": { \"type\": { \"kind\": \"eventHandler\", \"eventType\": \"MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>\" }, ... },\n110\t        \"disabled\": { \"type\": { \"kind\": \"boolean\" }, ... }\n111\t      },\n112\t      \"discriminantProp\": null\n113\t    }\n114\t  },\n115\t  \"diagnostics\": [],\n116\t  \"stats\": { \"filesParsed\": 3, \"durationMs\": 12, \"dtsCacheHits\": 2, ... }\n117\t}\n118\t```\n119\t\n120\t## Supported patterns\n121\t\n122\t| Pattern | Example |\n123\t|---------|---------|\n124\t| Function components | `function Button(props: ButtonProps)` |\n125\t| Arrow components | `const Button = (props: ButtonProps) => ...` |\n126\t| `React.forwardRef` | `forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(...)` |\n127\t| HOC-wrapped | `styled(Base)<ButtonProps>` |\n128\t| Interface inheritance | `interface ButtonProps extends HTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>` |\n129\t| Intersection aliases | `type ButtonProps = BaseProps & { variant?: string }` |\n130\t| `Omit` / `Pick` | `type ButtonProps = Omit<InputProps, 'value'>` |\n131\t| `ComponentPropsWithoutRef` | `ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>` |\n132\t| `VariantProps` | `VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants>` (CVA / TV / PandaCSS) |\n133\t| Discriminated unions | MUI-style `variant: 'filled' \\| 'outlined' \\| 'standard'` |\n134\t| JSDoc tags | `@description`, `@default`, `@deprecated`, `@internal` |\n135\t\n136\t## Repository\n137\t\n138\t```\n139\tcrates/core/          pure extraction logic (no I/O, no async, Send + Sync)\n140\tcrates/binding/       thin NAPI wrapper over core\n141\tcrates/cli/           clap + miette CLI\n142\tpackages/napi/        @oxc-react-docgen/napi (dev binary loader + TS types)\n143\tpackages/vite-plugin/ @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin\n144\tpackages/cli/         @oxc-react-docgen/cli (npx wrapper — execs crates/cli's binary, no reimplemented logic)\n145\tapps/validate/        accuracy comparison harness (react-docgen, rdt, ours)\n146\tfixtures/             real library .d.ts/.tsx files (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, etc.)\n147\t```\n148\t\n149\t## Contributing\n150\t\n151\t[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — setup, code style, commit conventions.  \n152\t[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) — pipeline, modules, key design decisions.\n153\t\n154\t## License\n155\t\n156\tAGPL-3.0-or-later — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\n157\t"}]},"uuid":"804fe1fd-959e-460a-a7d6-185ff5a74433","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:42:54.056Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/README.md","content":"# oxc-react-docgen\n\nReact component prop extraction powered by [OXC](https://oxc.rs). Parses TypeScript natively in Rust — no TypeScript compiler program, no type-checking pass, no startup tax.\n\n> **Status:** Core extraction, NAPI bindings, Vite plugin, CLI, and `docgen.config.ts` loading are complete.\n\n## Why\n\n`react-docgen-typescript` spins up a full TypeScript `Program` to extract props. On a mid-size design system this takes seconds — enough to noticeably delay Storybook startup and make HMR feel sluggish. OXC parses each file in parallel with no type-checking pass, so cold extraction on a 15-component fixture set (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, Radix) takes **32ms**.\n\nThe CLI can emit an RDT-compatible shape via `--format rdt` (see [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md)). The Vite plugin and NAPI binding currently expose this tool's own canonical format only — not a drop-in RDT replacement at that layer yet.\n\n## Install\n\n`@oxc-react-docgen/napi`, `@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin`, and `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` are not yet published to npm — there are no per-platform prebuilt binaries to install today. Until a release ships:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/orin-dx/oxc-react-docgen\ncd oxc-react-docgen\npnpm install\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/napi run build:napi   # builds the native addon for your platform\npnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin build\n```\n\n`pnpm run build:napi` (not a bare `cargo build`) matters: it invokes `napi build`, which places the compiled addon exactly where `packages/napi/index.js`'s generated loader expects it. This works as a monorepo-local dependency today; there are no published per-platform packages for it to fall back to yet. See [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md) if you're moving off `react-docgen-typescript` and want to know exactly what's compatible today.\n\n## Vite plugin\n\n```ts\n// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { oxcReactDocgen } from '@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    react(),\n    oxcReactDocgen({ srcDirs: ['src'] }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nMetadata is available on the `virtual:oxc-react-docgen` module and pushed via HMR as components change:\n\n```ts\nimport docgen from 'virtual:oxc-react-docgen'\n\ndocgen.components['Button'].props\n// {\n//   variant: {\n//     type: { kind: 'literalUnion', members: ['default', 'destructive', 'outline'], hasDefault: true },\n//     required: false,\n//     defaultValue: { value: '\"default\"', computed: false },\n//     description: '',\n//   },\n//   ...\n// }\n```\n\n## CLI\n\nThe CLI is a single Rust binary (`crates/cli`) — argument parsing, output formatting, and\n`--format rdt`/`--format storybook` serialization all live there and nowhere else.\n`@oxc-react-docgen/cli` (once published) is a thin npm wrapper that just execs the platform-appropriate compiled binary; it deliberately contains no reimplementation of CLI behavior, so there's exactly one place that behavior can drift.\n\n```bash\n# Once published: npx @oxc-react-docgen/cli extract --src src/ --out docgen.json\n# From source today: ./target/release/oxc-react-docgen (after cargo build --release)\n\n# One-shot extraction\noxc-react-docgen extract --src src/ --out docgen.json\n\n# Inspect a single file\noxc-react-docgen inspect src/components/Button.tsx\n\n# Watch mode\noxc-react-docgen watch --src src/\n\n# Shell completions\noxc-react-docgen completions zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_oxc-react-docgen\n\n# Full HTML attribute expansion instead of the default curated subset\noxc-react-docgen extract --src src/ --html-attributes full\n```\n\nSettings can also live in `docgen.config.ts` (`srcDirs`, `htmlAttributes`, `reactVersion`, `crossPackage`, and more — see `crates/cli/src/config.rs` for the full schema) instead of CLI flags.\n\n## Output shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"components\": {\n    \"Button\": {\n      \"displayName\": \"Button\",\n      \"filePath\": \"src/components/Button.tsx\",\n      \"props\": {\n        \"variant\": {\n          \"type\": { \"kind\": \"literalUnion\", \"members\": [\"default\", \"destructive\", \"outline\"], \"hasDefault\": true },\n          \"required\": false,\n          \"defaultValue\": { \"value\": \"\\\"default\\\"\", \"computed\": false },\n          \"description\": \"Visual style variant.\",\n          \"tags\": {}\n        }\n      },\n      \"inheritance\": [\n        { \"typeName\": \"ButtonHTMLAttributes\", \"htmlElement\": \"button\", \"omitted\": [], \"totalProps\": 147 }\n      ],\n      \"notableInherited\": {\n        \"onClick\": { \"type\": { \"kind\": \"eventHandler\", \"eventType\": \"MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>\" }, ... },\n        \"disabled\": { \"type\": { \"kind\": \"boolean\" }, ... }\n      },\n      \"discriminantProp\": null\n    }\n  },\n  \"diagnostics\": [],\n  \"stats\": { \"filesParsed\": 3, \"durationMs\": 12, \"dtsCacheHits\": 2, ... }\n}\n```\n\n## Supported patterns\n\n| Pattern | Example |\n|---------|---------|\n| Function components | `function Button(props: ButtonProps)` |\n| Arrow components | `const Button = (props: ButtonProps) => ...` |\n| `React.forwardRef` | `forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(...)` |\n| HOC-wrapped | `styled(Base)<ButtonProps>` |\n| Interface inheritance | `interface ButtonProps extends HTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>` |\n| Intersection aliases | `type ButtonProps = BaseProps & { variant?: string }` |\n| `Omit` / `Pick` | `type ButtonProps = Omit<InputProps, 'value'>` |\n| `ComponentPropsWithoutRef` | `ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>` |\n| `VariantProps` | `VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants>` (CVA / TV / PandaCSS) |\n| Discriminated unions | MUI-style `variant: 'filled' \\| 'outlined' \\| 'standard'` |\n| JSDoc tags | `@description`, `@default`, `@deprecated`, `@internal` |\n\n## Repository\n\n```\ncrates/core/          pure extraction logic (no I/O, no async, Send + Sync)\ncrates/binding/       thin NAPI wrapper over core\ncrates/cli/           clap + miette CLI\npackages/napi/        @oxc-react-docgen/napi (dev binary loader + TS types)\npackages/vite-plugin/ @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin\npackages/cli/         @oxc-react-docgen/cli (npx wrapper — execs crates/cli's binary, no reimplemented logic)\napps/validate/        accuracy comparison harness (react-docgen, rdt, ours)\nfixtures/             real library .d.ts/.tsx files (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, etc.)\n```\n\n## Contributing\n\n[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — setup, code style, commit conventions.  \n[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) — pipeline, modules, key design decisions.\n\n## License\n\nAGPL-3.0-or-later — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).\n","numLines":157,"startLine":1,"totalLines":157}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"94d6d217-2afa-4b86-ad4d-6d1003f4f594","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
