ory/peak RSS","description":"Also track peak memory during extraction, relevant for large monorepos but harder to measure fairly across three different language runtimes"}],"multiSelect":false},{"question":"\"Quality of output\" needs a concrete measurement, not just prose. What should be the primary metric?","header":"Quality metric","options":[{"label":"Prop-level agreement rate vs RDT (Recommended)","description":"For each fixture where RDT can run at all: % of props where name/type/required/default all match RDT exactly — apps/validate's compare:all harness already computes something close to this"},{"label":"Agreement rate + a taxonomy of divergences","description":"Same metric, plus every mismatch bucketed into categories (e.g. \"union discriminant not detected\", \"generic arg dropped\") so the shortcomings section is backed by counted evidence, not anecdotes"}],"multiSelect":false}],"answers":{"Where should the benchmark results live and how should they be delivered?":"docs/benchmarks.md (Recommended)","What should count as \"performance,\" concretely?":"Cold + incremental/watch-mode latency","\"Quality of output\" needs a concrete measurement, not just prose. What should be the primary metric?":"Agreement rate + a taxonomy of divergences"},"annotations":{}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4cde4c60-92fa-4b64-b53a-5fe6edf0b116","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
