{"parentUuid":"4058f594-e70e-47ef-a7e4-efb2d6a375ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPHJ51CnhGGzYeVfJjTn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`virtual:` is Vite's naming convention for plugin-synthesized modules — ones that don't exist as real files on disk. Quick answer, then I'll get back to the benchmark work:\n\nIn `packages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts`, the plugin declares `VIRTUAL_ID = 'virtual:oxc-react-docgen'` and implements two Vite hooks:\n- `resolveId(id)` — when Vite asks \"can you resolve `virtual:oxc-react-docgen`?\", it returns an internal resolved id (`\\0virtual:oxc-react-docgen`)\n- `load(id)` — when Vite asks \"give me the content for that resolved id,\" it returns `export default ${JSON.stringify(currentOutput)}` — the live extraction output, serialized on demand\n\nSo `import docgen from 'virtual:oxc-react-docgen'` never touches disk. The plugin intercepts that specifier and hands back freshly-computed JSON at request time (and pushes updates over HMR as files change — see the `hotUpdate` hook). The `\\0` prefix on the *resolved* id is a Rollup/Vite convention meaning \"this isn't a real file path, don't let other plugins or sourcemap tooling try to resolve it as one.\" The `virtual:` prefix on the user-facing specifier itself is just convention (other tools use it too, e.g. `virtual:pwa-register`) — it's not special to Vite's resolver, just a readability signal that this import doesn't correspond to a file.\n\nBack to the benchmark work now — fixing the `react-docgen` fixture-keying bug I found:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1154,"cache_read_input_tokens":244296,"output_tokens":1876,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1154,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1876,"cache_read_input_tokens":244296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1154},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPHJ3G2xazTCZkboSnyx","type":"assistant","uuid":"50f9b223-c7b4-4ee4-8616-c59488b94437","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:53:26.201Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"50f9b223-c7b4-4ee4-8616-c59488b94437","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPHJ51CnhGGzYeVfJjTn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WLdVoDjPTS5xspT25rQ6rF","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/apps/validate/src/run-react-docgen.ts","old_string":"for (const fixture of fixtures) {\n  const source = readFileSync(fixture.path, 'utf8')\n  const start = performance.now()\n  try {\n    const raw = parse(source, { filename: fixture.path })\n    const durationMs = performance.now() - start\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs,\n      output: normalize(Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [raw]),\n    })\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs: performance.now() - start,\n      output: {},\n      error: error.message,\n    })\n  }\n}","new_string":"for (const fixture of fixtures) {\n  const source = readFileSync(fixture.path, 'utf8')\n  const start = performance.now()\n  try {\n    const raw = parse(source, { filename: fixture.path })\n    const durationMs = performance.now() - start\n    const comps = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [raw]\n    // One entry per component, keyed `${fixture.name}/${displayName}` — matches\n    // rdt's and ours' keying. Previously this pushed one ToolResult per FILE\n    // (keyed by fixture.name alone, with every component packed into its\n    // `output`), which never joined against rdt/ours' per-component keys in\n    // compare.ts — a multi-component file silently broke the join for every\n    // component in it, and even single-component files only \"matched\" by\n    // accident of an exact string comparison that never actually held.\n    for (const comp of comps) {\n      const name = comp.displayName ?? 'Unknown'\n      results.push({\n        tool: 'react-docgen',\n        fixture: `${fixture.name}/${name}`,\n        durationMs,\n        output: normalize([comp]),\n      })\n    }\n    if (comps.length === 0) {\n      results.push({ tool: 'react-docgen', fixture: fixture.name, durationMs, output: {} })\n    }\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs: performance.now() - start,\n      output: {},\n      error: error.message,\n    })\n  }\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1154,"cache_read_input_tokens":244296,"output_tokens":1876,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1154,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1876,"cache_read_input_tokens":244296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1154},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPHJ3G2xazTCZkboSnyx","type":"assistant","uuid":"af348048-88a7-4f9b-bbe8-a0aa4a89a5f9","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:53:31.945Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"af348048-88a7-4f9b-bbe8-a0aa4a89a5f9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3129edff-280e-4bc2-ac9a-02718d779751","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WLdVoDjPTS5xspT25rQ6rF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/apps/validate/src/run-react-docgen.ts has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"c058ff90-b5f0-4632-9229-3066dc2074ed","timestamp":"2026-07-25T18:53:32.119Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/apps/validate/src/run-react-docgen.ts","oldString":"for (const fixture of fixtures) {\n  const source = readFileSync(fixture.path, 'utf8')\n  const start = performance.now()\n  try {\n    const raw = parse(source, { filename: fixture.path })\n    const durationMs = performance.now() - start\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs,\n      output: normalize(Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [raw]),\n    })\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs: performance.now() - start,\n      output: {},\n      error: error.message,\n    })\n  }\n}","newString":"for (const fixture of fixtures) {\n  const source = readFileSync(fixture.path, 'utf8')\n  const start = performance.now()\n  try {\n    const raw = parse(source, { filename: fixture.path })\n    const durationMs = performance.now() - start\n    const comps = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [raw]\n    // One entry per component, keyed `${fixture.name}/${displayName}` — matches\n    // rdt's and ours' keying. Previously this pushed one ToolResult per FILE\n    // (keyed by fixture.name alone, with every component packed into its\n    // `output`), which never joined against rdt/ours' per-component keys in\n    // compare.ts — a multi-component file silently broke the join for every\n    // component in it, and even single-component files only \"matched\" by\n    // accident of an exact string comparison that never actually held.\n    for (const comp of comps) {\n      const name = comp.displayName ?? 'Unknown'\n      results.push({\n        tool: 'react-docgen',\n        fixture: `${fixture.name}/${name}`,\n        durationMs,\n        output: normalize([comp]),\n      })\n    }\n    if (comps.length === 0) {\n      results.push({ tool: 'react-docgen', fixture: fixture.name, durationMs, output: {} })\n    }\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs: performance.now() - start,\n      output: {},\n      error: error.message,\n    })\n  }\n}","originalFile":"import { parse } from 'react-docgen'\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { discoverFixtures } from './fixtures.ts'\nimport type { ToolResult, NormalizedOutput } from './types.ts'\n\nfunction normalize(rdgOutput: any[]): NormalizedOutput {\n  const result: NormalizedOutput = {}\n  for (const comp of rdgOutput) {\n    const name = comp.displayName ?? 'Unknown'\n    result[name] = {\n      displayName: name,\n      description: comp.description ?? '',\n      props: Object.fromEntries(\n        Object.entries(comp.props ?? {}).map(([propName, prop]: [string, any]) => [\n          propName,\n          {\n            name: propName,\n            required: prop.required ?? false,\n            type: prop.type?.name ?? 'unknown',\n            description: prop.description ?? '',\n            defaultValue: prop.defaultValue?.value,\n          },\n        ]),\n      ),\n    }\n  }\n  return result\n}\n\nconst fixtures = discoverFixtures().filter((f) => f.isTsx)\nconst results: ToolResult[] = []\n\nfor (const fixture of fixtures) {\n  const source = readFileSync(fixture.path, 'utf8')\n  const start = performance.now()\n  try {\n    const raw = parse(source, { filename: fixture.path })\n    const durationMs = performance.now() - start\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs,\n      output: normalize(Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [raw]),\n    })\n  } catch (error: any) {\n    results.push({\n      tool: 'react-docgen',\n      fixture: fixture.name,\n      durationMs: performance.now() - start,\n      output: {},\n      error: error.message,\n    })\n  }\n}\n\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(results, null, 2))\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":36,"oldLines":12,"newStart":36,"newLines":26,"lines":["   try {","     const raw = parse(source, { filename: fixture.path })","     const durationMs = performance.now() - start","-    results.push({","-      tool: 'react-docgen',","-      fixture: fixture.name,","-      durationMs,","-      output: normalize(Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [raw]),","-    })","+    const comps = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : [raw]","+    // One entry per component, keyed `${fixture.name}/${displayName}` — matches","+    // rdt's and ours' keying. Previously this pushed one ToolResult per FILE","+    // (keyed by fixture.name alone, with every component packed into its","+    // `output`), which never joined against rdt/ours' per-component keys in","+    // compare.ts — a multi-component file silently broke the join for every","+    // component in it, and even single-component files only \"matched\" by","+    // accident of an exact string comparison that never actually held.","+    for (const comp of comps) {","+      const name = comp.displayName ?? 'Unknown'","+      results.push({","+        tool: 'react-docgen',","+        fixture: `${fixture.name}/${name}`,","+        durationMs,","+        output: normalize([comp]),","+      })","+    }","+    if (comps.length === 0) {","+      results.push({ tool: 'react-docgen', fixture: fixture.name, durationMs, output: {} })","+    }","   } catch (error: any) {","     results.push({","       tool: 'react-docgen',"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"af348048-88a7-4f9b-bbe