{"parentUuid":"cbd21fc3-7f31-400f-81cf-a23e94276cc4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPJ3EmXhRJ5bzY992eoi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":292284,"output_tokens":1886,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1886,"cache_read_input_tokens":292284,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPJ3BRcevrZkpEv1JxVv","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb5d35c9-04c3-432b-b89b-bbe3c390c6ef","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:03:18.631Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/apps/validate","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"eb5d35c9-04c3-432b-b89b-bbe3c390c6ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPJ3EmXhRJ5bzY992eoi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good question — let me lay out the landscape, then decide what to actually use here.\n\n**Rust micro-benchmarking crates:**\n- **`criterion`** — the de facto standard. Statistical rigor (outlier detection, confidence intervals), warm-up handling, and critically: persists historical runs under `target/criterion/` so `cargo bench` reports **regression/improvement vs. the last run**, plus an HTML report. This is what \"not hand-waving\" usually means in the Rust ecosystem.\n- **`divan`** (what this repo already uses) — newer, simpler macro API, faster to write. But no persisted history, no regression detection, no HTML report — just stdout numbers each run. Fine for a quick check, weaker for a claim you want to defend.\n- **`iai-callgrind`** — instruction-count based (via Valgrind), deterministic (zero run-to-run noise, no need for multiple samples), excellent for CI regression gates. Linux-only, and instruction count isn't the same thing as wall-clock/cache-effects, so it answers a narrower question.\n\n**For cross-process / cross-tool CLI comparisons** (which is what our cold-start problem actually is — comparing three separate binaries/runtimes, not three Rust functions): **`hyperfine`** is the standard tool, not a Rust benchmarking crate you `cargo add` — it's a CLI (written in Rust) that wraps arbitrary shell commands with proper warm-up runs, statistical analysis, outlier warnings, and can export directly to Markdown/JSON/CSV. My hand-rolled `bench-cold.ts` timing loop is exactly reinventing what hyperfine already does correctly."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":292284,"output_tokens":1886,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1886,"cache_read_input_tokens":292284,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPJ3BRcevrZkpEv1JxVv","type":"assistant","uuid":"120d3752-da6c-47f7-81dd-c346a5c955c4","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:03:24.715Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/apps/validate","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
