/`React.`-qualified key fallback; degrades gracefully |\n211-\n212----\n213-\n214-## Fixed bugs (previously tracked here as open)\n215-\n216-### Fixed: method-shorthand handler losing param type\n217-\n218-**Fixture:** `fixtures/rdt-compat/controlled.tsx`\n219-\n220-Previously: `onValueChange?(value: string): void` (TSMethodSignature form) emitted `eventType: \"...\"` instead of `eventType: \"string\"`, while the arrow-function form correctly emitted `eventType: \"boolean\"`. Root cause: the extractor's method-signature handling didn't extract parameter types the same way as property-signature handling. Fixed — confirmed live: `onValueChange` now correctly resolves to `(value: string) => void`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"91b90798-1bcd-44bf-ada9-571788149c56","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
