{"parentUuid":"9b29fa52-c723-4220-aba9-e0e44b662815","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPKn9aoHoJvv6BFSPFZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UoQKHtdm7isx2Zgc7LpkNs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(benchmarks): real cross-tool perf + quality comparison, replacing the old raw coverage ratio\n\nAdds docs/benchmarks.md: a proper, reproducible comparison against\nreact-docgen-typescript and react-docgen — both performance and output\nquality, plus an honest shortcomings/remediation section. Nothing in\nthat report is hand-waved; every number has a script that reproduces\nit.\n\nPerformance:\n- Migrated crates/core's benches from divan to criterion (statistical\n  rigor, persisted historical HTML reports under target/criterion/,\n  confidence intervals) per explicit request to use the more\n  defensible tool for a report making comparative claims.\n- Added an incremental-vs-cold bench using WatchSession — RDT and\n  react-docgen have no incremental API at all, so this number (10-13x\n  faster than this tool's own cold extraction) is a capability gap,\n  not just a speed gap.\n- Adopted hyperfine for cross-process/cross-tool cold-start timing\n  (apps/validate/bench-cold.sh) instead of a hand-rolled timing loop —\n  proper warmup runs, statistical analysis, markdown/JSON export.\n- Found and fixed a real methodology bug while building this: run-ours.ts\n  spawned one CLI process per fixture library (21 processes), so the\n  \"cold\" number was dominated by process-startup overhead (~885ms) not\n  actual extraction cost (~50ms for a single whole-corpus invocation,\n  confirmed via hyperfine). Fixed to invoke the CLI once across the\n  whole corpus (--src takes a comma-delimited list) — also just how\n  anyone would actually run this tool in practice.\n\nQuality (apps/validate/src/analyze.ts, new):\n- Real per-prop agreement rate (matched/mismatched/missing/extra) with\n  a type-diff taxonomy (cosmetic-formatting, literal-narrowed-vs-widened,\n  union-member-order, optional-undefined-representation,\n  structural-type-difference), replacing compare.ts's raw prop-count\n  ratio, which wasn't a real per-prop match rate and didn't account for\n  known design differences.\n- Fixed two real harness bugs found while validating early numbers\n  looked implausible:\n  - react-docgen-typescript represents union/literal types as\n    { name: 'enum', value: [...] } — reading .name alone compared the\n    literal string \"enum\" against our real type string for every\n    union-typed prop.\n  - react-docgen puts real TS type info under .tsType (with a .raw\n    field carrying the exact source text), not .type (a legacy\n    PropTypes-only field, absent for TS-typed props) — reading .type\n    alone silently produced \"unknown\" for nearly every TS-typed prop.\n- Fixed react-docgen's fixture keying: it pushed one ToolResult per\n  FILE (multi-component files collapsed into one output blob) while\n  rdt/ours key per-component — the react-docgen comparison axis never\n  actually joined against the other two before this.\n- Runs two oxc-react-docgen baselines (html-attributes=full for the\n  RDT comparison, which always fully expands the real HTML attribute\n  interface chain; html-attributes=none for the react-docgen\n  comparison, which resolves zero `extends` chains of its own) instead\n  of comparing both against one mode — the prior single-mode\n  comparison manufactured a huge fake \"missing/extra props\" count that\n  was really just a default-mode mismatch, not a quality signal.\n\nRoot-caused (not just counted) several real outlier components during\nthis work: a generic SVGAttributes<T>/HTMLProps<T>-extends gap newly\nfound in resolver/named.rs (actionable, no type checker needed), and\nconfirmed the Ariakit/ark-ui generic-type-parameter-substitution\noutliers trace to the same already-documented Corsa-deferred gap. Both\nwritten up with evidence in docs/benchmarks.md's shortcomings section\nrather than asserted without a concrete case.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":368748,"output_tokens":1495,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1495,"cache_read_input_tokens":368748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPKn6xYChVmKs1RJ9W7P","type":"assistant","uuid":"9adcb4ba-d0f1-4bfb-a5d5-cdaf731a6534","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:26:07.262Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
