{"parentUuid":"2e3cbbe8-41b0-4887-a500-2c5c3fd27eaf","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Muzs1352MstmvVPmPiAiU2","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":67},"type":"attachment","uuid":"00424a86-cb8c-49be-81dc-085d06ab4942","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:35:04.892Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"00424a86-cb8c-49be-81dc-085d06ab4942","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/README.md","snippet":"1\t# oxc-react-docgen\n2\t\n3\tReact component prop extraction powered by [OXC](https://oxc.rs). Parses TypeScript natively in Rust — no TypeScript compiler program, no type-checking pass, no startup tax.\n4\t\n5\t> **Status:** Core extraction, NAPI bindings, Vite plugin, CLI, and `docgen.config.ts` loading are complete.\n6\t\n7\t## Why\n8\t\n9\t`react-docgen-typescript` spins up a full TypeScript `Program` to extract props. On a mid-size design system this takes seconds — enough to noticeably delay Storybook startup and make HMR feel sluggish. OXC parses each file in parallel with no type-checking pass, so cold extraction on a 15-component fixture set (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, Radix) takes **32ms**.\n10\t\n11\tThe CLI can emit an RDT-compatible shape via `--format rdt` (see [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md)). The Vite plugin and NAPI binding currently expose this tool's own canonical format only — not a drop-in RDT replacement at that layer yet.\n12\t\n13\t## Install\n14\t\n15\t`@oxc-react-docgen/napi`, `@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin`, and `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` are not yet published to npm — there are no per-platform prebuilt binaries to install today. Until a release ships:\n16\t\n17\t```bash\n18\tgit clone https://github.com/orin-dx/oxc-react-docgen\n19\tcd oxc-react-docgen\n20\tpnpm install\n21\tpnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/napi run build:napi   # builds the native addon for your platform\n22\tpnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin build\n23\t```\n24\t\n25\t`pnpm run build:napi` (not a bare `cargo build`) matters: it invokes `napi build`, which places the compiled addon exactly where `packages/napi/index.js`'s generated loader expects it. This works as a monorepo-local dependency today; there are no published per-platform packages for it to fall back to yet. See [MIGRATING.md](MIGRATING.md) if you're moving off `react-docgen-typescript` and want to know exactly what's compatible today.\n26\t\n27\t## Vite plugin\n28\t\n29\t```ts\n30\t// vite.config.ts\n31\timport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n32\timport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\n33\timport { oxcReactDocgen } from '@oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin'\n34\t\n35\texport default defineConfig({\n36\t  plugins: [react(), oxcReactDocgen({ srcDirs: ['src'] })],\n37\t})\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\tMetadata is available on the `virtual:oxc-react-docgen` module and pushed via HMR as components change:\n41\t\n42\t```ts\n43\timport docgen from 'virtual:oxc-react-docgen'\n44\t\n45\tdocgen.components['Button'].props\n46\t// {\n47\t//   variant: {\n48\t//     type: { kind: 'literalUnion', members: ['default', 'destructive', 'outline'], hasDefault: true },\n49\t//     required: false,\n50\t//     defaultValue: { value: '\"default\"', computed: false },\n51\t//     description: '',\n52\t//   },\n53\t//   ...\n54\t// }\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\t## CLI\n58\t\n59\tThe CLI is a single Rust binary (`crates/cli`) — argument parsing, output formatting, and `--format rdt`/`--format storybook` serialization all live there and nowhere else. `@oxc-react-docgen/cli` (once published) is a thin npm wrapper that just execs the platform-appropriate compiled binary; it deliberately contains no reimplementation of CLI behavior, so there's exactly one place that behavior can drift.\n60\t\n61\t```bash\n62\t# Once published: npx @oxc-react-docgen/cli extract --src src/ --out docgen.json\n63\t# From source today: ./target/release/oxc-react-docgen (after cargo build --release)\n64\t\n65\t# One-shot extraction\n66\toxc-react-docgen extract --src src/ --out docgen.json\n67\t\n68\t# Inspect a single file\n69\toxc-react-docgen inspect src/components/Button.tsx\n70\t\n71\t# Watch mode\n72\toxc-react-docgen watch --src src/\n73\t\n74\t# Shell completions\n75\toxc-react-docgen completions zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_oxc-react-docgen\n76\t\n77\t# Full HTML attribute expansion instead of the default curated subset\n78\toxc-react-docgen extract --src src/ --html-attributes full\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\tSettings can also live in `docgen.config.ts` (`srcDirs`, `htmlAttributes`, `reactVersion`, `crossPackage`, and more — see `crates/cli/src/config.rs` for the full schema) instead of CLI flags.\n82\t\n83\t## Output shape\n84\t\n85\t```json\n86\t{\n87\t  \"components\": {\n88\t    \"Button\": {\n89\t      \"displayName\": \"Button\",\n90\t      \"filePath\": \"src/components/Button.tsx\",\n91\t      \"props\": {\n92\t        \"variant\": {\n93\t          \"type\": { \"kind\": \"literalUnion\", \"members\": [\"default\", \"destructive\", \"outline\"], \"hasDefault\": true },\n94\t          \"required\": false,\n95\t          \"defaultValue\": { \"value\": \"\\\"default\\\"\", \"computed\": false },\n96\t          \"description\": \"Visual style variant.\",\n97\t          \"tags\": {}\n98\t        }\n99\t      },\n100\t      \"inheritance\": [\n101\t        { \"typeName\": \"ButtonHTMLAttributes\", \"htmlElement\": \"button\", \"omitted\": [], \"totalProps\": 147 }\n102\t      ],\n103\t      \"notableInherited\": {\n104\t        \"onClick\": { \"type\": { \"kind\": \"eventHandler\", \"eventType\": \"MouseEvent<HTMLButtonElement>\" }, ... },\n105\t        \"disabled\": { \"type\": { \"kind\": \"boolean\" }, ... }\n106\t      },\n107\t      \"discriminantProp\": null\n108\t    }\n109\t  },\n110\t  \"diagnostics\": [],\n111\t  \"stats\": { \"filesParsed\": 3, \"durationMs\": 12, \"dtsCacheHits\": 2, ... }\n112\t}\n113\t```\n114\t\n115\t## Supported patterns\n116\t\n117\t| Pattern                    | Example                                                           |\n118\t| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n119\t| Function components        | `function Button(props: ButtonProps)`                             |\n120\t| Arrow components           | `const Button = (props: ButtonProps) => ...`                      |\n121\t| `React.forwardRef`         | `forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(...)`                 |\n122\t| HOC-wrapped                | `styled(Base)<ButtonProps>`                                       |\n123\t| Interface inheritance      | `interface ButtonProps extends HTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>` |\n124\t| Intersection aliases       | `type ButtonProps = BaseProps & { variant?: string }`             |\n125\t| `Omit` / `Pick`            | `type ButtonProps = Omit<InputProps, 'value'>`                    |\n126\t| `ComponentPropsWithoutRef` | `ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>`                              |\n127\t| `VariantProps`             | `VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants>` (CVA / TV / PandaCSS)       |\n128\t| Discriminated unions       | MUI-style `variant: 'filled' \\| 'outlined' \\| 'standard'`         |\n129\t| JSDoc tags                 | `@description`, `@default`, `@deprecated`, `@internal`            |\n130\t\n131\t## Repository\n132\t\n133\t```\n134\tcrates/core/          pure extraction logic (no I/O, no async, Send + Sync)\n135\tcrates/binding/       thin NAPI wrapper over core\n136\tcrates/cli/           clap + miette CLI\n137\tpackages/napi/        @oxc-react-docgen/napi (dev binary loader + TS types)\n138\tpackages/vite-plugin/ @oxc-react-docgen/vite-plugin\n139\tpackages/cli/         @oxc-react-docgen/cli (npx wrapper — execs crates/cli's binary, no reimplemented logic)\n140\tapps/validate/        accuracy comparison harness (react-docgen, rdt, ours)\n141\tfixtures/             real library .d.ts/.tsx files (shadcn, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, etc.)\n142\t```\n143\t\n144\t## Contributing\n145\t\n146\t[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) — setup, code style, commit conventions.  \n147\t[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) — pipeline, modules, key design decisions.\n148\t\n149\t## License\n150\t\n151\tAGPL-3.0-or-later — see [LICENSE](LICENSE)."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"29ca1c69-b567-44e9-84cb-1edb1c4c6165","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:35:04.916Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
