{"parentUuid":"bb58e11c-d067-4982-88a7-cdd81cd9db74","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPM9WaZ7MNMuYTbZEtt2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HEcVXsmu4Gq4hBbDmKL5LW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(extractor): resolve generic SVGAttributes<T>/HTMLProps<T> to their real element\n\ndocs/benchmarks.md's shortcomings section root-caused this: interfaces\nextending React.SVGAttributes<T>/HTMLProps<T> (e.g.\nfixtures/rdt-compat/svg-icon.tsx's IconProps extends\nReact.SVGAttributes<SVGSVGElement>) resolved almost no inherited props\nat all (2 own props instead of RDT's 488) even with\n--html-attributes full — a real, actionable gap, unlike this same\nreport's other outliers, which need a type checker.\n\nRoot cause: react_types::html_element_for maps interface name ->\nelement for the *concrete* forms (ButtonHTMLAttributes -> \"button\",\netc.), where the element is baked into the name itself. But\nSVGAttributes/SVGProps/HTMLProps carry no element in their name — the\nelement only shows up in the type argument at the call site\n(`SVGAttributes<SVGSVGElement>`). html_element_for correctly returns\nNone for these (SVGAttributes) or a useless generic \"div\" (HTMLProps),\nso classify_extends built an ExtendsRef::Builtin with element: None,\nand named.rs's step-6 silent-no-op list swallowed it as opaque before\nany expansion could happen.\n\nAdded html_element_from_type_arg — an explicit mapping from concrete\nDOM element type names (HTMLDivElement -> \"div\", SVGSVGElement ->\n\"svg\", etc.) to their real tag, deliberately NOT a strip-prefix/\nstrip-suffix/lowercase heuristic: that would get real tags wrong for\nseveral elements (HTMLAnchorElement's real tag is \"a\", not \"anchor\").\nFalls back to None (the prior safe behavior) for anything not in the\nlist rather than guessing. classify_extends now checks this for the\nthree generic forms before falling through to html_element_for's\nexisting static lookup, so a recognized concrete argument always wins.\n\nConfirmed against the real fixture this was found in:\nrdt-compat/svg-icon.tsx's Icon went from 2 props to 487 (RDT: 488),\nBox from 2 to 381 (RDT: 382) — matches almost exactly, the residual\nbeing the same known \"same-namespace sibling reference resolution\"\ngap docs/rdt-coverage.md already tracks separately. Curated mode\nbenefits too: Icon/Box now get real `inheritance`/`notableInherited`\nmetadata instead of being an opaque `composes: [\"React.SVGAttributes\"]`\nreference (see the updated rdt_compat snapshot).\n\nAdded test_generic_svg_attributes_extends_resolves_to_its_element_in_full_mode\n(confirmed RED before the fix: only the synthetic \"size\" own prop\nresolved, no real SVGAttributes field).\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":449,"cache_read_input_tokens":442788,"output_tokens":1110,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":449,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":442788,"cache_creation_input_tokens":449,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":449},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPM93Vdwe9VU3UZVuy4n","type":"assistant","uuid":"70b229ea-a16e-41b6-b528-b8a23ee7de82","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:44:01.381Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBra