{"parentUuid":"1f710194-5866-4f1a-a3ed-e9c0527dd765","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPMS8qpphcr3NGjL8BkD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_read_input_tokens":460067,"output_tokens":1947,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1947,"cache_read_input_tokens":460067,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPMS5Fn1yHpzVEcBqP1G","type":"assistant","uuid":"f7686b09-6cc7-460d-94b3-a7a670acdf91","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:47:44.582Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"f7686b09-6cc7-460d-94b3-a7a670acdf91","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPMS8qpphcr3NGjL8BkD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Real one — but first, your CI question, since it's been waiting:\n\n## CI best practices — where we stand\n\n**What we're doing well:** path-based job gating via moon's affected-graph (skip untouched language groups), matrix testing across Node versions, concurrency cancellation for superseded runs, fail-open on ambiguous cases rather than silently skipping checks, and (as of this session) the `docs` output ensures markdown-only PRs still get checked.\n\n**Where we deviate from common practice, and whether that's a problem:**\n\n1. **No dependency-update automation** (Dependabot/Renovate). This is a real gap — flagged in the original tooling audit, never actioned. Worth doing now: Renovate over Dependabot for this repo since it handles the Rust+pnpm+GitHub-Actions mixed-ecosystem update cadence more configurably (grouped PRs, custom schedules per ecosystem).\n2. **No `concurrency` group scoping per job**, only workflow-level — fine at current scale, would matter if jobs started taking many minutes and users pushed rapidly.\n3. **`cargo test`/`cargo bench` results aren't archived anywhere** — coverage uploads to Codecov, but bench results are `tee`'d to an artifact and never trended. If perf regressions matter to you, a lightweight bench-tracking action (e.g. `benchmark-action/github-action-benchmark`) that fails a PR when a benchmark regresses past a threshold, using this session's newly-criterion-based benches, would close that gap — currently nothing would catch a 2x slowdown creeping in.\n4. **The moon-affected-detection job re-implements path→category mapping by hand** (the case-statement I fixed earlier) instead of moon's own task-output-based caching (`moon run :test --affected` letting moon itself decide, rather than gating whole GH Actions jobs). The current approach is coarser but simpler to reason about; moon's native approach would be more precise (per-task, not per-language-group) at the cost of restructuring the workflow around moon commands rather than raw cargo/pnpm.\n5. **No `permissions:` block** at the workflow or job level — GitHub defaults to broad token permissions unless explicitly scoped down. Best practice is `permissions: contents: read` at the workflow level with elevated permissions only on jobs that need them (none of ours currently push, release, or comment, so read-only everywhere is correct and currently *implicit* rather than explicit — worth being explicit since implicit-broad is exactly the footgun `permissions:` exists to close).\n\nWant me to action any of these now, or keep going on the fluentui investigation first? I just found something more serious than a fluentui-specific gap.\n\n## The real finding: components silently collide across files in a single invocation"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_read_input_tokens":460067,"output_tokens":1947,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1947,"cache_read_input_tokens":460067,"cache_creation_input_tokens":843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPMS5Fn1yHpzVEcBqP1G","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d246b91-f35e-49a7-a2c5-cf76aa699e4d","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:47:57.971Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBr