{"parentUuid":"47ab9496-156a-4fad-af76-7d8524490304","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPMVQFcSYR6e79nHpcgq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good news: **23 of 32 components (72%) are near-perfect matches** — 0-2 props different, and that difference is always just React's own `ref`/`key` (which RDT includes as props and we correctly don't). The 17.7% aggregate isn't a real reflection of typical quality — it's dragged down entirely by **9 outlier components** (28%) that share one specific limitation: polymorphic component libraries (Ariakit, Base UI, Ark UI, Headless UI, one Emotion case) built on generic/conditional-type chains that need a real type checker to resolve, not a parser. This isn't a new regression or something we thought we'd fixed — it's the exact, long-documented \"no type checker\" boundary (Corsa-deferred), now measured precisely instead of asserted vaguely. On the 72% of real-world component patterns that don't hit that boundary, we're matching essentially exactly.\n\nThat said — investigating `fluentui` just surfaced something separate and more serious, unrelated to the type-checker boundary:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2225,"cache_read_input_tokens":463303,"output_tokens":921,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2225,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":463303,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2225},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPMVMGma5KZo3UWUwrFX","type":"assistant","uuid":"e7238151-0adf-41ba-aaf5-b7d954f9255d","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:48:28.390Z