{"parentUuid":"55822fc1-5110-4557-b352-81ff1d288089","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPN59y5SMM1Ma35YVkjQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0159Z8jkjrrBePZuYWvV2SC2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit add docs/benchmarks.md\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\ndocs(benchmarks): update numbers post-fix, root-cause the remaining outliers\n\nRegenerated all quality numbers after the SVGAttributes and\ncomponent-collision fixes (both landed as separate commits just\nbefore this). Icon/Box moved from the outlier table into the\nnear-perfect group; fluentui/Button — previously silently absent from\nevery table because of the collision bug, not merely inaccurate — is\nnow correctly included as a real outlier.\n\nRoot-caused the three components the report had previously left as\n\"not yet root-caused\": base-ui/MenuTrigger (mapped type over a generic,\nWithBaseUIEvent<T>), headlessui/Listbox's 3 components (conditional\ntype PropsOf<TTag> nested inside generic substitution), and\nfluentui/Button (a conditional type, Slot<Type,...>, combined with\nindexed access into a generic). All three land in the same\nalready-documented Corsa-deferred bucket as the Ariakit outliers — no\nnew actionable gaps, just more evidence for an existing one.\n\nAdded a \"Fixed during this report\" section documenting both bugs found\nand fixed, and a \"reading the aggregate percentage correctly\" note\ndirectly addressing the two different reasons a pairwise agreement\nrate can be low (this tool missing real props vs. the comparator\nmissing them) — a distinction the raw percentage can't make on its\nown and that came up directly while reviewing this report.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_inp