{"parentUuid":"f501768a-0841-42dd-a735-9565f64ca469","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPN9vBk5QLSWkmnsSkSu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Launching parallel sweeps across the codebase, split by area, to survey comment quality without me having to read every file myself."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1699,"cache_read_input_tokens":516474,"output_tokens":1289,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1699,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":516474,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1699},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPN9sZjLo8Wzt2Hhi2qB","type":"assistant","uuid":"3daf236f-b2af-4504-b65b-cf45e2759d45","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:57:03.631Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"3daf236f-b2af-4504-b65b-cf45e2759d45","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPN9vBk5QLSWkmnsSkSu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AfVtgsUgWRbCh2t35ETQbU","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Comment quality sweep: crates/core","prompt":"You're auditing comment quality in a Rust codebase (oxc-react-docgen, a React prop-extraction tool). Scope: everything under /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/src/ (the largest crate — extractor/, resolver/, pipeline/, types/, plus top-level files like cache.rs, import_map.rs, known.rs, react_types.rs, lib.rs).\n\nContext on what \"good\" looks like here: this project's established convention (see crates/core/CLAUDE.md and the rust-style skill) is that comments should explain WHY something is done a certain way — a hidden constraint, a workaround, a non-obvious invariant, a bug that was fixed and why the fix looks the way it does — never WHAT the code does (identifiers should make that obvious on their own). Comments should read like something a sharp, terse engineer wrote for a teammate: no throat-clearing, no filler, no restating the obvious, no hedging language, no \"AI-generated\" tells.\n\nYour job: read through the actual .rs files (not just grep) and flag every comment (line comments `//`, doc comments `///`/`//!`, block comments) that has ANY of these problems:\n1. **Restates what the code does** instead of explaining why (e.g. \"// increment the counter\" above `count += 1`)\n2. **AI-slop / filler language**: phrases like \"It's important to note that\", \"This is used to...\", \"Basically,\", \"Simply put,\", \"Note that this function...\", excessive hedging (\"might potentially\", \"could possibly\"), unnecessary meta-commentary, or overly verbose restating of something already said\n3. **Stale or contradicts the current code** (references a function/field/behavior that no longer exists or has changed)\n4. **Word salad**: technically-worded but doesn't actually convey information, or is vague where it should be specific\n5. **Redundant with a doc comment or adjacent comment** saying the same thing twice\n\nFor each flagged comment, report: file path, line number, the comment text verbatim, which category it falls into, and a one-line suggestion for what to do (delete it / rewrite it as X / keep but shorten). Also note comments that are GOOD examples of the house style (WHY-focused, terse) — I want calibration on what's already working, not just a list of problems.\n\nThis is a research/survey task — do NOT edit any files. Report back with a structured list grouped by file. If a file has zero issues, just say so briefly, don't pad the report. Focus your effort on files with real substance (resolver/*.rs, extractor/mod.rs, pipeline/mod.rs, import_map.rs are the highest-value targets — the smaller/simpler files like types/*.rs may have less to find).","subagent_type":"Explore","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1699,"cache_read_input_tokens":516474,"output_tokens":1289,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1699,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1289,"cache_read_input_tokens":516474,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1699},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPN9sZjLo8Wzt2Hhi2qB","type":"assistant","uuid":"16f89d66-9873-45b6-a7ee-8292c8729ad6","timestamp":"2026-07-25T19:57:15.426Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessi