li is \"thin command layer, no extraction logic\", binding is \"thin NAPI wrapper, delegates to core\").\n\nContext on what \"good\" looks like here: this project's established convention is that comments should explain WHY something is done a certain way — a hidden constraint, a workaround, a non-obvious invariant, a bug that was fixed and why the fix looks the way it does — never WHAT the code does (identifiers should make that obvious on their own). Comments should read like something a sharp, terse engineer wrote for a teammate: no throat-clearing, no filler, no restating the obvious, no hedging language, no \"AI-generated\" tells.\n\nYour job: read through the actual .rs files (not just grep) and flag every comment (line comments `//`, doc comments `///`/`//!`, block comments) that has ANY of these problems:\n1. **Restates what the code does** instead of explaining why (e.g. \"// increment the counter\" above `count += 1`)\n2. **AI-slop / filler language**: phrases like \"It's important to note that\", \"This is used to...\", \"Basically,\", \"Simply put,\", \"Note that this function...\", excessive hedging (\"might potentially\", \"could possibly\"), unnecessary meta-commentary, or overly verbose restating of something already said\n3. **Stale or contradicts the current code** (references a function/field/behavior that no longer exists or has changed)\n4. **Word salad**: technically-worded but doesn't actually convey information, or is vague where it should be specific\n5. **Redundant with a doc comment or adjacent comment** saying the same thing twice\n\nFor each flagged comment, report: file path, line number, the comment text verbatim, which category it falls into, and a one-line suggestion for what to do (delete it / rewrite it as X / keep but shorten). Also note comments that are GOOD examples of the house style (WHY-focused, terse) — I want calibration on what's already working, not just a list of problems.\n\nThis is a research/survey task — do NOT edit any files. Report back with a structured list grouped by file. If a file has zero issues, just say so briefly, don't pad the report.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/6e77fa42-b39d-4d85-9370-fe0b0fa9b104/tasks/ac09e7834ea5d2515.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7f5bbaf2-fb22-453c-a7c3-104778c75708","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
