{"parentUuid":"abaee307-e7bd-483e-87c8-1142a4365fd0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPNwCKbhmYQtbriA4TTz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Zn16VZEwhRQEpuNbE9qPu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit add -A\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nrefactor: comment-quality sweep across Rust and TS — fix stale citations, cut restates\n\nDispatched three parallel audits (crates/core, crates/cli+binding,\nTS packages) against the house style (WHY not WHAT, terse, no filler)\nafter auditing all three languages' formatter configs — .rustfmt.toml,\n.oxfmtrc.json, and clippy (which has no width setting; it's a linter,\nnot a formatter, so there was nothing to configure there) already\nagree on 120 chars, no changes needed.\n\nOverall finding: this codebase's comments were already close to the\ntarget style — the audits found zero AI-slop phrases and zero\nword-salad. What's fixed here:\n\n- **Stale citation, the one real correctness bug**: 5 comments across\n  crates/core, crates/cli, crates/binding, and one ADR cited\n  \"crates/core/CLAUDE.md non-negotiable #6\" — but crates/core/CLAUDE.md\n  has no numbered list; the non-negotiables live in the root CLAUDE.md.\n  Fixed all 5 to point at the right file.\n- **Restates-the-code-below comments** (~15 total): deleted from\n  extractor/component.rs, visit.rs, jsdoc.rs, interface.rs, known.rs —\n  things like `// Walk children for nested declarations` directly\n  above `walk::walk_variable_declaration(...)`, where the comment adds\n  nothing the identifier names didn't already say.\n- **Duplicated rationale at declaration + call site**\n  (packages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts): the same \"why\" explained twice\n  ~30-80 lines apart; kept the fuller version once, cut the repeat.\n- **Missing doc comments replaced by inline WHAT-comments**\n  (crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs): serialize_rdt/serialize_storybook\n  had `// RDT-compatible shape` / `// Storybook __docgenInfo shape`\n  instead of a real doc comment — replaced with a `///` explaining the\n  one actually non-obvious thing (methods is always [] and why).\n  Trimmed serialize_rdt's `props`-building loop's own restates too.\n- **One imprecise comment** (run-react-docgen-typescript.ts): \"falls\n  back if tsconfig not found\" overstated what the catch actually\n  guards against (any option-combination failure, not specifically a\n  missing file) — reworded to match what the code guarantees.\n- **Dead code found and removed**, not just its comments polished:\n  apps/validate/src/types.ts's `ComparisonResult` interface had zero\n  references anywhere in the repo (compare.ts computes the same shape\n  ad hoc with local variables instead) — deleted rather than leaving\n  four restating JSDoc comments on an unused type.\n\nFull test suite, clippy, fmt, oxlint/oxfmt, and cargo deny all green\nafter every change; ran both apps/validate/src/compare.ts and\nanalyze.ts end-to-end post-edit to confirm the types.ts deletion\ndidn't break anything at runtime.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":651,"cache_read_input_tokens":578261,"output_tokens":1186,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":651,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1186,"cache_read_input_tokens":578261,"cache_creation_input_tokens":651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":651},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPNw2TH48AcW9dCQ3G25","type":"assistant","uuid":"99cad094-76ca-4ce4-bb47-2fd9b8648a05","timestamp":"2026-07-2