{"parentUuid":"a5cc8147-6871-4ba1-9223-dfdfeed31f6d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPPynowH3WmJQ6kFciDg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clear, data-backed answer:\n\n- **2,696 of 2,720 missing props (99.1%)** come from the 10 already-documented outlier components — genuinely not something we chose to omit. These need a real type checker (generic substitution, conditional types) that OXC-based parsing structurally can't do. Real gap, not a design choice.\n- **The remaining 24 (0.9%)** — spread across 12 of the 23 near-perfect components — are **100% `ref` and `key`** (12 each). That's the one deliberate omission in the whole diff: React's own reconciliation/ref-forwarding mechanics, not real component API surface. RDT includes them as props; we correctly don't.\n\nTo your second question — no, we don't currently surface that information anywhere else either. I checked `ComponentEntry`'s full field list: no `isForwardRef` flag, no ref-type metadata, nothing. The extractor internally detects `forwardRef`-wrapped components (it has to, to find the right props type), but that detection result never makes it into the output — there's no trace of \"this component forwards a ref\" in the JSON today. So it's not \"captured elsewhere instead of as a prop\" — it's just not surfaced at all, on the reasoning that `ref`/`key` are mechanical React plumbing every component has implicitly, not information worth documenting per-component. That's a defensible call, but it's worth being precise: it's an omission, not a relocation.\n\nUpdating the report to state this precisely instead of the vague \"React's own special props\" line:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":806,"cache_read_input_tokens":609555,"output_tokens":1976,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":806,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1976,"cache_read_input_tokens":609555,"cache_creation_input_tokens":806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":806},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPPyfWeUs3MWeTcmPPFJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"e72e1799-0ca2-40a9-9f20-115ccff050bf","timestamp":"2026-07-25T20:21:12.570Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"e72e1799-0ca2-40a9-9f20-115ccff050bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPPynowH3WmJQ6kFciDg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U7JjHFaUCF4hHewcHi6ss2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\npython3 << 'PYEOF'\npath = 'docs/benchmarks.md'\ncontent = open(path).read()\n\nold = '''That 16.8% needs immediate context: **it is not evenly distributed.** Of the 33 compared components, **23 (70%) are near-perfect matches** (0-2 props different — e.g. `antd/Button`: 312 props vs. RDT's 313, the only difference being `ref`/`key`, React's own special props, which RDT includes and this tool correctly doesn't treat as a real prop). The low aggregate is driven entirely by **10 outlier components (30%)** where this tool currently resolves only a handful of props against RDT's 234-314 — every one of them now root-caused, and every one lands in the same category: a real type checker is required, this isn't a parser-fixable gap:'''\n\nnew = '''That 16.8% needs immediate context: **it is not evenly distributed, and the missing-props number is 99.1% one root cause.** Of the 2,720 props missing from this tool's output, **2,696 (99.1%) come from just 10 outlier components** (below) — all of them a real, structural gap needing a type checker, not something chosen to omit. The other 24 (0.9%, spread across 12 of the other 23 components) are **100% `ref`/`key`** — React's own reconciliation plumbing, which RDT lists as props and this tool deliberately doesn't. Worth being precise about that one: it's an omission, not a relocation — this tool doesn't surface forwardRef/ref-type metadata anywhere else either (checked `ComponentEntry`'s full field list — no such field exists), so \"we chose not to add it\" is accurate, but \"the same info lives elsewhere\" isn't. Excluding those 10 outliers, this tool's real-world agreement with RDT is effectively total (e.g. 