{"parentUuid":"1266f699-7ee6-4f43-b347-a036a1a7b009","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPQ7YbeGPgimSmNAkf13","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018EcF25peGsrfv3BqitUpb5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\ngit add docs/benchmarks.md\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\ndocs(benchmarks): drop the fixing-narrative, quantify the RDT diff precisely\n\nRemoved the \"Fixed during this report\" section and the harness-bug\nfixing story from the methodology note — a benchmarks report should\nstate the current, correct methodology and numbers, not narrate the\nprocess of getting there. That history still lives in the git log\n(commits 518a65f, b59830c) for anyone who wants it.\n\nReplaced the vague \"most components are near-perfect, ref/key is the\nonly difference\" framing with an exact breakdown, since the actual\nquestion worth answering is \"are these gaps real, or things we chose\nto omit for signal over noise\": of the 2,720 props missing from this\ntool's RDT comparison, 2,696 (99.1%) come from the 10 outlier\ncomponents — a real, structural type-checker gap, not something\nchosen to skip. The other 24 (0.9%, across 12 components) are 100%\nref/key. Checked whether that information is captured elsewhere\ninstead (ComponentEntry's full field list has no forwardRef/ref-type\nmetadata) — it isn't; it's a genuine omission, not a relocation, so\nthe report now says exactly that instead of \"RDT includes them and we\ncorrectly don't\" without qualification.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":623254,"output_tokens":582,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_