{"parentUuid":"779ae931-2f54-48e7-a2bd-5e2170d34116","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPR9j5rBQdwbFJj9zFf9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":632034,"output_tokens":2658,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":632034,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPR9ZtxCeKqcTStj78Xt","type":"assistant","uuid":"980e0b8d-563c-4f46-a3c0-e6c473bb91d0","timestamp":"2026-07-25T20:36:33.980Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"980e0b8d-563c-4f46-a3c0-e6c473bb91d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPR9j5rBQdwbFJj9zFf9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes to both — and there's already a real mechanism sitting half-built for exactly this. Two concrete findings:\n\n**1. RDT's format already has a field for \"here's what we know, we're not expanding it\": `composes`.** Real react-docgen output includes a `composes: string[]` array — the documented way to say \"this component's props are composed from another type we're listing by name, not flattening.\" Our own `ComponentEntry.composes: Vec<String>` already exists and is populated for a few known-opaque patterns (e.g. `ThemingProps`). But:\n- It's **never populated** for the actual outlier failures (mapped types, conditional types, generic-substitution dead ends) — those currently just return zero props with no trace.\n- Even where it *is* populated today, `serialize_rdt` in `crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs` doesn't include `composes` in the output JSON at all — I just checked, it's built from `displayName`/`props`/`description`/`methods`/`tags` only. The field gets silently dropped on the way out.\n\n**2. This closes real ground without a type checker, and it's cheap.** The fix isn't inference — it's graceful degradation we already do 90% of: when the resolver hits a mapped/conditional type it can't expand, it already builds the raw source text for the diagnostic message (`OPAQUE_TYPE`). Right now that text goes into `diagnostics` and the props map gets nothing. The stop-gap: on that same failure path, also push the raw type text into `composes` instead of returning empty — same `ResolvedChain::empty_with_compose(...)` mechanism already used for the known-opaque cases, just applied to the currently-silent dead ends too. Zero new resolution logic, zero perf cost (it only fires on paths that are already failing).\n\nFor `fluentui/Button` concretely: today `composes` is `[]` and the 3 `OPAQUE_TYPE` diagnostics are invisible to any RDT/Storybook consumer that only reads `props`. With this fix, `composes` would carry the actual unresolvable type text (`Slot<Type, AlternateAs>`'s conditional expression), so a docs UI could render \"additional props from: `Slot<Type,...>` (see source)\" instead of showing nothing.\n\nThis is real, scoped work — not a one-liner, since it touches several resolver dead-end points (`alias.rs`, `extends.rs`, `chain.rs`) plus the `serialize_rdt` fix. Given the \"optionally\" question:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":632034,"output_tokens":2658,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":632034,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdPR9ZtxCeKqcTStj78Xt","type":"assistant","uuid":"ffa1b7ec-0c74-4165-8f57-e7b2ca1dafa6","timestamp":"2026-07-25T20:36:45.053Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"ffa1b7ec-0c74-4165-8f57-e7b2ca1dafa6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPR9j5rBQdwbFJj9zFf9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QPjUrxhHhxWyNo8fXEaMpe","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Should populating `composes` on these currently-silent failure paths be the default behavior, or opt-in via a PipelineOptions flag?","header":"Opt-in vs default","options":[{"label":"Default on (Recommended)","description":"It only fires where output is currently empty anyway — strictly additive, can't make any currently-working case worse, and matches CLAUDE.md's own \"never fail silently\" rule"},{"label":"New opt-in flag (e.g. surface_unresolved_as_composes)","description":"Off by default, consumers explicitly enable it — more conservative, but adds an API surface for something that's arguably just fixing a gap in existing behavior"}]},{"question":"Want me to scope and implement this now, or write it up as a plan first given it touches several resolver files?","header":"Next step","options":[{"label":"Implement now with TDD (Recommended)","description":"Same rigor as the other fixes this session: RED test per dead-end path fixed, then GREEN, full suite + clippy + snapshot check before committing"},{"label":"Write a short plan first","description":"List every dead-end call site to fix before touching code, since this spans alias.rs/extends.rs/chain.rs/serialize_rdt"}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":632034,"output_tokens":2658,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2658,"cache_read_input_tokens":6320