{"parentUuid":"5221c0d4-6f5f-48a5-9d91-141ff31bad17","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdTTtXpP2znX4dqKA9fYB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187jiPKZW2QwCdpSh3z5dUC","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"tsgolint typescript-eslint tsgo type information linter"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2307,"cache_read_input_tokens":77939,"output_tokens":162,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2307,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":162,"cache_read_input_tokens":77939,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2307},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdTTtWaii7p8rrp5Wojrb","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ba5fd7d-5483-496c-8e3b-80f86ae7c39e","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:35.404Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"0ba5fd7d-5483-496c-8e3b-80f86ae7c39e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6925474d-182b-4bb8-800a-56f9380f5559","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0187jiPKZW2QwCdpSh3z5dUC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"tsgolint typescript-eslint tsgo type information linter\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"tsgolint/README.md at main · typescript-eslint/tsgolint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - typescript-eslint/tsgolint: ✨ Experimental proof-of-concept typescript-go powered JS/TS linter written in Go\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · typescript-eslint/tsgolint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - oxc-project/tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"oxlint-tsgolint - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancement: Use TS 7 (tsgo / typescript-go) for type information · Issue #10940 · typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/issues/10940\"},{\"title\":\"Oxlint Introduces Type-Aware Linting Preview - Socket.dev\",\"url\":\"https://socket.dev/blog/oxlint-type-aware-linting-preview\"},{\"title\":\"Type-Aware Linting | Oxlint\",\"url\":\"https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/type-aware.html\"},{\"title\":\"tsgolint: An Experimental Go-Powered Linter for TypeScript/JavaScript - OSRepos\",\"url\":\"https://osrepos.com/repo/typescript-eslint-tsgolint\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about tsgolint and its relationship with typescript-eslint and tsgo. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Overview\n\ntsgolint is an experimental proof-of-concept typescript-go powered JS/TS linter written in Go. It was created to explore faster typed linting with ESLint using TypeScript's Go port (tsgo / typescript-go) for type information.\n\n## Development Status\n\ntsgolint is a prototype in the early stages of development and is not actively being worked on, nor is it expected to be production ready. However, the project has evolved since its original creation.\n\n## Key Features\n\nThe architecture eliminates TS AST to ESTree AST conversions, with TS AST directly used in rules. Additionally, it supports parallel parsing, type checking and linting, using all available CPU cores.\n\n## Evolution and Current State\n\nThe functionality was forked from the original prototype under the typescript-eslint project, with the Oxc project adopting and slimming down the tool to focus solely on type-aware linting rules. tsgolint is now stable and powers Oxlint's type-aware linting mode.\n\n## Performance\n\nThe tool demonstrates a 20-40x speedup over ESLint + typescript-eslint by using native parsing, direct TS AST usage, and parallel processing.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9b242c3d-91c9-44dd-be3f-3650f13d7156","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:42.795Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"tsgolint typescript-eslint tsgo type information linter","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GrDeF5vgpeTgBdGLfHViD8","content":[{"title":"tsgolint/README.md at main · typescript-eslint/tsgolint","url":"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint/blob/main/README.md"},{"title":"GitHub - typescript-eslint/tsgolint: ✨ Experimental proof-of-concept typescript-go powered JS/TS linter written in Go","url":"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint"},{"title":"Releases · typescript-eslint/tsgolint","url":"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint/releases"},{"title":"GitHub - oxc-project/tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint"},{"title":"oxlint-tsgolint - npm","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-tsgolint"},{"title":"Enhancement: Use TS 7 (tsgo / typescript-go) for type information · Issue #10940 · typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint","url":"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/issues/10940"},{"title":"Oxlint Introduces Type-Aware Linting Preview - Socket.dev","url":"https://socket.dev/blog/oxlint-type-aware-linting-preview"},{"title":"Type-Aware Linting | Oxlint","url":"https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/type-aware.html"},{"title":"tsgolint: An Experimental Go-Powered Linter for TypeScript/JavaScript - OSRepos","url":"https://osrepos.com/repo/typescript-eslint-tsgolint"}]},"I found comprehensive information about tsgolint and its relationship with typescript-eslint and tsgo. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Overview\n\ntsgolint is an experimental proof-of-concept typescript-go powered JS/TS linter written in Go. It was created to explore faster typed linting with ESLint using TypeScript's Go port (tsgo / typescript-go) for type information.\n\n## Development Status\n\ntsgolint is a prototype in the early stages of development and is not actively being worked on, nor is it expected to be production ready. However, the project has evolved since its original creation.\n\n## Key Features\n\nThe architecture eliminates TS AST to ESTree AST conversions, with TS AST directly used in rules. Additionally, it supports parallel parsing, type checking and linting, using all available CPU cores.\n\n## Evolution and Current State\n\nThe functionality was forked from the original prototype under the typescript-eslint project, with the Oxc project adopting and slimming down the tool to focus solely on type-aware linting rules. tsgolint is now stable and powers Oxlint's type-aware linting mode.\n\n## Performance\n\nThe tool demonstrates a 20-40x speedup over ESLint + typescript-eslint by using native parsing, direct TS AST usage, and parallel processing."],"durationSeconds":7.333319833993912,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0ba5fd7d-5483-496c-8e3b-80f86ae7c39e","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"9b242c3d-91c9-44dd-be3f-3650f13d7156","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebSearch","toolUseID":"toolu_0187jiPKZW2QwCdpSh3z5dUC","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebSearch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":52},"type":"attachment","uuid":"efa1ee00-496c-49d3-92d6-b6593808c460","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:42.794Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"5221c0d4-6f5f-48a5-9d91-141ff31bad17","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6925474d-182b-4bb8-800a-56f9380f5559","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019dYLNeTjMmTznt5wyRrMGX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"oxlint tsgolint type-aware linting 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Type-Aware Linting | Oxlint\",\"url\":\"https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/type-aware.html\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Oxlint Type-Aware Linting Alpha | VoidZero\",\"url\":\"https://voidzero.dev/posts/announcing-oxlint-type-aware-linting-alpha\"},{\"title\":\"Migrating from ESLint to Oxlint: A Practical Guide | by Chirag | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@chirag.dev18/migrating-from-eslint-to-oxlint-a-practical-guide-f9795083342d\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Oxlint Type-Aware Linting | VoidZero\",\"url\":\"https://voidzero.dev/posts/announcing-oxlint-type-aware-linting\"},{\"title\":\"oxlint-tsgolint - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - sushichan044/oxc-project-tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sushichan044/oxc-project-tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tsgolint/oxc-project: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tsgolint/oxc-project\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - oxc-project/tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"Type-Aware Linting Stable\",\"url\":\"https://oxc.rs/blog/2026-07-22-type-aware-linting-stable\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about oxlint, tsgolint, and type-aware linting in 2026:\n\n## Overview\n\nIn Oxlint, type-aware linting is provided by tsgolint and is integrated into the Oxlint CLI and configuration system. tsgolint is a high-performant linter backend on top of typescript-go, the Go port of TypeScript.\n\n## Current Status in 2026\n\ntsgolint v7 is the type-aware linting engine behind Oxlint, tracking TypeScript v7.0.2 and bringing tsgolint to 59 of typescript-eslint's 61 type-aware rules. The latest announcement indicates that tsgolint is stable and powers Oxlint's type-aware linting mode.\n\n## How It Works\n\nOxlint (Rust) handles file traversal, ignore logic, configuration, non-type-aware rules, and reporting, while tsgolint (Go) builds TypeScript programs using typescript-go and executes type-aware rules, returning structured diagnostics to Oxlint.\n\n## Performance\n\ntsgolint is 20-40 times faster than ESLint + typescript-eslint. Initial oxlint with type-aware linting tests show repositories that previously took 1 minute to run with typescript-eslint now finish in <10 seconds.\n\n## Rule Coverage\n\ntsgolint executes lint rules that require TypeScript semantic analysis, using typescript-go for full compatibility with the TypeScript type system, and targets TypeScript 7 (codenamed Project Corsa).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"331f211f-f2a2-48fa-971c-ac5cc05191d2","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:42.932Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"oxlint tsgolint type-aware linting 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019zja68npUqZtSPTzJpHu86","content":[{"title":"Type-Aware Linting | Oxlint","url":"https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/type-aware.html"},{"title":"Announcing Oxlint Type-Aware Linting Alpha | VoidZero","url":"https://voidzero.dev/posts/announcing-oxlint-type-aware-linting-alpha"},{"title":"Migrating from ESLint to Oxlint: A Practical Guide | by Chirag | Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@chirag.dev18/migrating-from-eslint-to-oxlint-a-practical-guide-f9795083342d"},{"title":"Announcing Oxlint Type-Aware Linting | VoidZero","url":"https://voidzero.dev/posts/announcing-oxlint-type-aware-linting"},{"title":"oxlint-tsgolint - npm","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-tsgolint"},{"title":"GitHub - sushichan044/oxc-project-tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/sushichan044/oxc-project-tsgolint"},{"title":"GitHub - tsgolint/oxc-project: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/tsgolint/oxc-project"},{"title":"GitHub - oxc-project/tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint"},{"title":"Type-Aware Linting Stable","url":"https://oxc.rs/blog/2026-07-22-type-aware-linting-stable"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about oxlint, tsgolint, and type-aware linting in 2026:\n\n## Overview\n\nIn Oxlint, type-aware linting is provided by tsgolint and is integrated into the Oxlint CLI and configuration system. tsgolint is a high-performant linter backend on top of typescript-go, the Go port of TypeScript.\n\n## Current Status in 2026\n\ntsgolint v7 is the type-aware linting engine behind Oxlint, tracking TypeScript v7.0.2 and bringing tsgolint to 59 of typescript-eslint's 61 type-aware rules. The latest announcement indicates that tsgolint is stable and powers Oxlint's type-aware linting mode.\n\n## How It Works\n\nOxlint (Rust) handles file traversal, ignore logic, configuration, non-type-aware rules, and reporting, while tsgolint (Go) builds TypeScript programs using typescript-go and executes type-aware rules, returning structured diagnostics to Oxlint.\n\n## Performance\n\ntsgolint is 20-40 times faster than ESLint + typescript-eslint. Initial oxlint with type-aware linting tests show repositories that previously took 1 minute to run with typescript-eslint now finish in <10 seconds.\n\n## Rule Coverage\n\ntsgolint executes lint rules that require TypeScript semantic analysis, using typescript-go for full compatibility with the TypeScript type system, and targets TypeScript 7 (codenamed Project Corsa)."],"durationSeconds":7.678388000011444,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5221c0d4-6f5f-48a5-9d91-141ff31bad17","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"