{"parentUuid":"1224cef1-bc37-4f29-9f6b-c0ed2715ebe6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdTTuGCofDJmWmJ1JrrS7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HLZuCErL3kNBxC2jFUAFmm","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://oxc.rs/blog/2026-07-22-type-aware-linting-stable","prompt":"Explain the architecture of tsgolint's integration with oxlint: how oxlint (Rust) and tsgolint (Go, using typescript-go/tsgo) communicate, what tsgolint actually does (does it expose full type-checking/type resolution, or just lint rule execution?), what its installation/distribution model is, and whether it's usable as a standalone type-information provider outside of lint rules. Also note performance characteristics and current stability/rule coverage."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2481,"cache_read_input_tokens":80246,"output_tokens":698,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2481,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":698,"cache_read_input_tokens":80246,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2481},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdTTuF4bWBNwgcfzJAdhs","type":"assistant","uuid":"7272f1d8-a6a8-47da-b476-3ac4877751a7","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:49.856Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"7272f1d8-a6a8-47da-b476-3ac4877751a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdTTuGCofDJmWmJ1JrrS7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PJmXvLne7DYCPF6VBm4nFw","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint/blob/main/README.md","prompt":"Explain tsgolint's architecture: how it uses typescript-go (tsgo) for type checking, whether it exposes a general-purpose API/IPC protocol for querying type information (not just running built-in lint rules), what language it's written in, how rules are defined/extended, and what the IPC/communication protocol with a host process looks like."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2481,"cache_read_input_tokens":80246,"output_tokens":698,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2481,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":698,"cache_read_input_tokens":80246,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2481},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdTTuF4bWBNwgcfzJAdhs","type":"assistant","uuid":"d732ec76-52de-4fc1-b887-9eb5c44c01d3","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:51.393Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"7272f1d8-a6a8-47da-b476-3ac4877751a7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6925474d-182b-4bb8-800a-56f9380f5559","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HLZuCErL3kNBxC2jFUAFmm","type":"tool_result","content":"# tsgolint Architecture & Integration\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here's what we can determine about tsgolint's architecture:\n\n## Core Integration Model\n\nThe page indicates tsgolint functions as a **type-aware linting engine** integrated into Oxlint. Users invoke it through Oxlint's CLI with flags like `--type-aware` and `--type-check`, suggesting tsgolint operates as a component within Oxlint's execution pipeline rather than as a truly independent process.\n\n## Capabilities & Scope\n\ntsgolint appears focused specifically on **lint rule execution with type information** rather than exposing general-purpose type-checking APIs. The documentation states: \"Linting and type-checking then share the same TypeScript program, avoiding the duplicate setup and analysis required by a separate type-check command.\" This suggests tsgolint couples TypeScript's type resolution with rule evaluation, but the scope remains lint-centric.\n\nThe tool currently implements \"59 of typescript-eslint's 61 type-aware rules,\" indicating it transposes established ESLint rules into a type-informed context rather than building novel type-checking capabilities.\n\n## Distribution & Installation\n\nInstallation is npm-based: `pnpm add -D oxlint oxlint-tsgolint@7`. The versioning scheme ties directly to TypeScript releases (v7.0.2000 = TypeScript 7.0.2 + patch 0), suggesting pre-built binaries compatible with specific TypeScript versions.\n\n## Performance & Stability\n\nBenchmarks show \"12 to 18 times faster than ESLint with typescript-eslint\" across large codebases. The release represents \"Stable\" status, though the documentation notes only 59/61 typescript-eslint rules are covered.\n\n**Standalone usage as a type provider appears unsupported** based on available documentation."}]},"uuid":"f2a55f91-d692-40ff-951d-5320ee5134d0","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:58.670Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":139600,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# tsgolint Architecture & Integration\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here's what we can determine about tsgolint's architecture:\n\n## Core Integration Model\n\nThe page indicates tsgolint functions as a **type-aware linting engine** integrated into Oxlint. Users invoke it through Oxlint's CLI with flags like `--type-aware` and `--type-check`, suggesting tsgolint operates as a component within Oxlint's execution pipeline rather than as a truly independent process.\n\n## Capabilities & Scope\n\ntsgolint appears focused specifically on **lint rule execution with type information** rather than exposing general-purpose type-checking APIs. The documentation states: \"Linting and type-checking then share the same TypeScript program, avoiding the duplicate setup and analysis required by a separate type-check command.\" This suggests tsgolint couples TypeScript's type resolution with rule evaluation, but the scope remains lint-centric.\n\nThe tool currently implements \"59 of typescript-eslint's 61 type-aware rules,\" indicating it transposes established ESLint rules into a type-informed context rather than building novel type-checking capabilities.\n\n## Distribution & Installation\n\nInstallation is npm-based: `pnpm add -D oxlint oxlint-tsgolint@7`. The versioning scheme ties directly to TypeScript releases (v7.0.2000 = TypeScript 7.0.2 + patch 0), suggesting pre-built binaries compatible with specific TypeScript versions.\n\n## Performance & Stability\n\nBenchmarks show \"12 to 18 times faster than ESLint with typescript-eslint\" across large codebases. The release represents \"Stable\" status, though the documentation notes only 59/61 typescript-eslint rules are covered.\n\n**Standalone usage as a type provider appears unsupported** based on available documentation.","durationMs":6576,"url":"https://oxc.rs/blog/2026-07-22-type-aware-linting-stable"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7272f1d8-a6a8-47da-b476-3ac4877751a7","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"f2a55f91-d692-40ff-951d-5320ee5134d0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebFetch","toolUseID":"toolu_01HLZuCErL3kNBxC2jFUAFmm","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebFetch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":80},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2b1292a6-9675-4675-b32f-26bba9d8cb69","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:58.670Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
