{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01WgfHBzjuJQRSwzgT8RCB36","lastSequenceNum":15352}
{"parentUuid":"d732ec76-52de-4fc1-b887-9eb5c44c01d3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6925474d-182b-4bb8-800a-56f9380f5559","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PJmXvLne7DYCPF6VBm4nFw","type":"tool_result","content":"# tsgolint Architecture Overview\n\nBased on the README, here's what can be determined about tsgolint's design:\n\n## Language & Foundation\ntsgolint is **written in Go** and built as a proof-of-concept linter powered by Microsoft's typescript-go (tsgo) compiler. The project leverages tsgo for \"native speed parsing and type-checking.\"\n\n## Type Information Integration\nRather than converting TypeScript AST to ESTree format like typescript-eslint does, tsgolint uses the TS AST directly from typescript-go. This eliminates conversion overhead, contributing to its reported 20-40x performance improvement over ESLint.\n\n## Rule Architecture\nThe project implements **40 type-aware rules** currently, with rules apparently hardcoded into the linter rather than loaded via plugins. The README notes that \"JS-based plugins are not currently supported,\" though experimental support exists on a separate branch using the goja JavaScript engine.\n\n## API & Communication Protocol\nThe README provides **no documentation** about a general-purpose API, IPC protocol, or mechanism for querying type information beyond executing built-in lint rules. Such interfaces aren't mentioned as implemented features.\n\n## Important Context\nThe README emphasizes: **\"tsgolint is a prototype in the early stages of development. It is not actively being worked on,\"** and explicitly states this is an experiment without active development, serving only to explore architectural possibilities rather than represent planned directions for typescript-eslint itself."}]},"uuid":"d97bd125-2850-4195-ac19-62837225bf71","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:54:58.868Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":293762,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# tsgolint Architecture Overview\n\nBased on the README, here's what can be determined about tsgolint's design:\n\n## Language & Foundation\ntsgolint is **written in Go** and built as a proof-of-concept linter powered by Microsoft's typescript-go (tsgo) compiler. The project leverages tsgo for \"native speed parsing and type-checking.\"\n\n## Type Information Integration\nRather than converting TypeScript AST to ESTree format like typescript-eslint does, tsgolint uses the TS AST directly from typescript-go. This eliminates conversion overhead, contributing to its reported 20-40x performance improvement over ESLint.\n\n## Rule Architecture\nThe project implements **40 type-aware rules** currently, with rules apparently hardcoded into the linter rather than loaded via plugins. The README notes that \"JS-based plugins are not currently supported,\" though experimental support exists on a separate branch using the goja JavaScript engine.\n\n## API & Communication Protocol\nThe README provides **no documentation** about a general-purpose API, IPC protocol, or mechanism for querying type information beyond executing built-in lint rules. Such interfaces aren't mentioned as implemented features.\n\n## Important Context\nThe README emphasizes: **\"tsgolint is a prototype in the early stages of development. It is not actively being worked on,\"** and explicitly states this is an experiment without active development, serving only to explore architectural possibilities rather than represent planned directions for typescript-eslint itself.","durationMs":5884,"url":"https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint/blob/main/README.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d732ec76-52de-4fc1-b887-9eb5c44c01d3","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
