{"parentUuid":"b6230ee1-3597-4e2a-b517-a23b9e9bc0a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdTTvSq3jgoUx4gqMwh8t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1890,"cache_read_input_tokens":82727,"output_tokens":1491,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1491,"cache_read_input_tokens":82727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdTTvRa9HDoamvdwksuny","type":"assistant","uuid":"4176bf19-1e3c-4575-8e97-d708c9695f47","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:55:05.804Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"4176bf19-1e3c-4575-8e97-d708c9695f47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdTTvSq3jgoUx4gqMwh8t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Findings on tsgolint / tsgo relevance to our unresolvable-type gap (the composes stop-gap discussed earlier):\n\n**What tsgolint actually is:** A Go binary built on `typescript-go` (Microsoft's Go port of the TS compiler, \"tsgo\"/\"Project Corsa\"). It was originally a typescript-eslint prototype, since forked and slimmed down by the Oxc project specifically to power `oxlint --type-aware`. As of this week it hit stable (oxc.rs/blog/2026-07-22), covering 59/61 typescript-eslint type-aware rules, 12-40x faster than ESLint+typescript-eslint depending on the benchmark.\n\n**Architecture — this is the part that matters for us:** oxlint (Rust) handles file discovery/config/non-type-aware rules; it shells out to `oxlint-tsgolint` (a separate Go binary, published to npm) which builds a real `typescript-go` program and executes **hardcoded, built-in lint rules** against it, returning structured diagnostics back to oxlint. There is no general-purpose API, IPC protocol, or JSON mode for querying arbitrary type information — you can't ask it \"what does this conditional type resolve to\" the way you'd query `ts.TypeChecker`. Rules are compiled into the Go binary; JS-plugin rule support doesn't exist yet either (experimental branch only).\n\n**Answer to your actual question:** tsgolint doesn't give us a shortcut to real type resolution. It's a lint-rule executor, not an embeddable type-query service — using it would mean spawning a separate Go process per-file and having no way to ask it the specific question we need (\"what props does `Weird<'x'>` resolve to\"), only \"does rule X flag this line.\" The underlying `typescript-go` compiler is the thing with real type resolution, but consuming it directly means either FFI into Go (no Rust bindings exist) or shelling out to a tsgo/tsc-like process per file — which is exactly the performance cost our `composes` stop-gap was designed to avoid.\n\nSo: no viable path here for closing the generic-alias/conditional-type gap without reintroducing the type-checker performance cost we're trying to stay out of. The `composes` stop-gap (recording the raw unresolvable expression) remains the right-sized fix; a real fix for the remaining 6 outliers would require an actual embedded type checker, which is a fundamentally different tradeoff than what this tool is for.\n\nSources:\n- [Type-Aware Linting Stable](https://oxc.rs/blog/2026-07-22-type-aware-linting-stable)\n- [Type-Aware Linting | Oxlint](https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/linter/type-aware.html)\n- [tsgolint README (typescript-eslint/tsgolint)](https://github.com/typescript-eslint/tsgolint/blob/main/README.md)\n- [oxc-project/tsgolint](https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint)\n- [oxlint-tsgolint - npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-tsgolint)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1890,"cache_read_input_tokens":82727,"output_tokens":1491,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1491,"cache_read_input_tokens":82727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdTTvRa9HDoamvdwksuny","type":"assistant","uuid":"f4e51b29-8ec6-46d7-bd82-4b24eb401388","timestamp":"2026-07-27T23:55:16.580Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7",