{"parentUuid":"bfd48be0-d531-4fd8-aa11-c47556640048","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWqSqtftBnJFNLD4MAb3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SFqvp2Q4RPAKudeNX8JbcJ","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint","prompt":"Explain exactly how oxlint (the Rust process) communicates with tsgolint (the Go binary): process spawning, IPC mechanism (stdin/stdout, sockets, JSON-RPC, msgpack, etc.), how the TypeScript program/type-checker instance is built and shared, how diagnostics are serialized back, and any details on how typescript-go (tsgo) itself is invoked or embedded within tsgolint (is it a Go library dependency, a subprocess, LSP server, etc.)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":86227,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":413,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":86227,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":413,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":86227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":86227},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdWqSoqdy7vP6GrM5q7U1","type":"assistant","uuid":"41fb18fc-bda3-40ca-82de-4f8193b5e6b9","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:07.695Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"bfd48be0-d531-4fd8-aa11-c47556640048","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31441475-d6a0-4868-ba74-c8296e3b2e43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015fWENARahhh7jPbHjPWpLm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"oxlint tsgolint IPC protocol stdin stdout communication architecture\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Type-Aware Linting | oxc-project/oxc | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/oxc-project/oxc/5.6-type-aware-linting\"},{\"title\":\"Language Server support · Issue #71 · oxc-project/tsgolint\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint/issues/71\"},{\"title\":\"Oxlintはいかにしてtsgolintのlint ruleを呼び出しているのか - Speaker Deck\",\"url\":\"https://speakerdeck.com/syumai/how-oxlint-calls-tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Oxlint Type-Aware Linting | VoidZero\",\"url\":\"https://voidzero.dev/posts/announcing-oxlint-type-aware-linting\"},{\"title\":\"oxlint-tsgolint - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"Oxlint Type-Aware Preview\",\"url\":\"https://oxc.rs/blog/2025-08-17-oxlint-type-aware\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - oxc-project/tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint\"},{\"title\":\"oxlint-tsgolint - Tech Stack & Dependencies | DEVTOOL.TECH\",\"url\":\"https://npm.devtool.tech/explore/oxlint-tsgolint\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about the oxlint-tsgolint IPC communication architecture. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## Communication Protocol\n\nCommunication happens via stdin (input) and stdout (output). More specifically, writes the JSON payload to the child process's stdin and spawns a thread to consume stdout.\n\nAccording to additional details, the input to tsgolint is JSON, and the output is a custom binary format.\n\n## Subprocess Architecture\n\ntsgolint runs as a subprocess, operating in a headless mode. oxlint serves as the \"frontend\" for tsgolint, handling the CLI, path traversal, ignore logic, and diagnostic printing, while tsgolint acts as the backend for oxlint, accepting paths and configuration as input and outputting structured diagnostics.\n\n## Processing Flow\n\nThe architecture includes piping the JSON payload to the child process's stdin and processing by spawning a thread to consume stdout. Diagnostics from tsgolint are filtered against Oxc's DisableDirectives.\n\nThis IPC-based approach enables the common case to be extremely fast while enabling powerful type-aware checks when needed.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ea585027-c00e-4033-8a58-0dffdac64f29","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:11.805Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"oxlint tsgolint IPC protocol stdin stdout communication architecture","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FF4QjjTx5T9bSoLio8t5Pj","content":[{"title":"Type-Aware Linting | oxc-project/oxc | DeepWiki","url":"https://deepwiki.com/oxc-project/oxc/5.6-type-aware-linting"},{"title":"Language Server support · Issue #71 · oxc-project/tsgolint","url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint/issues/71"},{"title":"Oxlintはいかにしてtsgolintのlint ruleを呼び出しているのか - Speaker Deck","url":"https://speakerdeck.com/syumai/how-oxlint-calls-tsgolint"},{"title":"Announcing Oxlint Type-Aware Linting | VoidZero","url":"https://voidzero.dev/posts/announcing-oxlint-type-aware-linting"},{"title":"oxlint-tsgolint - npm","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/oxlint-tsgolint"},{"title":"Oxlint Type-Aware Preview","url":"https://oxc.rs/blog/2025-08-17-oxlint-type-aware"},{"title":"GitHub - oxc-project/tsgolint: Type aware linting for oxlint · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint"},{"title":"oxlint-tsgolint - Tech Stack & Dependencies | DEVTOOL.TECH","url":"https://npm.devtool.tech/explore/oxlint-tsgolint"}]},"I found relevant information about the oxlint-tsgolint IPC communication architecture. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## Communication Protocol\n\nCommunication happens via stdin (input) and stdout (output). More specifically, writes the JSON payload to the child process's stdin and spawns a thread to consume stdout.\n\nAccording to additional details, the input to tsgolint is JSON, and the output is a custom binary format.\n\n## Subprocess Architecture\n\ntsgolint runs as a subprocess, operating in a headless mode. oxlint serves as the \"frontend\" for tsgolint, handling the CLI, path traversal, ignore logic, and diagnostic printing, while tsgolint acts as the backend for oxlint, accepting paths and configuration as input and outputting structured diagnostics.\n\n## Processing Flow\n\nThe architecture includes piping the JSON payload to the child process's stdin and processing by spawning a thread to consume stdout. Diagnostics from tsgolint are filtered against Oxc's DisableDirectives.\n\nThis IPC-based approach enables the common case to be extremely fast while enabling powerful type-aware checks when needed."],"durationSeconds":6.982385833024979,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bfd48be0-d531-4fd8-aa11-c47556640048","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"ea585027-c00e-4033-8a58-0dffdac64f29","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebSearch","toolUseID":"toolu_015fWENARahhh7jPbHjPWpLm","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebSearch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":64},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9bcb15ad-0770-45fa-be13-3f983b186daa","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:11.804Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"41fb18fc-bda3-40ca-82de-4f8193b5e6b9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31441475-d6a0-4868-ba74-c8296e3b2e43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SFqvp2Q4RPAKudeNX8JbcJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Communication Between Oxlint and tsgolint\n\nBased on the provided documentation, specific technical details about the IPC mechanism, process spawning, serialization format, and typescript-go integration are **not explicitly documented** in this repository README.\n\n## What the Documentation Reveals\n\nThe README establishes the architectural relationship but omits implementation specifics:\n\n**Architecture Overview:**\nThe project describes a two-layer design where \"Oxlint handles file discovery, configuration, and output formatting, while `tsgolint` executes type-aware rules and emits semantic diagnostics.\"\n\n**typescript-go Integration:**\nThe documentation indicates that tsgolint \"runs directly on `typescript-go`\" and targets \"TypeScript 7 (codenamed **Project Corsa**).\" However, it doesn't clarify whether typescript-go operates as an embedded Go library dependency, a subprocess, or another integration pattern.\n\n**Where Implementation Details Exist:**\nThe README explicitly directs readers to \"ARCHITECTURE.md\" for \"Detailed technical documentation,\" suggesting that file contains the specific communication protocols, serialization methods (JSON-RPC, msgpack, etc.), and process spawning details you're asking about.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nTo answer your specific questions about stdin/stdout versus socket communication, JSON serialization format, TypeScript program instantiation, and how diagnostics traverse the system, you would need to consult the ARCHITECTURE.md file or examine the actual source code in the `internal/` and `cmd/tsgolint/` directories of the repository."}]},"uuid":"68b93448-fa20-4e84-8661-3178e3ade799","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:16.761Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":430294,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Communication Between Oxlint and tsgolint\n\nBased on the provided documentation, specific technical details about the IPC mechanism, process spawning, serialization format, and typescript-go integration are **not explicitly documented** in this repository README.\n\n## What the Documentation Reveals\n\nThe README establishes the architectural relationship but omits implementation specifics:\n\n**Architecture Overview:**\nThe project describes a two-layer design where \"Oxlint handles file discovery, configuration, and output formatting, while `tsgolint` executes type-aware rules and emits semantic diagnostics.\"\n\n**typescript-go Integration:**\nThe documentation indicates that tsgolint \"runs directly on `typescript-go`\" and targets \"TypeScript 7 (codenamed **Project Corsa**).\" However, it doesn't clarify whether typescript-go operates as an embedded Go library dependency, a subprocess, or another integration pattern.\n\n**Where Implementation Details Exist:**\nThe README explicitly directs readers to \"ARCHITECTURE.md\" for \"Detailed technical documentation,\" suggesting that file contains the specific communication protocols, serialization methods (JSON-RPC, msgpack, etc.), and process spawning details you're asking about.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nTo answer your specific questions about stdin/stdout versus socket communication, JSON serialization format, TypeScript program instantiation, and how diagnostics traverse the system, you would need to consult the ARCHITECTURE.md file or examine the actual source code in the `internal/` and `cmd/tsgolint/` directories of the repository.","durationMs":7001,"url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"41fb18fc-bda3-40ca-82de-4f8193b5e6b9","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main",