{"parentUuid":"4e55fdeb-f3e6-4929-b21c-92c8c53455f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWqTyAW9kzZeCfbwhk29","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JQjTi1ZBGrv5shi5PhhemU","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oxc-project/tsgolint/main/ARCHITECTURE.md","prompt":"Extract full technical detail on the IPC protocol between oxlint and tsgolint: process spawning, stdin JSON schema, stdout binary format, how typescript-go's Program/Checker is constructed, threading model, and process lifecycle."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2125,"cache_read_input_tokens":86227,"output_tokens":480,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":86227,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2125},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdWqTwnQiuHuUajxrFtzw","type":"assistant","uuid":"dffec015-d976-47e0-a5d0-5d9576909935","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:22.492Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"4e55fdeb-f3e6-4929-b21c-92c8c53455f8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31441475-d6a0-4868-ba74-c8296e3b2e43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4afLqaQcYGsd3ZbFLXH7D","type":"tool_result","content":"# Technical Analysis: Oxlint-to-Tsgolint Communication\n\n## Process Spawning and Lifecycle\n\nOxlint spawns tsgolint as a subprocess during linting initialization. The architecture uses a \"one-shot per run\" model rather than a persistent daemon. The `TsGoLintState` manages subprocess lifecycle through the `spawn_tsgolint` function, which executes the Go binary when type-aware rules are active or the `--type-check-only` flag is used.\n\n## JSON Input Protocol\n\nOxlint communicates via stdin using structured JSON payloads through the `TsGoLintPayload` data structure containing:\n\n- **paths**: Vector of file paths to analyze\n- **configs**: File-to-rule-settings mappings for granular configuration\n- **tsconfigPath**: TypeScript configuration file location\n- **typeCheck**: Boolean flag controlling compiler diagnostic reporting\n\nThe payload is serialized and written to the subprocess's stdin before linting commences.\n\n## Output Stream Format\n\nThe documentation mentions \"line-delimited JSON\" output from tsgolint's stdout, parsed through `TsGoLintMessageStream`, an iterator consuming the subprocess output. Three message variants are defined:\n\n- `Diagnostic` messages containing rule violations or compiler errors\n- `Error` messages for fatal linter failures  \n- `Heartbeat` signals for keep-alive purposes\n\n## TypeScript Program Construction\n\nThe documentation does not explicitly detail how typescript-go's TypeScript compiler/checker is initialized within tsgolint's Go binary. This internal architecture remains undocumented in the provided content.\n\n## Coordination and Filtering\n\nDiagnostics from tsgolint are post-processed against Oxlint's collected `DisableDirectives`, allowing user comments to suppress external findings. UTF-16 to UTF-8 offset conversion occurs during fix handling due to TypeScript's character encoding convention."}]},"uuid":"6f9d5790-6820-442b-94c9-b497f2276b88","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:30.053Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":1211551,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Technical Analysis: Oxlint-to-Tsgolint Communication\n\n## Process Spawning and Lifecycle\n\nOxlint spawns tsgolint as a subprocess during linting initialization. The architecture uses a \"one-shot per run\" model rather than a persistent daemon. The `TsGoLintState` manages subprocess lifecycle through the `spawn_tsgolint` function, which executes the Go binary when type-aware rules are active or the `--type-check-only` flag is used.\n\n## JSON Input Protocol\n\nOxlint communicates via stdin using structured JSON payloads through the `TsGoLintPayload` data structure containing:\n\n- **paths**: Vector of file paths to analyze\n- **configs**: File-to-rule-settings mappings for granular configuration\n- **tsconfigPath**: TypeScript configuration file location\n- **typeCheck**: Boolean flag controlling compiler diagnostic reporting\n\nThe payload is serialized and written to the subprocess's stdin before linting commences.\n\n## Output Stream Format\n\nThe documentation mentions \"line-delimited JSON\" output from tsgolint's stdout, parsed through `TsGoLintMessageStream`, an iterator consuming the subprocess output. Three message variants are defined:\n\n- `Diagnostic` messages containing rule violations or compiler errors\n- `Error` messages for fatal linter failures  \n- `Heartbeat` signals for keep-alive purposes\n\n## TypeScript Program Construction\n\nThe documentation does not explicitly detail how typescript-go's TypeScript compiler/checker is initialized within tsgolint's Go binary. This internal architecture remains undocumented in the provided content.\n\n## Coordination and Filtering\n\nDiagnostics from tsgolint are post-processed against Oxlint's collected `DisableDirectives`, allowing user comments to suppress external findings. UTF-16 to UTF-8 offset conversion occurs during fix handling due to TypeScript's character encoding convention.","durationMs":6557,"url":"https://deepwiki.com/oxc-project/oxc/5.6-type-aware-linting"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4e55fdeb-f3e6-4929-b21c-92c8c53455f8","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"6f9d5790-6820-442b-94c9-b497f2276b88","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebFetch","toolUseID":"toolu_01H4afLqaQcYGsd3ZbFLXH7D","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebFetch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":66},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c83a2fa1-27c5-478e-81da-b93cf663b769","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:30.053Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"dffec015-d976-47e0-a5d0-5d9576909935","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31441475-d6a0-4868-ba74-c8296e3b2e43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JQjTi1ZBGrv5shi5PhhemU","type":"tool_result","content":"# IPC Protocol Analysis\n\nBased on the provided documentation, **specific technical details about the IPC protocol are not disclosed**. The architecture document describes the conceptual relationship between Oxlint and tsgolint but omits implementation specifics.\n\n## What the Documentation Reveals\n\n**High-level integration model:**\nThe architecture shows Oxlint as the \"frontend\" handling \"File discovery, configuration, output formatting, rule orchestration\" while tsgolint serves as the \"backend\" providing \"Type-aware rule execution, TypeScript integration, and diagnostic generation.\"\n\n**Process model hint:**\nThe diagram references \"Master Thread → [Worker Pool]\" with \"Files + Rules → Rule Execution → Output,\" suggesting work distribution across CPU cores.\n\n## What Remains Undocumented\n\nThe document deliberately avoids specification of:\n\n- Process spawning mechanisms or lifecycle management\n- JSON schema for stdin communication\n- Binary format for stdout diagnostics\n- Program/Checker construction methodology\n- Threading synchronization details\n- Inter-process communication protocol specifics\n\n## Notable Transparency Note\n\nThe document explicitly states: \"This approach is not recommended for production use. We're waiting for official typescript-go APIs,\" indicating the implementation uses undocumented internal interfaces via Go's `linkname` directives.\n\n**Conclusion:** The provided content prioritizes architectural philosophy over protocol specification, likely because implementation details remain in flux pending official typescript-go stabilization."}]},"uuid":"e831e65c-0f25-46c6-a269-765295a525db","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:31.106Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":4186,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# IPC Protocol Analysis\n\nBased on the provided documentation, **specific technical details about the IPC protocol are not disclosed**. The architecture document describes the conceptual relationship between Oxlint and tsgolint but omits implementation specifics.\n\n## What the Documentation Reveals\n\n**High-level integration model:**\nThe architecture shows Oxlint as the \"frontend\" handling \"File discovery, configuration, output formatting, rule orchestration\" while tsgolint serves as the \"backend\" providing \"Type-aware rule execution, TypeScript integration, and diagnostic generation.\"\n\n**Process model hint:**\nThe diagram references \"Master Thread → [Worker Pool]\" with \"Files + Rules → Rule Execution → Output,\" suggesting work distribution across CPU cores.\n\n## What Remains Undocumented\n\nThe document deliberately avoids specification of:\n\n- Process spawning mechanisms or lifecycle management\n- JSON schema for stdin communication\n- Binary format for stdout diagnostics\n- Program/Checker construction methodology\n- Threading synchronization details\n- Inter-process communication protocol specifics\n\n## Notable Transparency Note\n\nThe document explicitly states: \"This approach is not recommended for production use. We're waiting for official typescript-go APIs,\" indicating the implementation uses undocumented internal interfaces via Go's `linkname` directives.\n\n**Conclusion:** The provided content prioritizes architectural philosophy over protocol specification, likely because implementation details remain in flux pending official typescript-go stabilization.","durationMs":6191,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oxc-project/tsgolint/main/ARCHITECTURE.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dffec015-d976-47e0-a5d0-5d9576909935","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
