{"parentUuid":"a66aa1ab-4a2f-49ae-963c-e87ceb0b0392","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWqV2c9jo1V1DTSg85to","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":88352,"output_tokens":1094,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1744,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1094,"cache_read_input_tokens":88352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1744},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdWqV19qZKy1WCcSkpFYy","type":"assistant","uuid":"3615d3e0-08b7-47f1-accc-d88863dbf4a2","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:33.744Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"3615d3e0-08b7-47f1-accc-d88863dbf4a2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWqV2c9jo1V1DTSg85to","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full picture, and there's a genuinely interesting wrinkle in it.\n\n**The interaction is a one-shot subprocess pipeline, not an embedded library call:**\n\n1. **Spawn.** Oxlint (Rust) spawns `tsgolint` as a child process per lint run — not a persistent daemon — via a `TsGoLintState`/`spawn_tsgolint` path, triggered whenever type-aware rules are enabled or `--type-check-only` is passed.\n2. **Input over stdin.** Oxlint writes a single JSON payload (`TsGoLintPayload`) to the child's stdin: file paths to check, per-file rule configs, the `tsconfig.json` path, and a `typeCheck` bool for whether to also report raw compiler diagnostics.\n3. **Output over stdout.** tsgolint streams back **line-delimited JSON** — `Diagnostic`, `Error`, and `Heartbeat` message variants — which Oxlint consumes via a `TsGoLintMessageStream` iterator on a dedicated thread while the main process keeps linting non-type-aware rules in parallel.\n4. **Reconciliation.** Oxlint filters tsgolint's diagnostics against its own `DisableDirectives` (so `// oxlint-disable` comments suppress externally-sourced findings too) and converts TypeScript's UTF-16 offsets to UTF-8 for its own diagnostic spans.\n\n**The interesting part, and the one relevant to what we discussed earlier:** tsgolint's own `ARCHITECTURE.md` admits it reaches into `typescript-go` through **Go `linkname` directives** — i.e. it's binding to typescript-go's *unexported/internal* symbols, not a stable public API, because typescript-go doesn't expose one yet. The doc says outright this \"is not recommended for production use,\" and that they're waiting on typescript-go to publish official APIs. So even the Oxc team's own integration with tsgo is a load-bearing hack around a compiler that hasn't committed to an embedding contract yet.\n\nThat reinforces the earlier conclusion for us: there's no stable, embeddable \"ask tsgo a type question\" interface to borrow, even unofficially — what exists is a fragile, linkname-based binding purpose-built for running a fixed set of lint rules, wrapped in a stdin/stdout subprocess protocol tuned for oxlint's specific I/O shape, not a general type-query service we could point at our resolver's dead ends.\n\nSources:\n- [Type-Aware Linting | oxc-project/oxc — DeepWiki](https://deepwiki.com/oxc-project/oxc/5.6-type-aware-linting)\n- [oxc-project/tsgolint](https://github.com/oxc-project/tsgolint)\n- [Oxlintはいかにしてtsgolintのlint ruleを呼び出しているのか](https://speakerdeck.com/syumai/how-oxlint-calls-tsgolint)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":88352,"output_tokens":1094,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1744,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1094,"cache_read_input_tokens":88352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1744},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdWqV19qZKy1WCcSkpFYy","type":"assistant","uuid":"96eae38b-ebc0-4f6a-8e7c-34cb20277e99","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:39:44.232Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
