{"parentUuid":"2524175b-6a65-452c-b60c-7b3b58de1894","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a1660bcf-696d-476b-9ca2-b0dc79ad750a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WutGHyWuZfxUhPGM6hZqPy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"TypeScript 7 typescript-go preview release npm @typescript/native-preview\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"TypeScript Native / TypeScript 7 (`@typescript/native-preview`, `tsgo`) Support · Issue #5381 · vuejs/language-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/vuejs/language-tools/issues/5381\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7.0 RC Moves Microsoft's Go Rewrite Into the Mainline Compiler -- Visual Studio Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/06/22/typescript-7-0-rc-moves-microsofts-go-rewrite-into-the-mainline-compiler.aspx\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 RC - TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-rc/\"},{\"title\":\"@typescript/native-preview - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@typescript/native-preview\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - microsoft/typescript-go: Staging repo for development of native port of TypeScript · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing TypeScript Native Previews - TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-native-previews/\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 Is Here: The Go Compiler Rewrite | Dennis Morello\",\"url\":\"https://morello.dev/blog/typescript-7-is-here\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7.0 RC: The Go-Native Compiler Has Landed\",\"url\":\"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-0-rc-go-native-compiler-2026-upgrade-guide\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 (tsgo): 10x Faster Compiler in 2026 | Nerd Level Tech\",\"url\":\"https://nerdleveltech.com/typescript-7-native-compiler-tsgo\"},{\"title\":\"@typescript/native-preview - npmx\",\"url\":\"https://npmx.dev/package/@typescript/native-preview\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about TypeScript 7, typescript-go, and the @typescript/native-preview package:\n\n## Overview\n\nTypeScript on Go (also known as TypeScript 7 or TypeScript Native) has been released as a public preview. The TypeScript team announced TypeScript 7.0 RC on June 18, describing it as a release built on \"a completely new foundation.\"\n\n## The @typescript/native-preview Package\n\nThis package provides a preview build of the native port of TypeScript. Not all features are implemented yet. This package is intended for testing and experimentation.\n\n## Installation and Usage\n\nFor the preview phase: You can install @typescript/native-preview and use the tsgo command. For TypeScript 7.0 RC and later, the command name is tsc.\n\nDuring the beta and nightly phases, the native compiler was only available under @typescript/native-preview with a binary named tsgo. As of the RC, the recommended path is the standard package: npm install -D typescript@rc. The tsc binary from that package is the Go-native compiler.\n\n## Performance\n\nThe native implementation was expected to \"drastically improve editor startup, reduce most build times by 10x, and substantially reduce memory usage.\"\n\n## Future Plans\n\nMicrosoft said that once TypeScript 7 is published with the latest npm tag, it expects \"all stable releases, major pre-releases, and nightlies\" to be published under the typescript package.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0da8f16f-4ad7-4171-aaec-aa579597c3f4","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:41:40.738Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"TypeScript 7 typescript-go preview release npm @typescript/native-preview","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Bvsu2NzuFZaz5YgpnyCYtH","content":[{"title":"TypeScript Native / TypeScript 7 (`@typescript/native-preview`, `tsgo`) Support · Issue #5381 · vuejs/language-tools","url":"https://github.com/vuejs/language-tools/issues/5381"},{"title":"TypeScript 7.0 RC Moves Microsoft's Go Rewrite Into the Mainline Compiler -- Visual Studio Magazine","url":"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/06/22/typescript-7-0-rc-moves-microsofts-go-rewrite-into-the-mainline-compiler.aspx"},{"title":"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 RC - TypeScript","url":"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-rc/"},{"title":"@typescript/native-preview - npm","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@typescript/native-preview"},{"title":"GitHub - microsoft/typescript-go: Staging repo for development of native port of TypeScript · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go"},{"title":"Announcing TypeScript Native Previews - TypeScript","url":"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-native-previews/"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 Is Here: The Go Compiler Rewrite | Dennis Morello","url":"https://morello.dev/blog/typescript-7-is-here"},{"title":"TypeScript 7.0 RC: The Go-Native Compiler Has Landed","url":"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-0-rc-go-native-compiler-2026-upgrade-guide"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 (tsgo): 10x Faster Compiler in 2026 | Nerd Level Tech","url":"https://nerdleveltech.com/typescript-7-native-compiler-tsgo"},{"title":"@typescript/native-preview - npmx","url":"https://npmx.dev/package/@typescript/native-preview"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about TypeScript 7, typescript-go, and the @typescript/native-preview package:\n\n## Overview\n\nTypeScript on Go (also known as TypeScript 7 or TypeScript Native) has been released as a public preview. The TypeScript team announced TypeScript 7.0 RC on June 18, describing it as a release built on \"a completely new foundation.\"\n\n## The @typescript/native-preview Package\n\nThis package provides a preview build of the native port of TypeScript. Not all features are implemented yet. This package is intended for testing and experimentation.\n\n## Installation and Usage\n\nFor the preview phase: You can install @typescript/native-preview and use the tsgo command. For TypeScript 7.0 RC and later, the command name is tsc.\n\nDuring the beta and nightly phases, the native compiler was only available under @typescript/native-preview with a binary named tsgo. As of the RC, the recommended path is the standard package: npm install -D typescript@rc. The tsc binary from that package is the Go-native compiler.\n\n## Performance\n\nThe native implementation was expected to \"drastically improve editor startup, reduce most build times by 10x, and substantially reduce memory usage.\"\n\n## Future Plans\n\nMicrosoft said that once TypeScript 7 is published with the latest npm tag, it expects \"all stable releases, major pre-releases, and nightlies\" to be published under the typescript package."],"durationSeconds":9.36325091701746,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2524175b-6a65-452c-b60c-7b3b58de1894","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"0da8f16f-4ad7-4171-aaec-aa579597c3f4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebSearch","toolUseID":"toolu_01WutGHyWuZfxUhPGM6hZqPy","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebSearch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":62},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f8d24320-33bf-4d30-a57f-72c254bbe687","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:41:40.737Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"f8d24320-33bf-4d30-a57f-72c254bbe687","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Explanatory"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"136e977b-68ef-4842-80e2-ad335f424d2d","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:41:40.741Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"136e977b-68ef-4842-80e2-ad335f424d2d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdWqeaPbaba8bc552gHTF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — actually, this moved fast since the last time this topic came up in TypeScript's own roadmap. To answer precisely:\n\n- **`@typescript/native-preview`** was the original early-release channel — an npm package shipping just the Go-native compiler binary (`tsgo` command) for testing, separate from mainline `typescript`.\n- It's since graduated: **TypeScript 7.0 hit RC on 2026-06-18**, and at that point the native compiler moved into the standard `typescript@rc` package itself (binary renamed from `tsgo` to the normal `tsc`). **TypeScript 7.0 went GA on 2026-07-08** — so as of now (late July), it's not a preview anymore, it's the shipping compiler, installable as plain `typescript@latest`, ~10x faster than TS 6.\n\n**But the piece that actually matters for what we discussed:** Microsoft has explicitly said the **stable programmatic/embedding API is not landing until TypeScript 7.1** — several months out from 7.0 GA. That's exactly the gap tsgolint's `ARCHITECTURE.md` was apologizing for (the `linkname`-into-internals hack, \"not recommended for production, waiting for official typescript-go APIs\"). So even with TS 7 now stable and installable, the thing we'd actually want to embed — a documented, stable way to ask the compiler \"resolve this type\" from outside — still doesn't exist yet. tsgolint's fragile binding remains the only way anyone's doing that today, 7.1 is when it's supposed to become a real option.\n\nSources:\n- [Announcing TypeScript 7.0 RC](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-rc/)\n- [TypeScript 7.0 RC Moves Microsoft's Go Rewrite Into the Mainline Compiler](https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/06/22/typescript-7-0-rc-moves-microsofts-go-rewrite-into-the-mainline-compiler.aspx)\n- [@typescript/native-preview - npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@typescript/native-preview)\n- [microsoft/typescript-go](https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2772,"cache_read_input_tokens":91244,"output_tokens":757,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":91244,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2772},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdWqeZFPDrZ9fnMom31mw","type":"assistant","uuid":"89badf66-ab54-4ada-8ada-e4197b6b222a","timestamp":"2026-07-29T18:41:52.436Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
