{"parentUuid":"1206f77f-9580-4bb2-afa6-e76c11066a98","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdX5RjcFEzS9sP6ApQBEq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qi3xmqQCgr6zcc63yK26LL","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"TypeScript 7.1 roadmap typescript-go public API embedding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":94835,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":138,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":94835,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":138,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":94835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":94835},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdX5RhUFyKVT6roFt6iAb","type":"assistant","uuid":"703f5fb6-9ba4-4d53-8b09-9aa9e43c2ebb","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:24.779Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"703f5fb6-9ba4-4d53-8b09-9aa9e43c2ebb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b870b22e-d218-4f4a-9a72-07f61da3639f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qi3xmqQCgr6zcc63yK26LL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"TypeScript 7.1 roadmap typescript-go public API embedding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Potential Public-Facing Go API for Embedding? · microsoft/typescript-go · Discussion #481\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go/discussions/481\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 Arrives to Rock VS Code with Go-Powered Speed -- Visual Studio Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/07/08/typescript-7-arrives-to-rock-vs-code-with-go-powered-speed.aspx\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7.0 RC Moves Microsoft's Go Rewrite Into the Mainline Compiler -- Visual Studio Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/06/22/typescript-7-0-rc-moves-microsofts-go-rewrite-into-the-mainline-compiler.aspx\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 One Week In: Migration Readiness Check\",\"url\":\"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-native-compiler-early-adopter-migration-readiness\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 Is Here: The Go Compiler Rewrite | Dennis Morello\",\"url\":\"https://morello.dev/blog/typescript-7-is-here\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 is out - the native Go port, what changed, and what to watch | TypeScriptPro\",\"url\":\"https://typescriptpro.com/blog/typescript-version-7-2026-07-08\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 - TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 Beta - TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-beta/\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 Is Generally Available - What the Go-Native Compiler Actually Changes\",\"url\":\"https://braindetox.kr/en/posts/typescript_v7_go_release_2026.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about TypeScript 7.1 and the public API for embedding:\n\n## TypeScript 7.1 Roadmap: Public API\n\nThe TypeScript team expects TypeScript 7.1 to ship with a new and different API. Stable programmatic API support is not expected until TypeScript 7.1 at the earliest.\n\n## Current State (TypeScript 7.0)\n\nTypeScript 7.0 does not ship with a public compiler API. Microsoft has stated 7.1 will introduce a new (and different) API, and until then any tool that consumes the programmatic TypeScript API cannot run on TypeScript 7.\n\nTypeScript 7 does not yet expose a stable programmatic API, so tools such as Volar that embed TypeScript into their own compilers and language services can only currently rely on TypeScript 6.0.\n\n## Impact on Ecosystem\n\nThe programmatic Language Service API is still in progress, and the TypeScript team has indicated that the existing JS-based API surface will not be carried forward into TS 7. On the historical 3-4 month release cadence, 7.1 lands around October 2026 — and every tool that embeds the compiler, from lint rules to template checkers to custom analyzers, will then have a porting project of its own.\n\n## Compatibility Package\n\nMicrosoft published @typescript/typescript6 so TypeScript 7 can run side-by-side with TypeScript 6 for utilities such as typescript-eslint that still need compiler programmatic access.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b74f2a6e-d18d-43ef-838a-7dd14c77f5af","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:34.305Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"TypeScript 7.1 roadmap typescript-go public API embedding","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KaVv5sPzAP7nPKoRTnMkZa","content":[{"title":"Potential Public-Facing Go API for Embedding? · microsoft/typescript-go · Discussion #481","url":"https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go/discussions/481"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 Arrives to Rock VS Code with Go-Powered Speed -- Visual Studio Magazine","url":"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/07/08/typescript-7-arrives-to-rock-vs-code-with-go-powered-speed.aspx"},{"title":"TypeScript 7.0 RC Moves Microsoft's Go Rewrite Into the Mainline Compiler -- Visual Studio Magazine","url":"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/06/22/typescript-7-0-rc-moves-microsofts-go-rewrite-into-the-mainline-compiler.aspx"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 One Week In: Migration Readiness Check","url":"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-native-compiler-early-adopter-migration-readiness"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 Is Here: The Go Compiler Rewrite | Dennis Morello","url":"https://morello.dev/blog/typescript-7-is-here"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 is out - the native Go port, what changed, and what to watch | TypeScriptPro","url":"https://typescriptpro.com/blog/typescript-version-7-2026-07-08"},{"title":"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 - TypeScript","url":"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0/"},{"title":"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 Beta - TypeScript","url":"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-beta/"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 Is Generally Available - What the Go-Native Compiler Actually Changes","url":"https://braindetox.kr/en/posts/typescript_v7_go_release_2026.html"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about TypeScript 7.1 and the public API for embedding:\n\n## TypeScript 7.1 Roadmap: Public API\n\nThe TypeScript team expects TypeScript 7.1 to ship with a new and different API. Stable programmatic API support is not expected until TypeScript 7.1 at the earliest.\n\n## Current State (TypeScript 7.0)\n\nTypeScript 7.0 does not ship with a public compiler API. Microsoft has stated 7.1 will introduce a new (and different) API, and until then any tool that consumes the programmatic TypeScript API cannot run on TypeScript 7.\n\nTypeScript 7 does not yet expose a stable programmatic API, so tools such as Volar that embed TypeScript into their own compilers and language services can only currently rely on TypeScript 6.0.\n\n## Impact on Ecosystem\n\nThe programmatic Language Service API is still in progress, and the TypeScript team has indicated that the existing JS-based API surface will not be carried forward into TS 7. On the historical 3-4 month release cadence, 7.1 lands around October 2026 — and every tool that embeds the compiler, from lint rules to template checkers to custom analyzers, will then have a porting project of its own.\n\n## Compatibility Package\n\nMicrosoft published @typescript/typescript6 so TypeScript 7 can run side-by-side with TypeScript 6 for utilities such as typescript-eslint that still need compiler programmatic access."],"durationSeconds":9.435388083994388,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"703f5fb6-9ba4-4d53-8b09-9aa9e43c2ebb","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"b74f2a6e-d18d-43ef-838a-7dd14c77f5af","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebSearch","toolUseID":"toolu_01Qi3xmqQCgr6zcc63yK26LL","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebSearch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":86},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e7e368fa-d1ee-4bf7-a6a7-463336b9292b","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:34.304Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"1206f77f-9580-4bb2-afa6-e76c11066a98","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b870b22e-d218-4f4a-9a72-07f61da3639f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0149EDks3nuCQ9QPpVDNG3fG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"TypeScript 7.1 programmatic API status release date 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 Now Stable: 10× Faster Builds, But Not for Vue or Svelte Yet\",\"url\":\"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320049/20260710/typescript-7-now-stable-10-faster-builds-not-vue-svelte-yet.htm\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7.0 RC: The Go-Native Compiler Has Landed\",\"url\":\"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-0-rc-go-native-compiler-2026-upgrade-guide\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 6.x to 7.0 Migration Guide - Agent Guide · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/nafiskabbo/01ccb4970515413076f3759486c39755\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 One Week In: Migration Readiness Check\",\"url\":\"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-native-compiler-early-adopter-migration-readiness\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7.0 Is GA: The 10x Compiler Migration Playbook\",\"url\":\"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-0-ga-native-compiler-migration-playbook-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 Beta - TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-beta/\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 is out - the native Go port, what changed, and what to watch | TypeScriptPro\",\"url\":\"https://typescriptpro.com/blog/typescript-version-7-2026-07-08\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 RC - TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-rc/\"},{\"title\":\"TypeScript 7 Arrives to Rock VS Code with Go-Powered Speed -- Visual Studio Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/07/08/typescript-7-arrives-to-rock-vs-code-with-go-powered-speed.aspx\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about TypeScript 7.1's programmatic API and release date:\n\n## Release Date\n\nThe TypeScript team expects 7.1 on a timeline similar to prior releases: three to four months, which puts it in the vicinity of October 2026.\n\n## Programmatic API Status\n\nMicrosoft has described TypeScript 7.1 as the release that closes the remaining ecosystem gaps — primarily the stable programmatic API that will let Volar and framework template type-checkers adopt the native compiler.\n\nCurrently, TypeScript 7.0 ships without a stable programmatic API — Microsoft expects TypeScript 7.1 to deliver a new, different one — which means Vue, Angular's template type-checking, Svelte, Astro, MDX, and Volar-based tooling cannot run on 7.0 yet.\n\nIn summary, the stable programmatic API is expected to arrive with TypeScript 7.1 around October 2026, which would unlock ecosystem support for various frameworks and tools that currently cannot run on TypeScript 7.0.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"766e7a45-a09b-401b-938e-45a2aa5d7e47","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:35.719Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"TypeScript 7.1 programmatic API status release date 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NdggU87FsutxqpcRKsiimK","content":[{"title":"TypeScript 7 Now Stable: 10× Faster Builds, But Not for Vue or Svelte Yet","url":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320049/20260710/typescript-7-now-stable-10-faster-builds-not-vue-svelte-yet.htm"},{"title":"TypeScript 7.0 RC: The Go-Native Compiler Has Landed","url":"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-0-rc-go-native-compiler-2026-upgrade-guide"},{"title":"TypeScript 6.x to 7.0 Migration Guide - Agent Guide · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/nafiskabbo/01ccb4970515413076f3759486c39755"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 One Week In: Migration Readiness Check","url":"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-native-compiler-early-adopter-migration-readiness"},{"title":"TypeScript 7.0 Is GA: The 10x Compiler Migration Playbook","url":"https://www.digitalapplied.com/blog/typescript-7-0-ga-native-compiler-migration-playbook-2026"},{"title":"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 Beta - TypeScript","url":"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-beta/"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 is out - the native Go port, what changed, and what to watch | TypeScriptPro","url":"https://typescriptpro.com/blog/typescript-version-7-2026-07-08"},{"title":"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 RC - TypeScript","url":"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-rc/"},{"title":"TypeScript 7 Arrives to Rock VS Code with Go-Powered Speed -- Visual Studio Magazine","url":"https://visualstudiomagazine.com/articles/2026/07/08/typescript-7-arrives-to-rock-vs-code-with-go-powered-speed.aspx"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about TypeScript 7.1's programmatic API and release date:\n\n## Release Date\n\nThe TypeScript team expects 7.1 on a timeline similar to prior releases: three to four months, which puts it in the vicinity of October 2026.\n\n## Programmatic API Status\n\nMicrosoft has described TypeScript 7.1 as the release that closes the remaining ecosystem gaps — primarily the stable programmatic API that will let Volar and framework template type-checkers adopt the native compiler.\n\nCurrently, TypeScript 7.0 ships without a stable programmatic API — Microsoft expects TypeScript 7.1 to deliver a new, different one — which means Vue, Angular's template type-checking, Svelte, Astro, MDX, and Volar-based tooling cannot run on 7.0 yet.\n\nIn summary, the stable programmatic API is expected to arrive with TypeScript 7.1 around October 2026, which would unlock ecosystem support for various frameworks and tools that currently cannot run on TypeScript 7.0."],"durationSeconds":11.23565933305025,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1206f77f-9580-4bb2-afa6-e76c11066a98","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
