{"parentUuid":"02a41ea8-cbb3-4583-bf98-be82cded1797","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdX5SjanWRugSS1p9NUwT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F5Apscn8jauyVijfMpbqdU","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go/discussions/481","prompt":"Summarize the current state of discussion on a public-facing Go API for embedding typescript-go: what shape is being proposed (Go library API vs JSON-RPC/LSP-style service vs something else), what's confirmed vs still undecided, and any timeline mentioned for TypeScript 7.1."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2681,"cache_read_input_tokens":94835,"output_tokens":237,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2681,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":94835,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2681},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdX5SiuMdDTGpcxV82yxZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e27cb02-93c3-463b-b329-88d7845df436","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:41.289Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"6e27cb02-93c3-463b-b329-88d7845df436","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b870b22e-d218-4f4a-9a72-07f61da3639f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F5Apscn8jauyVijfMpbqdU","type":"tool_result","content":"# Public-Facing Go API for TypeScript: Discussion Summary\n\n## Current Proposal Shape\n\nThe discussion lacks a formally proposed API shape. Instead, community members are requesting **any** accessible surface, with several suggesting an unstable/experimental approach:\n\n- One developer noted: \"An `unstable/` or `x/` passthrough that re-exports what people already reach for would do, with a doc comment saying it breaks whenever\"\n- Current workarounds involve `go:linkname` shims to access internal packages, indicating demand exists regardless of official support\n\n## Confirmed Status\n\n**Officially planned:** Jake Bailey (collaborator) confirmed in July 2026 that the team \"are going to do it when we move the repo back to github.com/microsoft/TypeScript\"\n\n**Current reality:** All compiler functionality lives in `internal` packages, making external use impossible through normal imports.\n\n## What Remains Undecided\n\n- Specific API surface and stability guarantees\n- Versioning strategy (Go's semver expectations conflict with TypeScript's versioning)\n- Whether to provide C ABI bindings (dismissed as \"doubling the size\")\n\n## Timeline\n\nBailey stated a possible timeline of \"before 7.1\" for exposure once the repository merges back to the main TypeScript project, though obstacles around existing tags need resolution first."}]},"uuid":"03775402-8d30-4879-b8a4-68368991549f","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:51.004Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":678654,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Public-Facing Go API for TypeScript: Discussion Summary\n\n## Current Proposal Shape\n\nThe discussion lacks a formally proposed API shape. Instead, community members are requesting **any** accessible surface, with several suggesting an unstable/experimental approach:\n\n- One developer noted: \"An `unstable/` or `x/` passthrough that re-exports what people already reach for would do, with a doc comment saying it breaks whenever\"\n- Current workarounds involve `go:linkname` shims to access internal packages, indicating demand exists regardless of official support\n\n## Confirmed Status\n\n**Officially planned:** Jake Bailey (collaborator) confirmed in July 2026 that the team \"are going to do it when we move the repo back to github.com/microsoft/TypeScript\"\n\n**Current reality:** All compiler functionality lives in `internal` packages, making external use impossible through normal imports.\n\n## What Remains Undecided\n\n- Specific API surface and stability guarantees\n- Versioning strategy (Go's semver expectations conflict with TypeScript's versioning)\n- Whether to provide C ABI bindings (dismissed as \"doubling the size\")\n\n## Timeline\n\nBailey stated a possible timeline of \"before 7.1\" for exposure once the repository merges back to the main TypeScript project, though obstacles around existing tags need resolution first.","durationMs":7650,"url":"https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go/discussions/481"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6e27cb02-93c3-463b-b329-88d7845df436","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"03775402-8d30-4879-b8a4-68368991549f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:WebFetch","toolUseID":"toolu_01F5Apscn8jauyVijfMpbqdU","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"WebFetch\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":74},"type":"attachment","uuid":"54b6172f-58a5-4061-9d66-b7c82ca0d53e","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:51.004Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"54b6172f-58a5-4061-9d66-b7c82ca0d53e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Explanatory"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eeca5568-a5e3-42ac-b4f8-b08807839650","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:42:51.010Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"eeca5568-a5e3-42ac-b4f8-b08807839650","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdX5TsN8XYBoRnSn4syyp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Status: it's coming, but still loosely defined, and the timeline is \"aim for 7.1\" not \"committed for 7.1.\"\n\n**Release timeline:** No 7.1 date yet, but going by TypeScript's usual 3-4 month cadence off the 2026-07-08 GA of 7.0, expect roughly **October 2026**.\n\n**What 7.1 is actually supposed to fix:** the missing stable programmatic API. 7.0 shipped with none — the old JS-based Language Service API surface isn't being carried forward at all, and Microsoft has said 7.1's API will be \"new and different,\" not a port of the old one. This is why Vue/Volar, Angular template checking, Svelte, Astro, and MDX tooling are all stuck on TypeScript 6 right now — they embed the compiler programmatically and have nothing to embed against on 7.\n\n**The Go-side API discussion (microsoft/typescript-go#481)** is where the real design conversation lives, and it's less settled than the marketing \"7.1 will have an API\" framing suggests:\n\n- Everything compiler-internal currently sits in Go `internal/` packages — unreachable from outside the module by Go's own language rules. Today's only access path is the same `go:linkname` hack tsgolint uses (reaching into unexported symbols), which the team itself calls unsupported.\n- Jake Bailey (Microsoft, works on the port) confirmed in July 2026 the team **will** expose something, but tied it to an infrastructure step first: moving the `typescript-go` repo back into `microsoft/TypeScript` proper. His stated target was \"before 7.1\" — a goal, not a shipped commitment — and he flagged unresolved mechanics (existing git tags, versioning scheme) blocking even that repo merge.\n- No settled API shape yet. Community ask is mostly \"just give us an `unstable/`-prefixed passthrough of what we're already reaching for via linkname, documented as breaking anytime\" rather than a fully-designed stable contract.\n- A C ABI binding (which would matter more to us than a Go-only API, since we're Rust) was explicitly discussed and dismissed for now — one commenter noted it'd double binary size, no counter-proposal offered.\n- Go's own semver expectations vs. TypeScript's release versioning are flagged as an open, unresolved tension — i.e., even the *versioning strategy* for a future Go API isn't decided.\n\nNet for us: even optimistically, \"7.1 has a real API\" is Microsoft's stated intent, not a locked scope — and there's no signal yet of a C-ABI or FFI-friendly surface, which is the part that would actually matter for embedding from Rust rather than Go. Worth checking back closer to October, but not something to plan the `composes` gap around yet.\n\nSources:\n- [Potential Public-Facing Go API for Embedding? · Discussion #481](https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go/discussions/481)\n- [TypeScript 7 Now Stable: 10× Faster Builds, But Not for Vue or Svelte Yet](https://www.techtimes.com/articles/320049/20260710/typescript-7-now-stable-10-faster-builds-not-vue-svelte-yet.htm)\n- [Announcing TypeScript 7.0 RC](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-7-0-rc/)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":729,"cache_read_input_tokens":97516,"output_tokens":1126,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":729,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":97516,"cache_creation_input_tokens":729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":729},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdX5TrCgCFgn9buYCFBLC","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fa87444-507e-49b5-8d10-efbca2f4937e","timestamp":"2026-07-29T21:43:06.483Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
