{"parentUuid":"a10937aa-7cb4-49dd-9d0a-9c782f6bf749","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi4NkszKi8hQyNymux6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"output_tokens":8585,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8585,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi4NjDmn5BruE5v9CKUM","type":"assistant","uuid":"2460cd92-33d9-4ad4-b64e-b8a630ee3822","timestamp":"2026-08-04T16:55:24.837Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"2460cd92-33d9-4ad4-b64e-b8a630ee3822","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi4NkszKi8hQyNymux6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PcLsgfGVDHSCmVn9nNh1Ce","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit extractor subsystem edge cases","subagent_type":"Explore","name":"audit-extractor","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"We're doing a comprehensive edge-case/failure-mode audit of oxc-react-docgen (a Rust tool that parses TSX/TS with OXC and extracts React component prop metadata, a drop-in replacement for react-docgen-typescript). This is research/documentation only — do NOT modify any code.\n\nYour scope: the extractor subsystem in crates/core/src/extractor/ (mod.rs, component.rs, alias.rs, interface.rs, jsdoc.rs, defaults.rs, visit.rs) and crates/core/src/types/collected.rs. This is the OXC AST visitor layer: it walks parsed TSX/TS source and produces `SourceData` (component declarations, prop-relevant type declarations, JSDoc, default values) before any cross-file resolution happens.\n\nProject non-negotiables (from CLAUDE.md) you should check adherence to: no `unwrap()` outside `#[cfg(test)]` (must use `?`), no AST refs escape `parse_file()` (allocator is local per call), always emit a `Diagnostic` when degrading instead of failing silently.\n\nFor each source file in scope, identify:\n1. **Component detection edge cases**: unusual ways a React component can be declared/exported that the visitor might miss or mishandle — e.g. `export default function() {}` (anonymous), `export default memo(forwardRef(...))`, HOC-wrapped components, components defined via `Object.assign`, components as class expressions vs class declarations, components exported via `export { X as Y }` or `export * from`, components with no props param, components using `React.FC<Props>` vs plain function typing, generic components (`function Comp<T>(props: Props<T>)`), components declared in .ts (not .tsx) files, multiple components per file, components with the same name in different files.\n2. **Prop-type declaration parsing edge cases**: interfaces vs type aliases vs inline object literals, intersections/unions of many members, recursive/self-referential types, generic type parameters with defaults or constraints, mapped types, conditional types, template literal types, `as const`, satisfies expressions, re-exported types from other files, namespaced types (`Foo.Bar`), ambient/declare types.\n3. **JSDoc parsing edge cases**: malformed or partial JSDoc, `@default` tag variants, multi-line descriptions, JSDoc on re-exported/aliased types, missing JSDoc, JSDoc with unusual tag ordering, block comments that look like JSDoc but aren't (`/** */` on unrelated code).\n4. **Default value extraction edge cases**: destructured defaults (`{ foo = 'bar' }`), defaultProps static property (legacy class components), complex default expressions (function calls, spread, ternaries), defaults referencing outer-scope variables/constants.\n5. **Panic/crash risks**: any indexing, slicing, `.unwrap()`, `.expect()`, arithmetic that isn't behind a bounds/overflow check, when walking malformed or adversarial ASTs (e.g. deeply nested types causing stack overflow via recursion, extremely large files).\n6. **Silent failure risks**: places where a parse/extraction failure would just skip data with no `Diagnostic` emitted, violating the \"always emit Diagnostic when degrading\" rule.\n\nFor each finding, note: exact file:line, whether existing tests in crates/core/tests/ or inline #[cfg(test)] modules already cover it (search first), and severity (crash risk / silent data loss / known-and-documented limitation / cosmetic).\n\nReport as a structured list grouped by category (1-6 above). Be concrete — cite code, don't speculate abstractly. Aim for thoroughness over brevity; this feeds a comprehensive gap-tracking document. Under 2500 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"output_tokens":8585,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8585,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi4NjDmn5BruE5v9CKUM","type":"assistant","uuid":"d71027f8-04d1-4a62-9ab0-378e5c0af3d6","timestamp":"2026-08-04T16:55:40.961Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
