 macOS), files that change between discovery and read (TOCTOU).\n2. **Parallel parse/merge (rayon)**: what happens if one file panics mid-parse — does it poison the whole batch or degrade gracefully per-file? Race conditions in merging into GlobalSourceData. Determinism: does parallel execution produce the same output every run (important for caching/snapshot tests), or could iteration order cause nondeterminism in diagnostics ordering, component dedup winner selection, etc.?\n3. **Component name collisions / dedup**: same component name in different files (recently fixed per git history — verify current dedup key logic in mod.rs's extract() function is actually collision-proof; check the exact key construction), same file processed twice, case-sensitivity issues.\n4. **Cache subsystem** (cache.rs): what happens on a corrupted cache file (partial write from a crash, wrong msgpack version, disk full during atomic swap), concurrent processes sharing the same cache dir, cache dir on read-only filesystem, mtime granularity issues (some filesystems have 1s mtime resolution — could a fast edit+rebuild within the same second get a stale cache hit?), eviction correctness at exactly 5000 entries, negative/zero-size files.\n5. **Cross-package .d.ts resolution / import_map.rs**: package.json parsing edge cases (missing, malformed, no \"types\"/\"typings\" field, exports map complexity), monorepo workspace symlinks (pnpm/yarn), circular package dependencies, missing node_modules entirely.\n6. **Watch mode** (watch.rs): rapid successive file changes (debounce correctness), file deleted while being processed, editor atomic-save patterns (write to temp file + rename — does the watcher see the right final file?), watch mode + cache interaction correctness.\n7. **Panic/crash risks**: unwrap/expect/indexing/arithmetic, especially any that could be triggered by filesystem state outside the tool's control (untrusted/adversarial input isn't the threat model here, but real-world messy filesystems are).\n\nFor each finding: exact file:line, whether existing tests already cover it (check crates/core/tests/ first), severity. Report grouped by category 1-7, concrete with code citations. Under 2800 words.","teammate_id":"audit-pipeline@session-0ae3953f","agent_id":"audit-pipeline@session-0ae3953f","agent_type":"Explore","model":"claude-sonnet-5","name":"audit-pipeline","color":"yellow","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-0ae3953f","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"84036792-a417-411c-a644-ed4a635f0166","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"b56b2438-a4c1-4645-806c-31b53ae1d763","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","toolUseID":"toolu_01Axp28TJ8xkAWkdqy3pv9VZ","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Agent\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":65},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e4bb52e9-8682-4a63-8545-1df611664f19","timestamp":"2026-08-04T16:56:19.626Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"e4bb52e9-8682-4a63-8545-1df611664f19","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi4NkszKi8hQyNymux6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ANUVP9AaC4b2D7VH4Lqnv6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit CLI and config edge cases","subagent_type":"Explore","name":"audit-cli","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"We're doing a comprehensive edge-case/failure-mode audit of oxc-react-docgen (a Rust tool that parses TSX/TS with OXC and extracts React component prop metadata, a drop-in replacement for react-docgen-typescript). This is research/documentation only — do NOT modify any code.\n\nYour scope: crates/cli/src/ (main.rs, config.rs, output.rs, commands/extract.rs, commands/check.rs, commands/completions.rs, commands/inspect.rs, commands/lsp.rs, commands/schema.rs, commands/watch.rs, commands/mod.rs) and crates/binding/src/lib.rs + crates/binding/build.rs (thin NAPI wrapper). Read crates/cli/CLAUDE.md first for the project's own rules for this crate (no println! in command handlers — output.rs/tracing only; miette for errors; config.rs runs user's docgen.config.ts via node+tsx with config path passed via env var, not shell string, specifically to avoid command injection).\n\nIdentify edge cases and failure modes in:\n1. **Config loading** (config.rs): missing docgen.config.ts (should fall back to defaults — verify), malformed/syntactically-invalid config file, config file that throws at runtime, missing node or tsx on PATH, node/tsx version incompatibilities, config file with unexpected types (e.g. src as a string instead of array), extremely large config, config path with spaces/special shell characters (verify the env-var passing actually avoids injection in all code paths — check for any place that might still interpolate into a shell string), timeout/hang if the config script never exits or does something async that never resolves.\n2. **CLI argument parsing** (main.rs, ExtractArgs etc.): conflicting flags, --out path that doesn't exist / isn't writable / is a directory, --format combined with --json (check documented precedence is actually enforced), invalid --react-version strings, empty --src list, --cache-dir pointing somewhere unwritable, --extra-builtins with malformed entries.\n3. **Exit code correctness**: every command's exit code paths — does every error condition map to a sensible, documented exit code? Cross-check cmd_extract's error-diagnostic-severity logic (already has tests for --json exit code) against check.rs, inspect.rs, schema.rs, lsp.rs, watch.rs — do they all handle the \"extraction produced Error-severity diagnostics\" case consistently, or do some silently exit 0?\n4. **Output writing**: what happens if --out write fails partway (disk full, permission denied) — is any partial file left behind? Does watch.rs handle repeated writes to the same --out path safely?\n5. **watch.rs command**: startup behavior if the initial extraction already has errors, behavior on Ctrl-C mid-extraction, terminal output interleaving with progress indicators.\n6. **lsp.rs**: malformed LSP requests, requests for files outside the configured src_dirs, hover requests on positions with no component/prop at that location, protocol errors (malformed JSON-RPC framing), what happens before the initial full extraction completes (race between \"ready\" and first request).\n7. **schema.rs**: does the exported JSON Schema stay in sync with the actual serde output of ComponentEntry/ExtractionOutput, or could they drift silently?\n8. **NAPI binding** (crates/binding): panics crossing the FFI boundary into Node (Rust panic = UB/crash in NAPI unless caught — check if there's a catch_unwind or equivalent), thread-safety of any shared state, what a Node caller sees on a Rust-side error (proper JS Error vs opaque crash).\n9. **Panic/crash risks**: unwrap/expect/indexing anywhere in scope, particularly on user-controlled input (CLI args, config file contents, file paths).\n\nFor each finding: exact file:line, whether existing tests already cover it (check crates/cli/tests/ and inline test modules first — note there's now a crates/cli/tests/ directory, check what's there), severity. Report grouped by category 1-9, concrete with code citations. Under 2800 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"output_tokens":8585,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8585,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi4NjDmn5BruE5v9CKUM","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1878d4f-49a4-4d5b-8785-cd43eff77263","timestamp":"2026-08-04T16:56:34.670Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"f1878d4f-49a4-4d5b-8785-cd43eff77263","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31ac2396-b3e2-4a0c-aa3a-65aa0375a150","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ANUVP9AaC4b2D7VH4Lqnv6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawned successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the ID below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagent_id: audit-cli@session-0ae3953f\nname: audit-cli\nThe agent is now running and will receive instructions via mailbox."}]}]},"uuid":"0a5b74e7-1443-4c56-9cb5-bf2f5bbd1991","timestamp":"2026-08-04T16:56:36.721Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"teammate_spawned","prompt":"We're doing a comprehensive edge-case/failure-mode audit of oxc-react-docgen (a Rust tool that parses TSX/TS with OXC and extracts React component prop metadata, a drop-in replacement for react-docgen-typescript). This is research/documentation only — do NOT modify any code.\n\nYour scope: crates/cli/src/ (main.rs, config.rs, output.rs, commands/extract.rs, commands/check.rs, commands/completions.rs, commands/inspect.rs, commands/lsp.rs, commands/schema.rs, commands/watch.rs, commands/mod.rs) and crates/binding/src/lib.rs + crates/binding/build.rs (thin NAPI wrapper). Read crates/cli/CLAUDE.md first for the project's own rules for this crate (no println! in command handlers — output.rs/tracing only; miette for errors; config.rs runs user's docgen.config.ts via node+tsx with config path passed via env var, not shell string, specifically to avoid command injection).\n\nIdentify edge cases and failure modes in:\n1. **Config loading** (config.rs): missing docgen.config.ts (should fall back to defaults — verify), malformed/syntactically-invalid config file, config file that throws at runtime, missing node or tsx on PATH, node/tsx version incompatibilities, config file with unexpected types (e.g. src as a string instead of array), extremely large config, config path with spaces/special shell characters (verify the env-var passing actually avoids injection in all code paths — check for any place that might still interpolate into a shell string), timeout/hang if the config script never exits or does something async that never resolves.\n2. **CLI argument parsing** (main.rs, ExtractArgs etc.): conflicting flags, --out path that doesn't exist / isn't writable / is a directory, --format combined with --json (check documented precedence is actually enforced), invalid --react-version strings, empty --src list, --cache-dir pointing somewhere unwritable, --extra-builtins with malformed entries.\n3. **Exit code correctness**: every command's exit code paths — does every error condition map to a sensible, documented exit code? Cross-check cmd_extract's error-diagnostic-severity logic (already has tests for --json exit code) against check.rs, inspect.rs, schema.rs, lsp.rs, watch.rs — do they all handle the \"extraction produced Error-severity diagnostics\" case consistently, or do some silently exit 0?\n4. **Output writing**: what happens if --out write fails partway (disk full, permission denied) — is any partial file left behind? Does watch.rs handle repeated writes to the same --out path safely?\n5. **watch.rs command**: startup behavior if the initial extraction already has errors, behavior on Ctrl-C mid-extraction, terminal output interleaving with progress indicators.\n6. **lsp.rs**: malformed LSP requests, requests for files outside the configured src_dirs, hover requests on positions with no component/prop at that location, protocol errors (malformed JSON-RPC framing), what happens before the initial full extraction completes (race between \"ready\" and first request).\n7. **schema.rs**: does the exported JSON Schema stay in sync with the actual serde output of ComponentEntry/ExtractionOutput, or could they drift silently?\n8. **NAPI binding** (crates/binding): panics crossing the FFI boundary into Node (Rust panic = UB/crash in NAPI unless caught — check if there's a catch_unwind or equivalent), thread-safety of any shared state, what a Node caller sees on a Rust-side error (proper JS Error vs opaque crash).\n9. **Panic/crash risks**: unwrap/expect/indexing anywhere in scope, particularly on user-controlled input (CLI args, config file contents, file paths).\n\nFor each finding: exact file:line, whether existing tests already cover it (check crates/cli/tests/ and inline test modules first — note there's now a crates/cli/tests/ directory, check what's there), severity. Report grouped by category 1-9, concrete with code citations. Under 2800 words.","teammate_id":"audit-cli@session-0ae3953f","agent_id":"audit-cli@session-0ae3953f","agent_type":"Explore","model":"claude-sonnet-5","name":"audit-cli","color":"purple","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-0ae3953f","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1878d4f-49a4-4d5b-8785-cd43eff77263","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"0a5b74e7-1443-4c56-9cb5-bf2f5bbd1991","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","toolUseID":"toolu_01ANUVP9AaC4b2D7VH4Lqnv6","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Agent\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":45},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6119ff78-ada0-46dd-a721-262cbe56b48b","timestamp":"2026-08-04T16:56:36.721Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"6119ff78-ada0-46dd-a721-262cbe56b48b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi4NkszKi8hQyNymux6h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014xwC5fdQgDXE87uZSv5UPA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit types, serialization, plugin edge cases","subagent_type":"Explore","name":"audit-types","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"We're doing a comprehensive edge-case/failure-mode audit of oxc-react-docgen (a Rust tool that parses TSX/TS with OXC and extracts React component prop metadata, a drop-in replacement for react-docgen-typescript). This is research/documentation only — do NOT modify any code.\n\nYour scope: crates/core/src/types/ (mod.rs, output.rs, diagnostic.rs, global.rs, collected.rs), crates/core/src/plugin.rs, crates/core/src/toon.rs, crates/core/src/react_types.rs, crates/core/src/known.rs, and the RDT/storybook serialization functions in crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs (serialize_rdt, serialize_storybook, rdt_type_json).\n\nIdentify edge cases and failure modes in:\n1. **Serialization correctness**: prop names or type strings containing characters that could break JSON (quotes, backslashes, unicode, extremely long strings), circular references in serialized output (could a recursive type produce infinite JSON?), numeric edge cases in default values (NaN, Infinity, very large numbers as literal defaults), the RDT `enum`-shape special-casing in rdt_type_json — does it handle a `PropType::Union` mixed with non-literal members correctly, or a LiteralUnion with zero or one members?\n2. **TOON format** (toon.rs): what happens with prop/type data that doesn't fit TOON's token-optimized assumptions — deeply nested structures, very large prop counts, unicode-heavy descriptions. Does it round-trip losslessly relative to canonical JSON, or is it deliberately lossy (and if lossy, is that documented)?\n3. **Diagnostic type** (diagnostic.rs): are all DiagnosticCode variants actually constructible with correct severity everywhere they're used across the codebase (search other files for `DiagnosticCode::` and `DiagnosticSeverity::` usage), or are there codes defined but never emitted (dead) or emitted with clearly wrong severity?\n4. **Plugin system** (plugin.rs): what happens if a plugin panics inside a hook — does it poison the whole extraction? Plugin hook ordering guarantees (if multiple plugins registered, is order deterministic?), plugins that mutate shared state unsafely, plugin hooks called on every file even when no plugins are registered (perf edge case, not correctness, but worth noting if there's needless overhead).\n5. **known.rs**: the library-specific type shortcuts (SxProps, VariantProps, etc.) — what happens when a user's codebase has a *different*, same-named type that happens to collide with one of these hardcoded shortcuts (false positive opaque-type shortcut)? Is this documented as a known tradeoff?\n6. **react_types.rs**: React builtin recognition — coverage gaps for newer React APIs (e.g. `use()`, Server Components-specific types, `ForwardedRef` variants), HTML element attribute mapping completeness (recently touched per git history for SVGAttributes/HTMLProps — check current state for remaining gaps), case sensitivity issues in element name matching.\n7. **Output types** (types/output.rs, types/global.rs): any field that can be in an inconsistent state relative to another field (e.g. `required: true` combined with a `default_value` present — contradictory prop state; does anything validate against this, or can the resolver produce it?).\n8. **Panic/crash risks**: unwrap/expect/indexing in scope.\n\nFor each finding: exact file:line, whether existing tests already cover it, severity. Report grouped by category 1-8, concrete with code citations. Under 2500 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"output_tokens":8585,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8585,"cache_read_input_tokens":106187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1416},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi4NjDmn5BruE5v9CKUM","type":"assistant","uuid":"28ebbfb4-e75b-4f44-b4ee-6030a6082d5b","timestamp":"2026-08-04T16:56:54.073Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
