tions — deeply nested structures, very large prop counts, unicode-heavy descriptions. Does it round-trip losslessly relative to canonical JSON, or is it deliberately lossy (and if lossy, is that documented)?\n3. **Diagnostic type** (diagnostic.rs): are all DiagnosticCode variants actually constructible with correct severity everywhere they're used across the codebase (search other files for `DiagnosticCode::` and `DiagnosticSeverity::` usage), or are there codes defined but never emitted (dead) or emitted with clearly wrong severity?\n4. **Plugin system** (plugin.rs): what happens if a plugin panics inside a hook — does it poison the whole extraction? Plugin hook ordering guarantees (if multiple plugins registered, is order deterministic?), plugins that mutate shared state unsafely, plugin hooks called on every file even when no plugins are registered (perf edge case, not correctness, but worth noting if there's needless overhead).\n5. **known.rs**: the library-specific type shortcuts (SxProps, VariantProps, etc.) — what happens when a user's codebase has a *different*, same-named type that happens to collide with one of these hardcoded shortcuts (false positive opaque-type shortcut)? Is this documented as a known tradeoff?\n6. **react_types.rs**: React builtin recognition — coverage gaps for newer React APIs (e.g. `use()`, Server Components-specific types, `ForwardedRef` variants), HTML element attribute mapping completeness (recently touched per git history for SVGAttributes/HTMLProps — check current state for remaining gaps), case sensitivity issues in element name matching.\n7. **Output types** (types/output.rs, types/global.rs): any field that can be in an inconsistent state relative to another field (e.g. `required: true` combined with a `default_value` present — contradictory prop state; does anything validate against this, or can the resolver produce it?).\n8. **Panic/crash risks**: unwrap/expect/indexing in scope.\n\nFor each finding: exact file:line, whether existing tests already cover it, severity. Report grouped by category 1-8, concrete with code citations. Under 2500 words.","teammate_id":"audit-types@session-0ae3953f","agent_id":"audit-types@session-0ae3953f","agent_type":"Explore","model":"claude-sonnet-5","name":"audit-types","color":"orange","tmux_session_name":"in-process","tmux_window_name":"in-process","tmux_pane_id":"in-process","team_name":"session-0ae3953f","is_splitpane":false,"plan_mode_required":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"28ebbfb4-e75b-4f44-b4ee-6030a6082d5b","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
