{"parentUuid":"17667eef-4ffc-4cc6-824d-478705a0e212","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi4w29tt3oHTa1oSwzm3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011RbzTaiCskRyMHYw7AoCH7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/rdt-coverage.md","limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4602,"cache_read_input_tokens":142466,"output_tokens":3529,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4602,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3529,"cache_read_input_tokens":142466,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4602},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi4vwf2GRGxRbeU4hVEB","type":"assistant","uuid":"715d4ad2-ef04-47c5-831e-e56483908a76","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:03:07.138Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"715d4ad2-ef04-47c5-831e-e56483908a76","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"31ac2396-b3e2-4a0c-aa3a-65aa0375a150","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011RbzTaiCskRyMHYw7AoCH7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# RDT Spec Coverage Matrix\n2\t\n3\tMaps each react-docgen-typescript (RDT) output field and component pattern to the fixtures that exercise it. Run `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core --test snapshots` to validate the original 8 snapshot fixtures. The 8 real-world library fixtures added since (fluentui, base-ui, antd, ark-ui, zendesk-garden, day-picker, headlessui, blueprint) aren't snapshot-tested — validate them via `pnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/validate compare:all`.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## PropType kinds\n8\t\n9\tEach `PropType` variant the resolver can emit; whether any fixture produces it.\n10\t\n11\t| Kind | Covered by |\n12\t| --- | --- |\n13\t| `string` | all fixtures |\n14\t| `number` | all fixtures |\n15\t| `boolean` | all fixtures |\n16\t| `null` | mui, shadcn |\n17\t| `unknown` | mui |\n18\t| `reactNode` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria |\n19\t| `cssProperties` | chakra, mui, react-aria, shadcn |\n20\t| `elementType` | chakra, mantine, mui |\n21\t| `stringLiteral` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria, shadcn |\n22\t| `union` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria, shadcn, **day-picker** (7-way discriminated) |\n23\t| `named` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria |\n24\t| `eventHandler` | all fixtures; real param names from `(open: boolean) => void`-style handlers (not a hardcoded `\"e\"`) verified against **headlessui**, **ark-ui** |\n25\t| `ref` | mantine, mui |\n26\t| `object` | mantine, **rdt-compat/types** (`raw_string()` renders real fields — `{ key: Type; key2?: Type2 }` — not the literal placeholder `\"object\"`) |\n27\t| `literalUnion` | mantine, shadcn, **panda** (after defineRecipe arg-index fix) |\n28\t| `array` | **rdt-compat/types** (`string[]` syntax), **day-picker** (`readonly string[]` type-operator form) |\n29\t| `tuple` | **rdt-compat/types** (`[number, number]`; `raw_string()` renders real elements, not the placeholder `\"tuple\"`) |\n30\t| `numberLiteral` | **rdt-compat/types** (`1 \\| 2 \\| 4 \\| 8`) |\n31\t| `boolLiteral` | **rdt-compat/types** (`true` literal type) |\n32\t| `undefined` | **rdt-compat/types** (explicit `?: undefined`) |\n33\t| `sxProps` | **rdt-compat/types** (unresolved `SxProps` ref → known-pattern shortcut) |\n34\t| `htmlAttributes` | **rdt-compat/types** (`ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>` as prop value); real per-element attribute resolution (not just this metadata layer) — see [HtmlAttributeMode](#htmlattributemode-curated--full--none) below |\n35\t| `intersection` | **rdt-compat/types** (`CSSProperties & { '--accent': string }`) |\n36\t| `opaque` | **rdt-compat/types** (inline conditional type `T extends A ? B : C`) |\n37\t| `void` | ❌ not covered — `() => void` captured as `eventHandler`, standalone `void` never appears |\n38\t| `never` | ❌ not covered — no real-world prop has type `never` |\n39\t| `any` | ❌ not covered — `any` suppressed by TypeScript `strict` in fixtures |\n40\t\n41\t> **Note on `void` / `never`:** These kinds exist in the type system for completeness but are not realistic prop types. A function return type `() => void` is always emitted as `eventHandler`, and `never` typically indicates a broken discriminant. No fixture is planned for either.\n42\t\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t## ComponentEntry fields\n46\t\n47\t| Field | Status | Covered by |\n48\t| --- | --- | --- |\n49\t| `displayName` | ✅ | all fixtures |\n50\t| `filePath` | ✅ | all fixtures |\n51\t| `description` (non-empty) | ✅ | mui Button, panda button |\n52\t| `description` (component JSDoc, no prop leak) | ✅ | fixed — see [Fixed: component description leak](#fixed-component-description-set-to-last-props-jsdoc) |\n53\t| `props` | ✅ | all fixtures |\n54\t| `inheritance` (non-empty) | ✅ | all fixtures |\n55\t| `notableInherited` | ✅ (curated mode only) | all fixtures — see [HtmlAttributeMode](#htmlattributemode-curated--full--none) |\n56\t| `discriminantProp: null` | ✅ | all fixtures; also correctly `null` for a _double_-discriminated union where no single field disambiguates every variant — **day-picker** (`mode` repeats across `PropsSingle`/`PropsSingleRequired`, only jointly unique with `required`) |\n57\t| `discriminantProp: \"variant\"` | ✅ | mui TextField |\n58\t| `discriminantProp` through an intersection-wrapped union (`Base & (A\\|B\\|C)`) | ✅ | **day-picker** — see [Fixed: intersection-wrapped discriminated unions](#fixed-discriminated-unions-wrapped-in-an-intersection) |\n59\t| `composes` (non-empty) | ✅ | mantine, shadcn, chakra, react-aria |\n60\t| `tags` (component-level, non-empty) | ✅ | **rdt-compat/jsdoc** (`@description`, `@default`, `@deprecated`, `@internal`) |"}]},"uuid":"a17700f3-753f-4921-936d-afb929e4786e","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:03:07.213Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/rdt-coverage.md","content":"# RDT Spec Coverage Matrix\n\nMaps each react-docgen-typescript (RDT) output field and component pattern to the fixtures that exercise it. Run `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core --test snapshots` to validate the original 8 snapshot fixtures. The 8 real-world library fixtures added since (fluentui, base-ui, antd, ark-ui, zendesk-garden, day-picker, headlessui, blueprint) aren't snapshot-tested — validate them via `pnpm --filter @oxc-react-docgen/validate compare:all`.\n\n---\n\n## PropType kinds\n\nEach `PropType` variant the resolver can emit; whether any fixture produces it.\n\n| Kind | Covered by |\n| --- | --- |\n| `string` | all fixtures |\n| `number` | all fixtures |\n| `boolean` | all fixtures |\n| `null` | mui, shadcn |\n| `unknown` | mui |\n| `reactNode` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria |\n| `cssProperties` | chakra, mui, react-aria, shadcn |\n| `elementType` | chakra, mantine, mui |\n| `stringLiteral` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria, shadcn |\n| `union` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria, shadcn, **day-picker** (7-way discriminated) |\n| `named` | chakra, mantine, mui, react-aria |\n| `eventHandler` | all fixtures; real param names from `(open: boolean) => void`-style handlers (not a hardcoded `\"e\"`) verified against **headlessui**, **ark-ui** |\n| `ref` | mantine, mui |\n| `object` | mantine, **rdt-compat/types** (`raw_string()` renders real fields — `{ key: Type; key2?: Type2 }` — not the literal placeholder `\"object\"`) |\n| `literalUnion` | mantine, shadcn, **panda** (after defineRecipe arg-index fix) |\n| `array` | **rdt-compat/types** (`string[]` syntax), **day-picker** (`readonly string[]` type-operator form) |\n| `tuple` | **rdt-compat/types** (`[number, number]`; `raw_string()` renders real elements, not the placeholder `\"tuple\"`) |\n| `numberLiteral` | **rdt-compat/types** (`1 \\| 2 \\| 4 \\| 8`) |\n| `boolLiteral` | **rdt-compat/types** (`true` literal type) |\n| `undefined` | **rdt-compat/types** (explicit `?: undefined`) |\n| `sxProps` | **rdt-compat/types** (unresolved `SxProps` ref → known-pattern shortcut) |\n| `htmlAttributes` | **rdt-compat/types** (`ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'button'>` as prop value); real per-element attribute resolution (not just this metadata layer) — see [HtmlAttributeMode](#htmlattributemode-curated--full--none) below |\n| `intersection` | **rdt-compat/types** (`CSSProperties & { '--accent': string }`) |\n| `opaque` | **rdt-compat/types** (inline conditional type `T extends A ? B : C`) |\n| `void` | ❌ not covered — `() => void` captured as `eventHandler`, standalone `void` never appears |\n| `never` | ❌ not covered — no real-world prop has type `never` |\n| `any` | ❌ not covered — `any` suppressed by TypeScript `strict` in fixtures |\n\n> **Note on `void` / `never`:** These kinds exist in the type system for completeness but are not realistic prop types. A function return type `() => void` is always emitted as `eventHandler`, and `never` typically indicates a broken discriminant. No fixture is planned for either.\n\n---\n\n## ComponentEntry fields\n\n| Field | Status | Covered by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `displayName` | ✅ | all fixtures |\n| `filePath` | ✅ | all fixtures |\n| `description` (non-empty) | ✅ | mui Button, panda button |\n| `description` (component JSDoc, no prop leak) | ✅ | fixed — see [Fixed: component description leak](#fixed-component-description-set-to-last-props-jsdoc) |\n| `props` | ✅ | all fixtures |\n| `inheritance` (non-empty) | ✅ | all fixtures |\n| `notableInherited` | ✅ (curated mode only) | all fixtures — see [HtmlAttributeMode](#htmlattributemode-curated--full--none) |\n| `discriminantProp: null` | ✅ | all fixtures; also correctly `null` for a _double_-discriminated union where no single field disambiguates every variant — **day-picker** (`mode` repeats across `PropsSingle`/`PropsSingleRequired`, only jointly unique with `required`) |\n| `discriminantProp: \"variant\"` | ✅ | mui TextField |\n| `discriminantProp` through an intersection-wrapped union (`Base & (A\\|B\\|C)`) | ✅ | **day-picker** — see [Fixed: intersection-wrapped discriminated unions](#fixed-discriminated-unions-wrapped-in-an-intersection) |\n| `composes` (non-empty) | ✅ | mantine, shadcn, chakra, react-aria |\n| `tags` (component-level, non-empty) | ✅ | **rdt-compat/jsdoc** (`@description`, `@default`, `@deprecated`, `@internal`) |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":432}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"715d4ad2-ef04-47c5-831e-e56483908a76","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
