{"parentUuid":"5215d2cc-2abb-42fe-b487-e8ba3b56407b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi56Z3WmphS58bPpPRvE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":159210,"output_tokens":977,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":159210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi56XQ3NcwJBrqRrbvXy","type":"assistant","uuid":"21de6502-0046-4e42-b2b0-872d731e4d08","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:04:35.900Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"21de6502-0046-4e42-b2b0-872d731e4d08","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi56Z3WmphS58bPpPRvE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe single most valuable thing this audit surfaces isn't any one bug — it's the pattern: nearly every subsystem has its own version of the same failure shape, \"give up and return an empty/default value with no trace.\" The resolver has `ResolvedChain::default()` instead of `empty_with_compose()`; the extractor has bare `None`/`return None` on malformed type args; discovery has `.flatten()` silently eating `Err`s; watch mode has `let _ = std::fs::write(...)`. That's a strong signal this isn't five unrelated problems needing five different fixes — it's one architectural discipline (non-negotiable #6: \"always emit a Diagnostic when degrading\") that was applied rigorously in some code paths and never retrofitted to others as the codebase grew. A single sweep-style fix (grep for `-> None`/`::default()`/`let _ =` at give-up points and ensure each pairs with a diagnostic) would likely close a large fraction of the P2 list at once, rather than needing 20 independent fixes.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nWrote the full findings to `docs/edge-cases.md` and linked it from `docs/STATUS.md`'s \"Where to look next\" section, matching the project's existing doc conventions (tables, no line wrapping, cross-referenced against `rdt-coverage.md`/`type-checker-integration.md` for gaps already tracked elsewhere).\n\n**Headline numbers:** 9 crash/hang risks, 5 silent-correctness bugs (wrong output, not just missing), ~20 silent-data-loss sites across extractor/resolver/pipeline/CLI/types, 2 contract inconsistencies. The two I'd flag as most worth your attention first:\n\n1. **`known.rs` shortcut precedence bug** (P0-1) — a real, demonstrable data-quality bug, not a hypothetical: `named.rs` correctly checks user-defined interfaces before falling back to hardcoded library shortcuts (SxProps, etc.), but `chain.rs`'s `extends`-clause path checks the shortcuts *first*. A project with its own `SxProps` interface extended via `extends` gets silently swapped for MUI's opaque shape.\n2. **Template-literal Cartesian-product blowup** (P1-1) — no cap on the M^N string expansion when a template literal has multiple parts each resolving to a sizable union. Realistic (design-system token unions are common), not just adversarial, and zero test coverage exists for it.\n\nI didn't fix anything — this was scoped as understand-and-document. Want me to start working through the P0 list (the wrong-not-missing bugs), or would you rather triage/re-prioritize first given the size of the P2 list?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":159210,"output_tokens":977,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":159210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi56XQ3NcwJBrqRrbvXy","type":"assistant","uuid":"11be6e27-6cfa-47b3-b332-152df73f0a75","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:04:48.129Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
