{"parentUuid":"e29e3b50-e81f-478d-bdbb-c0b674c06c80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi5LazUrYcA5CWUhecXv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":161009,"output_tokens":4388,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4388,"cache_read_input_tokens":161009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi5LYjYufpNe3URoUADM","type":"assistant","uuid":"6db3ee73-a2d7-474d-af93-220906b3c794","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:08:20.983Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"6db3ee73-a2d7-474d-af93-220906b3c794","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi5LazUrYcA5CWUhecXv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — do the architectural pass first. Here's why, concretely: when I look across the five audit reports, most of the ~20 \"silent data loss\" findings aren't 20 independent bugs, they're the same failure shape recurring in isolation — a give-up path returning `None`/`Default::default()`/discarding a `Result` with no `Diagnostic` attached. That's non-negotiable #6 applied rigorously in some places and never retrofitted elsewhere. Jumping straight to 30 independent fix-tickets would mean fixing that pattern 20 separate times instead of once, and would miss the actual question worth answering: *why* did a codebase with an explicit non-negotiable about this drift into violating it repeatedly? That's an architecture question (missing enforcement mechanism, missing shared abstraction, missing lint), not a per-finding one.\n\n**Proposed structure — four phases:**\n\n**Phase 0 — Root-cause / architectural analysis.** Not \"what's broken\" (we have that), but \"what's missing that let it happen.\" For each subsystem, look for the *mechanism* gap behind the pattern: is there no shared helper that pairs \"give up\" with \"emit diagnostic,\" so every call site reimplements it ad hoc and some forget? Could a custom clippy lint or a `#[must_use]`-style wrapper type catch `-> None`-without-diagnostic at compile time going forward? Same question for the plugin-panic/rayon-batch-panic cluster (P1-3/P1-4) — is there a missing `catch_unwind` boundary convention, and where's the one right place to add it once rather than at every call site? Output: a small number of *fix-pattern* clusters (not 30 tickets) plus, if warranted, a new ADR documenting the enforcement mechanism decided on.\n\n**Phase 1 — Plan.** Turn Phase 0's clusters + `docs/edge-cases.md` into a real implementation plan (writing-plans skill): one task per cluster, each with its own TDD edge-case tests, sized so clusters touching disjoint files can run in parallel and clusters touching the same file (e.g. `chain.rs` has both the P0-1 precedence bug and the P2 cycle-detection dead-end) are merged into one task rather than conflicting.\n\n**Phase 2 — Implementation.** TDD per cluster — failing test per edge case first, minimal fix, full verification (`cargo test`, clippy, fmt, snapshot review) before commit. Independent clusters in parallel via worktree isolation; shared-file clusters sequential.\n\n**Phase 3 — Docs.** Update `ARCHITECTURE.md`, write the new ADR if Phase 0 produces one, mark items fixed in `edge-cases.md`, update `STATUS.md`'s numbers.\n\nGiven you explicitly want agent teams/workflows for this, Phase 0 and Phase 2 are natural Workflow calls (parallel root-cause digging, then pipelined per-cluster implementation); Phase 1 is a single writing-plans pass off Phase 0's output."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":161009,"output_tokens":4388,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4388,"cache_read_input_tokens":161009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi5LYjYufpNe3URoUADM","type":"assistant","uuid":"92806281-2399-46ae-9833-760472275765","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:08:34.453Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"92806281-2399-46ae-9833-760472275765","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi5LazUrYcA5CWUhecXv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YMaH5xAPzm8ynpv33H5jdH","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Ready to kick off Phase 0 (the architectural root-cause workflow) now?","header":"Next step","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Yes, start Phase 0 now (Recommended)","description":"Launch a Workflow to dig into root causes per subsystem and propose fix-pattern clusters + any needed ADR. I'll report back before Phase 1 planning starts."},{"label":"Write the full 4-phase plan doc first","description":"Use writing-plans to produce a complete written plan spanning all 4 phases before any agent work begins, so you can review the whole shape upfront."},{"label":"Skip Phase 0, go straight to per-finding fixes","description":"Treat the 30 findings as independent tickets and start fixing top-down by severity, without a root-cause pass. Faster to start, but risks the same pattern getting re-fixed piecemeal."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":161009,"output_tokens":4388,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4388,"cache_read_input_tokens":161009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi5LYjYufpNe3URoUADM","type":"assistant","uuid":"3aad3eb6-c373-4e56-9a28-ee7c238a243b","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:08:40.235Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-4