{"parentUuid":"477c75f7-7c30-4858-bc6a-0d5a3fd48563","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi5cYZKw33KaYAHgs382","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019QdSbtiPHa4soBAfVTCBzh","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'edge-case-root-cause-analysis',\n  description: 'Phase 0: find architectural root causes behind the edge-case audit findings and propose fix-pattern clusters + enforcement mechanisms',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Cluster Analysis', detail: 'one agent per candidate root-cause cluster' },\n    { title: 'Synthesize', detail: 'merge into a single Phase 0 report' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst CLUSTER_SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object',\n  required: ['clusterName', 'rootCause', 'mechanismProposal', 'findingIds', 'adrNeeded'],\n  properties: {\n    clusterName: { type: 'string' },\n    rootCause: { type: 'string', description: 'the underlying architectural/process reason this pattern recurred, not a restatement of the symptom' },\n    mechanismProposal: { type: 'string', description: 'a concrete, code-level proposal to prevent recurrence — a shared helper/wrapper type, a custom lint, a single source of truth, a panic boundary convention, etc. Name exact files/functions where it would live.' },\n    findingIds: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' }, description: 'which finding IDs from docs/edge-cases.md actually belong to this cluster (confirm or correct the rough assignment given in the prompt)' },\n    misassignedNotes: { type: 'string', description: 'any findings originally assigned here that actually belong to a different cluster, or vice versa, and why' },\n    adrNeeded: { type: 'boolean' },\n    adrRationale: { type: 'string', description: 'if adrNeeded, what hard-to-reverse decision this ADR would record; if not, why the existing non-negotiables/ADRs already cover it' },\n  },\n}\n\nconst CONTEXT = `Read /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/edge-cases.md first for full context — it's a comprehensive audit of oxc-react-docgen (a Rust tool that parses TSX/TS with OXC and extracts React component prop metadata, a drop-in replacement for react-docgen-typescript) covering crash risks, silent data loss, and correctness bugs across the whole pipeline. Also read /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/CLAUDE.md and /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/crates/core/CLAUDE.md for the project's non-negotiables (no unwrap() outside tests, always emit a Diagnostic when degrading, FxHashMap/BTreeMap discipline) and /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/ for existing architectural decisions (0001-0004) so you don't propose a duplicate.\n\nThis is a root-cause analysis, not a re-audit — the findings are already catalogued. Your job is to read the ACTUAL CODE at the cited locations (not just trust the doc's summary) and answer: why did this pattern happen repeatedly instead of being caught once? Is there a missing shared abstraction, a missing lint/CI check, a missing code-review checklist item, duplicated logic that drifted out of sync, or something else? Then propose a concrete, specific mechanism that would fix the existing instances AND prevent new ones — not just \"add a diagnostic here,\" but \"here is the one place a shared helper/lint/type should live so every call site is forced to comply.\"`\n\nconst CLUSTERS = [\n  {\n    name: 'silent-degrade',\n    prompt: `${CONTEXT}\n\nYour cluster: the \"give up silently\" pattern — a give-up/degrade path returns None, ResolvedChain::default(), or otherwise drops data with no Diagnostic emitted, violating the project's own non-negotiable #6 (\"always emit a Diagnostic when degrading — never fail silently\").\n\nFindings assigned to this cluster (verify against the actual code, not just the doc): the entire \"Priority 2 — silent data loss\" section of docs/edge-cases.md (extractor: anonymous default export, class components, Object.assign compound components, class-expression components, satisfies expressions, classify_type_alias's Omit/Pick/etc silent vanish, extract_props_arg terminal None, failed-detector silence, computed property keys; resolver: chain.rs cycle-detected path not using empty_with_compose, func.rs multi-param function type, LiteralUnion-as-props-base; pipeline: permission-denied files, non-UTF8 filenames, empty src_dirs, same-name-same-file collision, overlapping src_dirs; cli: watch --out silent write failure; types: NumberLiteral NaN/Infinity, zero-member LiteralUnion).\n\nRead at least 5-6 of the actual cited call sites across at least 3 different files/subsystems (pick a representative sample spanning extractor, resolver, and pipeline) to see the ACTUAL shape of the code at each give-up point — is it always the same shape (a bare early return) or does it vary enough that one shared mechanism can't cover all of them? Check whether ResolvedChain::empty_with_compose() (resolver/mod.rs) already IS the intended shared mechanism for the resolver half, just inconsistently applied — if so, the root cause there might just be \"no lint/test enforces its use at every give-up site,\" which has a very different fix than \"no mechanism exists at all.\" Check whether the extractor's silent-None sites could share an analogous helper, or whether the extractor's Diagnostic-emission story needs a different mechanism than the resolver's (e.g. per-declaration diagnostics don't exist yet in the extractor at all per the doc — that's more foundational than a missing helper).\n\nReturn your findings via the required schema.`,\n  },\n  {\n    name: 'panic-containment',\n    prompt: `${CONTEXT}\n\nYour cluster: panic/crash/hang containment gaps — places where a panic, unbounded allocation, or hang isn't isolated to the smallest reasonable blast radius.\n\nFindings assigned to this cluster (verify against the actual code): plugin hook panics unwinding out of pipeline::extract() with zero catch_unwind anywhere in the repo (plugin.rs, pipeline/mod.rs:293,385); per-file parse/resolve rayon batches having no per-file catch_unwind (pipeline/mod.rs:260,357); watch.rs's poisoned-mutex .expect() permanently disabling a session (pipeline/watch.rs:93); LSP Content-Length unbounded allocation (cli/commands/lsp.rs:36); LSP hover advertised but unimplemented causing a client hang (cli/commands/lsp.rs:56,78); LSP malformed-header desync risk (cli/commands/lsp.rs:32-34); unbounded template-literal Cartesian product (resolver/template.rs:94-104); extractor's bracket-counting nesting guard not actually bounding conditional-type-chain recursion depth (extractor/mod.rs:38-40,105-120,311-471); NAPI create_session/close_session running unprotected on the JS thread unlike the other three entry points (crates/binding/src/lib.rs:132-138,193-195).\n\nThese look superficially unrelated (different subsystems, different failure shapes — allocation, recursion, thread panics, protocol hangs) — your job is to determine whether they share ONE root cause (e.g. \"this codebase has no established convention for where panic/resource-exhaustion boundaries belong, so each new subsystem re-derives its own answer, inconsistently\") or whether they're genuinely 2-3 unrelated gaps that each need their own fix. Read the actual code at each site. If you find a genuine common thread, propose where a boundary convention should live (e.g. \"every rayon par_iter().map() in pipeline/mod.rs should wrap its closure in catch_unwind and convert to a per-item Diagnostic — here's the exact helper signature\"). If some of these are unrelated, say so explicitly and split them into sub-groups with separate proposals rather than forcing a false unification.\n\nReturn your findings via the required schema. If you conclude this is actually 2+ independent groups, you may return multiple cluster entries — restructure clusterName/findingIds/etc as an array-of-clusters if needed, but keep the same field shape per cluster.`,\n  },\n  {\n    name: 'duplicated-logic-drift',\n    prompt: `${CONTEXT}\n\nYour cluster: bugs caused by two independent implementations of the same concept drifting out of sync, or precedence/ordering logic being reimplemented ad hoc at multiple call sites instead of sharing one source of truth.\n\nFindings assigned to this cluster (verify against the actual code): known.rs shortcut precedence being correct in resolver/named.rs (checks user-defined types before hardcoded library shortcuts, with an explicit comment explaining why) but WRONG in resolver/chain.rs's extends-clause path (checks hardcoded shortcuts first) — read both call sites in full; schema.rs's hand-written JSON Schema having already drifted from the real ComponentEntry/ExtractionStats/Diagnostic struct fields (cli/commands/schema.rs:17-67 vs core/types/output.rs:47-68,609-619 and core/types/diagnostic.rs:8-16); toon.rs's Union/Intersection truncation silently omitting the \"+N\" indicator that the sibling LiteralUnion code path in the SAME function correctly includes (toon.rs:110-132).\n\nDetermine: is there a common root cause across these three (e.g. \"the codebase has no policy of deriving serialized/duplicated representations from a single source, so every hand-written mirror silently drifts as the source evolves\"), and would a single class of fix apply to all three (e.g. schemars-derive for schema.rs, a shared precedence-check function called from both named.rs and chain.rs, a shared truncation-formatting helper for toon.rs)? Or are these three independent oversights that just happen to rhyme? Be honest if the fixes are genuinely unrelated even if the symptom (drift) rhymes.\n\nReturn your findings via the required schema.`,\n  },\n  {\n    name: 'contract-and-cache-correctness',\n    prompt: `${CONTEXT}\n\nYour cluster: two smaller but distinct groups — (a) CLI exit-code/behavior contract inconsistency across commands, and (b) cache/state correctness bugs that produce wrong (not missing) output.\n\nFindings assigned to this cluster (verify against the actual code): exit-code contract (0 success / 2 extraction-error) being documented and enforced only for extract/check, while watch always exits 0 regardless of extraction errors and inspect never surfaces Error-severity diagnostics found elsewhere in the tree (cli/main.rs:181-198 and the individual command files); DiagnosticCode::Unknown being defined but never constructed anywhere (types/diagnostic.rs:61); cache.rs's mtime+size cache key producing a stale hit on same-tick, same-size edits (cache.rs:181-191); ParsedProp allowing the contradictory state required:true + default_value:Some(_) with nothing preventing it (types/output.rs:79-99).\n\nRead the actual code for each. For the exit-code group specifically: is there a shared helper today for \"does this ExtractionOutput contain Error-severity diagnostics, and if so what's the right exit code\" — or does every command reimplement that check ad hoc (which would explain why some commands forgot it)? For the cache/state group: these two are more likely genuinely independent (a filesystem-timestamp-resolution limitation vs. a missing type invariant) — say so if that's what you find, don't force a unified story.\n\nReturn your findings via the required schema (or, if you conclude (a) and (b) are unrelated, return two cluster entries with the same schema shape).`,\n  },\n]\n\nphase('Cluster Analysis')\nconst clusterResults = await parallel(\n  CLUSTERS.map(c => () => agent(c.prompt, { label: c.name, phase: 'Cluster Analysis', schema: CLUSTER_SCHEMA }))\n)\n\nphase('Synthesize')\nconst synthesis = await agent(\n  `You are synthesizing a Phase 0 architectural root-cause analysis for oxc-react-docgen into a final report. Below are the outputs from 4 independent analysis agents, each examining a different candidate root-cause cluster behind the findings in /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/edge-cases.md.\n\n${JSON.stringify(clusterResults.filter(Boolean), null, 2)}\n\nRead /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/edge-cases.md and /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/README.md yourself to cross-check.\n\nProduce a final Phase 0 report as markdown (this will be shown directly to the user and used to drive Phase 1 implementation planning). Structure:\n\n1. A short intro (2-4 sentences): how many genuine root-cause clusters were found (note if any analysis agent split their assigned cluster further, or if two clusters turned out to actually be the same root cause — reconcile that here), and the overall takeaway.\n2. One section per confirmed cluster: name, root cause (the WHY, not the symptom), the concrete mechanism proposal (specific enough that Phase 1 can turn it directly into an implementation task — name the exact file/function/helper to add), which finding IDs/descriptions from edge-cases.md it resolves, and whether it needs a new ADR (if yes, draft the ADR's one-paragraph \"Decision\" and \"Context\" — don't write the full ADR file, just the core content for Phase 1 to expand).\n3. A short \"findings that turned out to be genuinely independent, not part of any cluster\" section, if any — list them plainly so Phase 1 treats them as standalone tasks rather than searching for a pattern that isn't there.\n4. A recommended task breakdown for Phase 1: one line per proposed implementation task (mechanism-cluster tasks first, then independent findings), noting which files each would touch so Phase 1 can identify which tasks can run in parallel (disjoint files) vs must be sequential/merged (shared files).\n\nDo not pad with generic caveats. Be concrete and decisive — this feeds directly into planning real implementation work. Under 1800 words.`,\n  { label: 'synthesis', phase: 'Synthesize' }\n)\n\nreturn { clusterResults, synthesis }\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_read_input_tokens":161249,"output_tokens":6968,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6968,"cache_read_input_tokens":161249,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi5cUmsf5vG1F78xCnjo","type":"assistant","uuid":"705ec3c0-d9ae-44af-a912-eb9ec0bbec38","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:12:38.766Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
