{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:17:59.967Z","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wruyd6jkk</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/0ae3953f-9438-46c4-a76a-88fce9eed529/tasks/wruyd6jkk.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Phase 0: find architectural root causes behind the edge-case audit findings and propose fix-pattern clusters + enforcement mechanisms\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"clusterResults\":[{\"clusterName\":\"Give-up-silently: graceful-degradation paths that skip the Diagnostic pairing\",\"rootCause\":\"Verified against actual code (resolver/chain.rs, resolver/func.rs, resolver/collected.rs, extractor/alias.rs, extractor/mod.rs, extractor/visit.rs, pipeline/discover.rs, pipeline/mod.rs). This is not one root cause but three, stratified by whether a shared mechanism already exists:\\n\\n(1) RESOLVER (chain.rs, func.rs): a convention already exists — `ResolvedChain::empty_with_compose(name)` bundles the \\\"give up, record what we couldn't resolve\\\" case, and `collected.rs::push_opaque_diagnostic` is a shared helper that pairs a `PropType::Opaque` with an Info diagnostic. But neither is the *only* way to construct these values: `ResolvedChain` derives `Default` and is a plain struct with no private fields, so `ResolvedChain::default()` (bare, no composes/diagnostic) is just as callable as the named constructor — chain.rs:40 (cycle path) reaches for the wrong one and nothing stops it. Likewise `PropType::Opaque { raw, reason }` is a plain struct-literal-constructible variant; I found ~10 construction sites across 5 files (collected.rs, func.rs, primitives.rs, named.rs, template.rs) and only 4 of them (collected.rs:79,103,107,150) route through `push_opaque_diagnostic` — func.rs:61 (MultiParamFunction), primitives.rs:181 (IndexedAccess), template.rs:39 (TemplateLiteral) build `PropType::Opaque` directly with no diagnostic call, invisible to any reviewer scanning the \\\"happy path.\\\" The helper functions are advisory, not enforced — classic drift from a convention that isn't structurally mandatory. This is the \\\"no lint/test enforces its use\\\" case, not \\\"no mechanism exists.\\\"\\n\\n(2) EXTRACTOR (alias.rs classify_type_alias, mod.rs extract_type_name_from_type, visit.rs component detectors): fundamentally more foundational — these are `Option&lt;T&gt;`-returning functions chained with `?` against AST shapes (`tp.params.first()?`, `_ =&gt; None`) or nested `if let Some(...) = a.or_else(b).or_else(c)` detector chains with no `else` branch. There is no signal channel distinguishing \\\"this AST shape doesn't apply here\\\" from \\\"this looked like a match but was malformed/unsupported\\\" — both collapse to the same `None`. `SourceData.diagnostics` does exist and extractor code CAN push into it (confirmed at extractor/mod.rs:108,134, both unrelated to this cluster — nesting-depth guard and a syntax error), but classify_type_alias and friends have never been wired to it despite having `&amp;mut self` in scope. This is a design gap, not a helper-drift gap: no helper could be \\\"used inconsistently\\\" here because none was ever built for this call shape.\\n\\n(3) PIPELINE (discover.rs, mod.rs): three unrelated bugs masquerading as one pattern. discover.rs:17's `walker.flatten()` drops `ignore::Walk`'s `Err` items — structural, because `discover_files` returns a bare `Vec&lt;Utf8PathBuf&gt;` with no diagnostic-return channel at all (same class of gap as (2)). mod.rs:220's empty-`src_dirs` miss is a plain boolean short-circuit bug (`!src_dirs.is_empty() &amp;&amp; ...`) — a logic error, not a missing abstraction. mod.rs:386's `components.insert(key, entry)` collision discards `insert`'s `Option&lt;V&gt;` return value that already tells you a collision happened — the data needed to diagnose it is right there and simply unused.\",\"mechanismProposal\":\"Three different fixes for three different root causes — do not apply one mechanism to all findings:\\n\\n**(1) Resolver — make the bare/wrong constructor uncallable, not just discouraged.**\\n- In `resolver/mod.rs`, stop deriving `Default` on `ResolvedChain` as a public-within-module escape hatch: keep a private `fn empty() -&gt; Self` used *only* inside `empty_with_compose`, and add one more named constructor, `ResolvedChain::give_up(type_name: String, diag: Option&lt;Diagnostic&gt;, state: &amp;mut ResolveState) -&gt; Self`, which pushes the diagnostic AND the composes entry in one call, replacing every current two-statement `state.diagnostics.push(...); ResolvedChain::empty_with_compose(...)` pair as well as the bare-`default()` cycle path at chain.rs:40 (which becomes `ResolvedChain::give_up(type_name.to_owned(), None, state)` — reviewers can now see explicitly that no diagnostic is attached there, or add one). Because `Default`/struct-literal construction of `ResolvedChain` outside `resolver/mod.rs`'s own impl block no longer compiles, every future give-up site in chain.rs/alias.rs/extends.rs is forced through the named constructors.\\n- Do the equivalent for `PropType::Opaque`: change it from `Opaque { raw: String, reason: OpaqueReason }` to a single-field tuple variant `Opaque(OpaqueDetail)` where `OpaqueDetail`'s fields are private to a new `resolver/opaque.rs`, and the only public entry point is `OpaqueDetail::give_up(state: &amp;mut ResolveState, what: &amp;str, ct_or_raw, file, reason: OpaqueReason) -&gt; PropType` — folding `push_opaque_diagnostic` into the constructor itself instead of leaving it as a sibling function callers can skip. Update the ~10 existing call sites (collected.rs ×6, func.rs, primitives.rs, named.rs, template.rs) to go through it — this mechanically fixes func.rs:54-61's missing diagnostic and prevents any new Opaque-degradation site from omitting one, since there is no other way to build the variant. This does touch `PropType`'s manual `to_json_value`/`from_json_value` (ADR 0002) — update both match arms, no new ADR needed for that part since the wire shape is unchanged, only the Rust-side constructor surface.\\n- Add one clippy.toml `disallowed-methods`/`disallowed-types` entry (or a `rg 'ResolvedChain\\\\s*\\\\{' -g '!resolver/mod.rs'` / `rg 'PropType::Opaque\\\\s*\\\\{' -g '!resolver/opaque.rs'` check wired into the existing CI/check flow referenced by the `/check` skill) as a backstop in case someone reintroduces a bare literal via `..Default::default()` spread syntax, which the type system alone won't catch.\\n\\n**(2) Extractor — add the missing signal channel, then make it a review-checklist item (no compiler enforcement is practical here given `?`-chained `Option` returns over AST shape matching).**\\n- Add one helper next to the two existing `self.data.diagnostics.push(...)` call sites in `extractor/mod.rs`: `fn record_skip(&amp;mut self, code: DiagnosticCode, message: impl Into&lt;String&gt;, span: Span)` (Info/Warning severity, reuses the existing `Diagnostic` shape). Add a new `DiagnosticCode` variant, e.g. `SkippedCandidate`, so these are filterable/countable separately from parse errors.\\n- Require (via the `crates/core/CLAUDE.md` checklist, not the compiler): every `match ref_name.as_str() { \\\"Omit\\\" =&gt; { ...?...  } ... _ =&gt; passthrough_or_none }` arm in `classify_type_alias` that bails on a *matched-but-malformed* shape (wrong arg count, unrecognized inner type) calls `self.record_skip(...)` before the `?`/`return None`; every component-detector `.or_else()` chain in `visit.rs` (both the PascalCase binding chain at 236-247 and `visit_function` at 262-293) ends with an explicit `else { self.record_skip(...) }` rather than silent fallthrough. This is a checklist addition, not a lint, because distinguishing \\\"not this shape, silently fine\\\" from \\\"this shape but unsupported, worth a diagnostic\\\" requires domain judgment a lint can't make.\\n- New detector coverage (anonymous default export, class components, `Object.assign` compound components, class-expression components, `satisfies`) is a separate, larger feature-gap task — record_skip only makes the *existing* miss visible; it doesn't add the missing detectors.\\n\\n**(3) Pipeline — three independent one-line-scale fixes, no shared abstraction:**\\n- `discover_files` gains a `&amp;mut Vec&lt;Diagnostic&gt;` (or returns `(Vec&lt;Utf8PathBuf&gt;, Vec&lt;Diagnostic&gt;)`) and the `walker.flatten()` becomes an explicit match that pushes an IoError diagnostic on `Err`, same pattern already used at mod.rs:269-272 for read failur\n... (truncated 38522 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/0ae3953f-9438-46c4-a76a-88fce9eed529/tasks/wruyd6jkk.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/subagents/workflows/wf_4893566b-115/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/workflows/scripts/edge-case-root-cause-analysis-wf_4893566b-115.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_4893566b-115'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>5</agent_count><agents_done>5</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>263674</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>58</tool_uses><duration_ms>317689</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
