{"parentUuid":"0f23be02-f437-4523-af44-6edf57bef722","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"33c33088-8732-4685-a296-f012e6bf5131","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RR6GRiq3pBRG76PedbPjTX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# NNNN. Short, decision-shaped title\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** Accepted **Date:** YYYY-MM-DD\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\tWhat forced this? The constraint, not the backstory. 2-4 sentences.\n8\t\n9\t## Decision\n10\t\n11\tWhat we're doing, stated plainly. One paragraph.\n12\t\n13\t## Consequences\n14\t\n15\tWhat this costs and what it buys. Bullets.\n16\t\n17\t-\n18\t-\n19\t\n20\t## Alternatives considered (optional)\n21\t\n22\tOnly if something else was a real contender. Name it and say why it lost — don't list every option that was never serious.\n23\t"}]},"uuid":"cc758cb2-2de7-4e79-bedd-aaa0b2352657","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:18:20.390Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0000-template.md","content":"# NNNN. Short, decision-shaped title\n\n**Status:** Accepted **Date:** YYYY-MM-DD\n\n## Context\n\nWhat forced this? The constraint, not the backstory. 2-4 sentences.\n\n## Decision\n\nWhat we're doing, stated plainly. One paragraph.\n\n## Consequences\n\nWhat this costs and what it buys. Bullets.\n\n-\n-\n\n## Alternatives considered (optional)\n\nOnly if something else was a real contender. Name it and say why it lost — don't list every option that was never serious.\n","numLines":23,"startLine":1,"totalLines":23}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f23be02-f437-4523-af44-6edf57bef722","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"cc758cb2-2de7-4e79-bedd-aaa0b2352657","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Read","toolUseID":"toolu_01RR6GRiq3pBRG76PedbPjTX","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Read\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":81},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a3ec4f0a-141d-45f0-bbc3-ae70a511499c","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:18:20.389Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"a3ec4f0a-141d-45f0-bbc3-ae70a511499c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi68NqXMWAtQJKuMmiu7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01END9d1YzatkgLfSbDUM4uT","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22233,"cache_read_input_tokens":177768,"output_tokens":1404,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22233,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":177768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22233,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22233},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi68LVdgrPZv13GpkB2v","type":"assistant","uuid":"6c0f0a52-94bf-4edf-83d7-1c2db399642a","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:18:20.783Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"6c0f0a52-94bf-4edf-83d7-1c2db399642a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"33c33088-8732-4685-a296-f012e6bf5131","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01END9d1YzatkgLfSbDUM4uT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 0002. Hand-write Serialize/Deserialize for PropType instead of deriving it\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** Accepted **Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n4\t\n5\t## Context\n6\t\n7\t`PropType` and `CollectedType` are recursive enums — variants nest through `Vec`/`Box`/`Option` back into the same type (`Union`, `Object`, `Array`, ...). At some point this project derived `Serialize`/`Deserialize` directly on a tagged `PropType` (`#[serde(tag = \"kind\")]`) and had to raise `#![recursion_limit]` to 2048 to get it to compile — each nesting level wraps the generated serializer in another layer during codegen, and the default limit (128) isn't enough for a real component tree.\n8\t\n9\t## Decision\n10\t\n11\t`PropType`, `CollectedType`, and `OpaqueReason` don't derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize`. Each has a hand-written impl (`to_json_value`/`from_json_value` for the first two) that builds a `serde_json::Value` directly instead of going through serde's derive machinery.\n12\t\n13\t## Consequences\n14\t\n15\t- Adding a new variant means updating the manual match in both directions by hand — the compiler won't remind you the way a derive would. `resolver/mod.rs`'s \"no wildcard matches\" convention is what catches a missed arm here instead.\n16\t- `CollectedObjectField` (a struct nested inside `CollectedType::Object`, not an enum) still derives normally — the recursion problem is specific to the recursive _enums_, not every type that touches them.\n17\t- The `#![recursion_limit = \"2048\"]` attribute in `crates/core/src/lib.rs` is left over from the old derive-based design. Verified 2026-07-22: the full workspace builds and every test passes with it removed — nothing in the current manual-impl code path needs it. Worth deleting as a follow-up; left as-is here since confirming that wasn't the point of this decision.\n18\t\n19\t## Alternatives considered\n20\t\n21\t`serde(remote)`, or just keeping the recursion-limit bump — both keep the derive, so you inherit the compile-time cost and a cryptic \"recursion limit exceeded\" the moment someone adds one more level of nesting. Manual impls trade a bit of hand-maintenance for a predictable compile time.\n22\t"}]},"uuid":"9b67cebf-2538-4092-a016-36b0bdf6cae3","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:18:20.874Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md","content":"# 0002. Hand-write Serialize/Deserialize for PropType instead of deriving it\n\n**Status:** Accepted **Date:** 2026-07-22 (retroactive)\n\n## Context\n\n`PropType` and `CollectedType` are recursive enums — variants nest through `Vec`/`Box`/`Option` back into the same type (`Union`, `Object`, `Array`, ...). At some point this project derived `Serialize`/`Deserialize` directly on a tagged `PropType` (`#[serde(tag = \"kind\")]`) and had to raise `#![recursion_limit]` to 2048 to get it to compile — each nesting level wraps the generated serializer in another layer during codegen, and the default limit (128) isn't enough for a real component tree.\n\n## Decision\n\n`PropType`, `CollectedType`, and `OpaqueReason` don't derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize`. Each has a hand-written impl (`to_json_value`/`from_json_value` for the first two) that builds a `serde_json::Value` directly instead of going through serde's derive machinery.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Adding a new variant means updating the manual match in both directions by hand — the compiler won't remind you the way a derive would. `resolver/mod.rs`'s \"no wildcard matches\" convention is what catches a missed arm here instead.\n- `CollectedObjectField` (a struct nested inside `CollectedType::Object`, not an enum) still derives normally — the recursion problem is specific to the recursive _enums_, not every type that touches them.\n- The `#![recursion_limit = \"2048\"]` attribute in `crates/core/src/lib.rs` is left over from the old derive-based design. Verified 2026-07-22: the full workspace builds and every test passes with it removed — nothing in the current manual-impl code path needs it. Worth deleting as a follow-up; left as-is here since confirming that wasn't the point of this decision.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n`serde(remote)`, or just keeping the recursion-limit bump — both keep the derive, so you inherit the compile-time cost and a cryptic \"recursion limit exceeded\" the moment someone adds one more level of nesting. Manual impls trade a bit of hand-maintenance for a predictable compile time.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6c0f0a52-94bf-4edf-83d7-1c2db399642a","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"9b67cebf-2538-4092-a016-36b0bdf6cae3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Read","toolUseID":"toolu_01END9d1YzatkgLfSbDUM4uT","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Read\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":75},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cfca80eb-a10b-4d3a-935b-1f0e95b5e420","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:18:20.873Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"cfca80eb-a10b-4d3a-935b-1f0e95b5e420","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi68NqXMWAtQJKuMmiu7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QUQCAFQiQpDHGMcJhJt6kb","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22233,"cache_read_input_tokens":177768,"output_tokens":1404,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22233,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1404,"cache_read_input_tokens":177768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22233,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22233},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi68LVdgrPZv13GpkB2v","type":"assistant","uuid":"c18cdb08-7964-47ce-b7e3-d8c1d172f18e","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:18:21.005Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"c18cdb08-7964-47ce-b7e3-d8c1d172f18e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"33c33088-8732-4685-a296-f012e6bf5131","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QUQCAFQiQpDHGMcJhJt6kb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Architecture Decision Records\n2\t\n3\tShort, dated records of _architectural_ decisions — ones that shape system structure, boundaries, or contracts other code depends on. Not a changelog, not a design doc, not a place to explain what the code does — comments and `ARCHITECTURE.md` already do that.\n4\t\n5\t## When to write one\n6\t\n7\tTwo gates, both required:\n8\t\n9\t1. **Architectural.** It affects one of: system structure (module/crate boundaries, how components interact), a dependency or technology choice that ripples across the codebase, a data format or contract other code depends on, or a cross-cutting constraint (performance model, correctness discipline, security model).\n10\t2. **Expensive to reverse and not obvious from the code.** If it gets reverted in a year, what breaks, and would anyone know why?\n11\t\n12\tIf either answer is no, it's not an ADR.\n13\t\n14\tGood candidates:\n15\t\n16\t- Choosing OXC over the TypeScript compiler — a technology choice that shapes the whole extraction pipeline\n17\t- A serialization format with a hidden constraint (msgpack's positional encoding) — a data contract other code depends on\n18\t- Dropping a dependency, or an approach that was tried and abandoned\n19\t\n20\tNot ADR material:\n21\t\n22\t- A single function's algorithm choice, confined to that function — that's a code comment\n23\t- A bug fix — commit message, and if it's the kind of thing that could recur, a line in `rdt-coverage.md`\n24\t- A behavior-preserving refactor — commit message is enough\n25\t- A naming or style convention — that's `CLAUDE.md` or a lint rule\n26\t- Anything already obvious from the code or from `CLAUDE.md`'s non-negotiables\n27\t\n28\t## Format\n29\t\n30\tOne file per decision: `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.md`, numbered sequentially, never reused. Copy `0000-template.md` to start.\n31\t\n32\t- **Never edit history.** If a decision changes, write a new ADR and mark the old one's status `Superseded by 000X`. Don't rewrite the old file to look like you knew all along.\n33\t- **Status** is one of: `Accepted`, `Superseded by NNNN`, `Deprecated`.\n34\t- Keep it short. If the technical depth doesn't fit on a screen, split it into its own doc and link it — see `0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md` pointing at `type-checker-integration.md` instead of inlining it.\n35\t\n36\t## Writing it\n37\t\n38\tWrite like you're explaining it to the next engineer over their shoulder, not presenting it to a committee. Don't hard-wrap paragraphs at a fixed column — one line per paragraph, let the editor soft-wrap. Every other doc in this repo already does this; hard-wrapping just makes future diffs noisy when a sentence gets edited.\n39\t\n40\t**Cut the filler.** If a sentence still means the same thing without a word, delete the word.\n41\t\n42\t| Instead of | Write |\n43\t| --- | --- |\n44\t| \"It's worth noting that this decision was made in order to leverage OXC's robust parsing capabilities\" | \"OXC parses in parallel with no type-checking pass\" |\n45\t| \"This represents a significant improvement in performance\" | \"32ms instead of several seconds\" |\n46\t| \"We decided to essentially utilize a positional encoding approach\" | \"We use positional encoding\" |\n47\t| \"In conclusion, this architecture provides a solid foundation going forward\" | (delete — you already said the thing) |\n48\t\n49\t**Banned by default:** _leverage, utilize, robust, seamless, cutting-edge, essentially, basically, in order to, it's worth noting, it is important to note, at the end of the day._ If one is genuinely the precise technical word for something, fine — but check first.\n50\t\n51\t**Concrete beats vague.** Name the file, the number, the benchmark. \"Slow\" is not a fact; \"several seconds on a mid-size design system\" is.\n52\t\n53\t**Active voice, plain structure.** \"We chose X because Y\" beats \"X was chosen due to Y considerations.\" Sentence-case headers, not Title Case.\n54\t\n55\t**Show the trade-off, not just the win.** A decision with no downside isn't a decision, it's a fact. Say what it costs.\n56\t\n57\t## What good looks like\n58\t\n59\tRead `0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md` — a real bug behind it, a real number (`recursion_limit = 2048`), a real consequence, four sections, no throat-clearing.\n60\t"}]},"uuid":"4594e6fe-e643-41de-abf2-8afb2cf4ba52","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:18:21.079Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/adr/README.md","content":"# Architecture Decision Records\n\nShort, dated records of _architectural_ decisions — ones that shape system structure, boundaries, or contracts other code depends on. Not a changelog, not a design doc, not a place to explain what the code does — comments and `ARCHITECTURE.md` already do that.\n\n## When to write one\n\nTwo gates, both required:\n\n1. **Architectural.** It affects one of: system structure (module/crate boundaries, how components interact), a dependency or technology choice that ripples across the codebase, a data format or contract other code depends on, or a cross-cutting constraint (performance model, correctness discipline, security model).\n2. **Expensive to reverse and not obvious from the code.** If it gets reverted in a year, what breaks, and would anyone know why?\n\nIf either answer is no, it's not an ADR.\n\nGood candidates:\n\n- Choosing OXC over the TypeScript compiler — a technology choice that shapes the whole extraction pipeline\n- A serialization format with a hidden constraint (msgpack's positional encoding) — a data contract other code depends on\n- Dropping a dependency, or an approach that was tried and abandoned\n\nNot ADR material:\n\n- A single function's algorithm choice, confined to that function — that's a code comment\n- A bug fix — commit message, and if it's the kind of thing that could recur, a line in `rdt-coverage.md`\n- A behavior-preserving refactor — commit message is enough\n- A naming or style convention — that's `CLAUDE.md` or a lint rule\n- Anything already obvious from the code or from `CLAUDE.md`'s non-negotiables\n\n## Format\n\nOne file per decision: `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.md`, numbered sequentially, never reused. Copy `0000-template.md` to start.\n\n- **Never edit history.** If a decision changes, write a new ADR and mark the old one's status `Superseded by 000X`. Don't rewrite the old file to look like you knew all along.\n- **Status** is one of: `Accepted`, `Superseded by NNNN`, `Deprecated`.\n- Keep it short. If the technical depth doesn't fit on a screen, split it into its own doc and link it — see `0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md` pointing at `type-checker-integration.md` instead of inlining it.\n\n## Writing it\n\nWrite like you're explaining it to the next engineer over their shoulder, not presenting it to a committee. Don't hard-wrap paragraphs at a fixed column — one line per paragraph, let the editor soft-wrap. Every other doc in this repo already does this; hard-wrapping just makes future diffs noisy when a sentence gets edited.\n\n**Cut the filler.** If a sentence still means the same thing without a word, delete the word.\n\n| Instead of | Write |\n| --- | --- |\n| \"It's worth noting that this decision was made in order to leverage OXC's robust parsing capabilities\" | \"OXC parses in parallel with no type-checking pass\" |\n| \"This represents a significant improvement in performance\" | \"32ms instead of several seconds\" |\n| \"We decided to essentially utilize a positional encoding approach\" | \"We use positional encoding\" |\n| \"In conclusion, this architecture provides a solid foundation going forward\" | (delete — you already said the thing) |\n\n**Banned by default:** _leverage, utilize, robust, seamless, cutting-edge, essentially, basically, in order to, it's worth noting, it is important to note, at the end of the day._ If one is genuinely the precise technical word for something, fine — but check first.\n\n**Concrete beats vague.** Name the file, the number, the benchmark. \"Slow\" is not a fact; \"several seconds on a mid-size design system\" is.\n\n**Active voice, plain structure.** \"We chose X because Y\" beats \"X was chosen due to Y considerations.\" Sentence-case headers, not Title Case.\n\n**Show the trade-off, not just the win.** A decision with no downside isn't a decision, it's a fact. Say what it costs.\n\n## What good looks like\n\nRead `0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md` — a real bug behind it, a real number (`recursion_limit = 2048`), a real consequence, four sections, no throat-clearing.\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c18cdb08-7964-47ce-b7e3-d8c1d172f18e","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
