{"parentUuid":"25183601-d7e6-4493-a4db-62cc6ed680f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi6FqKffbH17fBBH8ytu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Na6AaT6JHTNT9WXGhgwnUn","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/edge-cases.md","old_string":"## Suggested next step\n\nThis is a lot of surface area — 5 crash/hang risks, 5 silent-correctness bugs, ~20 silent-data-loss sites, 2 contract inconsistencies. Worth deciding scope before touching code: fix the P0 correctness bugs first (they're the ones producing *wrong* answers, which is worse than a documented gap), then the P1 hang risks that are realistic rather than adversarial (template-literal blowup, plugin/per-file panic containment), then triage the P2 silent-drop list — some of those (anonymous default export, class components) may be worth an explicit \"not supported\" diagnostic even if full support isn't warranted yet.","new_string":"## Root-cause analysis and implementation plan\n\nSee `root-cause-analysis.md` — the ~30 findings above collapse into 11 mechanism-level root causes plus 7 standalone tickets, each with a concrete fix proposal and a Phase 1 task breakdown grouped by shared-file conflicts. Two clusters (panic containment, schema derivation) are new architectural decisions with a draft ADR each; the rest are enforcement of an existing-but-unenforced pattern. Update the tables above to mark items fixed as Phase 2 implementation lands."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9654,"cache_read_input_tokens":204234,"output_tokens":973,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9654,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_to