t of surface area — 5 crash/hang risks, 5 silent-correctness bugs, ~20 silent-data-loss sites, 2 contract inconsistencies. Worth deciding scope before touching code: fix the P0 correctness bugs first (they're the ones producing *wrong* answers, which is worse than a documented gap), then the P1 hang risks that are realistic rather than adversarial (template-literal blowup, plugin/per-file panic containment), then triage the P2 silent-drop list — some of those (anonymous default export, class components) may be worth an explicit \"not supported\" diagnostic even if full support isn't warranted yet.","+See `root-cause-analysis.md` — the ~30 findings above collapse into 11 mechanism-level root causes plus 7 standalone tickets, each with a concrete fix proposal and a Phase 1 task breakdown grouped by shared-file conflicts. Two clusters (panic containment, schema derivation) are new architectural decisions with a draft ADR each; the rest are enforcement of an existing-but-unenforced pattern. Update the tables above to mark items fixed as Phase 2 implementation lands."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1eab98b4-6c85-4ba0-b3be-cb3ab2d46cfb","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
