{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:47:22.818Z","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>w33aybccq</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_017tF9TWF3bAdT8Z9Jyxy1w9</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/0ae3953f-9438-46c4-a76a-88fce9eed529/tasks/w33aybccq.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Adversarially stress-test root-cause-analysis.md: is each root cause actually correct, and would each mechanism proposal actually work\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"verdicts\":[{\"groupName\":\"4. No panic-containment boundary / ADR 0005\",\"perClusterVerdicts\":[{\"clusterOrFindingName\":\"4. No panic-containment boundary (root cause)\",\"rootCauseVerdict\":\"confirmed\",\"mechanismVerdict\":\"needs-adjustment\",\"issues\":\"Root-cause claims verified accurate: (1) `grep -rn catch_unwind` across the repo (excluding target/) returns zero hits in any .rs file — only doc mentions. (2) crates/binding/src/lib.rs:118-127 (extract_all), 144-166 (extract_file_incremental), 171-189 (initialize_session) all wrap their body in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking(move || {...}).await.map_err(...)?`, and a panic inside the closure produces `JoinError` on `.await` rather than propagating the unwind — accurate. (3) create_session (lib.rs:131-138) and close_session (lib.rs:192-195) are plain sync `#[napi] pub fn` with no spawn_blocking — accurate, matches doc's cited lines almost exactly. (4) pipeline/mod.rs:260 (parse rayon `.map()`) and :357 (resolve rayon `.map()`) have no per-item catch_unwind — accurate. (5) plugin.rs's `run_on_file_extracted`/`run_on_component_resolved` loops (lines 47-56) call `plugin.on_file_extracted(file_path, data)` / `plugin.on_component_resolved(entry)` directly with no isolation between plugins — accurate; these are called sequentially from pipeline/mod.rs:293 and :385 (not inside the rayon closures — both plugin hook call sites are in the sequential post-collect loops, so the doc's mechanism of wrapping 'each individual call' is targeting the right, already-sequential granularity). (6) watch.rs:93 `self.initialized.lock().expect(\\\"init lock poisoned\\\")` holds the guard across the entire body of `initialize()`, which calls `extract_with_global` (the same rayon+plugin pipeline) — so a panic during that call while the guard is held does poison the mutex permanently, exactly as claimed. All root-cause claims check out.\\n\\nHowever the Mechanism paragraph (line 45) has a real, verified gap: it proposes wrapping `plugin.on_x(...)` calls individually via `contain_panic&lt;T&gt;(label, f: impl FnOnce() -&gt; T + UnwindSafe)`, but `plugin.rs:49` (`plugin.on_file_extracted(file_path, data)` where `data: &amp;mut SourceData`) and `plugin.rs:55` (`plugin.on_component_resolved(entry)` where `entry: &amp;mut ComponentEntry`) each capture a `&amp;mut` reference. I verified empirically (rustc E0277) that `&amp;mut T` unconditionally does NOT implement `UnwindSafe` in std, regardless of T — this is a hard compile error, not a style nit. The doc never mentions this and gives no indication the fix needs `AssertUnwindSafe`. Using `AssertUnwindSafe` here isn't just plumbing either: it papers over the real hazard std's UnwindSafe bound exists to flag — if a plugin panics mid-mutation of `data`/`entry`, the caller (pipeline/mod.rs:293/385) unconditionally continues using that possibly half-mutated value afterward (`diagnostics.append(&amp;mut data.diagnostics)`, `global.merge(&amp;path, data)` at mod.rs:292/297; `components.insert(key, entry)` at mod.rs:386) with no rollback or corruption check. The mechanism needs to explicitly address this — either specify AssertUnwindSafe with a documented rationale for why partial mutation is acceptable here, or change the design so a caught panic discards the mutated value rather than trusting it. As written, 'wrap each individual plugin.on_x(...) call' is not directly buildable against the stated `contain_panic` signature.\"},{\"clusterOrFindingName\":\"Proposed ADR-0005\",\"rootCauseVerdict\":\"confirmed\",\"mechanismVerdict\":\"needs-adjustment\",\"issues\":\"Context/Decision/Consequences text is consistent with the verified root cause and doesn't overstate anything — 'accident of spawn_blocking's JoinError' is accurate per my read of lib.rs. One thing worth noting: the ADR (and root-cause doc) present create_session/close_session's lack of spawn_blocking as purely an oversight relative to their siblings, without checking whether napi-rs itself has any opt-in panic-safety knob that would change the fix's shape. I checked: napi-derive-backend 5.1.1 (matches pinned napi=\\\"3\\\"/napi-derive=\\\"3\\\") has an opt-in `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` attribute (napi-derive-backend/src/ast.rs:35, codegen/fn.rs:142-145) that wraps the generated function body in `std::panic::catch_unwind` — but it is opt-in (bool, unset by default) and none of the four `#[napi]` fns in lib.rs use it. So napi-rs does NOT auto-protect create_session/close_session (confirms edge-cases.md's P1-9 'needs verification' item in the direction the doc assumed), but this also surfaces a second, simpler sanctioned tool already available at the FFI boundary specifically (`#[napi(catch_unwind)]`) that the ADR doesn't mention as an alternative/complement to the custom `panic_guard::contain_panic` helper — worth a line in the ADR's reasoning since it changes the 'one sanctioned helper' framing at that boundary.\\n\\nSeparately: the ADR's Decision line says panics from 'a rayon `.map()`, a DocgenPlugin hook, or a NAPI entry point' are contained through 'one sanctioned helper' — but per the finding above, the plugin-hook case can't cleanly use that same helper without the AssertUnwindSafe caveat, so the ADR's claim of one uniform mechanism for all three call-site classes is slightly optimistic; the plugin case needs an explicit, documented exception/wrapper convention, not just a drop-in call.\"}],\"overallVerdict\":\"The empirical root-cause claims for cluster 4 hold up well under direct verification — zero catch_unwind in the repo, all three async NAPI entry points genuinely rely on spawn_blocking's JoinError as accidental protection, create_session/close_session genuinely skip it, the rayon closures at pipeline/mod.rs:260 and :357 genuinely have no per-item boundary, and watch.rs:93's mutex genuinely stays locked across the exact pipeline call that would panic. This section is safe to build a plan on as far as diagnosis goes. But the proposed mechanism has one concrete, verified defect that must be corrected before implementation: wrapping the plugin hook calls (plugin.rs:49,55) in `contain_panic&lt;T: FnOnce() -&gt; T + UnwindSafe&gt;` will not compile as literally described, because both calls capture a `&amp;mut` reference and `&amp;mut T` is unconditionally !UnwindSafe in std (verified via rustc reproduction). The plan needs an explicit decision — AssertUnwindSafe plus a stated rationale for tolerating partially-mutated SourceData/ComponentEntry after a caught panic, or a design that discards/validates the mutated value on panic rather than trusting it — before this task is handed to an implementer. The rayon closures at mod.rs:260/357 are comparatively low-risk (no &amp;mut captures observed; ResolutionContext at resolver/mod.rs:118-143 doesn't carry the PluginRegistry/trait-object fields that would create their own RefUnwindSafe problems), though DashMap/oxc_resolver::Resolver's exact RefUnwindSafe status wasn't exhaustively verified. The ADR draft is reasonable but should note napi-rs's own opt-in `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` (confirmed present in napi-derive-backend 5.1.1, opt-in only) as an available complementary mechanism at the FFI boundary specifically, and should soften its 'one sanctioned helper covers all three call-site classes' framing given the plugin-hook UnwindSafe wrinkle. No existing test locks in the current panic-crashes-everything behavior (no should_panic tests found touching pipeline/plugin/binding code), so fixing this is not a breaking-test-change concern.\"},{\"groupName\":\"Resolver give-up constructor discipline (cluster 1) + Resolver precedence ordering (cluster 8)\",\"perClusterVerdicts\":[{\"clusterOrFindingName\":\"8. Resolver precedence: two hand-copied orderings (P0-1)\",\"rootCauseVerdict\":\"confirmed\",\"mechanismVerdict\":\"needs-adjustment\",\"issues\":\"Verified directly: chain.rs's resolve_props_chain checks known-pattern shortcuts (Step 2, chain.rs:92-141, calling resolve_known) BEFORE canonical/type-alias/interface lookup (Steps 3-5, chain.rs:142-158). named\n... (truncated 54311 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/0ae3953f-9438-46c4-a76a-88fce9eed529/tasks/w33aybccq.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/subagents/workflows/wf_27dfc3ca-6f1/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/workflows/scripts/edge-case-adversarial-verify-wf_27dfc3ca-6f1.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_27dfc3ca-6f1'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>8</agent_count><agents_done>8</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>498763</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>161</tool_uses><duration_ms>488509</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
