explicit, documented exception/wrapper convention, not just a drop-in call.\"}],\"overallVerdict\":\"The empirical root-cause claims for cluster 4 hold up well under direct verification — zero catch_unwind in the repo, all three async NAPI entry points genuinely rely on spawn_blocking's JoinError as accidental protection, create_session/close_session genuinely skip it, the rayon closures at pipeline/mod.rs:260 and :357 genuinely have no per-item boundary, and watch.rs:93's mutex genuinely stays locked across the exact pipeline call that would panic. This section is safe to build a plan on as far as diagnosis goes. But the proposed mechanism has one concrete, verified defect that must be corrected before implementation: wrapping the plugin hook calls (plugin.rs:49,55) in `contain_panic&lt;T: FnOnce() -&gt; T + UnwindSafe&gt;` will not compile as literally described, because both calls capture a `&amp;mut` reference and `&amp;mut T` is unconditionally !UnwindSafe in std (verified via rustc reproduction). The plan needs an explicit decision — AssertUnwindSafe plus a stated rationale for tolerating partially-mutated SourceData/ComponentEntry after a caught panic, or a design that discards/validates the mutated value on panic rather than trusting it — before this task is handed to an implementer. The rayon closures at mod.rs:260/357 are comparatively low-risk (no &amp;mut captures observed; ResolutionContext at resolver/mod.rs:118-143 doesn't carry the PluginRegistry/trait-object fields that would create their own RefUnwindSafe problems), though DashMap/oxc_resolver::Resolver's exact RefUnwindSafe status wasn't exhaustively verified. The ADR draft is reasonable but should note napi-rs's own opt-in `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` (confirmed present in napi-derive-backend 5.1.1, opt-in only) as an available complementary mechanism at the FFI boundary specifically, and should soften its 'one sanctioned helper covers all three call-site classes' framing given the plugin-hook UnwindSafe wrinkle. No existing test locks in the current panic-crashes-everything behavior (no should_panic tests found touching pipeline/plugin/binding code), so fixing this is not a breaking-test-change concern.\"},{\"groupName\":\"Resolver give-up constructor discipline (cluster 1) + Resolver precedence ordering (cluster 8)\",\"perClusterVerdicts\":[{\"clusterOrFindingName\":\"8. Resolver precedence: two hand-copied orderings (P0-1)\",\"rootCauseVerdict\":\"confirmed\",\"mechanismVerdict\":\"needs-adjustment\",\"issues\":\"Verified directly: chain.rs's resolve_props_chain checks known-pattern shortcuts (Step 2, chain.rs:92-141, calling resolve_known) BEFORE canonical/type-alias/interface lookup (Steps 3-5, chain.rs:142-158). named\n... (truncated 54311 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/0ae3953f-9438-46c4-a76a-88fce9eed529/tasks/w33aybccq.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/subagents/workflows/wf_27dfc3ca-6f1/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-oxc-react-codegen/d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7/workflows/scripts/edge-case-adversarial-verify-wf_27dfc3ca-6f1.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_27dfc3ca-6f1'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>8</agent_count><agents_done>8</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>498763</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>161</tool_uses><duration_ms>488509</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"f758d112-a703-484f-b