{"parentUuid":"b75254ec-e4c6-4bfa-be3f-50b89d7f9f95","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8NahHCFJrvbth5RAL4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25182,"cache_read_input_tokens":243567,"output_tokens":1460,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25182,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":243567,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25182},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8NYAyLZcsNSx3BcCAF","type":"assistant","uuid":"b22d9d5c-9dc8-430d-a349-e3abc9e76fc4","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:47:49.138Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"b22d9d5c-9dc8-430d-a349-e3abc9e76fc4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8NahHCFJrvbth5RAL4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adversarial verification is thorough and found real, load-bearing problems — including two mechanisms that are outright **unsound** (won't compile / won't fix what they claim to fix), not just underspecified. Let me correct `root-cause-analysis.md` before the plan-drafting output gets assembled."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25182,"cache_read_input_tokens":243567,"output_tokens":1460,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25182,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":243567,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25182},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8NYAyLZcsNSx3BcCAF","type":"assistant","uuid":"4b3edee0-ebd8-4cbe-b9fe-1ce277c32514","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:47:50.492Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"4b3edee0-ebd8-4cbe-b9fe-1ce277c32514","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8NahHCFJrvbth5RAL4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EgaEMEbeYwBLicB56ZoKCQ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","offset":1,"limit":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25182,"cache_read_input_tokens":243567,"output_tokens":1460,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25182,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":243567,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25182},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8NYAyLZcsNSx3BcCAF","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b8f5efa-5621-4836-83b9-b36d170541a9","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:47:51.278Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"3b8f5efa-5621-4836-83b9-b36d170541a9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EgaEMEbeYwBLicB56ZoKCQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Root-Cause Analysis: `edge-cases.md` Findings\n2\t\n3\tPhase 0 of the edge-case remediation effort. Four parallel agents each took a candidate cluster from `edge-cases.md` and asked not \"what's broken\" (already catalogued) but \"what's missing that let it happen\" — reading the actual code at every cited site, not just trusting the audit's summary. Three of the four found their assigned cluster wasn't one mechanism, it was several; after splitting, **11 confirmed mechanism-level root causes** and **7 genuinely standalone findings** remain.\n4\t\n5\t**The overall pattern:** this codebase has good conventions in places that got established once — a named constructor, a depth counter, a truncation helper, a documented precedence order — but nothing makes those conventions load-bearing. They're advisory, so a parallel or later code path silently diverges from them. The fix shape repeats across clusters: turn an advisory helper into the *only* callable constructor, or add the one missing signal channel a class of code was never given. Two clusters (panic containment, schema derivation) are genuinely new architectural decisions and get an ADR; the rest are internal refactors of an existing-but-unenforced pattern.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Mechanism clusters\n10\t\n11\t### 1. Resolver give-up constructor discipline\n12\t\n13\t**Root cause:** `ResolvedChain::default()` and `PropType::Opaque { raw, reason }` are plain struct literals. The named \"give up, record a diagnostic\" constructors (`ResolvedChain::empty_with_compose`, `collected.rs::push_opaque_diagnostic`) already exist and are correct where used — but nothing stops a call site from reaching for the bare literal instead. 6 of ~10 `Opaque` construction sites (`func.rs:61`, `primitives.rs:181`, `template.rs:39`, plus others) and the cycle-detected path at `chain.rs:40` bypass the named constructor entirely, invisible to a reviewer scanning the happy path.\n14\t\n15\t**Mechanism:** In `resolver/mod.rs`, make `ResolvedChain`'s bare/`Default` construction private; add `ResolvedChain::give_up(type_name, diag, state)` as the only public \"give up\" entry point. Convert `PropType::Opaque { raw, reason }` to `PropType::Opaque(OpaqueDetail)` with private fields in a new `resolver/opaque.rs`, exposing only `OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, what, reason)`. Update the ~10 existing call sites and the two `PropType` serde match arms (ADR-0002 territory — the wire shape doesn't change, only the Rust constructor surface). Add an `rg`-based backstop to the `/check` flow for any reintroduced bare literal.\n16\t\n17\t**Resolves:** `resolver-chain-cycle-detected-default`, `resolver-func-multiparam-no-diagnostic`, `resolver-literalunion-as-props-base` (P2 items in `edge-cases.md`).\n18\t\n19\t**ADR:** No — enforcing an existing pattern, not introducing a new one.\n20\t\n21\t### 2. Extractor missing give-up signal channel\n22\t\n23\t**Root cause:** `classify_type_alias`, `extract_type_name_from_type`, and the component-detector `.or_else()` chains in `visit.rs` are `Option`-returning `?`-chains over AST shapes with no way to distinguish \"wrong shape, fine\" from \"matched but malformed, worth flagging.\" `SourceData.diagnostics` exists and other extractor code already pushes into it (nesting-depth guard, parse errors) — it was simply never wired to these specific functions. This is a design gap, not helper drift: no helper could be \"used inconsistently\" because none was ever built for this call shape.\n24\t\n25\t**Mechanism:** Add `fn record_skip(&mut self, code: DiagnosticCode, message: impl Into<String>, span: Span)` in `extractor/mod.rs`, plus a new `DiagnosticCode::SkippedCandidate` variant. Wire it into every malformed-but-matched arm in `alias.rs::classify_type_alias` and the end of each detector chain in `visit.rs` (lines 236-247, 262-293). This is a `crates/core/CLAUDE.md` checklist requirement, not a lint — distinguishing \"not this shape\" from \"this shape but unsupported\" needs domain judgment per call site.\n26\t\n27\t**Resolves:** `extractor-classify-type-alias-omit-pick-etc`, `extractor-extract-props-arg-terminal-none`, `extractor-failed-detector-silence`, `extractor-computed-property-keys`. New detector *coverage* (anonymous default export, class components, `Object.assign`, class-expression components, `satisfies`) is a separate feature-gap task — `record_skip` only makes the existing miss visible, it doesn't add support.\n28\t\n29\t**ADR:** No.\n30\t"}]},"uuid":"0e29b789-1129-4a80-b3f2-003d8668f791","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:47:51.341Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","content":"# Root-Cause Analysis: `edge-cases.md` Findings\n\nPhase 0 of the edge-case remediation effort. Four parallel agents each took a candidate cluster from `edge-cases.md` and asked not \"what's broken\" (already catalogued) but \"what's missing that let it happen\" — reading the actual code at every cited site, not just trusting the audit's summary. Three of the four found their assigned cluster wasn't one mechanism, it was several; after splitting, **11 confirmed mechanism-level root causes** and **7 genuinely standalone findings** remain.\n\n**The overall pattern:** this codebase has good conventions in places that got established once — a named constructor, a depth counter, a truncation helper, a documented precedence order — but nothing makes those conventions load-bearing. They're advisory, so a parallel or later code path silently diverges from them. The fix shape repeats across clusters: turn an advisory helper into the *only* callable constructor, or add the one missing signal channel a class of code was never given. Two clusters (panic containment, schema derivation) are genuinely new architectural decisions and get an ADR; the rest are internal refactors of an existing-but-unenforced pattern.\n\n---\n\n## Mechanism clusters\n\n### 1. Resolver give-up constructor discipline\n\n**Root cause:** `ResolvedChain::default()` and `PropType::Opaque { raw, reason }` are plain struct literals. The named \"give up, record a diagnostic\" constructors (`ResolvedChain::empty_with_compose`, `collected.rs::push_opaque_diagnostic`) already exist and are correct where used — but nothing stops a call site from reaching for the bare literal instead. 6 of ~10 `Opaque` construction sites (`func.rs:61`, `primitives.rs:181`, `template.rs:39`, plus others) and the cycle-detected path at `chain.rs:40` bypass the named constructor entirely, invisible to a reviewer scanning the happy path.\n\n**Mechanism:** In `resolver/mod.rs`, make `ResolvedChain`'s bare/`Default` construction private; add `ResolvedChain::give_up(type_name, diag, state)` as the only public \"give up\" entry point. Convert `PropType::Opaque { raw, reason }` to `PropType::Opaque(OpaqueDetail)` with private fields in a new `resolver/opaque.rs`, exposing only `OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, what, reason)`. Update the ~10 existing call sites and the two `PropType` serde match arms (ADR-0002 territory — the wire shape doesn't change, only the Rust constructor surface). Add an `rg`-based backstop to the `/check` flow for any reintroduced bare literal.\n\n**Resolves:** `resolver-chain-cycle-detected-default`, `resolver-func-multiparam-no-diagnostic`, `resolver-literalunion-as-props-base` (P2 items in `edge-cases.md`).\n\n**ADR:** No — enforcing an existing pattern, not introducing a new one.\n\n### 2. Extractor missing give-up signal channel\n\n**Root cause:** `classify_type_alias`, `extract_type_name_from_type`, and the component-detector `.or_else()` chains in `visit.rs` are `Option`-returning `?`-chains over AST shapes with no way to distinguish \"wrong shape, fine\" from \"matched but malformed, worth flagging.\" `SourceData.diagnostics` exists and other extractor code already pushes into it (nesting-depth guard, parse errors) — it was simply never wired to these specific functions. This is a design gap, not helper drift: no helper could be \"used inconsistently\" because none was ever built for this call shape.\n\n**Mechanism:** Add `fn record_skip(&mut self, code: DiagnosticCode, message: impl Into<String>, span: Span)` in `extractor/mod.rs`, plus a new `DiagnosticCode::SkippedCandidate` variant. Wire it into every malformed-but-matched arm in `alias.rs::classify_type_alias` and the end of each detector chain in `visit.rs` (lines 236-247, 262-293). This is a `crates/core/CLAUDE.md` checklist requirement, not a lint — distinguishing \"not this shape\" from \"this shape but unsupported\" needs domain judgment per call site.\n\n**Resolves:** `extractor-classify-type-alias-omit-pick-etc`, `extractor-extract-props-arg-terminal-none`, `extractor-failed-detector-silence`, `extractor-computed-property-keys`. New detector *coverage* (anonymous default export, class components, `Object.assign`, class-expression components, `satisfies`) is a separate feature-gap task — `record_skip` only makes the existing miss visible, it doesn't add support.\n\n**ADR:** No.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":185}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b8f5efa-5621-4836-83b9-b36d170541a9","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
