{"parentUuid":"841df561-5c01-4e7a-ae37-73d1208c453c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8TgCofb8M3WrqX5Ror","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A7hXh3jZXVBWE6WHbv6DKh","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","old_string":"**Mechanism:** Give `discover_files` a `&mut Vec<Diagnostic>` param, pushing on `Err` and on the non-UTF8-path fallback (reuse the pattern at `mod.rs:269-272`). Fix the `&&` guard at `mod.rs:220` and add a `src_dirs: []` regression test. Check `components.insert`'s return at `mod.rs:386` and push a collision diagnostic on `Some(_)` — this one change fixes both the same-name-same-file and overlapping-`src_dirs` findings at once.","new_string":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** give `discover_files` a `&mut Vec<Diagnostic>` param, pushing on `Err` and on the non-UTF8-path fallback (reuse the pattern at `mod.rs:269-272`). Also update `discover_files`'s two direct test call sites (`mod.rs:542,562`, currently calling it with the old 2-arg signature). Fix the `mod.rs:220` guard with a *distinct diagnostic message* for \"no source directories were configured\" vs. \"the configured directories don't exist on disk\" — dropping the `!is_empty()` conjunct alone routes an empty list into the \"missing dirs\" branch, which builds its message from `options.src_dirs.first()`/`.iter().join()` and would read as \"None of the configured source directories exist: \" with nothing after the colon, confusing for a genuinely-empty list. Check `components.insert`'s return at `mod.rs:386` and push a collision diagnostic on `Some(_)` — **this catches only a genuine 3+-way same-key collision, not the realistic 2-directory overlap case.** Tracing the actual keying logic: the disambiguation key is `format!(\"{} ({})\", base_name, entry.file_path)` applied to every occurrence after the first, so with exactly two duplicate mappings from the same file (what `[\"./src\", \"./src/components\"]`-style overlap actually produces via `component_mappings.extend()` with no dedup anywhere), the first gets the plain key and the second gets the disambiguated key — two *different* keys, so `insert` never sees a collision. Overlapping `src_dirs` needs its own separate fix: dedup `src_files` by canonical path after sorting in `discover.rs` (e.g. `files.dedup()` post-sort), or dedup `component_mappings` by `(name, file_path)` before the keying loop in `mod.rs`. Implement both — the insert-return check for genuine key collisions, and the dedup for the overlap case — don't rely on either alone."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4552,"cache_read_input_tokens":280302,"output_tokens":1018,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4552,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1018,"cache_read_input_tokens":280302,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4552},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8Tc5ksYYns3rxY8mZE","type":"assistant","uuid":"43fa7944-9715-408d-aff9-9a39fb1a5b28","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:48:54.905Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"43fa7944-9715-408d-aff9-9a39fb1a5b28","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A7hXh3jZXVBWE6WHbv6DKh","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"9c5c0bce-3170-48de-a0c7-b586a2ae23e5","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:48:54.966Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","oldString":"**Mechanism:** Give `discover_files` a `&mut Vec<Diagnostic>` param, pushing on `Err` and on the non-UTF8-path fallback (reuse the pattern at `mod.rs:269-272`). Fix the `&&` guard at `mod.rs:220` and add a `src_dirs: []` regression test. Check `components.insert`'s return at `mod.rs:386` and push a collision diagnostic on `Some(_)` — this one change fixes both the same-name-same-file and overlapping-`src_dirs` findings at once.","newString":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** give `discover_files` a `&mut Vec<Diagnostic>` param, pushing on `Err` and on the non-UTF8-path fallback (reuse the pattern at `mod.rs:269-272`). Also update `discover_files`'s two direct test call sites (`mod.rs:542,562`, currently calling it with the old 2-arg signature). Fix the `mod.rs:220` guard with a *distinct diagnostic message* for \"no source directories were configured\" vs. \"the configured directories don't exist on disk\" — dropping the `!is_empty()` conjunct alone routes an empty list into the \"missing dirs\" branch, which builds its message from `options.src_dirs.first()`/`.iter().join()` and would read as \"None of the configured source directories exist: \" with nothing after the colon, confusing for a genuinely-empty list. Check `components.insert`'s return at `mod.rs:386` and push a collision diagnostic on `Some(_)` — **this catches only a genuine 3+-way same-key collision, not the realistic 2-directory overlap case.** Tracing the actual keying logic: the disambiguation key is `format!(\"{} ({})\", base_name, entry.file_path)` applied to every occurrence after the first, so with exactly two duplicate mappings from the same file (what `[\"./src\", \"./src/components\"]`-style overlap actually produces via `component_mappings.extend()` with no dedup anywhere), the first gets the plain key and the second gets the disambiguated key — two *different* keys, so `insert` never sees a collision. Overlapping `src_dirs` needs its own separate fix: dedup `src_files` by canonical path after sorting in `discover.rs` (e.g. `files.dedup()` post-sort), or dedup `component_mappings` by `(name, file_path)` before the keying loop in `mod.rs`. Implement both — the insert-return check for genuine key collisions, and the dedup for the overlap case — don't rely on either alone.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":7,"newStart":39,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Root cause:** Three independent bugs, not one mechanism. `discover_files` returns a bare `Vec<Utf8PathBuf>` with no diagnostic-return channel at all, so `walker.flatten()` silently drops every `ignore::Walk` error. `pipeline/mod.rs:220`'s empty-`src_dirs` guard (`!options.src_dirs.is_empty() && ...`) is a plain boolean logic error. `pipeline/mod.rs:386`'s `components.insert(key, entry)` discards the `Option<ComponentEntry>` return value that already reveals a collision — the data needed to diagnose it is sitting right there, unused."," ","-**Mechanism:** Give `discover_files` a `&mut Vec<Diagnostic>` param, pushing on `Err` and on the non-UTF8-path fallback (reuse the pattern at `mod.rs:269-272`). Fix the `&&` guard at `mod.rs:220` and add a `src_dirs: []` regression test. Check `components.insert`'s return at `mod.rs:386` and push a collision diagnostic on `Some(_)` — this one change fixes both the same-name-same-file and overlapping-`src_dirs` findings at once.","+**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** give `discover_files` a `&mut Vec<Diagnostic>` param, pushing on `Err` and on the non-UTF8-path fallback (reuse the pattern at `mod.rs:269-272`). Also update `discover_files`'s two direct test call sites (`mod.rs:542,562`, currently calling it with the old 2-arg signature). Fix the `mod.rs:220` guard with a *distinct diagnostic message* for \"no source directories were configured\" vs. \"the configured directories don't exist on disk\" — dropping the `!is_empty()` conjunct alone routes an empty list into the \"missing dirs\" branch, which builds its message from `options.src_dirs.first()`/`.iter().join()` and would read as \"None of the configured source directories exist: \" with nothing after the colon, confusing for a genuinely-empty list. Check `components.insert`'s return at `mod.rs:386` and push a collision diagnostic on `Some(_)` — **this catches only a genuine 3+-way same-key collision, not the realistic 2-directory overlap case.** Tracing the actual keying logic: the disambiguation key is `format!(\"{} ({})\", base_name, entry.file_path)` applied to every occurrence after the first, so with exactly two duplicate mappings from the same file (what `[\"./src\", \"./src/components\"]`-style overlap actually produces via `component_mappings.extend()` with no dedup anywhere), the first gets the plain key and the second gets the disambiguated key — two *different* keys, so `insert` never sees a collision. Overlapping `src_dirs` needs its own separate fix: dedup `src_files` by canonical path after sorting in `discover.rs` (e.g. `files.dedup()` post-sort), or dedup `component_mappings` by `(name, file_path)` before the keying loop in `mod.rs`. Implement both — the insert-return check for genuine key collisions, and the dedup for the overlap case — don't rely on either alone."," "," **Resolves:** `pipeline-permission-denied-files`, `pipeline-non-utf8-filenames`, `pipeline-empty-src-dirs`, `pipeline-same-name-same-file-collision`, `pipeline-overlapping-src-dirs`."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43fa7944-9715-408d-aff9-9a39fb1a5b28","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
