{"parentUuid":"a7263e33-803e-42e7-b86e-4130970b6221","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Explanatory"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3bf5c68e-44f8-4271-9e4b-d9906c1faeff","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:49:11.952Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"3bf5c68e-44f8-4271-9e4b-d9906c1faeff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8Vy48ZUtiXQGEQySYd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MPne4BSU7M7nQPTexqcSYE","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","old_string":"**Mechanism:** Don't advertise `hoverProvider: true` until a handler exists. Make the `content_length: None` branch actually resync (consume to the next blank line) instead of silently `continue`ing past an unconsumed body. Longer-term, consider `lsp-server`/`lsp-types` instead of hand-rolled framing.","new_string":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** don't advertise `hoverProvider: true` until a handler exists. The `content_length: None` branch's originally-proposed fix — \"resync by consuming to the next blank line\" — is **ineffective as stated**: tracing the actual control flow, the header-reading loop already reads and breaks on the blank line *before* the `content_length: None` check runs, so \"consume to the next blank line\" would be a no-op against code that's already past that point. The real problem is structural: with no `Content-Length`, there is no way to know how many bytes the message body occupies, so it cannot be skip-consumed at all — the next read will misinterpret body bytes as new headers. Fix: treat a headerless/no-`Content-Length` message as unrecoverable and close or reset the connection with a diagnostic, rather than attempting to skip past it — LSP framing gives no other resync signal once this state is reached. Longer-term, consider `lsp-server`/`lsp-types` instead of hand-rolled framing."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1588,"cache_read_input_tokens":286128,"output_tokens":596,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1588,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":286128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1588,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1588},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8VwkW4F5pBgHDY52q2","type":"assistant","uuid":"16488fc2-de48-4f3b-a6ad-6739878336eb","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:49:18.533Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"16488fc2-de48-4f3b-a6ad-6739878336eb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPne4BSU7M7nQPTexqcSYE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"4f9c6e8e-54d2-4e43-a094-b2ad15d439f0","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:49:18.619Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","oldString":"**Mechanism:** Don't advertise `hoverProvider: true` until a handler exists. Make the `content_length: None` branch actually resync (consume to the next blank line) instead of silently `continue`ing past an unconsumed body. Longer-term, consider `lsp-server`/`lsp-types` instead of hand-rolled framing.","newString":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** don't advertise `hoverProvider: true` until a handler exists. The `content_length: None` branch's originally-proposed fix — \"resync by consuming to the next blank line\" — is **ineffective as stated**: tracing the actual control flow, the header-reading loop already reads and breaks on the blank line *before* the `content_length: None` check runs, so \"consume to the next blank line\" would be a no-op against code that's already past that point. The real problem is structural: with no `Content-Length`, there is no way to know how many bytes the message body occupies, so it cannot be skip-consumed at all — the next read will misinterpret body bytes as new headers. Fix: treat a headerless/no-`Content-Length` message as unrecoverable and close or reset the connection with a diagnostic, rather than attempting to skip past it — LSP framing gives no other resync signal once this state is reached. Longer-term, consider `lsp-server`/`lsp-types` instead of hand-rolled framing.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":71,"oldLines":7,"newStart":71,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Root cause:** `lsp.rs` is a new, zero-test, hand-rolled JSON-RPC framing layer with no capability/handler consistency check — it advertises `hoverProvider: true` with no hover handler behind it, and a malformed header desyncs the stream instead of resyncing."," ","-**Mechanism:** Don't advertise `hoverProvider: true` until a handler exists. Make the `content_length: None` branch actually resync (consume to the next blank line) instead of silently `continue`ing past an unconsumed body. Longer-term, consider `lsp-server`/`lsp-types` instead of hand-rolled framing.","+**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** don't advertise `hoverProvider: true` until a handler exists. The `content_length: None` branch's originally-proposed fix — \"resync by consuming to the next blank line\" — is **ineffective as stated**: tracing the actual control flow, the header-reading loop already reads and breaks on the blank line *before* the `content_length: None` check runs, so \"consume to the next blank line\" would be a no-op against code that's already past that point. The real problem is structural: with no `Content-Length`, there is no way to know how many bytes the message body occupies, so it cannot be skip-consumed at all — the next read will misinterpret body bytes as new headers. Fix: treat a headerless/no-`Content-Length` message as unrecoverable and close or reset the connection with a diagnostic, rather than attempting to skip past it — LSP framing gives no other resync signal once this state is reached. Longer-term, consider `lsp-server`/`lsp-types` instead of hand-rolled framing."," "," **Resolves:** P1-6, P1-7."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16488fc2-de48-4f3b-a6ad-6739878336eb","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
