{"parentUuid":"435dbe35-5c26-4a3a-956f-15a59007f287","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8XU3BWh6kFXjJdVSs8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sfr2rPkNknRBFDmbkwSQJu","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","old_string":"**Mechanism:** Derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain structs (`ComponentEntry`, `ParsedProp`, `ExtractionStats`, `Diagnostic`, `InheritedLayer`); call `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` from `cmd_schema()`. Hand-write `JsonSchema` impls for `PropType`/`CollectedType`/`OpaqueReason` — the three recursive enums ADR-0002 already exempted from derive machinery for `Serialize` — following that same precedent so the recursion-limit problem isn't reintroduced. If `schemars` as a new dependency is undesirable, the floor-level fix is a CI test that serializes a real fixture and validates it against `schema.rs`'s hand-written output.","new_string":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain structs (`ComponentEntry`, `ParsedProp`, `ExtractionStats`, `Diagnostic`, `InheritedLayer`); call `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` from `cmd_schema()`. Hand-write `JsonSchema` impls only for `PropType` and `CollectedType` — the two enums that are actually recursive and actually have hand-written `Serialize` impls today, per ADR-0002. **Verified correction: `OpaqueReason` is not recursive and does not hand-write `Serialize`.** It has an ordinary `#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]` with no self-referential field — ADR-0002's own text claims otherwise (asserting all three types hand-write their impl), and that ADR text is itself stale relative to the current code; the root-cause analysis originally propagated that stale claim without checking the source directly, exactly the kind of unverified inference this document is meant to avoid. `OpaqueReason` can derive `JsonSchema` normally, alongside the other plain structs — the fix is cheaper than originally stated. Flag ADR-0002's stale claim about `OpaqueReason` for a correction the next time that file is touched. If `schemars` as a new dependency is undesirable, the floor-level fix is a CI test that serializes a real fixture and validates it against `schema.rs`'s hand-written output."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3706,"cache_read_input_tokens":289485,"output_tokens":926,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3706,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":926,"cache_read_input_tokens":289485,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3706},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8XRwg2ofsaLpSt7Bt4","type":"assistant","uuid":"da94c47f-2515-492b-970c-d6c8d42e7acb","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:49:41.680Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"da94c47f-2515-492b-970c-d6c8d42e7acb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sfr2rPkNknRBFDmbkwSQJu","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"88c22272-5a16-48ac-b15a-453e7f276029","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:49:41.807Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","oldString":"**Mechanism:** Derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain structs (`ComponentEntry`, `ParsedProp`, `ExtractionStats`, `Diagnostic`, `InheritedLayer`); call `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` from `cmd_schema()`. Hand-write `JsonSchema` impls for `PropType`/`CollectedType`/`OpaqueReason` — the three recursive enums ADR-0002 already exempted from derive machinery for `Serialize` — following that same precedent so the recursion-limit problem isn't reintroduced. If `schemars` as a new dependency is undesirable, the floor-level fix is a CI test that serializes a real fixture and validates it against `schema.rs`'s hand-written output.","newString":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain structs (`ComponentEntry`, `ParsedProp`, `ExtractionStats`, `Diagnostic`, `InheritedLayer`); call `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` from `cmd_schema()`. Hand-write `JsonSchema` impls only for `PropType` and `CollectedType` — the two enums that are actually recursive and actually have hand-written `Serialize` impls today, per ADR-0002. **Verified correction: `OpaqueReason` is not recursive and does not hand-write `Serialize`.** It has an ordinary `#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]` with no self-referential field — ADR-0002's own text claims otherwise (asserting all three types hand-write their impl), and that ADR text is itself stale relative to the current code; the root-cause analysis originally propagated that stale claim without checking the source directly, exactly the kind of unverified inference this document is meant to avoid. `OpaqueReason` can derive `JsonSchema` normally, alongside the other plain structs — the fix is cheaper than originally stated. Flag ADR-0002's stale claim about `OpaqueReason` for a correction the next time that file is touched. If `schemars` as a new dependency is undesirable, the floor-level fix is a CI test that serializes a real fixture and validates it against `schema.rs`'s hand-written output.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":113,"oldLines":7,"newStart":113,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Root cause:** `cli/commands/schema.rs` hand-writes a JSON Schema as a `serde_json::json!()` literal instead of deriving it from `ComponentEntry`/`ExtractionStats`/`Diagnostic`. Every new field on those structs requires someone to remember to edit a second, structurally unrelated file — and the only existing test checks that the hand-written JSON is syntactically valid, never that it matches real serialized output, so drift is invisible to CI. Concrete drift already present: `.methods`/`.tags`, 5 of 9 `ExtractionStats` fields, and `.line`/`.column`/`.help` are all undocumented in the schema today."," ","-**Mechanism:** Derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain structs (`ComponentEntry`, `ParsedProp`, `ExtractionStats`, `Diagnostic`, `InheritedLayer`); call `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` from `cmd_schema()`. Hand-write `JsonSchema` impls for `PropType`/`CollectedType`/`OpaqueReason` — the three recursive enums ADR-0002 already exempted from derive machinery for `Serialize` — following that same precedent so the recursion-limit problem isn't reintroduced. If `schemars` as a new dependency is undesirable, the floor-level fix is a CI test that serializes a real fixture and validates it against `schema.rs`'s hand-written output.","+**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain structs (`ComponentEntry`, `ParsedProp`, `ExtractionStats`, `Diagnostic`, `InheritedLayer`); call `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` from `cmd_schema()`. Hand-write `JsonSchema` impls only for `PropType` and `CollectedType` — the two enums that are actually recursive and actually have hand-written `Serialize` impls today, per ADR-0002. **Verified correction: `OpaqueReason` is not recursive and does not hand-write `Serialize`.** It has an ordinary `#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]` with no self-referential field — ADR-0002's own text claims otherwise (asserting all three types hand-write their impl), and that ADR text is itself stale relative to the current code; the root-cause analysis originally propagated that stale claim without checking the source directly, exactly the kind of unverified inference this document is meant to avoid. `OpaqueReason` can derive `JsonSchema` normally, alongside the other plain structs — the fix is cheaper than originally stated. Flag ADR-0002's stale claim about `OpaqueReason` for a correction the next time that file is touched. If `schemars` as a new dependency is undesirable, the floor-level fix is a CI test that serializes a real fixture and validates it against `schema.rs`'s hand-written output."," "," **Resolves:** P0-5."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"da94c47f-2515-492b-970c-d6c8d42e7acb","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
