{"parentUuid":"df258c9a-1648-41e7-b9bf-5e5ee08e1c64","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8YBEAthqdA7qtdvMrA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011LCy4MDFLquT3eSHikHmSp","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","old_string":"**Mechanism:** Add `impl ExtractionOutput { pub fn max_severity(&self) -> Option<DiagnosticSeverity>; pub fn exit_code(&self, strict: bool) -> i32 }` in `core/types/output.rs` — pure data-in/data-out, same category as the existing `html_element()` helper, so it doesn't violate the core/no-terminal-code rule. Route `extract.rs` and `check.rs` through it (collapsing their inline checks). Change `cmd_watch` to return `Result<i32>` and call `exit_code(false)` after each pass, or explicitly gate propagation behind a `--ci` flag if always-0 is intentional for interactive use — document the choice either way instead of leaving it silent. Call `exit_code(false)` in `cmd_inspect` after a successful lookup so an Error diagnostic elsewhere in the tree surfaces even when the inspected component itself is fine.","new_string":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** add `impl ExtractionOutput { pub fn max_severity(&self) -> Option<DiagnosticSeverity>; pub fn exit_code(&self, strict: bool) -> i32 }` in `core/types/output.rs` — pure data-in/data-out, same category as the existing `html_element()` helper, so it doesn't violate the core/no-terminal-code rule. **Verified gap: `DiagnosticSeverity` has no ordering today** (`#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]`, no `Ord`/`PartialOrd`, no manual impl) — `max_severity()` needs one added before it can be implemented as a one-liner. Add `Ord`/`PartialOrd`/`Eq` (with variant declaration order double-checked against \"worst severity wins\" semantics — derived `Ord` ranks by declaration order, not by any inherent worst-to-best meaning) or a private `fn rank(&self) -> u8` helper used inside `max_severity()` instead of relying on derived `Ord`. Route `extract.rs` and `check.rs` through the new method (collapsing their inline checks) — note `check.rs` additionally supports a `--strict` warnings-escalate-to-1 path that `extract.rs`'s args have no equivalent flag for today; preserve that distinction rather than assuming the two commands' checks are fully identical. Change `cmd_watch` to return `Result<i32>` and call `exit_code(false)` after each pass, or explicitly gate propagation behind a `--ci` flag if always-0 is intentional for interactive use — document the choice either way instead of leaving it silent. Call `exit_code(false)` in `cmd_inspect` after a successful lookup so an Error diagnostic elsewhere in the tree surfaces even when the inspected component itself is fine."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_read_input_tokens":293191,"output_tokens":1096,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1096,"cache_read_input_tokens":293191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8Y9PJCApBeLLrWvH4E","type":"assistant","uuid":"142d5b7e-b785-4c40-b2d0-e3657e3dc17b","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:49:52.010Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"142d5b7e-b785-4c40-b2d0-e3657e3dc17b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011LCy4MDFLquT3eSHikHmSp","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"1f2fe724-a7aa-4a99-94fc-990d1907a9df","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:49:52.072Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","oldString":"**Mechanism:** Add `impl ExtractionOutput { pub fn max_severity(&self) -> Option<DiagnosticSeverity>; pub fn exit_code(&self, strict: bool) -> i32 }` in `core/types/output.rs` — pure data-in/data-out, same category as the existing `html_element()` helper, so it doesn't violate the core/no-terminal-code rule. Route `extract.rs` and `check.rs` through it (collapsing their inline checks). Change `cmd_watch` to return `Result<i32>` and call `exit_code(false)` after each pass, or explicitly gate propagation behind a `--ci` flag if always-0 is intentional for interactive use — document the choice either way instead of leaving it silent. Call `exit_code(false)` in `cmd_inspect` after a successful lookup so an Error diagnostic elsewhere in the tree surfaces even when the inspected component itself is fine.","newString":"**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** add `impl ExtractionOutput { pub fn max_severity(&self) -> Option<DiagnosticSeverity>; pub fn exit_code(&self, strict: bool) -> i32 }` in `core/types/output.rs` — pure data-in/data-out, same category as the existing `html_element()` helper, so it doesn't violate the core/no-terminal-code rule. **Verified gap: `DiagnosticSeverity` has no ordering today** (`#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]`, no `Ord`/`PartialOrd`, no manual impl) — `max_severity()` needs one added before it can be implemented as a one-liner. Add `Ord`/`PartialOrd`/`Eq` (with variant declaration order double-checked against \"worst severity wins\" semantics — derived `Ord` ranks by declaration order, not by any inherent worst-to-best meaning) or a private `fn rank(&self) -> u8` helper used inside `max_severity()` instead of relying on derived `Ord`. Route `extract.rs` and `check.rs` through the new method (collapsing their inline checks) — note `check.rs` additionally supports a `--strict` warnings-escalate-to-1 path that `extract.rs`'s args have no equivalent flag for today; preserve that distinction rather than assuming the two commands' checks are fully identical. Change `cmd_watch` to return `Result<i32>` and call `exit_code(false)` after each pass, or explicitly gate propagation behind a `--ci` flag if always-0 is intentional for interactive use — document the choice either way instead of leaving it silent. Call `exit_code(false)` in `cmd_inspect` after a successful lookup so an Error diagnostic elsewhere in the tree surfaces even when the inspected component itself is fine.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":123,"oldLines":7,"newStart":123,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Root cause:** The 0/1/2 exit-code mapping is a doc-comment convention re-typed per command, not a shared function — `extract.rs:68-71` and `check.rs:21-30` already implement the same check with syntactically different code. `ExtractionOutput` has no `exit_code()` method, plausibly because `crates/core/CLAUDE.md`'s \"no terminal/display code in `crates/core`\" rule got over-applied to mean \"no exit-code logic belongs in core either.\" `cmd_watch` returns `()`, not `Result<i32>` (main.rs hardcodes exit 0 for that arm); `cmd_inspect` never touches `output.diagnostics` at all. Both were plausibly written by copying the general command-handler shape without copying the exit-code block, because nothing — return type, trait, lint — forces a new command handler to remember it."," ","-**Mechanism:** Add `impl ExtractionOutput { pub fn max_severity(&self) -> Option<DiagnosticSeverity>; pub fn exit_code(&self, strict: bool) -> i32 }` in `core/types/output.rs` — pure data-in/data-out, same category as the existing `html_element()` helper, so it doesn't violate the core/no-terminal-code rule. Route `extract.rs` and `check.rs` through it (collapsing their inline checks). Change `cmd_watch` to return `Result<i32>` and call `exit_code(false)` after each pass, or explicitly gate propagation behind a `--ci` flag if always-0 is intentional for interactive use — document the choice either way instead of leaving it silent. Call `exit_code(false)` in `cmd_inspect` after a successful lookup so an Error diagnostic elsewhere in the tree surfaces even when the inspected component itself is fine.","+**Mechanism `[corrected]`:** add `impl ExtractionOutput { pub fn max_severity(&self) -> Option<DiagnosticSeverity>; pub fn exit_code(&self, strict: bool) -> i32 }` in `core/types/output.rs` — pure data-in/data-out, same category as the existing `html_element()` helper, so it doesn't violate the core/no-terminal-code rule. **Verified gap: `DiagnosticSeverity` has no ordering today** (`#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]`, no `Ord`/`PartialOrd`, no manual impl) — `max_severity()` needs one added before it can be implemented as a one-liner. Add `Ord`/`PartialOrd`/`Eq` (with variant declaration order double-checked against \"worst severity wins\" semantics — derived `Ord` ranks by declaration order, not by any inherent worst-to-best meaning) or a private `fn rank(&self) -> u8` helper used inside `max_severity()` instead of relying on derived `Ord`. Route `extract.rs` and `check.rs` through the new method (collapsing their inline checks) — note `check.rs` additionally supports a `--strict` warnings-escalate-to-1 path that `extract.rs`'s args have no equivalent flag for today; preserve that distinction rather than assuming the two commands' checks are fully identical. Change `cmd_watch` to return `Result<i32>` and call `exit_code(false)` after each pass, or explicitly gate propagation behind a `--ci` flag if always-0 is intentional for interactive use — document the choice either way instead of leaving it silent. Call `exit_code(false)` in `cmd_inspect` after a successful lookup so an Error diagnostic elsewhere in the tree surfaces even when the inspected component itself is fine."," "," **Resolves:** P3-1."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"142d5b7e-b785-4c40-b2d0-e3657e3dc17b","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
