{"parentUuid":"aa1e3ecb-a648-4148-83df-8dc233a20600","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8aahrrHkZF2xbShGCv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019SnkvJUqv3CMAB3PiSqmXR","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","old_string":"**Decision:** Panics reachable from a rayon `.map()`, a `DocgenPlugin` hook, or a NAPI entry point are contained at per-file/per-plugin/per-call granularity through one sanctioned helper, `panic_guard::contain_panic`, converting the payload into a `Diagnostic` (or `napi::Error`) instead of aborting a batch, killing the whole pipeline, or poisoning a session lock.","new_string":"**Decision:** Panics reachable from a rayon `.map()`, a `DocgenPlugin` hook, or a NAPI entry point are contained at per-file/per-plugin/per-call granularity through one sanctioned helper, `panic_guard::contain_panic`, converting the payload into a `Diagnostic` (or `napi::Error`) instead of aborting a batch, killing the whole pipeline, or poisoning a session lock. `contain_panic` wraps its closure in `AssertUnwindSafe` internally (documented rationale: this codebase's data has no interior mutability that could leave an observably-torn state behind a caught panic), so callers never need to reason about `UnwindSafe` themselves — including the plugin-hook call sites, whose `&mut` captures are otherwise `!UnwindSafe`. At the NAPI boundary specifically, `napi-rs`'s own opt-in `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` attribute is a viable complementary or alternative mechanism worth considering alongside `contain_panic`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2496,"cache_read_input_tokens":295437,"output_tokens":642,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2496,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":295437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2496},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8aYMiSfdcS1KT6Y2pU","type":"assistant","uuid":"4561924d-9648-402e-bef1-4de3c1f129c1","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:50:23.857Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"4561924d-9648-402e-bef1-4de3c1f129c1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019SnkvJUqv3CMAB3PiSqmXR","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"0e28ba8b-dc95-42da-a57c-ae8187615c0e","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:50:23.922Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen/docs/root-cause-analysis.md","oldString":"**Decision:** Panics reachable from a rayon `.map()`, a `DocgenPlugin` hook, or a NAPI entry point are contained at per-file/per-plugin/per-call granularity through one sanctioned helper, `panic_guard::contain_panic`, converting the payload into a `Diagnostic` (or `napi::Error`) instead of aborting a batch, killing the whole pipeline, or poisoning a session lock.","newString":"**Decision:** Panics reachable from a rayon `.map()`, a `DocgenPlugin` hook, or a NAPI entry point are contained at per-file/per-plugin/per-call granularity through one sanctioned helper, `panic_guard::contain_panic`, converting the payload into a `Diagnostic` (or `napi::Error`) instead of aborting a batch, killing the whole pipeline, or poisoning a session lock. `contain_panic` wraps its closure in `AssertUnwindSafe` internally (documented rationale: this codebase's data has no interior mutability that could leave an observably-torn state behind a caught panic), so callers never need to reason about `UnwindSafe` themselves — including the plugin-hook call sites, whose `&mut` captures are otherwise `!UnwindSafe`. At the NAPI boundary specifically, `napi-rs`'s own opt-in `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` attribute is a viable complementary or alternative mechanism worth considering alongside `contain_panic`.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":153,"oldLines":7,"newStart":153,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Context:** No existing ADR covers panic/unwind policy. Panic safety today is an accident of `tokio::spawn_blocking`'s `JoinError`, inconsistent across NAPI entry points, plugin hooks, and rayon batches — `create_session`/`close_session` don't even get that accidental protection, and `watch.rs`'s `std::sync::Mutex` can poison permanently as a direct consequence. Picking the wrong granularity now (per-batch vs. per-file vs. per-plugin) is expensive to fix retroactively once call sites depend on it."," ","-**Decision:** Panics reachable from a rayon `.map()`, a `DocgenPlugin` hook, or a NAPI entry point are contained at per-file/per-plugin/per-call granularity through one sanctioned helper, `panic_guard::contain_panic`, converting the payload into a `Diagnostic` (or `napi::Error`) instead of aborting a batch, killing the whole pipeline, or poisoning a session lock.","+**Decision:** Panics reachable from a rayon `.map()`, a `DocgenPlugin` hook, or a NAPI entry point are contained at per-file/per-plugin/per-call granularity through one sanctioned helper, `panic_guard::contain_panic`, converting the payload into a `Diagnostic` (or `napi::Error`) instead of aborting a batch, killing the whole pipeline, or poisoning a session lock. `contain_panic` wraps its closure in `AssertUnwindSafe` internally (documented rationale: this codebase's data has no interior mutability that could leave an observably-torn state behind a caught panic), so callers never need to reason about `UnwindSafe` themselves — including the plugin-hook call sites, whose `&mut` captures are otherwise `!UnwindSafe`. At the NAPI boundary specifically, `napi-rs`'s own opt-in `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` attribute is a viable complementary or alternative mechanism worth considering alongside `contain_panic`."," "," **Consequences:**"," - One bad file, plugin, or session call degrades to a diagnostic instead of taking down everything sharing its batch/pipeline/session."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4561924d-9648-402e-bef1-4de3c1f129c1","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
