2 already accepted for `Serialize`, now doubled. Scoped to 2 enums (`PropType`, `CollectedType`), not 3.\n- Every plain-struct field addition is schema-correct automatically; only the two recursive enums need manual attention going forward.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":164,"oldLines":11,"newStart":164,"newLines":11,"lines":[" "," **Context:** `schema.rs`'s hand-written schema has already drifted from `ComponentEntry`/`ExtractionStats`/`Diagnostic`'s real fields, undetected because the only test checks JSON syntax validity, not field-set parity. ADR-0002 already established the precedent of hand-writing `Serialize` for the three recursive enums (`PropType`, `CollectedType`, `OpaqueReason`) to avoid a recursion-limit blowup."," ","-**Decision:** Derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain output structs; hand-write matching `JsonSchema` impls for the three recursive enums, mirroring their existing hand-written `Serialize` impls. `cmd_schema()` calls `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` instead of building a `json!()` literal by hand.","+**Decision:** Derive `schemars::JsonSchema` on the plain output structs, including `OpaqueReason` (verified non-recursive, already using an ordinary `derive` for `Serialize` — not one of the hand-written cases despite ADR-0002's text suggesting otherwise); hand-write matching `JsonSchema` impls only for `PropType` and `CollectedType`, the two enums that are actually recursive and actually hand-write `Serialize` today. `cmd_schema()` calls `schemars::schema_for!(ExtractionOutput)` instead of building a `json!()` literal by hand."," "," **Consequences:**","-- A second hand-maintained trait impl per recursive enum whenever a variant is added — the same \"compiler won't remind you\" tradeoff ADR-0002 already accepted for `Serialize`, now doubled.","-- Every plain-struct field addition is schema-correct automatically; only the three recursive enums need manual attention going forward.","+- A second hand-maintained trait impl per recursive enum whenever a variant is added — the same \"compiler won't remind you\" tradeoff ADR-0002 already accepted for `Serialize`, now doubled. Scoped to 2 enums (`PropType`, `CollectedType`), not 3.","+- Every plain-struct field addition is schema-correct automatically; only the two recursive enums need manual attention going forward."," - New dependency (`schemars`) — if that's undesirable, the floor-level alternative is a CI test that serializes a real fixture and validates it against the hand-written schema, catching drift without adding a dependency."," "," ---"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ff47f432-c3ce-48e3-840e-4e570d3f33f6","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
