{"parentUuid":"68034953-cda8-4d42-ba2b-146d17f9d1d9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2kpTWQR54m3vNfe4ziy5W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t### Task 1: `ResolvedChain::give_up` — cycle-detected path stops silently degrading\n2\t\n3\t**Files:**\n4\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs:345-395` (the `ResolvedChain` struct + `impl` block)\n5\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs:39-41,108,120,191`\n6\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/resolver/alias.rs:106,116,168,178,291,380`\n7\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/resolver/extends.rs:65`\n8\t- Test: inline `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` in `crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs` (existing convention — `empty_ctx()`/`resolve_type()` helpers already live there)\n9\t\n10\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n11\t```rust\n12\t// crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs, inside `mod tests`\n13\t\n14\t// ── Test: self-referential extends must emit a diagnostic, not silently\n15\t// return an empty chain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16\t// Regression test for: chain.rs's cycle-detected path returned a bare\n17\t// `ResolvedChain::default()` with zero diagnostic when a type's own extends\n18\t// chain referenced itself, silently degrading with no trace — unlike every\n19\t// other give-up path in the resolver.\n20\t\n21\t#[test]\n22\tfn test_self_referential_extends_emits_diagnostic_instead_of_silent_default() {\n23\t    let file_path = Utf8PathBuf::from(\"/test/cycle.tsx\");\n24\t    let scoped_key = format!(\"{}:LoopProps\", file_path);\n25\t\n26\t    let mut global = GlobalSourceData::default();\n27\t    global.interfaces.insert(\n28\t        scoped_key.clone(),\n29\t        CollectedInterface {\n30\t            scoped_key: scoped_key.clone(),\n31\t            name: \"LoopProps\".into(),\n32\t            file_path: file_path.clone(),\n33\t            props: vec![RawProp {\n34\t                name: \"id\".into(),\n35\t                collected_type: CollectedType::String,\n36\t                required: false,\n37\t                description: String::new(),\n38\t                tags: BTreeMap::new(),\n39\t                span_start: 0,\n40\t                span_end: 0,\n41\t            }],\n42\t            // Self-referential — LoopProps extends itself.\n43\t            extends: vec![ExtendsRef::SameFile { name: \"LoopProps\".into(), type_args: vec![] }],\n44\t            description: String::new(),\n45\t            tags: BTreeMap::new(),\n46\t        },\n47\t    );\n48\t\n49\t    let ctx = ResolutionContext::new(Arc::new(global), &PipelineOptions::default());\n50\t    let mapping = ComponentMapping {\n51\t        component_name: \"Loop\".into(),\n52\t        props_type_name: \"LoopProps\".into(),\n53\t        props_type_args: vec![],\n54\t        file_path: file_path.clone(),\n55\t        description: String::new(),\n56\t        tags: BTreeMap::new(),\n57\t        span_start: 0,\n58\t        span_end: 0,\n59\t        param_defaults: FxHashMap::default(),\n60\t    };\n61\t\n62\t    let (entry, diagnostics) = resolve_component(&mapping, &ctx);\n63\t\n64\t    // Own prop still resolves fine — the cycle is only in the extends chain.\n65\t    assert!(entry.props.contains_key(\"id\"));\n66\t    assert!(\n67\t        diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.message.to_lowercase().contains(\"circular\")),\n68\t        \"Expected a diagnostic about the circular extends reference, got {:?}\",\n69\t        diagnostics\n70\t    );\n71\t}\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\t- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n75\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_self_referential_extends_emits_diagnostic_instead_of_silent_default -- --nocapture`\n76\tExpected: FAIL — `resolve_component` returns diagnostics with no \"circular\" message, because `chain.rs:40` returns `ResolvedChain::default()` on the cycle hit without pushing anything.\n77\t\n78\t- [ ] **Step 3: Write minimal implementation**\n79\t\n80\tIn `crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs`, replace the `ResolvedChain` struct/impl:\n81\t```rust\n82\t/// Result of resolving a props chain (including extends).\n83\tstruct ResolvedChain {\n84\t    /// Resolved props (may include inherited props).\n85\t    props: Vec<ParsedProp>,\n86\t    /// Inheritance layers, outermost first.\n87\t    inheritance: Vec<InheritedLayer>,\n88\t    /// Inherited props keyed by name — for notable_inherited population.\n89\t    inherited_by_name: FxHashMap<String, ParsedProp>,\n90\t    /// Type names that could not be resolved.\n91\t    composes: Vec<String>,\n92\t    /// Discriminant prop name if this is a discriminated union.\n93\t    discriminant_prop: Option<String>,\n94\t}\n95\t\n96\timpl ResolvedChain {\n97\t    /// The base empty chain. Deliberately not `Default` — every accumulator\n98\t    /// site (`resolve_interface_chain`, `resolve_base_as_chain`, ...) that\n99\t    /// wants \"start empty, then push into\" calls this directly instead; the\n100\t    /// two *give-up* entry points (`empty_with_compose`, `give_up`) are the\n101\t    /// only public-facing \"this type contributes nothing\" signals. Visible to\n102\t    /// `chain`/`alias`/`extends` since they're child modules of `resolver`.\n103\t    fn empty() -> Self {\n104\t        Self {\n105\t            props: Vec::new(),\n106\t            inheritance: Vec::new(),\n107\t            inherited_by_name: FxHashMap::default(),\n108\t            composes: Vec::new(),\n109\t            discriminant_prop: None,\n110\t        }\n111\t    }\n112\t\n113\t    fn empty_with_compose(type_name: String) -> Self {\n114\t        Self { composes: vec![type_name], ..Self::empty() }\n115\t    }\n116\t\n117\t    /// Give up resolving `type_name` — record it in `composes` (same as\n118\t    /// `empty_with_compose`) and, if `diag` is given, push it onto `state`\n119\t    /// first. The sanctioned \"give up\" entry point for every \"this type\n120\t    /// couldn't be followed further, stop here\" path. Replaces the bare\n121\t    /// `ResolvedChain::default()` the cycle-detected branch used to return,\n122\t    /// which let that one give-up site skip explaining why.\n123\t    fn give_up(type_name: String, diag: Option<Diagnostic>, state: &mut ResolveState) -> Self {\n124\t        if let Some(d) = diag {\n125\t            state.diagnostics.push(d);\n126\t        }\n127\t        Self::empty_with_compose(type_name)\n128\t    }\n129\t\n130\t    /// Merge a parent chain into self — own props already in `self.props` take priority.\n131\t    fn merge_parent(&mut self, parent: ResolvedChain) {\n132\t        // Collect existing prop names so we can skip duplicates.\n133\t        let existing: FxHashSet<String> = self.props.iter().map(|p| p.name.clone()).collect();\n134\t\n135\t        for prop in parent.props {\n136\t            if !existing.contains(&prop.name) {\n137\t                self.props.push(prop.clone());\n138\t            }\n139\t            // Always populate inherited_by_name so notable lookup works.\n140\t            self.inherited_by_name.entry(prop.name.clone()).or_insert(prop);\n141\t        }\n142\t\n143\t        // Prepend parent inheritance layers (parent is further up the chain).\n144\t        let mut new_inheritance = parent.inheritance;\n145\t        new_inheritance.append(&mut self.inheritance);\n146\t        self.inheritance = new_inheritance;\n147\t\n148\t        self.composes.extend(parent.composes);\n149\t        for (name, prop) in parent.inherited_by_name {\n150\t            self.inherited_by_name.entry(name).or_insert(prop);\n151\t        }\n152\t\n153\t        if self.discriminant_prop.is_none() {\n154\t            self.discriminant_prop = parent.discriminant_prop;\n155\t        }\n156\t    }\n157\t}\n158\t```\n159\t(Note: `#[derive(Default)]` is removed from the struct — `empty()` replaces it.)\n160\t\n161\tIn `crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs`, replace the cycle-detected branch (lines 39-41):\n162\t```rust\n163\t    let visit_key: CompactString = format!(\"{}:{}<{}>\", consuming_file, type_name, type_args.join(\",\")).into();\n164\t    if !state.visited.insert(visit_key) {\n165\t        return ResolvedChain::give_up(\n166\t            type_name.to_owned(),\n167\t            Some(Diagnostic {\n168\t                severity: DiagnosticSeverity::Info,\n169\t                message: format!(\n170\t                    \"Circular type reference detected resolving '{}' in '{}' — stopping here to avoid infinite recursion\",\n171\t                    type_name, consuming_file\n172\t                ),\n173\t                file: Some(consuming_file.to_string()),\n174\t                line: None,\n175\t                column: None,\n176\t                help: Some(\"This type (directly or indirectly) extends or references itself.\".into()),\n177\t                code: DiagnosticCode::MaxDepthExceeded,\n178\t            }),\n179\t            state,\n180\t        );\n181\t    }\n182\t```\n183\tAnd fix the two now-invalid `..Default::default()` accumulator sites in the same file:\n184\t- Line 108: `KnownPatternResult::Props(props) => ResolvedChain { props, ..Default::default() },` → `KnownPatternResult::Props(props) => ResolvedChain { props, ..ResolvedChain::empty() },`\n185\t- Line 120: `ResolvedChain { inheritance: vec![layer], ..Default::default() }` → `ResolvedChain { inheritance: vec![layer], ..ResolvedChain::empty() }`\n186\t- Line 191: `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::default();` → `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::empty();`\n187\t\n188\tIn `crates/core/src/resolver/alias.rs`, replace each bare-default accumulator site:\n189\t- Line 106: `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::default();` → `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::empty();`\n190\t- Line 116: `ResolvedChain::default()` → `ResolvedChain::empty()`\n191\t- Line 168: `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::default();` → `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::empty();`\n192\t- Line 178: `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::default();` → `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::empty();`\n193\t- Line 291: `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::default();` → `let mut chain = ResolvedChain::empty();`\n194\t- Line 380: `ResolvedChain { props: merged_props.into_values().collect(), discriminant_prop: discriminant, ..Default::default() }` → `ResolvedChain { props: merged_props.into_values().collect(), discriminant_prop: discriminant, ..ResolvedChain::empty() }`\n195\t\n196\tIn `crates/core/src/resolver/extends.rs`, line 65: `return (ResolvedChain::default(), Some(layer));` → `return (ResolvedChain::empty(), Some(layer));`\n197\t\n198\t- [ ] **Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n199\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_self_referential_extends_emits_diagnostic_instead_of_silent_default -- --nocapture` then `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core`\n200\tExpected: PASS, full suite green (the `empty()`-substitution sites are pure renames with identical behavior, so existing snapshot/unit tests act as the regression net for them).\n201\t\n202\t- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n203\t```bash\n204\tgit add crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs crates/core/src/resolver/alias.rs crates/core/src/resolver/extends.rs\n205\tgit commit -m \"fix(resolver): emit a diagnostic on self-referential extends instead of silently defaulting\"\n206\t```\n207\t\n208\t---\n209\t\n210\t### Task 2: `OpaqueDetail` — make `PropType::Opaque` unconstructible except through a give-up constructor\n211\t\n212\t**Files:**\n213\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/types/output.rs:1-8` (imports), `:140-207` (`PropType` enum — `Opaque` variant), `:275` (`raw_string`), `:294-397` (`to_tagged_value`), `:399-537` (`from_tagged_value`)\n214\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/toon.rs:143`, `:243` (test)\n215\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/known.rs:102-111,126-129,133-136,193-196,221-224,228-231` (construction sites), `:387-389,423-425,432-434,525-527,535-537` (test assertions — exact line numbers will shift slightly as edits land; match by content)\n216\t- Test: inline `#[cfg(test)]` module in `types/output.rs`\n217\t\n218\t**Note on file placement:** the root-cause doc proposed a new `resolver/opaque.rs`, but `PropType` is defined in `crates/core/src/types/output.rs` and `crates/core/CLAUDE.md`'s module layout has `resolver/` depend on `types/`, never the reverse — putting `OpaqueDetail` in `resolver/` would make `types/output.rs` import from `resolver/`, an architecture violation. `OpaqueDetail` is defined in `types/output.rs` itself instead; `ResolveState`/`Diagnostic` (needed by `give_up`) already live in `types/`, so no new cross-module dependency is introduced.\n219\t\n220\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n221\t```rust\n222\t// crates/core/src/types/output.rs, inside a new `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` block\n223\t// (add this module at the end of the file if one doesn't already exist there)\n224\t\n225\t#[cfg(test)]\n226\tmod opaque_detail_tests {\n227\t    use super::*;\n228\t    use crate::types::global::ResolveState;\n229\t\n230\t    #[test]\n231\t    fn give_up_pushes_the_diagnostic_and_builds_the_opaque_payload() {\n232\t        let mut state = ResolveState::default();\n233\t        let diagnostic = Diagnostic {\n234\t            severity: DiagnosticSeverity::Info,\n235\t            message: \"gave up\".into(),\n236\t            file: None,\n237\t            line: None,\n238\t            column: None,\n239\t            help: None,\n240\t            code: DiagnosticCode::OpaqueType,\n241\t        };\n242\t\n243\t        let pt = OpaqueDetail::give_up(&mut state, \"SomeType\", OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded, diagnostic);\n244\t\n245\t        assert_eq!(state.diagnostics.len(), 1);\n246\t        assert_eq!(state.diagnostics[0].message, \"gave up\");\n247\t        let PropType::Opaque(detail) = &pt else { panic!(\"expected PropType::Opaque, got {:?}\", pt) };\n248\t        assert_eq!(detail.raw(), \"SomeType\");\n249\t        assert_eq!(detail.reason(), &OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded);\n250\t    }\n251\t\n252\t    #[test]\n253\t    fn opaque_round_trips_through_the_tagged_json_wire_format() {\n254\t        let pt = OpaqueDetail::new(\"A<B> | C\", OpaqueReason::UnsupportedExpression);\n255\t        let json = pt.to_tagged_value();\n256\t        let restored = PropType::from_tagged_value(&json).expect(\"should deserialize\");\n257\t        assert_eq!(pt, restored);\n258\t    }\n259\t}\n260\t```\n261\t\n262\t- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n263\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core opaque_detail_tests -- --nocapture`\n264\tExpected: FAIL to compile — `OpaqueDetail` doesn't exist yet.\n265\t\n266\t- [ ] **Step 3: Write minimal implementation**\n267\t\n268\tIn `crates/core/src/types/output.rs`, add the import and change the `Opaque` variant (replace the struct-style variant at line ~202):\n269\t```rust\n270\tuse super::global::ResolveState; // add alongside the existing `use super::diagnostic::Diagnostic;`\n271\t```\n272\t```rust\n273\t    // ── Unresolvable — graceful degradation\n274\t    Opaque(OpaqueDetail),\n275\t```\n276\t\n277\tAdd the `OpaqueDetail` type right after the `PropType` enum closes (after line 207, before `impl PropType`):\n278\t```rust\n279\t/// The private payload of `PropType::Opaque`. Fields are unreachable from\n280\t/// outside this module — the only ways to build one are `give_up` (pushes\n281\t/// the diagnostic that explains the degradation, then builds the value) and\n282\t/// `new` (for the one documented exception: `known.rs`, which has no\n283\t/// diagnostics channel of its own and pushes its own diagnostic separately\n284\t/// via `known::push_known_opaque_diagnostic` — see that function's doc\n285\t/// comment). Read the payload back through `raw()`/`reason()`.\n286\t#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\n287\tpub(crate) struct OpaqueDetail {\n288\t    raw: std::string::String,\n289\t    reason: OpaqueReason,\n290\t}\n291\t\n292\timpl OpaqueDetail {\n293\t    pub(crate) fn new(raw: impl Into<std::string::String>, reason: OpaqueReason) -> PropType {\n294\t        PropType::Opaque(OpaqueDetail { raw: raw.into(), reason })\n295\t    }\n296\t\n297\t    /// The sanctioned \"give up and record why\" constructor — pushes\n298\t    /// `diagnostic` onto `state` before building the value, so a resolver\n299\t    /// call site that reaches for this can't forget to explain the\n300\t    /// degradation the way the old bare `PropType::Opaque { .. }` literal let\n301\t    /// call sites do.\n302\t    pub(crate) fn give_up(\n303\t        state: &mut ResolveState,\n304\t        raw: impl Into<std::string::String>,\n305\t        reason: OpaqueReason,\n306\t        diagnostic: Diagnostic,\n307\t    ) -> PropType {\n308\t        state.diagnostics.push(diagnostic);\n309\t        Self::new(raw, reason)\n310\t    }\n311\t\n312\t    pub(crate) fn raw(&self) -> &str {\n313\t        &self.raw\n314\t    }\n315\t\n316\t    pub(crate) fn reason(&self) -> &OpaqueReason {\n317\t        &self.reason\n318\t    }\n319\t}\n320\t```\n321\t\n322\tUpdate `raw_string` (line 275):\n323\t```rust\n324\t            PropType::Opaque(detail) => detail.raw.clone(),\n325\t```\n326\t(same-module access — direct field access is fine inside `output.rs`.)\n327\t\n328\tUpdate `to_tagged_value`'s `Opaque` arm (lines 366-395) — only the match pattern changes, body is unchanged since it's still inside `output.rs`:\n329\t```rust\n330\t            PropType::Opaque(OpaqueDetail { raw, reason }) => {\n331\t                let reason_val = match reason {\n332\t                    OpaqueReason::ConditionalType => serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"conditionalType\"}),\n333\t                    OpaqueReason::MappedType => serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"mappedType\"}),\n334\t                    OpaqueReason::ModuleAugmentation => {\n335\t                        serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"moduleAugmentation\"})\n336\t                    }\n337\t                    OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { function_name } => {\n338\t                        serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"runtimeDependent\", \"functionName\": function_name})\n339\t                    }\n340\t                    OpaqueReason::UnresolvableImport { specifier } => {\n341\t                        serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"unresolvableImport\", \"specifier\": specifier})\n342\t                    }\n343\t                    OpaqueReason::PandaCodegenMissing => {\n344\t                        serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"pandaCodegenMissing\"})\n345\t                    }\n346\t                    OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded => serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"depthExceeded\"}),\n347\t                    OpaqueReason::IndexedAccess { expression } => {\n348\t                        serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"indexedAccess\", \"expression\": expression})\n349\t                    }\n350\t                    OpaqueReason::TemplateLiteral { expression } => {\n351\t                        serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"templateLiteral\", \"expression\": expression})\n352\t                    }\n353\t                    OpaqueReason::MultiParamFunction => serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"multiParamFunction\"}),\n354\t                    OpaqueReason::UnsupportedExpression => {\n355\t                        serde_json::json!({\"type\": \"unsupportedExpression\"})\n356\t                    }\n357\t                };\n358\t                serde_json::json!({\"kind\": \"opaque\", \"raw\": raw, \"reason\": reason_val})\n359\t            }\n360\t```\n361\t\n362\tUpdate `from_tagged_value`'s `\"opaque\"` arm (line ~529) and fallback arm (line ~531-534) — construction via `OpaqueDetail::new` since deserialization isn't a \"give up\" decision (the diagnostic already fired when the value was first produced):\n363\t```rust\n364\t            \"opaque\" => {\n365\t                let raw = v[\"raw\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").to_owned();\n366\t                let reason = match v[\"reason\"][\"type\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"depthExceeded\") {\n367\t                    \"conditionalType\" => OpaqueReason::ConditionalType,\n368\t                    \"mappedType\" => OpaqueReason::MappedType,\n369\t                    \"moduleAugmentation\" => OpaqueReason::ModuleAugmentation,\n370\t                    \"runtimeDependent\" => OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent {\n371\t                        function_name: v[\"reason\"][\"functionName\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").to_owned(),\n372\t                    },\n373\t                    \"unresolvableImport\" => OpaqueReason::UnresolvableImport {\n374\t                        specifier: v[\"reason\"][\"specifier\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").to_owned(),\n375\t                    },\n376\t                    \"pandaCodegenMissing\" => OpaqueReason::PandaCodegenMissing,\n377\t                    \"indexedAccess\" => OpaqueReason::IndexedAccess {\n378\t                        expression: v[\"reason\"][\"expression\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").to_owned(),\n379\t                    },\n380\t                    \"templateLiteral\" => OpaqueReason::TemplateLiteral {\n381\t                        expression: v[\"reason\"][\"expression\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").to_owned(),\n382\t                    },\n383\t                    \"multiParamFunction\" => OpaqueReason::MultiParamFunction,\n384\t                    \"unsupportedExpression\" => OpaqueReason::UnsupportedExpression,\n385\t                    _ => OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded,\n386\t                };\n387\t                Ok(OpaqueDetail::new(raw, reason))\n388\t            }\n389\t            other => Ok(OpaqueDetail::new(format!(\"unknown PropType kind: {}\", other), OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded)),\n390\t```\n391\t\n392\tIn `crates/core/src/toon.rs`:\n393\t- Line 143: `PropType::Opaque { raw, .. } => format!(\"opaque({raw})\"),` → `PropType::Opaque(detail) => format!(\"opaque({})\", detail.raw()),`\n394\t- Line 243 (test): `assert_eq!(format_type_compact(&PropType::Opaque { raw: \"CustomType\".into(), reason: crate::types::output::OpaqueReason::ConditionalType }), \"opaque(CustomType)\");` → `assert_eq!(format_type_compact(&crate::types::output::OpaqueDetail::new(\"CustomType\", crate::types::output::OpaqueReason::ConditionalType)), \"opaque(CustomType)\");`\n395\t\n396\tIn `crates/core/src/known.rs`, convert every direct-construction site to `OpaqueDetail::new(...)` (these callers push their own diagnostic separately via `push_known_opaque_diagnostic` — see that function's doc comment, unchanged behavior):\n397\t- Lines 100-106:\n398\t```rust\n399\t                Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(PropType::Union(vec![\n400\t                    base.clone(),\n401\t                    OpaqueDetail::new(\"/* module augmentation */\", OpaqueReason::ModuleAugmentation),\n402\t                ])))\n403\t```\n404\t- Lines 108-111: `Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(OpaqueDetail::new(\"OverridableStringUnion\", OpaqueReason::ModuleAugmentation)))`\n405\t- Lines 126-129: `\"ThemingProps\" => Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(OpaqueDetail::new(\"ThemingProps\", OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { function_name: \"chakra\".into() }))),`\n406\t- Lines 133-136: `\"StylesApiProps\" => Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(OpaqueDetail::new(\"StylesApiProps\", OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { function_name: \"createStyles\".into() }))),`\n407\t- Lines 193-196: `return Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(OpaqueDetail::new(format!(\"VariantProps<typeof {}>\", name_str), OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { function_name: \"cva\".into() })));`\n408\t- Lines 221-224: `Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(OpaqueDetail::new(format!(\"VariantProps<typeof {}>\", name_str), OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { function_name: \"cva\".into() })))`\n409\t- Lines 228-231: `_ => Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(OpaqueDetail::new(\"VariantProps<...>\", OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { function_name: \"cva\".into() }))),`\n410\t\n411\tAnd its test assertions (`PropType::Opaque { reason: X, .. }` → guard on `.reason()`):\n412\t```rust\n413\t        assert!(matches!(\n414\t            result,\n415\t            Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(PropType::Opaque(ref d))) if d.reason() == &OpaqueReason::ModuleAugmentation\n416\t        ));\n417\t```\n418\t(same substitution — `d.reason() == &OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { .. }` doesn't compile as a `==`, so use `matches!(d.reason(), OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { .. })`) at every occurrence: `test_overridable_string_union_no_args`, `test_theming_props_is_runtime_dependent`, `test_styles_api_props_is_runtime_dependent`, `test_recipe_variant_props_no_args_is_opaque`, `test_variant_props_named_not_in_global_is_opaque`. Concretely, e.g.:\n419\t```rust\n420\t    #[test]\n421\t    fn test_theming_props_is_runtime_dependent() {\n422\t        let result = resolve_known(\"ThemingProps\", &[], &GlobalSourceData::default(), &FxHashMap::default());\n423\t        assert!(matches!(\n424\t            result,\n425\t            Some(KnownPatternResult::Type(PropType::Opaque(ref d)))\n426\t                if matches!(d.reason(), OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { .. })\n427\t        ));\n428\t    }\n429\t```\n430\tApply the same shape to the other four assertions listed above (swap the reason pattern per test: `OpaqueReason::ModuleAugmentation` for `test_overridable_string_union_no_args`, `OpaqueReason::RuntimeDependent { .. }` for the rest).\n431\t\n432\tFinally, resolve every other now-non-compiling `PropType::Opaque { .. }` pattern/construction across the crate that Task 2 doesn't otherwise cover, so the crate builds (these are handled for real in Tasks 3-8, but the crate must compile at the end of *this* task too — replace them mechanically with the equivalent tuple-variant/accessor form for now; Tasks 3-8 then route the resolver-internal ones through `give_up` for real):\n433\t- `crates/core/src/resolver/collected.rs:25,80,104,108,151` → `OpaqueDetail::new(...)` (temporary; Task 3 upgrades to `give_up`)\n434\t- `crates/core/src/resolver/func.rs:61` → `OpaqueDetail::new(raw, OpaqueReason::MultiParamFunction)` (temporary; Task 4 upgrades to `give_up`)\n435\t- `crates/core/src/resolver/primitives.rs:181` → `OpaqueDetail::new(expression.clone(), OpaqueReason::IndexedAccess { expression })` (temporary; Task 5 upgrades to `give_up`)\n436\t- `crates/core/src/resolver/template.rs:39` → `OpaqueDetail::new(raw.clone(), OpaqueReason::TemplateLiteral { expression: raw })` (temporary; Task 6 upgrades to `give_up`)\n437\t- `crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs:29,75` → `OpaqueDetail::new(...)` at 29 (temporary; Task 3 upgrades), pattern-match fix at 75: `if let PropType::Opaque(detail) = &pt { push_known_opaque_diagnostic(&mut state.diagnostics, detail.reason(), name.as_str(), consuming_file); }`\n438\t- `crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs:123` — same pattern-match fix: `if let PropType::Opaque(detail) = &pt { push_known_opaque_diagnostic(&mut state.diagnostics, detail.reason(), type_name_bare, consuming_file); }`\n439\t- `crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs` test assertions at lines 1924, 1972, 1989, 2028, 2132, 2180, 2194, 2205, 2218 — e.g. `matches!(result, PropType::Opaque { reason: OpaqueReason::TemplateLiteral { .. }, .. })` → `matches!(&result, PropType::Opaque(d) if matches!(d.reason(), OpaqueReason::TemplateLiteral { .. }))`, and the bare `matches!(result, PropType::Opaque { .. })` occurrences → `matches!(result, PropType::Opaque(_))`.\n440\t\n441\t- [ ] **Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n442\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core opaque_detail_tests -- --nocapture` then `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core` and `cargo clippy -p oxc-react-docgen-core -- -D warnings`\n443\tExpected: PASS — new tests pass, full suite compiles and passes (no behavior change yet, only the constructor surface).\n444\t\n445\t- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n446\t```bash\n447\tgit add crates/core/src/types/output.rs crates/core/src/toon.rs crates/core/src/known.rs crates/core/src/resolver/collected.rs crates/core/src/resolver/func.rs crates/core/src/resolver/primitives.rs crates/core/src/resolver/template.rs crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs\n448\tgit commit -m \"refactor(resolver): make PropType::Opaque unconstructible outside OpaqueDetail::new/give_up\"\n449\t```\n450\t\n451\t---\n452\t\n453\t### Task 3: Route `collected.rs`'s and `named.rs`'s depth-exceeded Opaque sites through `give_up`\n454\t\n455\t**Files:**\n456\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/resolver/collected.rs:22-26,78-81,101-109,150-152,157-174`\n457\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs:27-30`\n458\t- Test: inline in `crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs`'s existing `mod tests` — `test_conditional_type_opaque_emits_diagnostic`, `test_mapped_type_opaque_emits_diagnostic`, `test_keyof_opaque_emits_diagnostic`, `test_complex_raw_fallback_opaque_emits_diagnostic` (Test 21 block, already present) already assert a diagnostic is emitted for every one of these sites — this task is a pure refactor behind that existing net, plus one new test for the previously-untested depth-exceeded path.\n459\t\n460\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n461\t```rust\n462\t// crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs, inside `mod tests`, near Test 21\n463\t\n464\t#[test]\n465\tfn test_depth_exceeded_opaque_carries_the_max_depth_diagnostic() {\n466\t    let ctx = empty_ctx();\n467\t    let mut state = ResolveState::default();\n468\t    let result = super::collected::resolve_collected_type(\n469\t        &CollectedType::String,\n470\t        Utf8Path::new(\"/test/button.tsx\"),\n471\t        &ctx,\n472\t        &mut state,\n473\t        MAX_DEPTH + 1,\n474\t    );\n475\t    let PropType::Opaque(detail) = &result else { panic!(\"expected Opaque, got {:?}\", result) };\n476\t    assert_eq!(detail.reason(), &OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded);\n477\t    assert!(\n478\t        state.diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code == DiagnosticCode::MaxDepthExceeded),\n479\t        \"expected a MaxDepthExceeded diagnostic, got {:?}\",\n480\t        state.diagnostics\n481\t    );\n482\t}\n483\t```\n484\t\n485\t- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n486\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_depth_exceeded_opaque_carries_the_max_depth_diagnostic -- --nocapture`\n487\tExpected: This one actually already passes today (the depth-exceeded branch already pushes `max_depth_diagnostic` before constructing the literal) — confirm it passes *before* touching the code, so it's a locked-in regression guard rather than a new-behavior test; the real \"fails first\" signal for this task is Step 3 not compiling until `push_opaque_diagnostic` is rewired to return a `Diagnostic` for `give_up` to consume — run `cargo build -p oxc-react-docgen-core` after making the diagnostic-builder change below and confirm the four `Test 21` assertions and this new test all still pass once the give_up wiring lands.\n488\t\n489\t- [ ] **Step 3: Write minimal implementation**\n490\t\n491\tIn `crates/core/src/resolver/collected.rs`, change `push_opaque_diagnostic` from a side-effecting `fn(&mut ResolveState, ...)` into a pure `Diagnostic` builder, and route every Opaque site through `OpaqueDetail::give_up`:\n492\t```rust\n493\tpub fn resolve_collected_type(\n494\t    ct: &CollectedType,\n495\t    consuming_file: &Utf8Path,\n496\t    ctx: &ResolutionContext,\n497\t    state: &mut ResolveState,\n498\t    depth: u8,\n499\t) -> PropType {\n500\t    if depth > MAX_DEPTH {\n501\t        let diag = super::max_depth_diagnostic(&format!(\"type '{}'\", ct.to_raw_string()), consuming_file);\n502\t        return OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, ct.to_raw_string(), OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded, diag);\n503\t    }\n504\t\n505\t    match ct {\n506\t        // ... unchanged primitive/literal/composite arms ...\n507\t\n508\t        CollectedType::KeyOf(_) => {\n509\t            let diag = opaque_diagnostic(\"a standalone 'keyof'\", ct, consuming_file);\n510\t            OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, ct.to_raw_string(), OpaqueReason::MappedType, diag)\n511\t        }\n512\t\n513\t        CollectedType::AtFile { file, inner } => resolve_collected_type(inner, file, ctx, state, depth),\n514\t\n515\t        CollectedType::IndexedAccess { obj, key } => {\n516\t            resolve_indexed_access(obj, key, consuming_file, ctx, state, depth)\n517\t        }\n518\t\n519\t        CollectedType::TemplateLiteral(parts) => resolve_template_literal(parts, consuming_file, ctx, state, depth),\n520\t\n521\t        CollectedType::Function { params, param_names, return_type } => {\n522\t            resolve_function_type(params, param_names, return_type, consuming_file, ctx, state, depth)\n523\t        }\n524\t\n525\t        CollectedType::Conditional { .. } => {\n526\t            let diag = opaque_diagnostic(\"a conditional type\", ct, consuming_file);\n527\t            OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, ct.to_raw_string(), OpaqueReason::ConditionalType, diag)\n528\t        }\n529\t        CollectedType::Mapped { .. } => {\n530\t            let diag = opaque_diagnostic(\"a mapped type\", ct, consuming_file);\n531\t            OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, ct.to_raw_string(), OpaqueReason::MappedType, diag)\n532\t        }\n533\t\n534\t        CollectedType::Raw(s) => {\n535\t            let trimmed = s.trim();\n536\t            if let Some(name) = trimmed.strip_prefix(\"typeof \") {\n537\t                return PropType::Named { name: name.trim().into(), args: vec![] };\n538\t            }\n539\t            if trimmed.starts_with('\"') && trimmed.ends_with('\"') && trimmed.len() >= 2 {\n540\t                return PropType::StringLiteral(trimmed[1..trimmed.len() - 1].to_owned());\n541\t            }\n542\t            if trimmed.starts_with('\\'') && trimmed.ends_with('\\'') && trimmed.len() >= 2 {\n543\t                return PropType::StringLiteral(trimmed[1..trimmed.len() - 1].to_owned());\n544\t            }\n545\t            match trimmed {\n546\t                \"string\" => return PropType::String,\n547\t                \"number\" => return PropType::Number,\n548\t                \"boolean\" => return PropType::Boolean,\n549\t                \"null\" => return PropType::Null,\n550\t                \"undefined\" => return PropType::Undefined,\n551\t                \"never\" => return PropType::Never,\n552\t                \"void\" => return PropType::Void,\n553\t                \"any\" => return PropType::Any,\n554\t                \"unknown\" => return PropType::Unknown,\n555\t                _ => {}\n556\t            }\n557\t            if !trimmed.is_empty()\n558\t                && !trimmed.contains(' ')\n559\t                && !trimmed.contains('|')\n560\t                && !trimmed.contains('&')\n561\t                && !trimmed.contains('<')\n562\t            {\n563\t                PropType::Named { name: trimmed.into(), args: vec![] }\n564\t            } else {\n565\t                let diag = opaque_diagnostic(\"an unparsable raw type expression\", ct, consuming_file);\n566\t                OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, s.clone(), OpaqueReason::UnsupportedExpression, diag)\n567\t            }\n568\t        }\n569\t    }\n570\t}\n571\t\n572\t/// Build the diagnostic explaining why a `CollectedType` degrades to\n573\t/// `PropType::Opaque` — expanding it needs the TypeScript type checker (or,\n574\t/// for the Raw fallback, needs the extractor to understand a syntax shape it\n575\t/// doesn't yet). Pure builder — the caller passes the result to\n576\t/// `OpaqueDetail::give_up`, which pushes it.\n577\tfn opaque_diagnostic(what: &str, ct: &CollectedType, file: &Utf8Path) -> Diagnostic {\n578\t    Diagnostic {\n579\t        severity: DiagnosticSeverity::Info,\n580\t        message: format!(\n581\t            \"'{}' is {} and can't be statically resolved — it will appear as opaque\",\n582\t            ct.to_raw_string(),\n583\t            what\n584\t        ),\n585\t        file: Some(file.to_string()),\n586\t        line: None,\n587\t        column: None,\n588\t        help: None,\n589\t        code: DiagnosticCode::OpaqueType,\n590\t    }\n591\t}\n592\t```\n593\t\n594\tIn `crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs`, replace lines 27-30:\n595\t```rust\n596\t    if depth > MAX_DEPTH {\n597\t        let diag = super::max_depth_diagnostic(&format!(\"named type '{}'\", name), consuming_file);\n598\t        return OpaqueDetail::give_up(state, name.to_string(), OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded, diag);\n599\t    }\n600\t```\n601\t\n602\t- [ ] **Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n603\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_depth_exceeded_opaque_carries_the_max_depth_diagnostic test_conditional_type_opaque_emits_diagnostic test_mapped_type_opaque_emits_diagnostic test_keyof_opaque_emits_diagnostic test_complex_raw_fallback_opaque_emits_diagnostic -- --nocapture` then `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core`\n604\tExpected: PASS, full suite green.\n605\t\n606\t- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n607\t```bash\n608\tgit add crates/core/src/resolver/collected.rs crates/core/src/resolver/named.rs crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs\n609\tgit commit -m \"refactor(resolver): route collected.rs/named.rs Opaque sites through OpaqueDetail::give_up\"\n610\t```\n611\t\n612\t---\n613\t\n614\t### Task 4: Fix `func.rs`'s multi-param function type — missing diagnostic\n615\t\n616\t**Files:**\n617\t- Modify: `crates/core/src/resolver/func.rs:54-62`\n618\t- Test: inline in `crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs`'s existing `mod tests` (next to Test 16, the existing multi-param-function test that only checks the `PropType`, never the diagnostic)\n619\t\n620\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n621\t```rust\n622\t// crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs, inside `mod tests`, right after the\n623\t// existing multi-param-function `PropType` test (Test 16)\n624\t\n625\t#[test]\n626\tfn test_multi_param_function_opaque_emits_diagnostic() {\n627\t    // Regression test for: func.rs's multi-param function degrade\n628\t    // constructed PropType::Opaque directly with no diagnostic at all — the\n629\t    // only Opaque-producing path in the resolver that gave up silently.\n630\t    let ctx = empty_ctx();\n631\t    let mut state = ResolveState::default();\n632\t    let ct = CollectedType::Function {\n633\t        params: vec![CollectedType::String, CollectedType::Number],\n634\t        param_names: vec![Some(\"a\".into()), Some(\"b\".into())],\n635\t        return_type: Box::new(CollectedType::Void),\n636\t    };\n637\t    let result = super::collected::resolve_collected_type(&ct, Utf8Path::new(\"/test/button.tsx\"), &ctx, &mut state, 0);\n638\t    assert!(\n639\t        matches!(&result, PropType::Opaque(d) if matches!(d.reason(), OpaqueReason::MultiParamFunction)),\n640\t        \"Expected MultiParamFunction opaque, got {:?}\",\n641\t        result\n642\t    );\n643\t    assert!(\n644\t        !state.diagnostics.is_empty(),\n645\t        \"expected a diagnostic for a multi-param function type, got none\"\n646\t    );\n647\t}\n648\t```\n649\t\n650\t- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n651\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_multi_param_function_opaque_emits_diagnostic -- --nocapture`\n652\tExpected: FAIL — `state.diagnostics` is empty, since `func.rs:61` currently constructs `PropType::Opaque` with no diagnostic push anywhere on this path.\n653\t\n654\t- [ ] **Step 3: Write minimal implementation**\n655\t\n656\tIn `crates/core/src/resolver/func.rs`, replace the final block of `resolve_function_type` (lines 54-61):\n657\t```rust\n658\t    // Multi-param function — describe as opaque.\n659\t    let param_strs: Vec<String> = params.iter().map(|p| p.to_raw_string()).collect();\n660\t    let raw = format!(\"({}) => {}\", param_strs.join(\", \"), return_type.to_raw_string());\n661\t\n662\t    // Resolve the return type to see if it's ReactNode.\n663\t    let _ = resolve_collected_type(return_type, consuming_file, ctx, state, depth + 1);\n664\t\n665\t    let diagnostic = Diagnostic {\n666\t        severity: DiagnosticSeverity::Info,\n667\t        message: format!(\n668\t            \"'{}' is a multi-parameter function typ