   \"variant\".to_string(),\n308\t            PropType::String,\n309\t            true,\n310\t            None,\n311\t            \"desc\".to_string(),\n312\t            Default::default(),\n313\t            None,\n314\t            vec![],\n315\t        );\n316\t\n317\t        assert!(prop.required);\n318\t    }\n319\t}\n320\t```\n321\t\n322\t- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n323\tRun: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core new_normalizes_required_false_when_default_value_present -- --nocapture`\n324\tExpected: FAIL to compile — `ParsedProp::new` does not exist yet.\n325\t\n326\t- [ ] **Step 3: Write minimal implementation**\n327\t\n328\tIn `crates/core/src/types/output.rs`, change the struct's fields to `pub(crate)` and add the constructor:\n329\t```rust\n330\tpub struct ParsedProp {\n331\t    /// Prop name\n332\t    pub(crate) name: String,\n333\t    /// Resolved semantic type\n334\t    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n335\t    pub(crate) prop_type: PropType,\n336\t    /// Whether the prop is required\n337\t    pub(crate) required: bool,\n338\t    /// Default value if known (from destructured params or JSDoc)\n339\t    pub(crate) default_value: Option<DefaultValue>,\n340\t    /// JSDoc description of the prop\n341\t    pub(crate) description: String,\n342\t    /// JSDoc @tags on the prop (@deprecated, @since, @see, etc.)\n343\t    pub(crate) tags: BTreeMap<String, String>,\n344\t    /// Interface/type where this prop was originally declared\n345\t    pub(crate) parent: Option<PropParent>,\n346\t    /// All declarations of this prop name (for overloads/merging)\n347\t    pub(crate) declarations: Vec<PropParent>,\n348\t}\n349\t\n350\timpl ParsedProp {\n351\t    /// Constructs a `ParsedProp`, normalizing the `required`/`default_value`\n352\t    /// relationship: RDT convention is that a supplied default value makes a\n353\t    /// prop effectively optional regardless of what `required` was computed\n354\t    /// as upstream (e.g. a destructured param with both