{"parentUuid":"9bc5e79d-e51c-42ff-b7f2-e0fa5edb2334","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8cfd87e5-e489-465b-a51f-4926a8373775","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DDK5B3vg3LHVi9viZoKLve","type":"tool_result","content":"=== pipeline: dedup / distinct message check ===\n271:    // short-circuits to `false` when `src_dirs` itself is empty (`!true` is\n304:Expected: FAIL — `.expect(...)` panics: `output.diagnostics` is empty because the current guard's `&&` short-circuit skips both branches when `src_dirs` is empty.\n316:            message: \"No source directories configured — src_dirs is empty\".into(),\n370:    // ── test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic ─\n377:    // same insert-time collision an overlapping-src_dirs config produces: the\n379:    // a plain Vec extended per merge, no dedup — see types/global.rs), and the\n384:    fn test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic() {\n412:Run: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic -- --nocapture`\n443:                     the later one is kept in the output. Check for overlapping src_dirs or a genuine \\\n454:Run: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic -- --nocapture`\n\n=== allocation-caps-and-lsp: resync check ===\n268:### Task 4: Resync (don't silently `continue`) past a malformed/headerless frame\n281:        // Blank line reached with no Content-Length header at all — the\n297:        // No bytes at all (client closed the connection) is a normal,\n318:/// a normal, expected way for a client to close the connection.\n376:git commit -m \"fix(lsp): close the connection on a malformed header block instead of desyncing the stream\"\n\n=== toon-schema-cli-contract: OpaqueReason / Ord check ===\n85:**Note on approach:** Considered deriving `schemars::JsonSchema` (root-cause-analysis.md's proposed ADR-0006) but rejected it here: `schemars` isn't a dependency anywhere in the workspace today (`grep schemars Cargo.toml` — nothing), and doing it properly means hand-writing `JsonSchema` impls for `PropType` (16 variants, ~250 lines in its existing hand-written `Serialize` impl alone), `CollectedType`, and `OpaqueReason`, mirroring ADR-0002's precedent. That's a multi-day addition, not a bite-sized fix, and this cluster is grouped with two unrelated small fixes. Taking the floor-level option instead: a drift-detection test that serializes a real `ExtractionOutput` and checks every field name it produces shows up somewhere in `schema.rs`'s hand-written schema. No ADR — root-cause-analysis.md's own text says ADR only applies if option (a) is taken.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"20f420bb-1ad2-459e-a343-cd48fc7f7978","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:52:53.719Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== pipeline: dedup / distinct message check ===\n271:    // short-circuits to `false` when `src_dirs` itself is empty (`!true` is\n304:Expected: FAIL — `.expect(...)` panics: `output.diagnostics` is empty because the current guard's `&&` short-circuit skips both branches when `src_dirs` is empty.\n316:            message: \"No source directories configured — src_dirs is empty\".into(),\n370:    // ── test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic ─\n377:    // same insert-time collision an overlapping-src_dirs config produces: the\n379:    // a plain Vec extended per merge, no dedup — see types/global.rs), and the\n384:    fn test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic() {\n412:Run: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic -- --nocapture`\n443:                     the later one is kept in the output. Check for overlapping src_dirs or a genuine \\\n454:Run: `cargo test -p oxc-react-docgen-core test_overlapping_src_dirs_causing_a_key_collision_emits_a_diagnostic -- --nocapture`\n\n=== allocation-caps-and-lsp: resync check ===\n268:### Task 4: Resync (don't silently `continue`) past a malformed/headerless frame\n281:        // Blank line reached with no Content-Length header at all — the\n297:        // No bytes at all (client closed the connection) is a normal,\n318:/// a normal, expected way for a client to close the connection.\n376:git commit -m \"fix(lsp): close the connection on a malformed header block instead of desyncing the stream\"\n\n=== toon-schema-cli-contract: OpaqueReason / Ord check ===\n85:**Note on approach:** Considered deriving `schemars::JsonSchema` (root-cause-analysis.md's proposed ADR-0006) but rejected it here: `schemars` isn't a dependency anywhere in the workspace today (`grep schemars Cargo.toml` — nothing), and doing it properly means hand-writing `JsonSchema` impls for `PropType` (16 variants, ~250 lines in its existing hand-written `Serialize` impl alone), `CollectedType`, and `OpaqueReason`, mirroring ADR-0002's precedent. That's a multi-day addition, not a bite-sized fix, and this cluster is grouped with two unrelated small fixes. Taking the floor-level option instead: a drift-detection test that serializes a real `ExtractionOutput` and checks every field name it produces shows up somewhere in `schema.rs`'s hand-written schema. No ADR — root-cause-analysis.md's own text says ADR only applies if option (a) is taken.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9bc5e79d-e51c-42ff-b7f2-e0fa5edb2334","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
