{"parentUuid":"3e6ca8ec-0c71-40e3-b721-d6e7bbb64bcc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FWJFXwTWjYF5kAAyYb4n81","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"oxc-react-codegen\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":56},"type":"attachment","uuid":"95bb5b3f-0be7-463e-a5de-42cabd815505","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:54:46.135Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"95bb5b3f-0be7-463e-a5de-42cabd815505","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Explanatory"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"90a3f163-ecda-4cd5-97e4-cb1203d474a7","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:54:46.144Z","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
{"parentUuid":"90a3f163-ecda-4cd5-97e4-cb1203d474a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cdi8veGUoAtdcBMC1R7wb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe most telling moment in this whole pipeline was the plan-drafting agents *overriding* the root-cause document's original mechanism without being told to — Part B's Task 2 independently placed `OpaqueDetail` in `types/output.rs` instead of the originally-proposed `resolver/opaque.rs`, with an explicit note explaining that the latter would violate the project's own no-reverse-dependency rule. That agent wasn't running an adversarial-verification prompt; it was just told \"read the actual code, don't trust the doc's summary\" while drafting. That's a cheaper lever than a dedicated skeptic pass: instructing implementers to re-derive from source rather than transcribe a spec catches a class of error before it ever needs adversarial catching. The dedicated adversarial pass still earned its cost here — it caught the `ParsedProp` `pub(crate)` bug and the plugin-hook `UnwindSafe` compile error that slipped through even careful reading — but it's notable that \"read real code\" alone already prevented several of the errors a less careful drafting pass would have propagated verbatim.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nEverything from this session is committed to disk (nothing staged/committed to git yet — that's your call):\n\n- **`docs/edge-cases.md`** — the original 30-finding audit\n- **`docs/root-cause-analysis.md`** — 11 root causes + 7 standalone findings, corrected post-adversarial-review (every `[corrected]` marker shows exactly what changed and why)\n- **`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-04-edge-case-remediation.md`** — 43 TDD tasks across 7 parts, ready to execute\n\nTwo mechanisms started out **unsound** and are now fixed in both the analysis and the plan: the resolver give-up constructor (originally would've broken `known.rs`'s architecture and the wire-format `Deserialize` impl — narrowed to the 3 real sites, redesigned to respect the reverse-dependency rule) and the `ParsedProp` invariant (originally `pub(crate)` fields, which wouldn't compile against `crates/cli` and wouldn't stop the same-crate misuse it targeted — now a sealed-field pattern that does both).\n\nGiven the plan's size, I'd suggest **subagent-driven-development** for execution — fresh implementer per task, spec-compliance review then code-quality review before each moves on, starting with Part A. Want me to kick that off, or would you like to read through the plan first?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":285,"cache_read_input_tokens":353186,"output_tokens":847,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":285,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":353186,"cache_creation_input_tokens":285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":285},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdi8vaVGG5F6uKGtvzd3y","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d8a0956-a1b7-4fe8-8ad3-7fbbc3f60cef","timestamp":"2026-08-04T17:55:00.554Z","effort":"medium","session_id":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/oxc-react-codegen","sessionId":"d83be67f-8b07-459c-989b-529791ef5ca7","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"delightful-booping-fern"}
